"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkwebsite=globalThis.webpackChunkwebsite||[]).push([[22083],{44204(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"rentiva-v6.4.1-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.4.1-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-11-19-rentiva-v6.4.1-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-11-19-rentiva-v6.4.1-release.md","title":"Rentiva 6.4.1 \u2014 Eine Willkommens-E-Mail f\xfcr ein neues Konto sowie korrekt angezeigte Buchungskalender-\xdcbersicht und Dashboard-Daten","description":"6.4.1 ist ein kleines Update, das korrigiert, was ein Admin auf drei Bildschirmen sieht und was ein neuer Kunde erh\xe4lt. Die \xdcbersicht im Buchungskalender zeigt jetzt die Abholungs- und R\xfcckgabezeiten, den Gesamtbetrag mit der W\xe4hrung deines Shops und Datumsangaben im Format deiner Website. \u201eAnstehende Vorg\xe4nge\u201c im Dashboard schreibt seine Datumsangaben in deiner Admin-Sprache. Ein Kunde, dessen Konto WooCommerce anlegt, erh\xe4lt eine Willkommens-E-Mail statt zwei. Nichts zu konfigurieren, kein Datenbankschritt. Du nutzt Rentiva Pro? Nichts zu tun: Pro 6.5.1 funktioniert mit 6.4.1.","date":"2026-11-19T18:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"bookings","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/bookings"},{"inline":true,"label":"email","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/email"},{"inline":true,"label":"woocommerce","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/woocommerce"}],"readingTime":2.06,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v6.4.1-release","title":"Rentiva 6.4.1 \u2014 Eine Willkommens-E-Mail f\xfcr ein neues Konto sowie korrekt angezeigte Buchungskalender-\xdcbersicht und Dashboard-Daten","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","bookings","email","woocommerce"],"date":"2026-11-19T18:00"},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva Pro 6.5.0 \u2014 Provision f\xfcr den richtigen Anbieter, Datenschutzanfragen per E-Mail, ein funktionierender Anbietervertrag und Berichte in der Zeitzone der Website","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.5.0-release"}},"content":"6.4.1 ist ein kleines Update, das korrigiert, was ein Admin auf drei Bildschirmen sieht und was ein neuer Kunde erh\xe4lt. Die \xdcbersicht im Buchungskalender zeigt jetzt die Abholungs- und R\xfcckgabezeiten, den Gesamtbetrag mit der W\xe4hrung deines Shops und Datumsangaben im Format deiner Website. \u201eAnstehende Vorg\xe4nge\u201c im Dashboard schreibt seine Datumsangaben in deiner Admin-Sprache. Ein Kunde, dessen Konto WooCommerce anlegt, erh\xe4lt eine Willkommens-E-Mail statt zwei. Nichts zu konfigurieren, kein Datenbankschritt. **Du nutzt Rentiva Pro?** Nichts zu tun: Pro 6.5.1 funktioniert mit 6.4.1.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Eine Willkommens-E-Mail f\xfcr ein neues Konto\\n\\nWenn WooCommerce das Konto eines Kunden angelegt hat, beim Checkout oder unter \u201eMein Konto\u201c, erhielt der Kunde zwei Willkommensnachrichten: die eigene Neues-Konto-E-Mail von WooCommerce und die E-Mail \u201eWillkommen bei \u2026\u201c von Rentiva. Jetzt wird die Willkommens-E-Mail von Rentiva f\xfcr diese Konten \xfcbersprungen, sodass der Kunde nur eine erh\xe4lt.\\n\\nWenn du die Neues-Konto-E-Mail von WooCommerce deaktiviert hast (**WooCommerce > Einstellungen > E-Mails**), wird die Willkommens-E-Mail von Rentiva weiterhin gesendet, sodass niemand ohne eine bleibt. Kunden, deren Konten vor diesem Update angelegt wurden, sind nicht betroffen.\\n\\n## Die \xdcbersicht im Buchungskalender\\n\\nKlicke auf einen gebuchten Tag unter **Buchungen > Kalender**, um die \xdcbersicht zu \xf6ffnen.\\n\\n- **Abholungs- und R\xfcckgabezeiten** erscheinen jetzt unter den Datumsangaben. Sie wurden immer mit der Buchung gespeichert, aber die \xdcbersicht zeigte \u201e\u2014\u201c.\\n- **Der Gesamtbetrag** enth\xe4lt die W\xe4hrung deines Shops und ist wie in der Buchungsliste formatiert (zum Beispiel $237.60 statt 237.6).\\n- **Datumsangaben und der Erstellungszeitpunkt** folgen dem Datums- und Zeitformat deiner Website (**Einstellungen > Allgemein**).\\n\\nAn einem Tag mit mehreren Buchungen zeigt die Liste in der \xdcbersicht die Daten jeder Buchung mit ihren Uhrzeiten.\\n\\n## Datumsangaben im Dashboard\\n\\n- **Anstehende Vorg\xe4nge** schreibt seine Datumsangaben in deiner Admin-Sprache. Bisher wurde die Sprache des Browsers verwendet, sodass ein englischer Admin-Bildschirm in einem t\xfcrkischen Browser \u201e20 Kas\u201c anzeigte.\\n- Eine Buchung wird nicht mehr **einen Tag zu fr\xfch** angezeigt, wenn sich dein Browser westlich von UTC befindet (zum Beispiel in Amerika).\\n\\n## Kleinere Korrekturen\\n\\n- Die **Liste der gesperrten Tage** im Fahrzeug-Editor funktioniert jetzt auch f\xfcr Admins, deren Sprache Portugiesisch (AO90) ist.\\n- Eine **Neuinstallation** schreibt keinen Datenbankfehler \u201eTable \u2026 doesn\'t exist\u201c mehr ins Log.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Wo du es bekommst.** Rentiva ist auf [WordPress.org](https://wordpress.org/plugins/mhm-rentiva/) und auf GitHub als [`v6.4.1`](https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva/releases/tag/v6.4.1) verf\xfcgbar. WordPress bietet es als gew\xf6hnliches Update an. Die vollst\xe4ndige Liste der \xc4nderungen findest du in den [Versionshinweisen zu 6.4.0](/blog/rentiva-v6.4.0-release) und im Changelog des Plugins."},{"id":"rentiva-pro-v6.5.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.5.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-11-18-rentiva-pro-v6.5.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-11-18-rentiva-pro-v6.5.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva Pro 6.5.0 \u2014 Provision f\xfcr den richtigen Anbieter, Datenschutzanfragen per E-Mail, ein funktionierender Anbietervertrag und Berichte in der Zeitzone der Website","description":"6.5.0 korrigiert den Umgang mit Anbietergeldern, Stornierungen und personenbezogenen Daten. Die Provision geht jetzt an den Anbieter, dem das gebuchte Fahrzeug geh\xf6rt; bisher konnte sie an den Kunden gehen, der die Buchung vorgenommen hat. Eine Erstattung macht nur noch eine Provision r\xfcckg\xe4ngig, die tats\xe4chlich gutgeschrieben wurde. Nachrichten, Anbieterdaten und Einwilligungsnachweise erscheinen jetzt in den Datenschutz-Werkzeugen von WordPress, und die Buttons \u201eDatenexport anfordern\u201c und \u201eDatenl\xf6schung anfordern\u201c unter \u201eMein Konto\u201c starten eine Datenschutzanfrage, die per E-Mail best\xe4tigt wird. Wenn du \u201eAnbietervertrag erforderlich\u201c aktivierst, wird jetzt immer ein Vertrag angezeigt \u2013 mit einer Startvorlage, wenn der Text leer ist. Berichte und Anbieteranalysen richten sich nach der Zeitzone der Website. Pro 6.5.0 erfordert WordPress 7.0 oder neuer und Rentiva (Lite) 6.4.0 oder neuer: Aktualisiere zuerst Lite, dann Pro.","date":"2026-11-18T22:30:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"pro","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/pro"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"privacy","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/privacy"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"}],"readingTime":6.73,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-pro-v6.5.0-release","title":"Rentiva Pro 6.5.0 \u2014 Provision f\xfcr den richtigen Anbieter, Datenschutzanfragen per E-Mail, ein funktionierender Anbietervertrag und Berichte in der Zeitzone der Website","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","pro","vendor","privacy","security"],"date":"2026-11-18T22:30"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.4.1 \u2014 Eine Willkommens-E-Mail f\xfcr ein neues Konto sowie korrekt angezeigte Buchungskalender-\xdcbersicht und Dashboard-Daten","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.4.1-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.4.0 \u2014 Neue Suche, Ergebnisseite und Fahrzeugkarte, ein Buchungspreis, der dem berechneten Betrag entspricht, und WordPress 7.0","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.4.0-release"}},"content":"6.5.0 korrigiert den Umgang mit Anbietergeldern, Stornierungen und personenbezogenen Daten. Die Provision geht jetzt an den Anbieter, dem das gebuchte Fahrzeug geh\xf6rt; bisher konnte sie an den Kunden gehen, der die Buchung vorgenommen hat. Eine Erstattung macht nur noch eine Provision r\xfcckg\xe4ngig, die tats\xe4chlich gutgeschrieben wurde. Nachrichten, Anbieterdaten und Einwilligungsnachweise erscheinen jetzt in den Datenschutz-Werkzeugen von WordPress, und die Buttons \u201eDatenexport anfordern\u201c und \u201eDatenl\xf6schung anfordern\u201c unter \u201eMein Konto\u201c starten eine Datenschutzanfrage, die per E-Mail best\xe4tigt wird. Wenn du \u201eAnbietervertrag erforderlich\u201c aktivierst, wird jetzt immer ein Vertrag angezeigt \u2013 mit einer Startvorlage, wenn der Text leer ist. Berichte und Anbieteranalysen richten sich nach der Zeitzone der Website. **Pro 6.5.0 erfordert WordPress 7.0 oder neuer und Rentiva (Lite) 6.4.0 oder neuer: Aktualisiere zuerst Lite, dann Pro.**\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::caution Provisionszeilen, die vor diesem Update geschrieben wurden, werden nicht korrigiert\\nDie Provision geht jetzt an den Eigent\xfcmer des gebuchten Fahrzeugs, und f\xfcr die eigenen Fahrzeuge der Website wird keine Provisionszeile geschrieben. Zeilen, die vor diesem Update geschrieben wurden, werden nicht korrigiert.\\n:::\\n\\n:::caution Die Datenschutz-Buttons unter \u201eMein Konto\u201c wirken nicht mehr sofort\\n\u201eDatenexport anfordern\u201c und \u201eDatenl\xf6schung anfordern\u201c er\xf6ffnen jetzt eine WordPress-Datenschutzanfrage, die der Kunde per E-Mail best\xe4tigt. \xdcber den Button wird nichts heruntergeladen oder gel\xf6scht.\\n:::\\n\\n## Die Provision geht an den richtigen Anbieter\\n\\n- **Die Provision wird dem Anbieter gutgeschrieben, dem das Fahrzeug geh\xf6rt.** Bisher wurde sie dem Kunden gutgeschrieben, der die Buchung vorgenommen hat (oder niemandem), und eine Erstattung f\xfcr ein eigenes Fahrzeug der Website belastete den Kunden. Jetzt belastet eine Erstattung den Anbieter, dessen Gutschrift sie r\xfcckg\xe4ngig macht, und die Einnahmen sowie \u201eBuchungen, letzte 30 Tage\u201c im Anbieter-Panel z\xe4hlen die richtigen Buchungen.\\n- **Eine Erstattung erzeugt nur dann eine Zeile, wenn eine Gutschrift existiert.** Eine Erstattung, die vor der Bezahlung der Bestellung eintraf (zum Beispiel eine Bank\xfcberweisung, die noch in Bearbeitung war und erstattet wurde), hinterlie\xdf beim Anbieter eine Belastung f\xfcr Geld, das nie gutgeschrieben worden war. Eine wartende Erstattung wird jetzt geschrieben, wenn die Zahlung abgeschlossen ist \u2013 zum Provisionssatz dieser Gutschrift.\\n- **Stornierungssperren gelten nur f\xfcr Anbieterfahrzeuge.** Wenn ein Administrator eine Buchung f\xfcr sein eigenes Fahrzeug im Bearbeitungsbildschirm der Buchung stornierte, wurden die Termine dieses Fahrzeugs f\xfcr 30 Tage gesperrt. Die Sperre gilt jetzt nur noch f\xfcr Fahrzeuge, die von einem Anbieter eingestellt wurden.\\n- **Der Zuverl\xe4ssigkeitswert z\xe4hlt die richtigen Stornierungen.** Er z\xe4hlte jede Stornierung, die die Benutzer-ID des Anbieters trug \u2013 auch eine durch einen Administrator, der sp\xe4ter Anbieter wurde, oder durch einen Anbieter, der seine eigene Miete unter \u201eMein Konto\u201c stornierte \u2013, und er z\xe4hlte nach dem Erstellungsdatum der Buchung, sodass eine vor sieben Monaten vorgenommene und gestern stornierte Buchung \xfcbersehen wurde. Jetzt z\xe4hlt er nur Stornierungen, die als Anbieter vorgenommen wurden, nach dem Datum der Stornierung und in der Zeitzone der Website. Die Termine werden nicht mehr gesperrt, wenn ein Anbieter seine eigene Miete unter \u201eMein Konto\u201c storniert.\\n- **Ausgeblendete Einstellungen:** \u201eSperrzeitraum f\xfcr stornierte Buchungen (Tage)\u201c und \u201eAbgezogene Punkte pro Stornierung\u201c sind in den Einstellungen des Anbieter-Marktplatzes ausgeblendet, weil es noch keinen Bildschirm gibt, auf dem ein Anbieter die Buchung eines Kunden stornieren kann. Gespeicherte Werte bleiben erhalten und gelten weiterhin.\\n- **Strafsperrtage:** Strafsperrtage nach einer Anbieterstornierung gelten in der Fahrzeugsuche jetzt als gebucht und werden nach 30 Tagen (Stornierungstag plus 29) automatisch aufgehoben. \u201eAuf alle anwenden\u201c und \u201eVon allen entfernen\u201c kopieren oder l\xf6schen keine Strafsperrtage mehr. Termine, die du manuell gesperrt hast, bleiben erhalten.\\n\\n## Datenschutz-Werkzeuge\\n\\n- **Drei Pro-Eintr\xe4ge in den Datenschutz-Werkzeugen von WordPress.** Werkzeuge > Personenbezogene Daten exportieren und Personenbezogene Daten l\xf6schen enthalten jetzt Nachrichten (die Konversationen des Kunden), Anbieterdaten (Bewerbungen, Profil, Auszahlungen, Berichte und Zuverl\xe4ssigkeitswert, auch von abgelehnten Bewerbern) und Einwilligungsnachweise. Sie funktionieren auch, wenn die Lizenz abgelaufen ist. Bankkonten werden nur mit ihren letzten vier Ziffern exportiert. Anbieterdatens\xe4tze bleiben beim L\xf6schen erhalten (gesetzliche Aufbewahrungspflicht), und das Ergebnis weist darauf hin. Der vorgeschlagene Text f\xfcr die Datenschutzerkl\xe4rung erh\xe4lt einen Pro-Abschnitt.\\n- **Der Anbieterexport ist vollst\xe4ndig.** Er bl\xe4ttert jetzt durch alle Bewerbungen, Auszahlungen und Berichte; bisher stoppte er bei 20 Bewerbungen und 500 Auszahlungen bzw. Berichten, meldete trotzdem immer, er sei fertig, und abgelehnte Auszahlungen fehlten.\\n- **Anfragen unter \u201eMein Konto\u201c werden per E-Mail best\xe4tigt** (siehe Hinweis oben). Die Best\xe4tigungs-E-Mail wird f\xfcr dasselbe Konto und dieselbe Aktion innerhalb von 10 Minuten nicht erneut gesendet, und der alte Export, der auch Sitzungstoken und die verschl\xfcsselte IBAN enthielt, ist entfernt.\\n- **Eine einzige Einwilligungsantwort.** Die Datenschutz-Einwilligungskarte unter \u201eMein Konto\u201c und die Buchungspr\xfcfung lasen unterschiedliche Antworten, sodass ein Kunde, der die Karte akzeptiert hatte, trotzdem als nicht einwilligend behandelt werden konnte. Beide lesen jetzt dieselbe Antwort.\\n- **T\xfcrkisch:** Der Einwilligungshinweis nennt KVKK (Gesetz Nr. 6698) statt der DSGVO.\\n\\n## Ein Anbietervertrag, der immer angezeigt wird\\n\\nWar \u201eAnbietervertrag erforderlich\u201c aktiviert und der Text leer, sahen Bewerber keinen Vertrag und der Administrator keine Warnung. Bei leerem Text wird jetzt eine integrierte, \xfcbersetzbare Vorlage angezeigt, die Inserate, Buchungen, Provision und Auszahlungen, Stornierungen, Sch\xe4den und Versicherung, personenbezogene Daten, Sperrung und K\xfcndigung sowie \xc4nderungen abdeckt. Sie ist ein Ausgangspunkt zur \xdcberpr\xfcfung, keine Rechtsberatung. Der Vertrag zeigt au\xdferdem einfache Formatierungen (# \xdcberschriften, **fett**, - Listen, --- Trennlinien) statt roher Symbole.\\n\\n## Berichte in der Zeitzone der Website\\n\\nBuchungsdaten in den Kunden- und Buchungsberichten und im CSV-Export, die gebuchten Tage im Fahrzeugbericht, die Standardzeitr\xe4ume der Berichte, der Ablauf der Stornierungssperre und die Tageseinteilung der Anbieteranalysen richten sich jetzt nach der Zeitzone der Website, sodass eine Buchung kurz vor oder nach Mitternacht nicht mehr am falschen Tag landet.\\n\\n## Fehlerbehebungen und Aufr\xe4umarbeiten\\n\\n- **Backslashes bleiben erhalten.** Ein Backslash, der im Fahrzeugformular f\xfcr Anbieter (Titel, Beschreibung, Marke, Modell, Farbe, Kilometerstand, Kennzeichen, Stadt), in Feldern der Anbieterbewerbung und der Ablehnungsnotiz, in der externen Referenz einer Auszahlung (\u201eBANK\\\\6\u201c wurde als \u201eBANK6\u201c gespeichert), in Zeilen der Transfer-Zusatzleistungen und im Verlauf des Anbieterwerts eingegeben wurde, ging beim Speichern verloren.\\n- **Die Anbietertabelle:** Wenn du auf Seite 2 einen Filter ge\xe4ndert hast, wurde Seite 2 mit dem neuen Filter und danach Seite 1 gesendet, und eine langsame Antwort konnte eine neuere \xfcberschreiben. Seite und Filter \xe4ndern sich jetzt gemeinsam in einer Anfrage, Tabelle und Seitennavigation bleiben w\xe4hrend des Ladens sichtbar, und \u201eWird geladen \u2026\u201c erscheint nur vor der ersten Antwort.\\n- **Bildschirm \u201eFahrzeug bearbeiten\u201c.** Er zeigt die Pro-Boxen in der Reihenfolge des neuen Designs nach den Seitenboxen von Lite (sofern du die Boxen nicht selbst angeordnet hast), jeweils mit einem \u201ePro\u201c-Label. Die Box \u201eLebenszyklus\u201c zeigt den Status als farbige Pille mit einer Warnung, wenn noch 10 Tage oder weniger verbleiben, und ihre Farben sind auf Wei\xdf gut lesbar. Die Boxen \u201eDokumente\u201c und \u201eTransfer\u201c verwenden dieselben Stile, und \u201enur Vermietung\u201c blendet die Transfer-Felder sofort aus, statt sie wegzuschieben.\\n- **Die Karte eines reinen Transfer-Fahrzeugs** hat keinen Vergleichen-Button mehr, sodass der Vergleich nur Fahrzeuge enth\xe4lt, die gemietet werden k\xf6nnen.\\n- **Funktioniert mit Lite 6.4.0.** Pro funktioniert mit dem neu gestalteten Buchungsformular, \u201eMein Konto\u201c, Vergleich, Kalender, Kontakt und Bewertungen in Lite 6.4.0. Das Fenster f\xfcr Transfer-Zusatzleistungen zeigt das W\xe4hrungssymbol der Website f\xfcr sich allein, und die Seite mit den Anbieterbuchungen l\xe4dt ihre eigenen Stile. Wenn du Standorte \xe4nderst oder einen Transfer-Import ausf\xfchrst, wird die zwischengespeicherte Standortliste aktualisiert.\\n- **Lizenzerinnerung.** In den letzten 14 Tagen nennt sie das Ablaufdatum, verlinkt die Lizenzseite und bietet \u201eIn 3 Tagen erinnern\u201c an; sie erscheint auf den Rentiva-Bildschirmen, unter Plugins und im WordPress-Dashboard statt auf jeder Admin-Seite.\\n- **T\xfcrkisch:** \u201eDetails\u201c hei\xdft \xfcberall \u201eAyr\u0131nt\u0131\u201c, wie in Lite, die \xdcberschrift des Filterbereichs im Anbieterverzeichnis lautet \u201eFiltre\u201c und der Anwenden-Button im Anbieter-Kontobuch \u201eFiltrele\u201c.\\n\\n## Was du nach dem Update pr\xfcfen solltest\\n\\n- **Update-Reihenfolge:** zuerst Rentiva (Lite) 6.4.0, dann Pro 6.5.0. Beide ben\xf6tigen WordPress 7.0 oder neuer (bisher 6.7).\\n- **Provision:** Zeilen, die vor diesem Update geschrieben wurden, werden nicht korrigiert; ber\xfccksichtige das, wenn du fr\xfchere Anbietereinnahmen durchsiehst.\\n- **Anbietervertrag:** Wenn \u201eAnbietervertrag erforderlich\u201c aktiviert ist, lies den Text, den Bewerber jetzt sehen \u2013 besonders, wenn deiner leer war.\\n- **Datenschutzanfragen:** Informiere deine Kunden, dass die Buttons unter \u201eMein Konto\u201c jetzt eine Best\xe4tigungs-E-Mail senden.\\n- **Einstellungen des Anbieter-Marktplatzes:** Die beiden Stornierungseinstellungen sind ausgeblendet, ihre gespeicherten Werte gelten aber weiterhin.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Wo du es bekommst.** Pro 6.5.0 ist f\xfcr Lizenzinhaber an derselben Stelle wie bisher auf wpalemi.com erh\xe4ltlich. Aktualisiere zuerst [Rentiva auf 6.4.0](/blog/rentiva-v6.4.0-release). Das vollst\xe4ndige \xc4nderungsprotokoll liegt dem Plugin in beiden Sprachen bei."},{"id":"rentiva-v6.4.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.4.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-11-18-rentiva-v6.4.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-11-18-rentiva-v6.4.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva 6.4.0 \u2014 Neue Suche, Ergebnisseite und Fahrzeugkarte, ein Buchungspreis, der dem berechneten Betrag entspricht, und WordPress 7.0","description":"6.4.0 gestaltet die Seiten neu, die Besucher zuerst sehen, und sorgt daf\xfcr, dass der angezeigte Preis auch der berechnete Preis ist. Die Suchleiste, die Ergebnisseite und die Fahrzeugkarte folgen dem neuen Frontend-Design, mit einem Kategoriefilter, Filter-Chips, einer Vergleichsleiste und einer Filterschublade auf Smartphones. Mit Suchdaten zeigt jede Karte den Gesamtpreis f\xfcr die Miete. Das Buchungsformular nennt genau den Betrag, den WooCommerce berechnet: Saisonpreise wirken sich jetzt auf die Zahlung aus, und Steuern kommen nur noch von WooCommerce. Auch Mein Konto folgt dem neuen Design. Rentiva ben\xf6tigt jetzt WordPress 7.0 oder neuer, und du musst nach dem Update deinen Seiten-Cache leeren \u2013 siehe die Hinweise unten. Die Version ist auf WordPress.org ver\xf6ffentlicht, daher bietet WordPress sie dir als gew\xf6hnliches Update an; die WordPress.org-Seite hat jetzt acht Screenshots. Du verwendest Rentiva Pro? Aktualisiere Pro nach diesem Release auf 6.5.0; Pro 6.4.x funktioniert bis dahin weiter.","date":"2026-11-18T22:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"search","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/search"},{"inline":true,"label":"booking","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/booking"},{"inline":true,"label":"woocommerce","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/woocommerce"},{"inline":true,"label":"account","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/account"},{"inline":true,"label":"accessibility","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/accessibility"}],"readingTime":13.39,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v6.4.0-release","title":"Rentiva 6.4.0 \u2014 Neue Suche, Ergebnisseite und Fahrzeugkarte, ein Buchungspreis, der dem berechneten Betrag entspricht, und WordPress 7.0","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","search","booking","woocommerce","account","accessibility"],"date":"2026-11-18T22:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva Pro 6.5.0 \u2014 Provision f\xfcr den richtigen Anbieter, Datenschutzanfragen per E-Mail, ein funktionierender Anbietervertrag und Berichte in der Zeitzone der Website","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.5.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva Pro 6.4.0 \u2014 Transfers nutzen deine eingestellte Anzahlung, der Transfer-Warenkorb wird auf dem Server berechnet, sichere Editor-Vorschauen","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.4.0-release"}},"content":"6.4.0 gestaltet die Seiten neu, die Besucher zuerst sehen, und sorgt daf\xfcr, dass der angezeigte Preis auch der berechnete Preis ist. Die Suchleiste, die Ergebnisseite und die Fahrzeugkarte folgen dem neuen Frontend-Design, mit einem Kategoriefilter, Filter-Chips, einer Vergleichsleiste und einer Filterschublade auf Smartphones. Mit Suchdaten zeigt jede Karte den Gesamtpreis f\xfcr die Miete. Das Buchungsformular nennt genau den Betrag, den WooCommerce berechnet: Saisonpreise wirken sich jetzt auf die Zahlung aus, und Steuern kommen nur noch von WooCommerce. Auch Mein Konto folgt dem neuen Design. **Rentiva ben\xf6tigt jetzt WordPress 7.0 oder neuer, und du musst nach dem Update deinen Seiten-Cache leeren** \u2013 siehe die Hinweise unten. Die Version ist auf WordPress.org ver\xf6ffentlicht, daher bietet WordPress sie dir als gew\xf6hnliches Update an; die WordPress.org-Seite hat jetzt acht Screenshots. **Du verwendest Rentiva Pro?** Aktualisiere Pro nach diesem Release auf 6.5.0; Pro 6.4.x funktioniert bis dahin weiter.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::caution Rentiva ben\xf6tigt jetzt WordPress 7.0 oder neuer\\nBisher war es 6.7. Die Testsuite lief unter WordPress 6.7 und 6.9 nicht fehlerfrei durch, und auch das aktuelle WooCommerce setzt 7.0 voraus. Websites mit einer \xe4lteren WordPress-Version bleiben bei 6.3.1, bis sie WordPress aktualisieren.\\n:::\\n\\n:::caution Leere nach dem Update deinen Seiten-Cache\\nLeere den Cache deines Hosters, LiteSpeed Cache, WP Rocket und \xc4hnliches. Eine von 6.3.x zwischengespeicherte Seite beh\xe4lt das alte Markup des Buchungsformulars und des Kalenders, das die neuen Skripte nicht steuern, bis der Cache geleert wird. Der eigene kurzlebige Cache von Rentiva beginnt von selbst neu.\\n:::\\n\\n:::caution Wenn dein Theme Rentiva-Templates \xfcberschreibt\\nTemplates unter `templates/shortcodes/*` und `templates/partials/*` (Buchungsformular, Verf\xfcgbarkeitskalender, Kontaktformular, Fahrzeugdetails, Bewertungsformular und Suche) haben neues Markup. Ein Theme, das sie \xfcberschreibt, beh\xe4lt sein altes Markup, das die neuen Skripte nicht steuern: Entferne oder aktualisiere diese \xdcberschreibungen nach dem Update. Ein Theme, das `templates/account/*.php` \xfcberschreibt, beh\xe4lt sein altes Markup und kann ungestylt aussehen, weil die alten Konto-Stylesheets auf diesen Seiten nicht mehr geladen werden. Ein Theme, das `myaccount/dashboard.php` von WooCommerce \xfcberschreibt, beh\xe4lt sein eigenes.\\n:::\\n\\n## Eine neue Suchleiste und Ergebnisseite\\n\\n- **Die Suchleiste ist eine Zeile:** Abholort, Abholdatum und -uhrzeit, R\xfcckgabedatum (die R\xfcckgabeuhrzeit folgt der Abholuhrzeit) und \u201eSuchen\u201c, mit sichtbaren Beschriftungen. Sie \xf6ffnet sich mit der Suche des Besuchers oder, wenn Daten erforderlich sind, mit morgen 10:00 Uhr bis drei Tage sp\xe4ter (l\xe4nger, wenn die Mindestmietdauer l\xe4nger ist). Es gibt keine Tabs: Die Option \u201eShow Rental Tab\u201c wurde aus dem Block und dem Elementor-Widget entfernt, und ein gespeicherter Wert wird ignoriert. Bei nur einem Abholort zeigt die Leiste ihn als Textzeile statt als Liste.\\n- **Die Ergebnisseite hat eine Filterspalte** mit einem Kategoriefilter, entfernbaren Chips f\xfcr aktive Filter, einer Zeile mit der Anzahl der Fahrzeuge, den Daten und der Anzahl der Tage, Sortierung nach Gesamtpreis, wenn Daten gesetzt sind, einem Raster-/Listen-Umschalter und Seitenschaltfl\xe4chen. Beim \xc4ndern eines Filters, der Sortierung oder der Seite bleiben die Daten und alle Filter erhalten.\\n- **Auf Smartphones** zeigt die Ergebnisseite eine Zusammenfassungskarte mit einem Link \u201e\xc4ndern\u201c und \xf6ffnet die Filter in einer bildschirmf\xfcllenden Schublade, die sich mit der Tastatur bedienen l\xe4sst.\\n- **Eine Vergleichsleiste** zeigt, wie viele Fahrzeuge ausgew\xe4hlt sind (bis zu 3), ihre Namen und einen Link zur Vergleichsseite. Der Vergleichs-Shortcode vergleicht bis zu 3 Fahrzeuge (bisher 4).\\n- **Leere Ergebnisse erkl\xe4ren den Grund:** noch keine Daten gew\xe4hlt, keine Fahrzeuge f\xfcr die Daten frei, die Filter lassen nichts \xfcbrig oder keine Fahrzeuge eingestellt.\\n- **Eine bereits vergangene Abholzeit** kann von Kunden nicht mehr berechnet oder gebucht werden. Die Suche weist darauf hin und listet die Fahrzeuge ohne Daten auf. Ein Administrator kann eine Miete weiterhin nachtr\xe4glich erfassen.\\n- **Mit Seiten-Caching f\xfcr Besucher** h\xe4ngt die zwischengespeicherte Ergebnisseite von jedem Filter, der Seitennummer, den Daten und der Vergleichsliste des Besuchers ab, sodass die Ergebnisse eines Besuchers keinem anderen angezeigt werden. Die Filteroptionen werden aktualisiert, wenn ein Fahrzeug gespeichert wird.\\n- **Daten passen in ihre Felder.** Mit dem Standard-Datumsformat von WordPress (\u201eSeptember 30, 2026\u201c) ragt ein Datum in der Suchleiste oder in der Buchungskarte der Fahrzeugseite nicht mehr \xfcber sein Feld hinaus. Die Leiste bricht nach der ihr zugewiesenen Breite um, nicht nach der Bildschirmbreite: Jedes Feld beh\xe4lt Platz f\xfcr ein langes Datum, und eines, das nicht passt, r\xfcckt in die n\xe4chste Zeile. In der Inhaltsspalte von Twenty Twenty-Five (eine 565px breite Leiste) belegen Abholung und R\xfcckgabe je eine Zeile, darunter \u201eSuchen\u201c; ab etwa 800px Breite (1000px mit Abholort) ist die Leiste einzeilig. Auf Smartphones steht die Uhrzeit unter ihrem Datum. In der \xfcblichen 340px breiten Buchungskarte belegt jedes Datum eine Zeile neben seiner Uhrzeit (auf Smartphones darunter). Die Leiste beh\xe4lt ihre Breite innerhalb von Zeilen- und Stapel-Bl\xf6cken sowie Elementor-Zeilencontainern.\\n\\n## Eine neu gestaltete Fahrzeugkarte\\n\\n- **Die Karte ist neu gestaltet** in Fahrzeugrastern, -listen, hervorgehobenen Fahrzeugen, Suchergebnissen und Mein Konto > Favoriten. Mit Suchdaten zeigt sie den Gesamtpreis f\xfcr die Miete einschlie\xdflich erforderlicher Zusatzleistungen sowie den Preis pro Tag. Sie listet Sitzpl\xe4tze, Getriebe und Kraftstoff, die Anzahlung und den Zeitraum f\xfcr kostenlose Stornierung auf. Die Elementor-Stileinstellungen f\xfcr Fahrzeugkarten funktionieren weiter, und beim Update wird das von Elementor generierte CSS einmal neu erstellt, damit gespeicherte Fahrzeugkarten-Stile auf die neue Karte angewendet werden.\\n- **Die Summe geht auf.** Eine Karte mit Suchdaten nennt die erforderlichen Leistungen, die ihr Gesamtpreis enth\xe4lt, und was sie hinzuf\xfcgen (\u201eErforderliche Leistung enthalten: Vollkasko 25,00 $\u201c).\\n- **Karten in einer Reihe stimmen \xfcberein.** Sie ordnen Preis und Buchen-Schaltfl\xe4che gleich an, abh\xe4ngig von der Kartenbreite: Auf einer schmalen Karte steht der Preis \xfcber der Schaltfl\xe4che, auf einer breiten daneben. Bisher schob ein nur ein Pixel breiterer Preis (1,750.00 neben 850.00) die Schaltfl\xe4che einer Karte nach unten, w\xe4hrend die Nachbarkarten sie neben dem Preis behielten.\\n- **Au\xdferdem behoben:** Das Buchungsformular zeigt die Details des Fahrzeugs (Sitzpl\xe4tze, Getriebe, Kraftstoff) wieder unter seinem Namen an, das Hauptfoto der Fahrzeugdetailseite f\xfcllt auf Elementor-Seiten seinen Rahmen aus, statt nur seinen oberen Teil zu zeigen, und die Karten im Slider f\xfcr hervorgehobene Fahrzeuge sind alle so hoch wie die h\xf6chste.\\n\\n## Buchungsformular und Preis\\n\\n- **Das Buchungsformular nennt genau den berechneten Betrag.** Saisonpreise gelten, wenn aktiviert, f\xfcr die Zahlung und den gespeicherten Buchungsgesamtbetrag, nicht nur f\xfcr den Preis auf dem Bildschirm. Anzahlung und Restbetrag werden aus demselben Gesamtbetrag berechnet.\\n- **Steuern kommen nur noch von WooCommerce.** Preise im Buchungsformular werden \xfcber die Steueranzeige von WooCommerce dargestellt (die Einstellung \u201ePreise im Warenkorb und an der Kasse anzeigen\u201c und das Suffix f\xfcr die Preisanzeige). Rentiva zeigt keine eigene Steuerzeile mehr an, und die eigenen Steuereinstellungen (Fahrzeugeinstellungen > Preise inkl. Steuern und Steuersatz (%)) wurden entfernt. Steuern werden unter WooCommerce > Einstellungen > Steuer konfiguriert. Die berechnete Steuer \xe4ndert sich nicht: WooCommerce hat sie schon immer berechnet. Bestehende Buchungen behalten ihre gespeicherten Gesamtbetr\xe4ge.\\n- **Abhol- und R\xfcckgabezeiten werden korrekt gespeichert.** Eine \xfcber die WooCommerce-Kasse erstellte Buchung speicherte Abholung und R\xfcckgabe als Ortszeit, die als UTC gelesen wurde. Auf einer Website au\xdferhalb von UTC blockierte sie das Fahrzeug daher f\xfcr die falschen Stunden (in Istanbul um drei Stunden versetzt), und eine Buchung am sp\xe4ten Abend konnte sich mit einer anderen \xfcberschneiden. Neue Buchungen speichern die tats\xe4chliche Zeit, und ein einmaliger Schritt beim Update korrigiert bestehende Buchungen, auch die im Papierkorb.\\n- **Datumsfehler sagen, was falsch ist.** Ein R\xfcckgabedatum vor (oder am) Abholdatum wird mit \u201eDas R\xfcckgabedatum muss nach dem Abholdatum liegen.\u201c statt mit \u201eUng\xfcltiges Datums-/Uhrzeitformat.\u201c beantwortet \u2013 im Buchungsformular, beim Preis, bei der Verf\xfcgbarkeitspr\xfcfung, im Bildschirm f\xfcr manuelle Buchungen und in der Suche; das Formular h\xe4lt \u201eBuchen\u201c gesperrt, bis die Daten korrigiert sind.\\n- **Optionaler Mietvertrag.** Unter Einstellungen > Buchung > Mietvertrag (standardm\xe4\xdfig deaktiviert). Ist er erforderlich, setzt der Kunde vor der Buchung ein H\xe4kchen bei der Einwilligung unter dem Vertrag, und der Server lehnt eine Buchung ohne Einwilligung ab. Der Zeitpunkt und die Version des akzeptierten Textes werden mit der Buchung gespeichert und in deren Box \u201eKundenkonto\u201c angezeigt. Ein leerer Text verwendet eine integrierte, \xfcbersetzbare Vorlage: ein Ausgangspunkt, keine Rechtsberatung.\\n- **Kontakt-Shortcode:** Ein `[rentiva_contact type=\\"booking\\"]`- oder `type=\\"feedback\\"`-Shortcode, der `show_topic_selector` nicht setzt, beh\xe4lt wie in 6.3.1 sein festes Formular mit dem Feld f\xfcr das Wunschdatum oder die Bewertung. Bl\xf6cke und Elementor-Widgets folgen ihrem Schalter \u201eThemenauswahl anzeigen\u201c, der standardm\xe4\xdfig aktiviert ist: Deaktiviere ihn, um ein festes Buchungs- oder Feedbackformular zu behalten.\\n- **Kleineres:** Auf einer Seite mit Buchungsformular und Verf\xfcgbarkeitskalender wird die Verf\xfcgbarkeitszeile des Formulars nicht mehr als zweiter Kalender gestartet. Die Einstellung \u201eKlassische Warenkorb-Seite\u201c (Einstellungen > Zahlung) ersetzt den Warenkorb-Block nur, wenn der Warenkorb eine Miete enth\xe4lt, und beh\xe4lt diesen Warenkorb klassisch, bis er geleert wird; ein Warenkorb nur mit Shop-Produkten beh\xe4lt den Warenkorb-Block und seine Express-Zahlungsschaltfl\xe4chen.\\n\\n## Verf\xfcgbarkeitskalender\\n\\n- **Ein teilweise freier Tag wird angezeigt.** Der R\xfcckgabetag einer Buchung ist ab der R\xfcckgabezeit plus Puffer frei, der Abholtag der n\xe4chsten bis zu deren Abholzeit minus Puffer (halb schattiert, mit der Uhrzeit). Ein vom Betreiber manuell gesperrter Tag zeigt \u201eGeschlossen\u201c statt \u201eGebucht\u201c. Wird ein R\xfcckgabetag als Beginn gew\xe4hlt, wird die Abholzeit dorthin verschoben und darauf hingewiesen.\\n- **Der Kalender zeigt standardm\xe4\xdfig 2 Monate** (bisher 1); ein explizites `months_to_show` gilt weiterhin.\\n- **Ein Kalender, dessen `vehicle_id` ein Fahrzeug nennt, das nicht existiert oder nicht vermietet werden kann,** zeigt \u201eFahrzeug nicht gefunden.\u201c statt des Kalenders eines anderen Fahrzeugs.\\n- **Auf Smartphones** bricht die Verf\xfcgbarkeitslegende der Fahrzeugseite (Ausgew\xe4hlt, Teilweise verf\xfcgbar, Gebucht, Geschlossen) in eine zweite Zeile um, statt \xfcber den Seitenrand hinauszulaufen.\\n\\n## Mein Konto\\n\\n- **Mein Konto folgt dem neuen Design.** Das Dashboard begr\xfc\xdft den Kunden und zeigt die n\xe4chste Miete; die Buchungsseite zeigt den Fortschritt, die Zahlung, wann die kostenlose Stornierung endet und wie viel erstattet wird. Das Dashboard zeigt eine heute fr\xfcher abgeholte Miete weiterhin als n\xe4chste Miete an statt \u201eDu hast keine bevorstehenden Mieten.\u201c\\n- **Meine Buchungen ist aufgeteilt** in Bevorstehend, Vergangen und Storniert (jeweils mit Anzahl; der Abschnitt steht in der Adresse als `mhmrentiva_view`). Es zeigt zwei vollst\xe4ndige Daten und die Buchungsnummer, die Kunden in E-Mails sehen, und wird auf Smartphones zu einer Karte pro Buchung. Das Men\xfc zeigt die Anzahl der bevorstehenden Buchungen und der gespeicherten Fahrzeuge. Die alte Filterbox und das Suchfeld sind entfallen; Links, die deren Werte enthalten, schr\xe4nken die Liste weiterhin ein. Meine Favoriten verwendet dasselbe Layout.\\n- **Jeder Abschnitt hat seine eigene Reihenfolge:** Bevorstehend mit der fr\xfchesten Abholung zuerst, Vergangen und Storniert mit den neuesten zuerst. Gespeicherte Bl\xf6cke und Widgets, die die alte Standardreihenfolge verwendeten, folgen ihr ebenfalls. Die neue Reihenfolge-Option \u201eAutomatik\u201c ist der Standard; eine explizit gew\xe4hlte Reihenfolge gilt weiterhin.\\n- **Men\xfcnamen:** \u201eMeine Buchungen\u201c, \u201eMeine Favoriten\u201c und \u201eZahlungsverlauf\u201c. Die eigenen Eintr\xe4ge von WooCommerce bleiben unver\xe4ndert.\\n- **Eine druckbare Buchungs\xfcbersicht** \u2013 \xfcber das Dashboard, die Buchungsseite und die Danke-Seite. Sie ist keine Rechnung.\\n- **\u201eBankbeleg hochladen.\u201c** So hei\xdft der Datei-Upload des Kunden jetzt. Er erscheint, und der Server akzeptiert oder entfernt eine Datei, nur solange eine Buchung auf Zahlung oder Best\xe4tigung wartet und kein Geld eingegangen ist. Mitarbeiter k\xf6nnen eine Datei weiterhin entfernen. Im T\xfcrkischen hei\xdft der Beleg \xfcberall \u201edekont\u201c.\\n- **Zahlungsverlauf** zeigt den Fahrzeugnamen, den tats\xe4chlich gezahlten Betrag und den richtigen Status f\xfcr eine bezahlte Buchung.\\n- **Kleineres:** \u201eEinwilligung widerrufen\u201c in den Datenschutzeinstellungen erscheint erst, wenn der Kunde eingewilligt hat, und \u201eAlle Favoriten entfernen\u201c zeigt keine Fehlermeldung mehr, bevor es ausgef\xfchrt wird. Eine Seite mit dem eingestellten Kunden-Dashboard (Shortcode, Block oder Elementor-Widget) zeigte G\xe4sten \xfcberall au\xdfer auf der plugineigenen Seite /panel/ eine leere Seite; jetzt zeigt sie den Hinweis \u201eDein Konto ist umgezogen\u201c mit einem Link zu Mein Konto, wo sich das Anmeldeformular befindet.\\n- **Mit Rentiva Pro 6.4.x** zeigt das Fenster f\xfcr Transfer-Zusatzleistungen die W\xe4hrung wieder neben den Betr\xe4gen an.\\n- **Schriftart:** Die neuen Frontend-Seiten verwenden Plus Jakarta Sans, ausgeliefert von deiner eigenen Website (dieselbe Schriftdatei, die die Admin-Bildschirme bereits verwendet haben). Die ungenutzten Schriftdateien von Source Serif 4 werden nicht mehr mitgeliefert.\\n\\n## Stornierungen, Erstattungen und Zahlungen\\n\\n- **Die Frist f\xfcr kostenlose Stornierung** verwendete bei manuell erstellten Buchungen die falsche Abholzeit; behoben.\\n- **Erstattungen \xfcber die Box \u201eZahlungsverwaltung\u201c.** Eine Erstattung \xfcber die Box \u201eZahlungsverwaltung\u201c der Buchung wurde ab einem Tag nach der Buchung \u201eaufgrund der Stornierungsbedingungen\u201c abgelehnt, egal wie weit die Abholung entfernt war. Die Stornierungsfrist z\xe4hlt jetzt \xfcberall ab der Abholung: Die Box zeigt diese Frist, und die Erstattung einer stornierten Buchung zahlt deren erstattungsf\xe4higes Guthaben aus. Die Box bietet nicht mehr an, eine bereits stornierte, abgeschlossene oder erstattete Buchung zu stornieren. Der Filter `mhmrentiva_cancellation_deadline_hours`, der nur diesen falschen Ein-Tages-Wert bei manuell erstellten Buchungen setzte, wurde entfernt; die Frist wird unter Einstellungen > Buchung > Stornierungsfrist (Stunden) festgelegt.\\n- **Zahlungen des Restbetrags.** Eine fehlgeschlagene oder abgebrochene Zahlung des Restbetrags storniert die Buchung nicht mehr. Eine Restzahlung, die nicht mehr zum offenen Betrag der Buchung passt, gleicht ihn nicht stillschweigend aus: Der offene Betrag bleibt bestehen, und die Buchung wird mit einer Bestellnotiz f\xfcr die Mitarbeiter markiert. Nur der aktuelle Zahlungslink der Buchung kann die Restzahlung entgegennehmen.\\n- **Au\xdferhalb der Website bezahlte Buchungen.** Eine manuell eingetragene und au\xdferhalb der Website bezahlte Buchung (bar oder per Karte bei der Abholung) wird nach Ablauf der Zahlungsfrist oder nach dem Abholtag nicht mehr automatisch storniert, und der Kunde erh\xe4lt keine Mitteilung mehr, dass das Zahlungsfenster abgelaufen ist. Eine manuell eingetragene, online bezahlte Buchung beh\xe4lt ihre Frist.\\n- **Eine vollst\xe4ndige Erstattung \xfcber den WooCommerce-Bestellbildschirm** vor Beginn der Miete (best\xe4tigt, ausstehend oder auf Zahlung wartend) blockierte das Fahrzeug weiterhin: Die Zahlung wurde als erstattet angezeigt, w\xe4hrend die Buchung aktiv blieb. Jetzt wird sie storniert, wodurch ihre Daten frei werden. Eine vollst\xe4ndig erstattete abgeschlossene Miete wird weiterhin als erstattet markiert, und eine laufende Miete beh\xe4lt ihre Daten, da das Fahrzeug unterwegs ist. Der Kunde erh\xe4lt daf\xfcr eine E-Mail, die Erstattungsmitteilung, und keine zweite Stornierungsmitteilung.\\n- **Eine Aktualisierung, die nur die Notiz, den Status oder ein anderes Feld \xe4ndert, das den Preis nicht beeinflusst,** zeigt bei einer Buchung, deren gespeicherter Gesamtbetrag von den heutigen Tarifen abweicht, nicht mehr die Warnung \u201eFahrzeug, Daten und Zusatzleistungen wurden nicht ge\xe4ndert\u201c.\\n\\n## Verwaltung, Sprachen und Barrierefreiheit\\n\\n- **Die Tabellen \u201eKunden\u201c und \u201eKontaktnachrichten\u201c** sind f\xfcr Screenreader benannt und zeigen im K\xe4stchen \u201eAlle ausw\xe4hlen\u201c eine teilweise ausgew\xe4hlte Seite an. Die Kundentabelle sortiert \xfcber eine echte Schaltfl\xe4che, die die sortierte Spalte ansagt. mhm/ui-core ist 0.20.1.\\n- **Der Admin-Hinweis zu einem WooCommerce-Warenkorb- oder Kasse-Block l\xe4sst sich ausblenden:** \u201eVerstanden, nicht mehr anzeigen\u201c blendet ihn f\xfcr diesen Administrator auf allen Bildschirmen aus.\\n- **Export und L\xf6schung personenbezogener Daten umfassen Buchungen im Papierkorb.** Eine Buchung im Papierkorb enth\xe4lt die Daten des Kunden, bis der Papierkorb geleert wird; sie wird an Ort und Stelle anonymisiert und bleibt im Papierkorb.\\n- **Zahlen folgen der Sprache der Seite.** Kilometerstand und Hubraum von Fahrzeugen werden so geschrieben, wie die Sprache der Seite Zahlen schreibt: Eine englische Seite zeigt \u201e18,500 km\u201c und \u201e1.6 L\u201c, eine t\xfcrkische Seite \u201e18.500 km\u201c und \u201e1,6 L\u201c. Bisher wurde der Kilometerstand immer mit t\xfcrkischen Trennzeichen und der Hubraum immer mit englischen geschrieben.\\n- **Mehrsprachige Websites (Polylang, WPML)** zeigen die Verf\xfcgbarkeitsmeldung der Fahrzeugseite und die Beschriftungen f\xfcr Kraftstoff, Getriebe und Kategorie in der Suchseitenleiste in der Sprache des Besuchers. Beide Antworten wurden f\xfcr alle Besucher in der Sprache des ersten Besuchers zwischengespeichert, sodass ein t\xfcrkisches \u201ebereits gebucht\u201c auf die englische Seite gelangen konnte. Die Caches enthalten jetzt keinen Text mehr, und vor diesem Release zwischengespeicherte Eintr\xe4ge werden ebenfalls neu formuliert.\\n- **Drei t\xfcrkische \xdcbersetzungen** beginnen wie ihre Originale mit Kleinbuchstaben.\\n- **Sicherheit:** Die REST-Nonce wird nicht mehr auf jeder Seite ausgegeben. Sie wird auf Mein-Konto-Seiten, auf Seiten mit dem Shortcode \u201eMeine Buchungen\u201c oder \u201eZahlungsverlauf\u201c und auf Seiten mit dem Suchformular ausgegeben.\\n- **Entfernt:** Das Dashboard liest die nicht registrierten Optionen `mhmrentiva_customer_dashboard_welcome`, `mhmrentiva_customer_favorites` und `mhmrentiva_customer_booking_history` nicht mehr. Kein Einstellungsbildschirm hat sie geschrieben; ein manuell gesetzter Wert hat keine Wirkung mehr.\\n\\n## Was du nach dem Update pr\xfcfen solltest\\n\\n- **WordPress-Version:** Sie muss 7.0 oder neuer sein.\\n- **Seiten-Cache:** Leere ihn.\\n- **Theme-\xdcberschreibungen:** Entferne oder aktualisiere \xdcberschreibungen der Templates f\xfcr Buchungsformular, Kalender, Kontaktformular, Fahrzeugdetails, Bewertungsformular, Suche und Konto.\\n- **Steuern:** Die eigenen Steuereinstellungen von Rentiva sind entfallen; pr\xfcfe WooCommerce > Einstellungen > Steuer und die Einstellung zur Preisanzeige.\\n- **Kontaktformulare:** Shortcodes, Bl\xf6cke und Widgets, die `type=\\"booking\\"` oder `type=\\"feedback\\"` verwenden, verhalten sich wie oben beschrieben.\\n- **Rentiva Pro:** Aktualisiere Pro auf 6.5.0.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Bezugsquellen.** Rentiva gibt es auf [WordPress.org](https://wordpress.org/plugins/mhm-rentiva/) und auf GitHub als [`v6.4.0`](https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva/releases/tag/v6.4.0); beide enthalten dieselben Dateien. WordPress.org h\xe4lt neue Versionen einige Stunden zur\xfcck, bevor Websites das Update angeboten wird. **Du verwendest Rentiva Pro?** Aktualisiere zuerst Rentiva, dann [Pro auf 6.5.0](/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.5.0-release). Das vollst\xe4ndige \xc4nderungsprotokoll in beiden Sprachen wird mit dem Plugin ausgeliefert."},{"id":"rentiva-pro-v6.4.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.4.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-10-24-rentiva-pro-v6.4.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-10-24-rentiva-pro-v6.4.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva Pro 6.4.0 \u2014 Transfers nutzen deine eingestellte Anzahlung, der Transfer-Warenkorb wird auf dem Server berechnet, sichere Editor-Vorschauen","description":"Mit 6.4.0 berechnen Transfers das, was in deinen Einstellungen steht. Der Transfer-Warenkorb ermittelt jetzt den Preis jedes Transfers auf dem Server und berechnet die unter Einstellungen > Transfer festgelegte Anzahlung; bisher \xfcbernahm er den Preis aus dem Browser und berechnete immer den vollen Betrag. Pro-Widgets zeigen in den Editoren sichere Vorschauen, und Pro-E-Mails erhalten \xfcbersetzte Namen und die Website-Sprache. Beim Update l\xe4uft kein Datenbankschritt. Aktualisiere zuerst MHM Rentiva (Lite) auf 6.3.0, dann Pro. Neben Rentiva 6.2.1 oder \xe4lter schaltet Pro 6.4.0 seine Funktionen ab, bis Rentiva aktualisiert ist \u2013 f\xfchre die beiden Updates also direkt nacheinander durch.","date":"2026-10-24T06:30:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"pro","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/pro"},{"inline":true,"label":"transfer","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/transfer"},{"inline":true,"label":"payments","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/payments"},{"inline":true,"label":"elementor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/elementor"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"}],"readingTime":4.7,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-pro-v6.4.0-release","title":"Rentiva Pro 6.4.0 \u2014 Transfers nutzen deine eingestellte Anzahlung, der Transfer-Warenkorb wird auf dem Server berechnet, sichere Editor-Vorschauen","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","pro","transfer","payments","elementor","security"],"date":"2026-10-24T06:30"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.4.0 \u2014 Neue Suche, Ergebnisseite und Fahrzeugkarte, ein Buchungspreis, der dem berechneten Betrag entspricht, und WordPress 7.0","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.4.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.3.0 \u2014 Eine websiteweite Anzahlung f\xfcr Mieten, sichere Editor-Vorschauen, wirksame E-Mail-Einstellungen und ein serverseitig gepr\xfcftes Buchungsformular","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.3.0-release"}},"content":"Mit 6.4.0 berechnen Transfers das, was in deinen Einstellungen steht. Der Transfer-Warenkorb ermittelt jetzt den Preis jedes Transfers auf dem Server und berechnet die unter Einstellungen > Transfer festgelegte Anzahlung; bisher \xfcbernahm er den Preis aus dem Browser und berechnete immer den vollen Betrag. Pro-Widgets zeigen in den Editoren sichere Vorschauen, und Pro-E-Mails erhalten \xfcbersetzte Namen und die Website-Sprache. Beim Update l\xe4uft kein Datenbankschritt. **Aktualisiere zuerst MHM Rentiva (Lite) auf 6.3.0, dann Pro.** Neben Rentiva 6.2.1 oder \xe4lter schaltet Pro 6.4.0 seine Funktionen ab, bis Rentiva aktualisiert ist \u2013 f\xfchre die beiden Updates also direkt nacheinander durch.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::caution Pr\xfcfe deine Transfer-Anzahlungen\\nTransfers berechnen jetzt die unter **Einstellungen > Transfer** festgelegte Anzahlung statt des vollen Betrags. **Der eigene Anzahlungssatz eines Fahrzeugs hat Vorrang:** Ein Fahrzeug, das einen eigenen Satz gespeichert hat (der alte Standard hat 10 eingetragen), berechnet diese Anzahlung auch bei Transfers, selbst wenn die Transfer-Einstellung \u201eVollst\xe4ndige Zahlung erforderlich\u201c lautet. Leere das Anzahlungsfeld des Fahrzeugs, damit es der Transfer-Einstellung folgt. **Die Anbieter-Provision wird auf den online berechneten Betrag ermittelt**, bei einem solchen Transfer also auf die Anzahlung; ein offline kassierter Restbetrag erzeugt keinen Provisionseintrag.\\n:::\\n\\n## Transfers berechnen, was in deinen Einstellungen steht\\n\\n- **Die Transfer-Anzahlungseinstellung wird angewendet.** Egal, was unter Einstellungen > Transfer (\u201eZahlungsart\u201c / \u201eAnzahlungssatz (%)\u201c) gew\xe4hlt war, Transfers wurden bisher vollst\xe4ndig berechnet. Der Warenkorb berechnet jetzt die von dir festgelegte Anzahlung.\\n- **Der eigene Anzahlungssatz eines Fahrzeugs \xfcberschreibt die Transfer-Einstellung**, wie bei Vermietungen \u2013 siehe den Kasten oben.\\n- **Anbieter-Fahrzeuge** erhalten keine feste Anzahlung von 20 % mehr; sie folgen der websiteweiten Einstellung.\\n- Unter Einstellungen > Transfer beginnt das Feld f\xfcr den Anzahlungssatz bei 1 (w\xe4hle \u201eVollst\xe4ndige Zahlung erforderlich\u201c f\xfcr keine Anzahlung), und die Seite erkl\xe4rt, dass der eigene Satz eines Fahrzeugs Vorrang hat.\\n- Benutzerdefinierte Standorttypen, die im Tab \u201eTransfer\u201c gespeichert wurden, werden jetzt wirksam; ein \xe4lterer gespeicherter Wert blendet sie nicht mehr aus.\\n\\n## Ein auf dem Server berechneter Transfer-Warenkorb\\n\\n- **Jeder Transfer wird auf dem Server berechnet.** Ein vom Browser gesendeter Preis wird ignoriert.\\n- **Ein Fahrzeug, das die Transfersuche f\xfcr diese Route nicht anbietet, kann nicht hinzugef\xfcgt werden** \u2013 nicht f\xfcr Transfers angeboten, belegt, Route nicht zugewiesen oder zu klein.\\n- **Das Anbieter-Fahrzeugformular akzeptiert keinen Anzahlungswert mehr, den es nicht anzeigt.** Ein Anbieter konnte einen solchen Wert manuell senden und so sowohl die Anzahlung als auch die Provisionsbasis senken.\\n- **Warenkorb- und Bestellpositionen lauten \u201eVIP Transfer: A \u279d B\u201c** im Block-Warenkorb, im Mini-Warenkorb und in der gespeicherten Bestellung statt des allgemeinen Buchungsnamens. Jede Zusatzleistung wird einmal mit ihrem Preis aufgef\xfchrt, die zus\xe4tzliche Zeile \u201eZusatzleistungen gesamt\u201c entf\xe4llt, die Zeile mit dem R\xfcckgabedatum ist in jeder Website-Sprache ausgeblendet, und die Zeile \u201eDauer\u201c in Bestellungen hei\xdft jetzt \u201eGesch\xe4tzte Dauer\u201c, wie im Warenkorb.\\n\\n## Elementor und die Editoren\\n\\n- **Die Elementor-Widgets \u201eTransfer Results\u201c (11 Einstellungen) und \u201eMeine Nachrichten\u201c (1 Einstellung)** haben einen Abschnitt \u201eZus\xe4tzliche Einstellungen\u201c mit denselben Einstellungen wie ihre Bl\xf6cke. Die Standardwerte entsprechen der heutigen Ausgabe, gespeicherte Seiten sehen also gleich aus.\\n- **Sichere Vorschauen.** Im Elementor- und im Block-Editor werden Transfer Results, Vendor Profile, Meine Nachrichten, Transfer Search, Beliebte Routen und Vendor Directory im selben Vorschaurahmen dargestellt wie die Widgets von Rentiva. Solange du keine Suchstandorte oder keinen Anbieter ausw\xe4hlst, zeigen sie Beispiel-Transfers, einen Beispiel-Anbieter und Beispiel-Nachrichtenverl\xe4ufe mit einem Hinweis; ausgew\xe4hlte Standorte f\xfchren eine echte Suche aus, und ein ausgew\xe4hlter Anbieter zeigt dessen Profil. Deine eigenen Nachrichten erscheinen nie, und die Formulare sind inaktiv. Vendor Profile erkl\xe4rt, wenn kein Anbieter gefunden wird, statt einen leeren Kasten anzuzeigen.\\n- **Pro-Bl\xf6cke sind \xfcbersetzt** und befinden sich zusammen mit den Rentiva-Bl\xf6cken in der Kategorie \u201eRentiva\u201c. Das Pr\xe4fix \u201eMHM \u201c wurde aus den Namen der Pro-Widgets und -Bl\xf6cke entfernt, und zwei Blocktitel haben sich ge\xe4ndert: \u201eNachrichten\u201c hei\xdft jetzt \u201eMeine Nachrichten\u201c und \u201eBeliebte Transferrouten\u201c hei\xdft jetzt \u201eBeliebte Routen\u201c.\\n\\n## E-Mails\\n\\n- **Die E-Mail-Vorschau listet alle 31 Pro-Vorlagen mit \xfcbersetztem Namen auf** (sie zeigten \u201eVendor approved\u201c, \u201ePayout approved\u201c usw. auf Englisch), jeweils gef\xfcllt mit Beispieldaten zu Anbieter, Auszahlung, Provision, Bericht und Nachricht statt leerer L\xfccken.\\n- **Pro-E-Mails verwenden die Website-Sprache**, zusammen mit denen von Rentiva, auch w\xe4hrend ein Admin mit einer anderen Profilsprache arbeitet.\\n\\n## Fehlerbehebungen\\n\\n- Der Export personenbezogener Daten enth\xe4lt wieder die Lieblingsfahrzeuge des Kunden.\\n- Fehlermeldungen auf der Seite \u201eMeine Nachrichten\u201c zeigen ihren Text an; vier davon waren leer.\\n- Transfer Results liefert kein veraltetes zwischengespeichertes Ergebnis mehr, wenn sich Einstellungen zweimal innerhalb derselben Sekunde \xe4ndern, und seine Einstellung `columns` hat ein Minimum von 1, sodass 0 oder ein nicht numerischer Wert kein leeres Raster mehr erzeugt.\\n- Die Einheit der Transferdauer (\u201eMin.\u201c) ist \xfcbersetzt.\\n- **T\xfcrkisch:** \u201eDeposit Rate (%)\u201c lautet jetzt \u201eKapora oran\u0131\u201c, \u201eFull Payment Required\u201c lautet \u201eTam \xf6deme gerekli\u201c, E-Mail-Texte sagen \u201eetkin\u201c, und die Formulierungen f\xfcr Abholung / R\xfcckgabe wurden zu \u201eTeslim alma / D\xf6n\xfc\u015f\u201c hin angepasst.\\n\\n:::caution Bekannte Einschr\xe4nkung (unver\xe4ndert seit 6.3.0)\\nEin Anbieter, dessen IBAN nach dem Update auf 6.3.0 nicht gelesen werden konnte, kann keine Auszahlung anfordern, bis die IBAN erneut eingegeben wird, und 6.4.0 hat noch immer kein Formular zur Eingabe. Der Admin-Hinweis listet jeden betroffenen Anbieter auf.\\n:::\\n\\n## F\xfcr Entwickler\\n\\nErfordert MHM Rentiva 6.3.0 (angehoben von 6.2.0). Entfernt: eine alte Transfer-Einstellungsseite, die \xfcber kein Men\xfc und keinen Link erreichbar war, ihr Speicher-Handler und die Action `admin_post_mhmrentiva_save_transfer_settings`. Der Transfer-Warenkorb liest nur noch die `mhmrentiva_transfer_deposit_*`-Schl\xfcssel des Tabs \u201eTransfer\u201c, nicht mehr `rentiva_transfer_deposit_*`. Pro h\xe4ngt sich in Rentivas `mhmrentiva_cart_item_name`, `mhmrentiva_email_template_labels`, `mhmrentiva_email_preview_context` und `mhmrentiva_parity_labels` ein. Die `_html`-Filter von Vendor Directory, Vendor Profile und Beliebte Routen erhalten jetzt auch die fr\xfchen leeren Ausgaben, mit normalisierten Attributen.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Bezugsquelle.** Pro 6.4.0 ist auf GitHub als `v6.4.0` ver\xf6ffentlicht und wird \xfcber den Rentiva-Pro-Download auf wpalemi.com bereitgestellt. Aktualisiere zuerst [Rentiva auf 6.3.0](/blog/rentiva-v6.3.0-release). Das vollst\xe4ndige \xc4nderungsprotokoll wird in beiden Sprachen mit dem Plugin ausgeliefert."},{"id":"rentiva-v6.3.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.3.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-10-24-rentiva-v6.3.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-10-24-rentiva-v6.3.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva 6.3.0 \u2014 Eine websiteweite Anzahlung f\xfcr Mieten, sichere Editor-Vorschauen, wirksame E-Mail-Einstellungen und ein serverseitig gepr\xfcftes Buchungsformular","description":"6.3.0 fasst die Arbeit seit 6.2.1 zusammen. F\xfcr Mieten gibt es eine websiteweite Anzahlungseinstellung, ein Fahrzeug, das nur f\xfcr Transfers eingestellt ist, kann nicht mehr gemietet werden, und Rentiva-Widgets zeigen sichere Vorschauen im Elementor- und im Block-Editor. E-Mail-Einstellungen, die gespeichert, aber ignoriert wurden, greifen jetzt, und das Buchungsformular pr\xfcft auf dem Server, was es bisher vom Browser \xfcbernommen hat. Beim Update l\xe4uft kein Datenbankschritt. 6.3.1 folgte noch am selben Tag mit einer Korrektur f\xfcr Elementor-Websites \u2013 siehe Ende dieses Beitrags. Die Version ist auf WordPress.org ver\xf6ffentlicht, daher bietet WordPress sie dir als ganz normales Update an. Du verwendest Rentiva Pro? Aktualisiere Pro direkt danach auf 6.4.0.","date":"2026-10-24T06:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"payments","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/payments"},{"inline":true,"label":"elementor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/elementor"},{"inline":true,"label":"blocks","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/blocks"},{"inline":true,"label":"email","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/email"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"}],"readingTime":8.1,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v6.3.0-release","title":"Rentiva 6.3.0 \u2014 Eine websiteweite Anzahlung f\xfcr Mieten, sichere Editor-Vorschauen, wirksame E-Mail-Einstellungen und ein serverseitig gepr\xfcftes Buchungsformular","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","payments","elementor","blocks","email","security"],"date":"2026-10-24T06:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva Pro 6.4.0 \u2014 Transfers nutzen deine eingestellte Anzahlung, der Transfer-Warenkorb wird auf dem Server berechnet, sichere Editor-Vorschauen","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.4.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.2.1 \u2014 Elementor-Widgets schreiben die Kontodaten der speichernden Person nicht mehr in den gespeicherten Text einer Seite","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.2.1-release"}},"content":"6.3.0 fasst die Arbeit seit 6.2.1 zusammen. F\xfcr Mieten gibt es eine websiteweite Anzahlungseinstellung, ein Fahrzeug, das nur f\xfcr Transfers eingestellt ist, kann nicht mehr gemietet werden, und Rentiva-Widgets zeigen sichere Vorschauen im Elementor- und im Block-Editor. E-Mail-Einstellungen, die gespeichert, aber ignoriert wurden, greifen jetzt, und das Buchungsformular pr\xfcft auf dem Server, was es bisher vom Browser \xfcbernommen hat. Beim Update l\xe4uft kein Datenbankschritt. 6.3.1 folgte noch am selben Tag mit einer Korrektur f\xfcr Elementor-Websites \u2013 siehe Ende dieses Beitrags. Die Version ist auf WordPress.org ver\xf6ffentlicht, daher bietet WordPress sie dir als ganz normales Update an. **Du verwendest Rentiva Pro?** Aktualisiere Pro direkt danach auf 6.4.0.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Eine websiteweite Anzahlung f\xfcr Mieten\\n\\n**Einstellungen > Zahlung** hat zwei neue Felder: **Zahlungsart f\xfcr Mieten** (vollst\xe4ndige Zahlung oder prozentuale Anzahlung, Standard: prozentual) und **Anzahlungssatz (%)** (1\u2013100, Standard: 10). Die Standardwerte behalten das bisherige Verhalten bei. Der Tab \u201eZahlung\u201c wird jetzt immer angezeigt; bisher erschien er nur ohne WooCommerce. Jede Preisansicht liest denselben Satz.\\n\\n- **Der eigene Anzahlungssatz eines Fahrzeugs hat weiterhin Vorrang** vor der websiteweiten Einstellung.\\n- **Ein leeres Anzahlungsfeld folgt jetzt der websiteweiten Einstellung.** Es bedeutet nicht mehr fest 10 %, und das Buchungsformular berechnet deshalb nicht mehr den vollen Betrag.\\n- Das Fahrzeugfeld akzeptiert 1\u2013100 (bisher war es auf 50 begrenzt), und die Bearbeitungsansicht nennt den websiteweiten Wert, auf den es zur\xfcckf\xe4llt.\\n\\n## Fahrzeuge nur f\xfcr Transfers k\xf6nnen nicht mehr gemietet werden\\n\\nEin Fahrzeug, dessen Serviceart \u201enur Transfer\u201c ist, erscheint nicht mehr im Fahrzeugraster und in der Fahrzeugliste, in Suchergebnissen, bei hervorgehobenen Fahrzeugen, im Buchungsformular, bei Alternativen, im Fahrzeugwechsler des Kalenders oder in der Liste f\xfcr manuelle Buchungen, und seine Seite hat keinen Buchungsbutton. Der Server lehnt eine Mietbuchung, ein Angebot oder eine Zahlung daf\xfcr ab. Transferbuchungen f\xfcr dieses Fahrzeug sind nicht betroffen, und ein Fahrzeug ohne Serviceart bleibt mietbar.\\n\\n## Sichere Vorschauen in Elementor und im Block-Editor\\n\\n- **Rentiva-Widgets werden in einem Vorschau-Frame gerendert.** Konto-Widgets (Meine Buchungen, Favoriten, Zahlungsverlauf, Fahrzeugvergleich, Benutzer-Dashboard) zeigen immer Beispielzeilen mit dem Hinweis \u201eVorschau: Beispieldaten\u201c \u2013 niemals deine eigenen Kontodaten. Fahrzeugdetails und das Bewertungsformular zeigen ein Beispielfahrzeug, wenn die Seite keines hat, und einen deutlichen Hinweis, wenn die Fahrzeug-ID falsch ist. Katalog-Widgets zeigen deine echten \xf6ffentlichen Daten. Formulare im Editor sind funktionslos.\\n- **Eine Kategorie \u201eRentiva\u201c.** Alle Rentiva-Bl\xf6cke befinden sich im Block-Inserter in einer Kategorie \u201eRentiva\u201c, und die Elementor-Widget-Kategorie hei\xdft jetzt \u201eRentiva\u201c; gespeicherte Seiten sind nicht betroffen. Das Pr\xe4fix \u201eMHM \u201c wurde aus den Widget- und Blocknamen entfernt.\\n- **Elementors Abschnitt \u201eParity Controls\u201c hei\xdft jetzt \u201eZus\xe4tzliche Einstellungen\u201c**, mit \xfcbersetzbaren Beschriftungen und Optionen. Gespeicherte Widget-Einstellungen bleiben unver\xe4ndert.\\n- **Die Einstellungsbereiche der Bl\xf6cke sind \xfcbersetzt.** Wenn ein Sprachpaket von WordPress.org installiert ist, haben dessen neuere \xdcbersetzungen Vorrang, und Texte, die das Paket noch nicht enth\xe4lt, kommen aus den plugineigenen \xdcbersetzungen, statt auf Englisch angezeigt zu werden.\\n\\n## Ignorierte E-Mail-Einstellungen greifen jetzt\\n\\n- **Eine Vorlage wird nur gesendet, solange ihr K\xe4stchen \u201eAktiviert\u201c angehakt ist.** Eine nie gespeicherte Vorlage gilt als aktiviert, so wie die Ansicht es anzeigt. Vorschauen und Testversand ignorieren das K\xe4stchen. Die globalen Schalter f\xfcr Buchungs- und Willkommens-E-Mails passen jetzt zu den Vorlagen, die sie benennen; vorher passten sie zu keiner.\\n- **Eine einzige Stornierungs-E-Mail.** Wenn eine Buchung storniert wird, erh\xe4lt der Kunde die Vorlage \u201eBuchung storniert\u201c (oder die Vorlage f\xfcr automatische Stornierung, wenn diese zutrifft) statt der allgemeinen Status-E-Mail plus einer zweiten Stornierungs-E-Mail. Ist diese Vorlage deaktiviert, wird nichts gesendet. Sie folgt jetzt wie jede andere E-Mail \u201eAusgehende E-Mails aktivieren\u201c und dem Testmodus. Die Admin-Kopie und Admin-Benachrichtigungen werden weiterhin versendet, im Testmodus an die Testadresse.\\n- **Die Felder \u201eAdmin-E-Mail\u201c werden verwendet.** Buchungsbenachrichtigungen gehen an die Adresse unter \u201eBuchungsbenachrichtigungen\u201c, Erstattungsbenachrichtigungen an die unter \u201eErstattungs-E-Mails\u201c. Ein leeres oder ung\xfcltiges Feld f\xe4llt weiterhin auf die E-Mail-Adresse des Website-Admins zur\xfcck. Admin-Benachrichtigungen, die direkt gesendet wurden, beachten jetzt ebenfalls den Testmodus.\\n- **Kunden-E-Mails verwenden die Sprache der Website**, auch wenn der ausl\xf6sende Admin in seinem Profil eine andere Sprache verwendet.\\n- Das K\xe4stchen \u201eAktiviert\u201c, der Betreff und der Inhalt der E-Mail \u201eBuchung storniert\u201c werden jetzt gespeichert, und die E-Mail-Vorschau listet jede Vorlage unter ihrem \xfcbersetzten Namen auf und f\xfcllt sie mit Beispieldaten.\\n- Buchungs-E-Mails zeigen in Betreff und Inhalt eine einzige Buchungsnummer (die Bestellnummer, sofern vorhanden), und der Konto-Button der Stornierungs-E-Mail \xf6ffnet die Buchung.\\n\\n## Vom Server gepr\xfcfte Buchungen\\n\\n- **Das Buchungsformular pr\xfcft auf dem Server**, was der Browser f\xfcr die R\xfcckgabezeit, erforderliche Zusatzleistungen und die Zahlungsart sendet. Die R\xfcckgabezeit wird auf dem Server auf die Abholzeit gesetzt, sodass der berechnete Zeitraum auch der blockierte ist. Erforderliche Zusatzleistungen werden erzwungen und als angehakt und gesperrt angezeigt. Als Zahlungsart wird nur \u201edeposit\u201c oder \u201efull\u201c akzeptiert.\\n- **Beim Speichern einer Buchung im Adminbereich wird die Berechnung des Buchungsformulars verwendet.** Zusatzleistungen fallen nicht mehr aus der Gesamtsumme heraus, es wird keine feste Anzahlung von 20 % mehr berechnet, der Wochenendtarif wird nicht mehr ignoriert, und Transferbuchungen werden nicht mehr zum Tagespreis des Fahrzeugs neu berechnet.\\n- **Beim Bearbeiten einer Buchung im Adminbereich wird die Verf\xfcgbarkeit gepr\xfcft.** Das Verschieben einer Buchung auf belegte Termine oder die erneute Best\xe4tigung einer stornierten Buchung, deren Termine bereits vergeben wurden, wird mit einem Hinweis abgelehnt. Eine verschobene Buchung gibt ihre alten Termine frei und belegt die neuen.\\n- Wenn das gew\xe4hlte Fahrzeug nicht frei ist, zeigt das Buchungsformular den Hinweis und vorgeschlagene Alternativen an, und der Buchungsbutton bleibt deaktiviert, bis ein verf\xfcgbares Fahrzeug oder verf\xfcgbare Termine gew\xe4hlt sind.\\n\\n## Was du nach dem Update pr\xfcfen solltest\\n\\n- **Anzahlungsfelder der Fahrzeuge:** Ein Fahrzeug mit leerem Feld folgt jetzt dem websiteweiten Satz unter \u201eEinstellungen > Zahlung\u201c; eines mit eigenem Satz beh\xe4lt diesen.\\n- **E-Mail-Vorlagen:** Eine Vorlage, deren K\xe4stchen \u201eAktiviert\u201c nicht angehakt ist, wird nicht mehr gesendet. Sieh dir die K\xe4stchen in der Ansicht der E-Mail-Einstellungen an.\\n- **Felder \u201eAdmin-E-Mail\u201c** unter \u201eBuchungsbenachrichtigungen\u201c und \u201eErstattungs-E-Mails\u201c: Sie werden jetzt verwendet, also stelle sicher, dass sie die richtige Adresse enthalten.\\n- **R\xfcckgabeort im Suchformular:** Er ist jetzt standardm\xe4\xdfig ausgeblendet; er spiegelte nur den Abholort wider, und nichts hat ihn verwendet. F\xfcge `show_dropoff_location=\\"true\\"` zum Shortcode, Block oder Elementor-Widget hinzu, um ihn anzuzeigen.\\n- **Fahrzeuge nur f\xfcr Transfers** verschwinden aus den Mietlisten und dem Buchungsformular.\\n\\n## Kleinere \xc4nderungen, die dir auffallen werden\\n\\n- **Die Buchungsseite des Kunden entspricht der Buchung.** Ausstehende, stornierte und abgeschlossene Buchungen erhalten eine eigene \xdcberschrift; die Anzahlung wird erst als bezahlt angezeigt, wenn die Zahlung eingegangen ist; \u201eRestbetrag bezahlen\u201c wartet auf die Anzahlung; Hinweise zur Abholung erscheinen nur bei best\xe4tigten Buchungen. Die Buchungsnummer ist in der Liste, im Dashboard und in der Detailansicht gleich und kann gesucht werden.\\n- **Warenkorb und Bestellung:** Jede Buchung erscheint als Name des Fahrzeugs plus \u201eMiete\u201c mit dem Bild des Fahrzeugs, jede Zusatzleistung wird einmal mit ihrem Preis aufgef\xfchrt, Transfers haben keine Zeile f\xfcr das R\xfcckgabedatum, und Bestelldaten verwenden das Datumsformat der Website. Preise im Buchungsformular folgen der W\xe4hrungsposition und dem Tausendertrennzeichen des Shops.\\n- **Fahrzeugseiten:** Die Bewertungs\xfcbersicht zeigt f\xfcr jeden Sternwert einen Balken (1 und 2 Sterne fehlten); \u201e\xc4hnliche Fahrzeuge\u201c wird ausgeblendet, wenn leer, und listet das Fahrzeug selbst nicht mehr auf; Besucher sehen unter Bewertungen keinen rohen `[rentiva_login_form]`-Text mehr, und \u201eRegistrieren\u201c erscheint nur, wenn die Website Registrierungen erlaubt.\\n- **Der Fahrzeugvergleich** zeigt Standardzeilen, bis du eigene ausw\xe4hlst, und deine erste Auswahl wird gespeichert. \u201eAuf Standard zur\xfccksetzen\u201c im Tab \u201eAnzeige\u201c stellt die Standardfelder wieder her, statt sie auszublenden.\\n- **Verf\xfcgbarkeitskalender:** W\xe4hlst du denselben Tag f\xfcr Abholung und R\xfcckgabe, \xf6ffnet sich das Buchungsformular mit ausgef\xfclltem Abholdatum statt eines Fehlers. Zwei Kalender auf einer Seite steuern sich nicht mehr gegenseitig, und das Fahrzeug-Dropdown funktioniert wieder.\\n- **Einstellungen, die jetzt erhalten bleiben:** Der Standard-Mietstandort im Tab \u201eFahrzeug\u201c wird gespeichert, die Suche verwendet dessen Mindestmiettage, das Kontaktformular verwendet die Support-E-Mail aus dem Tab \u201eAllgemein\u201c, und das Feld f\xfcr das Headerbild der E-Mails ist sichtbar.\\n- **\xdcbersetzungen:** Die t\xfcrkische \xdcbersetzung wurde vollst\xe4ndig \xfcberpr\xfcft, t\xfcrkische Websites schreiben Prozentangaben als \u201e%20\u201c, und Admin-Ansichten zeigen k\xfcrzlich hinzugef\xfcgte Texte nicht mehr auf Englisch an, wenn ein Sprachpaket von WordPress.org installiert ist.\\n\\n## Sicherheit\\n\\nNeben den oben genannten Pr\xfcfungen im Buchungsformular: Ein Fahrzeugtitel mit Apostroph macht den Button \u201eAnderes Fahrzeug w\xe4hlen\u201c im Kalender nicht mehr funktionsunf\xe4hig, Fahrzeugdaten im Verf\xfcgbarkeitskalender und in der Ansicht zur Buchungsbearbeitung werden immer als Text behandelt, und der Lazy Loader l\xe4dt keine externen Inhalte oder Skripte mehr aus `data-lazy`-Attributen.\\n\\n## F\xfcr Entwickler\\n\\nNeue Filter: `mhmrentiva_cart_item_name`, `mhmrentiva_email_template_labels`, `mhmrentiva_email_preview_context`, `mhmrentiva_parity_labels`, `mhmrentiva_translation_dirs`, `mhmrentiva_render_context` und `mhmrentiva_settings_programmatic_keys`. Add-ons k\xf6nnen sich ab 6.3.0 auf `DepositCalculator::resolve_rate()`, `VehicleDataHelper::get_service_type()` / `allows_service()` / `service_meta_query()`, `RenderContext`, `BlockRegistry::register_block()` und `CurrencyHelper::format_percentage()` verlassen. `Util::has_overlap_locked()` akzeptiert optional eine auszuschlie\xdfende Buchung. Die Typen `content` und `script` des `data-lazy`-Loaders wurden entfernt, ebenso die ungenutzte `mhmrentiva_booking_validation`-Anbindung.\\n\\n## Nachtrag zu 6.3.1\\n\\n6.3.1 folgte am selben Tag mit zwei Korrekturen:\\n\\n- **Mit Elementor erstellte Seiten werden gefunden.** Ein Rentiva-Widget oder ein `[rentiva_*]`-Shortcode in einem Elementor-Widget befindet sich in den Daten von Elementor statt im Seiteninhalt, daher hat Rentivas Seitensuche es \xfcbersehen: \u201eJetzt buchen\u201c-Buttons und andere Links fielen auf die Startseite zur\xfcck, und \u201eShortcode-Seiten\u201c f\xfchrte die Seite als fehlend auf. Eine Seite mit dem Shortcode oder Block im Inhalt hat weiterhin Vorrang. Auf Elementor-Websites, deren Fahrzeugdetailseite jetzt gefunden wird, werden Fahrzeugseiten unter diese Seite verschoben, mit einer 301-Weiterleitung von `/vehicle/...`, wie auf Block- und Shortcode-Websites.\\n- **\xdcbersetzungsplatzhalter in Hinweisen** verwenden jetzt ein Format, das das \xdcbersetzungstool von WordPress.org pr\xfcfen kann, und der t\xfcrkische Katalog verwendet die Pluralformel, die translate.wordpress.org verwendet.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Bezugsquelle.** Rentiva ist auf [WordPress.org](https://wordpress.org/plugins/mhm-rentiva/) und auf GitHub als [`v6.3.0`](https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva/releases/tag/v6.3.0) verf\xfcgbar; beide enthalten dieselben Dateien. WordPress.org h\xe4lt neue Versionen einige Stunden zur\xfcck, bevor Websites das Update angeboten wird. **Du verwendest Rentiva Pro?** Aktualisiere zuerst Rentiva, dann [Pro auf 6.4.0](/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.4.0-release). Das vollst\xe4ndige \xc4nderungsprotokoll in beiden Sprachen liegt dem Plugin bei."},{"id":"rentiva-v6.2.1-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.2.1-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-10-13-rentiva-v6.2.1-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-10-13-rentiva-v6.2.1-release.md","title":"Rentiva 6.2.1 \u2014 Elementor-Widgets schreiben die Kontodaten der speichernden Person nicht mehr in den gespeicherten Text einer Seite","description":"6.2.1 ist eine Datenschutzkorrektur f\xfcr Websites, die Seiten mit Elementor erstellen. Die Elementor-Widgets von Rentiva konnten die Kontodaten der Person, die eine Seite gespeichert hat, im gespeicherten Text dieser Seite hinterlassen, wo die Website-Suche sie finden konnte. Diese Version unterbindet das und bereinigt die bereits betroffenen Seiten. Sie ist auf WordPress.org ver\xf6ffentlicht, daher bietet WordPress sie dir als normales Update an. Wenn du Elementor verwendest, aktualisiere jetzt und f\xfchre die beiden Schritte unter \u201eNach dem Update\u201c aus.","date":"2026-10-13T06:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"elementor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/elementor"},{"inline":true,"label":"privacy","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/privacy"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"}],"readingTime":2.11,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v6.2.1-release","title":"Rentiva 6.2.1 \u2014 Elementor-Widgets schreiben die Kontodaten der speichernden Person nicht mehr in den gespeicherten Text einer Seite","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","elementor","privacy","security"],"date":"2026-10-13T06:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.3.0 \u2014 Eine websiteweite Anzahlung f\xfcr Mieten, sichere Editor-Vorschauen, wirksame E-Mail-Einstellungen und ein serverseitig gepr\xfcftes Buchungsformular","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.3.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva Pro 6.3.0 \u2013 IBANs und Dokumente der Anbieter verschl\xfcsselt gespeichert, Nachrichten als Unterhaltungen neu aufgebaut und alle Anbieter-Einstellungen an einem Ort","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.3.0-release"}},"content":"6.2.1 ist eine Datenschutzkorrektur f\xfcr Websites, die Seiten mit Elementor erstellen. Die Elementor-Widgets von Rentiva konnten die Kontodaten der Person, die eine Seite gespeichert hat, im gespeicherten Text dieser Seite hinterlassen, wo die Website-Suche sie finden konnte. Diese Version unterbindet das und bereinigt die bereits betroffenen Seiten. Sie ist auf WordPress.org ver\xf6ffentlicht, daher bietet WordPress sie dir als normales Update an. **Wenn du Elementor verwendest, aktualisiere jetzt und f\xfchre die beiden Schritte unter \u201eNach dem Update\u201c aus.**\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Was war das Problem\\n\\nWenn eine Seite, ein Beitrag oder ein Template mit einem Rentiva-Elementor-Widget gespeichert wurde, hat Elementor zus\xe4tzlich eine Klartextkopie davon im Beitragsinhalt gespeichert. Die Rentiva-Widgets haben in diese Kopie geschrieben, was die speichernde Person gesehen hat: ihre Buchungen, ihren Zahlungsverlauf, ihre Favoriten, ihre E-Mail-Adresse und Sicherheitstoken. Die Website-Suche liest diese Kopie, daher konnte auf einer ver\xf6ffentlichten Seite jeder diese Daten finden.\\n\\n## Was sich \xe4ndert\\n\\n- **Rentiva-Widgets schreiben nichts mehr in die Klartextkopie**, die Elementor beim Speichern einer Seite ablegt.\\n- **Sie lassen auch die Markdown-Kopie von Elementor leer** und werden nie im gemeinsamen Element-Cache von Elementor gespeichert, selbst wenn die Cache-Einstellungen eines Widgets auf \u201eAktiv\u201c stehen.\\n- **F\xfcr Besucher \xe4ndert sich nichts.** Die Seite selbst zeigt jedem Besucher weiterhin seine eigenen Daten.\\n\\n## Betroffene Seiten werden f\xfcr dich bereinigt\\n\\nNach dem Update baut ein einmaliger Hintergrundjob den gespeicherten Klartext jeder Elementor-Seite, jedes Beitrags und jedes Templates mit einem Rentiva-Widget neu auf, Entw\xfcrfe eingeschlossen, und verwirft die zwischengespeicherte Markdown-Kopie. Er l\xe4uft \xfcber WP-Cron in Stapeln von 50, wiederholt fehlgeschlagene Seiten und wartet zwischen den Versuchen l\xe4nger, solange er keine Fortschritte macht. Er \xe4ndert weder das \xc4nderungsdatum einer Seite noch erstellt er eine Revision, sodass deine Seiten ihre Daten und ihren Verlauf behalten.\\n\\n## Nach dem Update\\n\\n1. **Leere deinen Seiten-Cache**, damit zwischengespeicherte Kopien einer betroffenen Seite ersetzt werden.\\n2. **Du verwendest ein Such-Plugin?** Baue dessen Index neu auf, damit es den alten Text vergisst.\\n3. Optional kannst du den eigenen Cache von Elementor unter **Elementor > Tools > Clear Files & Data** leeren.\\n\\n:::note \xc4ltere Revisionen\\n\xc4ltere Revisionen einer betroffenen Seite enthalten noch den alten Text. Nur Benutzer, die diese Seite bearbeiten d\xfcrfen, k\xf6nnen sie sehen.\\n:::\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Wo du es bekommst.** 6.2.1 ist auf [WordPress.org](https://wordpress.org/plugins/mhm-rentiva/) und auf GitHub als [`v6.2.1`](https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva/releases/tag/v6.2.1) verf\xfcgbar; beide enthalten dieselben Dateien. WordPress.org h\xe4lt neue Versionen einige Stunden zur\xfcck, bevor Websites das Update angeboten wird. Das vollst\xe4ndige \xc4nderungsprotokoll in beiden Sprachen wird mit dem Plugin ausgeliefert."},{"id":"rentiva-pro-v6.3.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.3.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-10-11-rentiva-pro-v6.3.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-10-11-rentiva-pro-v6.3.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva Pro 6.3.0 \u2013 IBANs und Dokumente der Anbieter verschl\xfcsselt gespeichert, Nachrichten als Unterhaltungen neu aufgebaut und alle Anbieter-Einstellungen an einem Ort","description":"6.3.0 sch\xfctzt, was Anbieter \xfcbermitteln: IBANs, Ausweisdokumente und Fahrzeugdokumente werden verschl\xfcsselt und von der Mediathek ferngehalten. Nachrichten werden als Unterhaltungen neu aufgebaut, und die Anbieterverwaltung erh\xe4lt eine Detailseite f\xfcr Anbieter sowie einen zentralen Ort f\xfcr alle Anbieter-Einstellungen. Aktualisiere zuerst MHM Rentiva (Lite) auf 6.2.0, danach Pro. Rentiva Pro 6.1.0 oder \xe4lter bricht neben Rentiva 6.2.0 im Anbieter-Panel mit einem Fehler ab, f\xfchre die beiden Updates also direkt nacheinander durch.","date":"2026-10-11T06:30:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"pro","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/pro"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"},{"inline":true,"label":"messages","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/messages"},{"inline":true,"label":"admin","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/admin"}],"readingTime":4.34,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-pro-v6.3.0-release","title":"Rentiva Pro 6.3.0 \u2013 IBANs und Dokumente der Anbieter verschl\xfcsselt gespeichert, Nachrichten als Unterhaltungen neu aufgebaut und alle Anbieter-Einstellungen an einem Ort","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","pro","vendor","security","messages","admin"],"date":"2026-10-11T06:30"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.2.1 \u2014 Elementor-Widgets schreiben die Kontodaten der speichernden Person nicht mehr in den gespeicherten Text einer Seite","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.2.1-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.2.0 \u2014 Kontaktnachrichten erhalten einen eigenen Bildschirm, das Kunden-Dashboard wird eingestellt, und ignorierte Block- und Elementor-Einstellungen greifen jetzt","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.2.0-release"}},"content":"6.3.0 sch\xfctzt, was Anbieter \xfcbermitteln: IBANs, Ausweisdokumente und Fahrzeugdokumente werden verschl\xfcsselt und von der Mediathek ferngehalten. Nachrichten werden als Unterhaltungen neu aufgebaut, und die Anbieterverwaltung erh\xe4lt eine Detailseite f\xfcr Anbieter sowie einen zentralen Ort f\xfcr alle Anbieter-Einstellungen. **Aktualisiere zuerst MHM Rentiva (Lite) auf 6.2.0, danach Pro.** Rentiva Pro 6.1.0 oder \xe4lter bricht neben Rentiva 6.2.0 im Anbieter-Panel mit einem Fehler ab, f\xfchre die beiden Updates also direkt nacheinander durch.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## IBANs und Dokumente der Anbieter werden verschl\xfcsselt gespeichert\\n\\n- **IBANs und Ausweisdokumente** (Ausweis, F\xfchrerschein, Adressnachweis) werden verschl\xfcsselt und au\xdferhalb der Mediathek gespeichert. Dokumente werden nur als JPG, PNG oder PDF akzeptiert und auf Typ und Gr\xf6\xdfe gepr\xfcft. Administratoren zeigen eine IBAN \xfcber \u201eAnzeigen / Kopieren / Ausblenden\u201c an und \xf6ffnen Dokumente \xfcber Routen, die protokollieren, wer sie angesehen hat; Auszahlungsabrechnungen zeigen eine maskierte IBAN.\\n- **Fahrzeugschein und Versicherungsdokumente** verlassen ebenfalls die \xf6ffentliche Mediathek. Der Bearbeitungsbildschirm des Fahrzeugs enth\xe4lt eine Box \u201eFahrzeugdokumente\u201c mit protokolliertem Betrachter, und der Administrator erh\xe4lt eine E-Mail, wenn ein Anbieter ein Dokument erneuert.\\n- **Beim Update werden vorhandene IBANs und Dokumente umgewandelt, und die alten Dokument-Anh\xe4nge werden aus der Mediathek gel\xf6scht, sobald sie** in den verschl\xfcsselten Speicher **kopiert wurden**. Galerie- oder Titelbild-Eintr\xe4ge, die auf eine solche Datei verwiesen, werden entfernt.\\n\\n**Empfohlen:** Ohne weitere Einrichtung stammen die Verschl\xfcsselungsschl\xfcssel aus den WordPress-Schl\xfcsseln in `wp-config.php`, sodass eine \xc4nderung dieser Schl\xfcssel gespeicherte IBANs und Dokumente unlesbar macht. Definiere `MHM_RENTIVA_SENSITIVE_KEY` in `wp-config.php`, um den Daten einen eigenen Schl\xfcssel zu geben \u2013 ein Admin-Hinweis empfiehlt dies, erkl\xe4rt, wo die Zeile hingeh\xf6rt, und gibt eine fertige `define()`-Zeile mit einem neuen Schl\xfcssel aus.\\n\\n:::caution Bekannte Einschr\xe4nkung\\nEin Anbieter, dessen IBAN nach dem Update nicht gelesen werden konnte \u2013 zum Beispiel, weil die WordPress-Schl\xfcssel in `wp-config.php` nach der Freigabe des Anbieters ge\xe4ndert wurden \u2013, **kann keine Auszahlung anfordern, bis die IBAN erneut eingegeben wird, und 6.3.0 hat kein Formular, um sie einzugeben.** Der Admin-Hinweis nennt und verlinkt jeden betroffenen Anbieter.\\n:::\\n\\n## Nachrichten, als Unterhaltungen neu aufgebaut\\n\\nEine Unterhaltung besteht aus einer ersten Nachricht und ihren Antworten. Es gibt einen neuen Admin-Posteingang und eine Verlaufsansicht \u2013 Priorit\xe4t, letzte Aktivit\xe4t, Kunde, Status und zugeh\xf6rige Buchung \u2013 mit seitlichen Karten, die sich einklappen lassen und ihren Zustand speichern. Kunden sehen nur ihre eigenen Unterhaltungen, als reinen Text. Die E-Mail-Regeln sind eindeutig: eine Status-E-Mail nur bei einer einzelnen \xc4nderung durch einen Administrator, genau eine E-Mail pro Antwort eines Administrators, keine bei Massenaktionen oder beim Update und eine automatische Antwort nur bei einer neuen Unterhaltung. Nachrichten haben eigene Berechtigungen. Vorhandene Nachrichten werden einmalig beim Update umgewandelt, ohne dass E-Mails versendet werden. E-Mail-Benachrichtigungen f\xfcr Nachrichten lassen sich jetzt tats\xe4chlich abschalten.\\n\\n## Anbieterverwaltung\\n\\n- **Eine Detailseite f\xfcr Anbieter:** Kennzahlen, Kontakt (Stadt bearbeitbar), Zahlung und Steuern mit protokollierter IBAN-Anzeige, die genehmigte Bewerbung und ihre Dokumente, Zuverl\xe4ssigkeit und Abzeichen, die effektive Provision und ihre Herkunft, Buchungen und Bewertungen zu den Fahrzeugen des Anbieters sowie Sperren / Reaktivieren.\\n- **Die Anbieterverwaltung \xf6ffnet sich mit \u201eAktive Anbieter\u201c**, mit E-Mail, Stadt, Fahrzeuganzahl, effektiver Provision und Bewertung pro Anbieter, einer Z\xe4hlerleiste und einer Karte \u201eUmsatz nach Stadt\u201c. Die Aktionen Genehmigen, Ablehnen, IBAN und Sperren werden innerhalb der Seite best\xe4tigt statt in einem Browser-Pop-up. Eine Bewerbung wird abgelehnt, wenn ihre drei Dokumente nicht angeh\xe4ngt sind.\\n- **Alle Anbieter-Einstellungen wandern nach Plugin-Einstellungen > Anbieter-Marktplatz**, und die Anbieterverwaltung verliert ihren Tab \u201eEinstellungen\u201c. Ein neuer Schalter \u201eNeue Anbieter-Bewerbungen annehmen\u201c ist standardm\xe4\xdfig aktiviert. Die Einstellungen f\xfcr Listungsgeb\xfchren werden jetzt tats\xe4chlich gespeichert. Die acht verstreuten Anbieter-Optionen werden beim Update dorthin verschoben.\\n- Im Rentiva-Bildschirm **Kunden** tragen Anbieter das Abzeichen \u201eAnbieter\u201c oder \u201eGesperrter Anbieter\u201c, und der Bildschirm **Buchungen** erh\xe4lt einen Anbieter-Filter und eine Anbieter-Spalte.\\n\\n## Fehlerbehebungen\\n\\n- **Eine Neuinstallation ohne gespeicherten Provisionssatz legt WooCommerce-Zahlungen, -Abschl\xfcsse und -Erstattungen nicht mehr lahm.** Die Provision wird mit einer Bestellnotiz zur\xfcckgehalten und mit dem sp\xe4ter gespeicherten Satz erfasst; ein Admin-Hinweis zeigt, wie viele zur\xfcckgehalten werden.\\n- Eine einzelne ausstehende Anbieter-Bewerbung leert nicht mehr das Dashboard aller anderen angemeldeten Kunden.\\n- Anbieter-E-Mails (13 Vorlagen und die Auszahlungsabrechnung) verlinken auf den passenden Bereich des Anbieter-Panels, statt Anbieter zur\xfcck zu \u201eMein Konto\u201c zu schicken.\\n- Kunden-, Fahrzeug- und Umsatzberichte z\xe4hlen nur abgeschlossene und best\xe4tigte Buchungen, und gleichzeitige \xc4nderungen des globalen Satzes \xfcberschreiben sich nicht mehr gegenseitig.\\n- Alle sechs Pro-Elementor-Widgets wenden die in ihnen gespeicherten Einstellungen an, und Einstellungen, die gespeichert, aber ignoriert wurden, greifen jetzt \u2013 zum Beispiel das Layout \u201eVertikal\u201c der Transfer-Suche und der Filter nach Herkunftstyp bei \u201eBeliebte Routen\u201c, der jetzt deine gespeicherten Standorttypen auflistet. Einstellungen, die nie eine Wirkung hatten, wurden aus dem Nachrichten-Block, den Transfer-Ergebnissen, der Transfer-Suche und \u201eBeliebte Routen\u201c entfernt.\\n\\n## F\xfcr Entwickler\\n\\nEntfernt: die Action `mhmrentiva_message_read`, der Filter `mhmrentiva_account_vendor_panel`, die alten Handler des Nachrichtenformulars und Methoden wie `Message::mark_as_read()`, `VendorApplicationManager::encrypt_iban()` / `decrypt_iban()` sowie die REST-Routen `GET/POST /vendors/settings`. `mhmrentiva_message_status_changed` \xfcbergibt jetzt die ID der ersten Nachricht der Unterhaltung und `array( \'actor\' => \u2026 )`. **Gespeicherte IBANs \xe4ndern ihr Format:** Code, der die IBAN-Meta direkt ausliest, funktioniert nicht mehr. F\xfcnf Datenbankschritte laufen einmalig beim Update.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Bezugsquelle.** Pro 6.3.0 ist auf GitHub als `v6.3.0` ver\xf6ffentlicht und wird \xfcber den Rentiva-Pro-Download auf wpalemi.com bereitgestellt. Aktualisiere zuerst [Rentiva auf 6.2.0](/blog/rentiva-v6.2.0-release). Das vollst\xe4ndige Changelog wird mit dem Plugin in beiden Sprachen ausgeliefert."},{"id":"rentiva-v6.2.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.2.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-10-11-rentiva-v6.2.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-10-11-rentiva-v6.2.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva 6.2.0 \u2014 Kontaktnachrichten erhalten einen eigenen Bildschirm, das Kunden-Dashboard wird eingestellt, und ignorierte Block- und Elementor-Einstellungen greifen jetzt","description":"6.2.0 b\xfcndelt vier Wochen Arbeit. Kontaktnachrichten ziehen auf einen eigenen Bildschirm um und ihre Anh\xe4nge in einen privaten Ordner, das separate Kunden-Dashboard wird zugunsten von \u201eMein Konto\u201c eingestellt, und Block- und Elementor-Einstellungen, die gespeichert wurden, aber nie auf der Seite ankamen, greifen jetzt. Die Version ist auf WordPress.org ver\xf6ffentlicht, daher bietet WordPress sie dir als ganz normales Update an. Nutzt du Rentiva Pro? Pro 6.1.0 oder \xe4lter bricht neben diesem Release im Anbieter-Panel mit einem Fehler ab \u2013 aktualisiere Pro direkt danach auf 6.3.0.","date":"2026-10-11T06:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"contact","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/contact"},{"inline":true,"label":"elementor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/elementor"},{"inline":true,"label":"blocks","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/blocks"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"},{"inline":true,"label":"admin","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/admin"}],"readingTime":5.2,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v6.2.0-release","title":"Rentiva 6.2.0 \u2014 Kontaktnachrichten erhalten einen eigenen Bildschirm, das Kunden-Dashboard wird eingestellt, und ignorierte Block- und Elementor-Einstellungen greifen jetzt","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","contact","elementor","blocks","security","admin"],"date":"2026-10-11T06:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva Pro 6.3.0 \u2013 IBANs und Dokumente der Anbieter verschl\xfcsselt gespeichert, Nachrichten als Unterhaltungen neu aufgebaut und alle Anbieter-Einstellungen an einem Ort","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.3.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva Pro 6.2.0 \u2014 ein eigener Bereich f\xfcr Anbieter, eine W\xe4hrung im Hauptbuch und Erstattungen, die die Provision exakt zur\xfcckbuchen","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.2.0-release"}},"content":"6.2.0 b\xfcndelt vier Wochen Arbeit. Kontaktnachrichten ziehen auf einen eigenen Bildschirm um und ihre Anh\xe4nge in einen privaten Ordner, das separate Kunden-Dashboard wird zugunsten von \u201eMein Konto\u201c eingestellt, und Block- und Elementor-Einstellungen, die gespeichert wurden, aber nie auf der Seite ankamen, greifen jetzt. Die Version ist auf WordPress.org ver\xf6ffentlicht, daher bietet WordPress sie dir als ganz normales Update an. **Nutzt du Rentiva Pro?** Pro 6.1.0 oder \xe4lter bricht neben diesem Release im Anbieter-Panel mit einem Fehler ab \u2013 aktualisiere Pro direkt danach auf 6.3.0.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Kontaktnachrichten erhalten einen eigenen Bildschirm\\n\\n**MHM Rentiva > Kontaktnachrichten** ist ein neuer Bildschirm: Statistiken, Tabs f\xfcr Neu / Gelesen / Beantwortet, ein Monatsfilter, eine Suche, Massenaktionen und eine Detailansicht mit der Karte des Absenders und seinen weiteren Nachrichten. Du kannst per E-Mail antworten und eine Nachricht als beantwortet markieren, und das Men\xfc zeigt an, wie viele ungelesen sind. Links zur alten Liste und zu den alten Bearbeitungsbildschirmen \xf6ffnen den neuen Bildschirm, und bestehende Nachrichten werden beim Update einmalig als gelesen markiert.\\n\\n## Anh\xe4nge ziehen in einen privaten Ordner um\\n\\nAnh\xe4nge aus dem Kontaktformular werden jetzt in einem privaten Ordner, `uploads/mhm-rentiva-private/contact/`, unter zuf\xe4lligen Namen gespeichert. Sie lassen sich nur \xfcber den Button **Herunterladen** des Administrators herunterladen, und wenn du eine Nachricht l\xf6schst, wird auch ihre Datei gel\xf6scht. Beim Update werden bestehende Anh\xe4nge dorthin verschoben und **ihre alten \xf6ffentlichen Adressen funktionieren nicht mehr**; jede Datei, die nicht verschoben werden kann, wird einmalig in einem Admin-Hinweis aufgef\xfchrt. Anh\xe4nge sind auf 5 MB begrenzt.\\n\\n- **Unter nginx** f\xfcgst du die Deny-Regel aus dem Datenschutzabschnitt der Readme des Plugins hinzu: `location ^~ /wp-content/uploads/mhm-rentiva-private/ { deny all; }`. Unter Apache wird der Ordner mit einer `.htaccess` ausgeliefert, die den direkten Zugriff verweigert.\\n- **Nutzt du ein Media-Offload-Plugin?** Schlie\xdfe den Ordner davon aus.\\n\\n## Das Kunden-Dashboard wird eingestellt\\n\\n`[rentiva_user_dashboard]`, der zugeh\xf6rige Block und das Elementor-Widget rendern kein Dashboard mehr. Ein angemeldeter Kunde sieht eine Zeile und einen Link zu **Mein Konto**; Besucher sehen nichts; Administratoren sehen zus\xe4tzlich einen Hinweis, der sie bittet, es von der Seite zu entfernen. Der Block und das Widget sind in den Editoren ausgeblendet, und \u201eShortcode Pages\u201c bietet nicht mehr an, die Seite zu erstellen. Kunden finden ihre Buchungen, Favoriten und Zahlungen unter \u201eMein Konto\u201c. Siehe [Master-Konto-Dashboard (eingestellt)](/docs/features-usage/shortcodes/user-dashboard).\\n\\n## Ignorierte Block- und Elementor-Einstellungen greifen jetzt\\n\\n- **Gespeicherte Einstellungen kommen auf der Seite an.** Dazu geh\xf6ren: Typ, Telefon-, Firmen-, Fahrzeug-, Priorit\xe4ts- und Anhangfelder, Theme und automatische Antwort des Kontaktformulars (bisher wurde jedes Formular als \u201egeneral\u201c gerendert); die Spalten der Fahrzeugliste; der Abschnitt \u201eRatings & Reviews\u201c der Fahrzeugdetails, der jetzt \u201eBewertungen anzeigen\u201c folgt; die H\xf6he des Verf\xfcgbarkeitskalenders. Die Standardwerte behalten das alte Aussehen bei, sodass sich eine Seite nur dort \xe4ndert, wo eine dieser Einstellungen ge\xe4ndert worden war.\\n- **Elementor-Stil-Steuerelemente** f\xfcr Fahrzeugkarten, Listen, Raster, hervorgehobene Fahrzeuge und den Buchungsbutton gestalten jetzt die Seite \u2013 die meisten davon griffen vorher ins Leere. Farben oder Abst\xe4nde, die du fr\xfcher gespeichert, aber nie gesehen hast, k\xf6nnen jetzt erscheinen.\\n- **Block-Einstellungen bleiben erhalten.** Eine im Block-Editor ge\xe4nderte und gespeicherte Einstellung wird nicht mehr bei jedem Rendern \xfcberschrieben.\\n- **Einstellungen, die nie etwas bewirkt haben, wurden entfernt** \u2013 aus Bl\xf6cken, Widgets und Shortcodes. Ein gespeicherter Wert wird einfach ignoriert, und die Seite wird wie bisher gerendert. Die Shortcode-Seiten dieser Dokumentation f\xfchren sie nicht mehr auf.\\n- **Zwei Shortcode-Attribute wurden in der Praxis umbenannt:** Featured Vehicles liest `show_book_button` nicht mehr \u2013 verwende `show_booking_button=\\"0\\"` \u2013 und Unified Search liest `layout` nicht mehr \u2013 verwende `search_layout=\\"vertical\\"`. Search Results hat eine einzige **Standard-Sortierreihenfolge** (`default_sort`) statt \u201eSort By\u201c und \u201eSort Order\u201c.\\n\\n## Kleinere \xc4nderungen, die dir auffallen werden\\n\\n- **Fahrzeugkarten** zeigen ein Bild im Format 3:2 und die tats\xe4chliche Bewertung des Fahrzeugs; ein Fahrzeug ohne Bewertungen zeigt keine an, und der Platzhalter \u201e\u2605 4.8 (120 reviews)\u201c ist verschwunden. Der Buchungsbutton zeigt \u201eNicht verf\xfcgbar\u201c, wenn das Fahrzeug au\xdfer Betrieb ist, und folgt ansonsten dem Text des Widgets, danach deinem globalen Text f\xfcr den Button \u201eJetzt buchen\u201c. Das Buchungsformular \xfcbernimmt dasselbe Aussehen und passt zum Layout der Fahrzeugdetails.\\n- **Kundenbildschirm:** Total Spent, Active, VIP und Avg. Spend z\xe4hlen nur abgeschlossene oder best\xe4tigte Buchungen, Kunden, die \xfcber WooCommerce bezahlt haben, zeigen ihre Telefonnummer und Adresse, und ein Kunde mit zwei Telefoneintr\xe4gen erscheint nicht mehr doppelt.\\n- **Listen unter \u201eMein Konto\u201c:** Seite 2 der Zahlungshistorie ist wieder erreichbar, und \u201eMeine Buchungen\u201c sowie die Zahlungshistorie filtern vor dem Seitenumbruch, sodass eine gefilterte Seite vollst\xe4ndig gef\xfcllt ist.\\n- **\u201eLoad More\u201c bei den Testimonials** beh\xe4lt Reihenfolge, Filter und Anzeigeoptionen bei.\\n- **Das Frontend wird nicht mehr dunkel**, nur weil das Betriebssystem des Besuchers im Dunkelmodus ist; dar\xfcber entscheiden dein Theme und die plugineigene Einstellung \u201eDark Mode\u201c.\\n\\n## Sicherheit und Datenschutz\\n\\n- Die Galerie und das Beitragsbild eines Fahrzeugs akzeptieren nur Bilder, die der bearbeitende Benutzer hochgeladen hat oder verwenden darf, und niemals ein sensibles Dokument. Fr\xfcher gespeicherte Galerieeintr\xe4ge werden nur angezeigt, wenn ihre Herkunft vertrauensw\xfcrdig ist. Um ein Bild an ein Fahrzeug anzuh\xe4ngen, ist die Berechtigung zum Bearbeiten dieses Fahrzeugs erforderlich.\\n- Der benutzerdefinierte Empf\xe4nger eines Kontaktformulars (`email_to`) wird nur verwendet, solange diese Adresse auf der Seite, die das Formular enth\xe4lt, noch eingetragen ist; andernfalls geht die Nachricht an den globalen Empf\xe4nger.\\n- Die IP-Adresse des Besuchers ist nicht mehr in der Admin-E-Mail enthalten, und Typ und Priorit\xe4t des Kontaktformulars werden gegen die zul\xe4ssigen Werte gepr\xfcft.\\n- Die Datenbankbereinigung l\xf6scht keine Nachrichten-Thread-, Provisionsr\xfcckbehalt- und Anbieter-IBAN-Eintr\xe4ge von Rentiva Pro mehr.\\n\\n## F\xfcr Entwickler\\n\\nZehn Hooks und die Klassen des Kunden-Dashboards wurden entfernt, darunter die `mhmrentiva_dashboard_*`-Filter und drei `mhmrentiva_availability_calendar_*`-Filter; `render_shortcode()` und `output_shortcode()` bleiben als veraltete Shims erhalten \u2013 verwende `render_canonical()`. Zu den neuen Hooks geh\xf6ren `mhmrentiva_contact_recipient_fallback`, `mhmrentiva_gallery_attachment_allowed` und `mhmrentiva_retired_dashboard_notice`, dazu REST-Routen unter `mhm-rentiva/v1/contact-messages` (nur f\xfcr Administratoren). Beim Update laufen einmalig drei Datenbankschritte: Kontaktstatus, Kontaktanh\xe4nge und Elementor-Stil-IDs.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Wo du sie bekommst.** 6.2.0 ist auf [WordPress.org](https://wordpress.org/plugins/mhm-rentiva/) und auf GitHub als [`v6.2.0`](https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva/releases/tag/v6.2.0) verf\xfcgbar; beide enthalten dieselben Dateien. WordPress.org h\xe4lt neue Versionen einige Stunden zur\xfcck, bevor Websites das Update angeboten wird. **Nutzt du Rentiva Pro?** Aktualisiere zuerst Rentiva, dann [Pro auf 6.3.0](/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.3.0-release) \u2013 Pro 6.1.0 oder \xe4lter bricht neben diesem Release im Anbieter-Panel mit einem Fehler ab. Das vollst\xe4ndige Changelog in beiden Sprachen wird mit dem Plugin ausgeliefert."},{"id":"rentiva-pro-v6.2.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.2.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-09-17-rentiva-pro-v6.2.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-09-17-rentiva-pro-v6.2.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva Pro 6.2.0 \u2014 ein eigener Bereich f\xfcr Anbieter, eine W\xe4hrung im Hauptbuch und Erstattungen, die die Provision exakt zur\xfcckbuchen","description":"Anbieter erhalten einen eigenen Bereich, und das Geld dahinter steht auf einer einheitlichen Grundlage: eine W\xe4hrung im Hauptbuch und Erstattungen, die genau die gutgeschriebene Provision zur\xfccknehmen. Aktualisiere zuerst MHM Rentiva auf 6.1.5, dann Pro. Findet Pro eine \xe4ltere Rentiva-Version, deaktiviert es sich mit einem Hinweis und legt nichts an.","date":"2026-09-17T06:30:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"pro","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/pro"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"payouts","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/payouts"},{"inline":true,"label":"money","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/money"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"}],"readingTime":3.93,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-pro-v6.2.0-release","title":"Rentiva Pro 6.2.0 \u2014 ein eigener Bereich f\xfcr Anbieter, eine W\xe4hrung im Hauptbuch und Erstattungen, die die Provision exakt zur\xfcckbuchen","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","pro","vendor","payouts","money","security"],"date":"2026-09-17T06:30"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.2.0 \u2014 Kontaktnachrichten erhalten einen eigenen Bildschirm, das Kunden-Dashboard wird eingestellt, und ignorierte Block- und Elementor-Einstellungen greifen jetzt","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.2.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.1.5 \u2014 Die Datenbankbereinigung l\xf6scht nicht mehr, was ihr nicht geh\xf6rt","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.1.5-release"}},"content":"Anbieter erhalten einen eigenen Bereich, und das Geld dahinter steht auf einer einheitlichen Grundlage: eine W\xe4hrung im Hauptbuch und Erstattungen, die genau die gutgeschriebene Provision zur\xfccknehmen. **Aktualisiere zuerst MHM Rentiva auf 6.1.5, dann Pro.** Findet Pro eine \xe4ltere Rentiva-Version, deaktiviert es sich mit einem Hinweis und legt nichts an.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Ein Bereich, mit dem Anbieter arbeiten k\xf6nnen\\n\\nPro legt automatisch eine Seite **Anbieterbereich** unter der Adresse `satici-panel` an, mit f\xfcnf Abschnitten: \xdcbersicht, Meine Inserate, Buchungen, Einnahmen & Auszahlungen und Bewertungen. Der alte Anbieterbereich unter Mein Konto leitet jetzt dauerhaft dorthin weiter.\\n\\n- Unter **Meine Inserate** kann ein Anbieter ein Inserat pausieren, fortsetzen, zur\xfcckziehen, verl\xe4ngern und erneut einstellen. Angezeigt werden nur die Aktionen, die der aktuelle Status des Inserats zul\xe4sst; ein nie freigegebenes Inserat zeigt keine, und eines, das auf seine Inseratsgeb\xfchr wartet, zeigt *Zahlung abschlie\xdfen*. Ein abgelehntes Inserat zeigt den Ablehnungshinweis, und ein zur\xfcckgezogenes Inserat beh\xe4lt seinen Buchungsverlauf.\\n- Unter **Einnahmen & Auszahlungen** fordert ein Anbieter eine Auszahlung an. Solange eine Anforderung aussteht, zeigt der Bereich diese Anforderung statt des Formulars.\\n- Ein Administrator kann den Bereich \xf6ffnen, um zu sehen, was Anbieter sehen. Ein gesperrter Anbieter sieht, warum sein Zugang beendet wurde, und ein Bewerber, dessen Bewerbung noch aussteht, sieht deren Status, statt zum Bewerbungsformular zur\xfcckgeschickt zu werden.\\n\\n## Eine W\xe4hrung im Hauptbuch\\n\\nDas Anbieter-Hauptbuch erfasst jetzt jeden Betrag in **der Basisw\xe4hrung des Shops**, mit der eigenen Dezimalgenauigkeit des Shops \u2014 auch wenn ein Besucher \xfcber Currency Switcher in einer anderen W\xe4hrung bezahlt hat. Die Provision aus einer solchen Bestellung wird mit **dem in dieser Bestellung gespeicherten Wechselkurs** umgerechnet. Deshalb ben\xf6tigt diese Version Rentiva 6.1.5: 6.1.5 verhindert, dass die Datenbankbereinigung von Rentiva genau diesen gespeicherten Kurs l\xf6scht.\\n\\nGuthaben und Summen ber\xfccksichtigen nur Betr\xe4ge in der Basisw\xe4hrung. Ein Guthaben, das ein Anbieter noch in einer anderen W\xe4hrung hat, wird auf der Karte \u201eVerf\xfcgbares Guthaben\u201c gesondert aufgef\xfchrt, statt stillschweigend hinzugerechnet zu werden. Die Geldspalten des Hauptbuchs werden durch ein einmaliges Datenbank-Update auf vier Dezimalstellen erweitert; der Pr\xfcf-Hash jeder bestehenden Hauptbuchzeile bleibt unver\xe4ndert.\\n\\n## Erstattungen nehmen genau das zur\xfcck, was gutgeschrieben wurde\\n\\nEine Erstattung bucht die Provision jetzt **kumulativ** zur\xfcck, verkn\xfcpft mit der Provision, zu der sie geh\xf6rt. Jede Folge von Teilerstattungen \u2014 auch eine, die vor der Provision selbst erfasst wurde \u2014 nimmt genau das zur\xfcck, was gutgeschrieben wurde, in der W\xe4hrung dieser Provision. Erstattungen f\xfcr dieselbe Bestellung werden nacheinander verarbeitet, sodass zwei gleichzeitig eingehende nicht mehr beide die volle Provision zur\xfcckbuchen k\xf6nnen.\\n\\n## \u201eInsgesamt ausgezahlt\u201c zeigte nach einer echten Auszahlung 0\\n\\nAuszahlungen, die auf der Seite \u201eAuszahlungen\u201c freigegeben wurden, wurden unter einem Typ erfasst, den die Summen nicht erkannten, und als *reserviert* statt als bezahlt \u2014 ein Status, aus dem sie nie herausgeholt wurden. \u201eInsgesamt ausgezahlt\u201c zeigte beim Anbieter 0, und die Einnahmen z\xe4hlten die Auszahlung als negativ. Auszahlungen werden jetzt als bezahlt erfasst, und auf diese Weise vor dieser Version freigegebene werden beim n\xe4chsten Laden einer Admin-Seite korrigiert.\\n\\n## Lies das vor dem Update\\n\\n- **Sicherheit.** Bei aktivierten Inseratsgeb\xfchren legte eine Anfrage zum Verl\xe4ngern oder erneuten Einstellen das Inserat in den Warenkorb des anfragenden Anbieters, **bevor gepr\xfcft wurde, ob das Inserat ihm geh\xf6rt** \u2014 ein aktiver Anbieter konnte so das Inserat eines anderen Anbieters verl\xe4ngern oder erneut einstellen. Die Eigent\xfcmerschaft wird jetzt zuerst gepr\xfcft.\\n- Bei aktivierten Inseratsgeb\xfchren wurde bei einer kostenpflichtigen Verl\xe4ngerung oder Neueinstellung au\xdferdem die Geb\xfchr erhoben, **bevor** gepr\xfcft wurde, ob das Inserat verl\xe4ngert oder erneut eingestellt werden konnte: Eine Verl\xe4ngerung nach Ablauf der Kulanzfrist wurde bezahlt und blieb abgelaufen, und eine Neueinstellung \xfcbersprang ihre Wartezeit. Die Regeln werden jetzt vor dem Checkout und erneut beim Abschluss der Zahlung gepr\xfcft.\\n- Auf einer Website, auf der Rentiva vor Pro aktiviert wurde \u2014 die einzige Reihenfolge, die Pro zul\xe4sst \u2014, wurden die eigenen Tabellen von Pro (Anbieter-Hauptbuch, Auszahlungsprotokoll, Schl\xfcsselregister, Provisionsrichtlinie, Anbieterberichte und die Transfer-Tabellen) nie angelegt, sodass **keine Provision erfasst wurde und nichts den Grund nannte**. Pro legt jetzt beim n\xe4chsten Laden einer Admin-Seite jede fehlende Tabelle an und versucht es weiter, bis alle vorhanden sind.\\n- Die Integrit\xe4tspr\xfcfung des Hauptbuchs schrieb ihr Ergebnis innerhalb ihrer eigenen schreibgesch\xfctzten Transaktion, sodass eine festgestellte Abweichung nie gespeichert wurde. Jetzt wird sie gespeichert.\\n\\n## Au\xdferdem in diesem Release\\n\\nDaten im Hauptbuch werden in der Zeitzone deiner Website statt in UTC angezeigt. Der Anbieterbereich schl\xe4gt nicht mehr fehl, wenn WooCommerce au\xdferhalb der Plugin-Seite deaktiviert wird, und zwei gleichzeitige Aufrufe beim ersten Laden k\xf6nnen nicht mehr zwei Anbieterbereich-Seiten anlegen. Auf \u201eAnbieterverwaltung\u201c und \u201eAnbieterberichte\u201c sind Admin-Hinweise bereits vorhanden, wenn die Seite zum ersten Mal erscheint. Der Anbieterbereich und die Meldungen zu Inseratsgeb\xfchren sind ins T\xfcrkische \xfcbersetzt.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Wo du es bekommst.** Pro 6.2.0 ist auf GitHub als `v6.2.0` ver\xf6ffentlicht und wird \xfcber den Rentiva-Pro-Download auf wpalemi.com bereitgestellt. Aktualisiere zuerst [Rentiva auf 6.1.5](/blog/rentiva-v6.1.5-release). Das vollst\xe4ndige \xc4nderungsprotokoll wird in beiden Sprachen mit dem Plugin ausgeliefert."},{"id":"rentiva-v6.1.5-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.1.5-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-09-17-rentiva-v6.1.5-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-09-17-rentiva-v6.1.5-release.md","title":"Rentiva 6.1.5 \u2014 Die Datenbankbereinigung l\xf6scht nicht mehr, was ihr nicht geh\xf6rt","description":"Wenn du MHM Currency Switcher neben Rentiva betreibst, konnte ein einziger Klick in Rentivas Datenbankbereinigung die Festpreise deiner Produkte l\xf6schen. 6.1.5 schlie\xdft diese L\xfccke, sorgt daf\xfcr, dass die Bereinigung nichts l\xf6scht, was sie nicht zuvor sichern konnte, und behebt einen Filter in der Buchungsliste, der nie fertig geladen wurde. Die Version ist auf WordPress.org ver\xf6ffentlicht, daher bietet WordPress sie dir als ganz normales Update an \u2014 danach musst du nichts erneut speichern.","date":"2026-09-17T06:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"maintenance","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/maintenance"},{"inline":true,"label":"bookings","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/bookings"},{"inline":true,"label":"admin","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/admin"}],"readingTime":3.51,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v6.1.5-release","title":"Rentiva 6.1.5 \u2014 Die Datenbankbereinigung l\xf6scht nicht mehr, was ihr nicht geh\xf6rt","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","maintenance","bookings","admin"],"date":"2026-09-17T06:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva Pro 6.2.0 \u2014 ein eigener Bereich f\xfcr Anbieter, eine W\xe4hrung im Hauptbuch und Erstattungen, die die Provision exakt zur\xfcckbuchen","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.2.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva Pro 6.1.0 \u2014 Eine L\xf6schschaltfl\xe4che, die nur ein Kunde dr\xfccken kann","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.1.0-release"}},"content":"Wenn du MHM Currency Switcher neben Rentiva betreibst, konnte ein einziger Klick in Rentivas Datenbankbereinigung die Festpreise deiner Produkte l\xf6schen. 6.1.5 schlie\xdft diese L\xfccke, sorgt daf\xfcr, dass die Bereinigung nichts l\xf6scht, was sie nicht zuvor sichern konnte, und behebt einen Filter in der Buchungsliste, der nie fertig geladen wurde. Die Version ist auf WordPress.org ver\xf6ffentlicht, daher bietet WordPress sie dir als ganz normales Update an \u2014 danach musst du nichts erneut speichern.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Die Bereinigung entfernt nur, was zu Rentiva geh\xf6rt\\n\\nUnter **MHM Rentiva > Einstellungen > Datenbankbereinigung** hat die Bereinigung ung\xfcltiger Metadaten jeden Datenschl\xfcssel, der mit `_mhm` beginnt, als Rentivas eigenen behandelt. Die Schl\xfcssel von MHM Currency Switcher beginnen genauso, daher hat die Bereinigung **die Festpreise jedes Produkts** entfernt und in Shops, deren Bestellungen als Beitr\xe4ge gespeichert werden, **die bei jeder Bestellung erfasste W\xe4hrung, den Wechselkurs und die Basisw\xe4hrung**.\\n\\nSchl\xfcssel unter `_mhmcs_` \u2014 die von Currency Switcher \u2014 bleiben jetzt unangetastet. Ein Schl\xfcssel, der dem Pr\xe4fix nur \xe4hnelt, wird weiterhin bereinigt.\\n\\n## Keine Sicherung, keine L\xf6schung\\n\\nDrei Bereinigungen kopieren das, was sie entfernen wollen, zun\xe4chst in eine Sicherungstabelle: ung\xfcltige Metadaten, verwaiste Metadaten und alte Protokolle. Keine von ihnen hat je gepr\xfcft, ob die Kopie tats\xe4chlich angelegt wurde. Konnte die Sicherungstabelle nicht erstellt oder nicht bef\xfcllt werden, wurden die Zeilen trotzdem gel\xf6scht \u2014 und die Ergebnisseite nannte dennoch eine Sicherung, die sie gar nicht enthielt.\\n\\nJede der drei **l\xf6scht jetzt nichts**, sofern nicht beide Schritte ihrer Sicherung erfolgreich waren. Sie teilt dir mit, warum sie abgebrochen hat, und entfernt eine Sicherungstabelle, die sie zwar erstellt, aber nicht bef\xfcllen konnte. Die Bereinigung alter Protokolle entscheidet Tabelle f\xfcr Tabelle, sodass die anderen Tabellen weiterhin bereinigt werden.\\n\\nAuch zwei kleinere Fehler an derselben Stelle sind behoben: Zwei in derselben Sekunde gestartete Bereinigungen teilen sich keine Sicherungstabelle mehr, und ein langes benutzerdefiniertes Tabellenpr\xe4fix besch\xe4digt nicht mehr den Namen der Sicherungstabelle. Eine abgebrochene Bereinigung zeigt ihren eigentlichen Grund statt \u201e[object Object]\u201c an.\\n\\nDie [Seite zur Datenbankbereinigung](/docs/core-configuration/maintenance) in dieser Dokumentation beschreibt die Werkzeuge jetzt mit den Bezeichnungen, die du auf dem Bildschirm siehst, einschlie\xdflich der Stelle, an der sich die Bereinigung ung\xfcltiger Metadaten befindet.\\n\\n## Der Filter \u201eAusstehend\u201c \xf6ffnet sich wieder\\n\\nIn der Buchungsliste konnte ein Klick auf den Chip **Ausstehend** dazu f\xfchren, dass die Seite endlos lud. Der Filter war als Datenbankabfrage aufgebaut, die mit jedem bei einer Buchung gespeicherten Detail wuchs; auf einer Testseite mit echten Buchungsdaten arbeitete die Datenbank nach 77 Sekunden immer noch daran. Jeder Status-Chip findet seine Buchungen jetzt in einem Schritt, nach derselben Regel, die auch die Zahl auf dem Chip verwendet \u2014 Liste und Zahl stimmen also weiterhin \xfcberein. Das Filtern nach Kennzeichen grenzt die Liste eines Chips jetzt ein, statt sie zu ersetzen. Dieser Fehler bestand seit 6.1.0.\\n\\n## Kleinere Dinge, die dir im Adminbereich auffallen werden\\n\\n- **Hinweise bleiben an ihrem Platz.** Ein Hinweis wie die Lizenzwarnung rutschte bisher auf den meisten Admin-Seiten einen Moment nach dem Erscheinen der Seite unter den Seitentitel und schob die Seite nach unten. Jetzt ist er bereits da, wenn die Seite erstmals angezeigt wird. Unter Einstellungen > Benachrichtigungsvorlagen erscheint er nicht mehr doppelt, und unter Einstellungen wird er nicht mehr zu einem Pop-up, das nach vier Sekunden verschwindet.\\n- **Das Men\xfc steht direkt \xfcber WooCommerce** statt unterhalb der WooCommerce-Men\xfcs Produkte, Zahlungen und Analysen, sodass Rentivas lange Liste an Seiten im Blick bleibt. Es steht weiterhin unter den WordPress-eigenen Men\xfcs Beitr\xe4ge, Medien, Seiten und Kommentare.\\n- **Fahrzeugeinstellungen > Display & Preview** zeigt dein erstes Fahrzeug mit Beitragsbild \u2014 sein Foto, seinen Namen und seinen Tagespreis \u2014 statt eines grauen Platzhalters und eines Beispielautos.\\n\\n## Au\xdferdem in dieser Version\\n\\nDie Meldung \u201eKeine Fahrzeuge gefunden\u201c des Suchfilters wird jetzt auch auf ihrem AJAX-Pfad maskiert, die Bearbeitungsseite f\xfcr Fahrzeuge l\xf6st keine PHP-Warnung mehr aus, wenn die Einstellung f\xfcr Fahrzeugdetails leer ist, und ungenutztes JavaScript der E-Mail-Seite, das vier nicht existierende Admin-Aktionen aufrief, wurde entfernt.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Wo du sie bekommst.** 6.1.5 ist auf [WordPress.org](https://wordpress.org/plugins/mhm-rentiva/) und auf GitHub als [`v6.1.5`](https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva/releases/tag/v6.1.5) verf\xfcgbar; beide enthalten dieselben Dateien. WordPress.org h\xe4lt neue Versionen einige Stunden zur\xfcck, bevor Websites das Update angeboten wird. **Du nutzt Rentiva Pro?** Pro 6.2.0 setzt diese Version voraus \u2014 aktualisiere zuerst Rentiva. Das vollst\xe4ndige \xc4nderungsprotokoll in beiden Sprachen wird mit dem Plugin ausgeliefert."},{"id":"rentiva-pro-v6.1.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.1.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-09-08-rentiva-pro-v6.1.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-09-08-rentiva-pro-v6.1.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva Pro 6.1.0 \u2014 Eine L\xf6schschaltfl\xe4che, die nur ein Kunde dr\xfccken kann","description":"In diesem Release geht es vor allem um eine Frage: Was passiert, wenn ein Konto gel\xf6scht wird? Die Antwort war in 6.0.0 an drei verschiedenen Stellen schlechter, als sie h\xe4tte sein sollen \u2014 und eine davon vernichtete die Nachrichten eines Kunden auf Websites, die die Compliance-Funktion nie gekauft hatten. Aktualisiere zuerst MHM Rentiva auf 6.1.4, dann Pro. Diesmal gibt es keine Datenmigration und keine umbenannten Hooks.","date":"2026-09-08T02:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"pro","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/pro"},{"inline":true,"label":"privacy","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/privacy"},{"inline":true,"label":"gdpr","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/gdpr"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"},{"inline":true,"label":"money","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/money"}],"readingTime":6.61,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-pro-v6.1.0-release","title":"Rentiva Pro 6.1.0 \u2014 Eine L\xf6schschaltfl\xe4che, die nur ein Kunde dr\xfccken kann","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","pro","privacy","gdpr","security","money"],"date":"2026-09-08T02:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.1.5 \u2014 Die Datenbankbereinigung l\xf6scht nicht mehr, was ihr nicht geh\xf6rt","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.1.5-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.1.4 \u2014 Eine per ID verkn\xfcpfte Buchung verschwindet nicht mehr aus der Kunden\xfcbersicht","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.1.4-release"}},"content":"In diesem Release geht es vor allem um eine Frage: Was passiert, wenn ein Konto gel\xf6scht wird? Die Antwort war in 6.0.0 an drei verschiedenen Stellen schlechter, als sie h\xe4tte sein sollen \u2014 und eine davon vernichtete die Nachrichten eines Kunden auf Websites, die die Compliance-Funktion nie gekauft hatten. **Aktualisiere zuerst MHM Rentiva auf 6.1.4, dann Pro.** Diesmal gibt es keine Datenmigration und keine umbenannten Hooks.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Die Schaltfl\xe4che zur Selbstl\xf6schung war f\xfcr alle aktiv\\n\\nDie DSGVO-Werkzeuge von Pro platzieren im Kundenkontobereich eine Schaltfl\xe4che \u201eMeine Daten l\xf6schen\u201c. Ihre einzige Voraussetzung war, angemeldet zu sein.\\n\\nJeder angemeldete Benutzer kam an sie heran \u2014 ein Redakteur, ein Shop-Manager, **ein Administrator**. Wer DELETE eintippte und best\xe4tigte, l\xf6ste die Kontol\xf6schung von WordPress f\xfcr das eigene Konto der aktuellen Sitzung aus. Alles, was dieses Konto verfasst hatte, verschwand mit, und Anh\xe4nge landen nicht im Papierkorb, sofern eine Website das nicht ausdr\xfccklich aktiviert \u2014 die hochgeladenen Dateien wurden also endg\xfcltig vernichtet statt wiederherstellbar zu bleiben. Jeder andere Inhaltstyp, den das Konto verfasst hatte \u2014 darunter Elementor-Vorlagen \u2014, wurde auf dieselbe Weise gel\xf6scht.\\n\\nDer Handler lehnt jetzt jedes Konto ab, das nicht ausschlie\xdflich die Kundenrolle hat. Ein Administrator, der die Schaltfl\xe4che dr\xfcckt, erh\xe4lt den Hinweis, dass das Konto nicht per Selbstbedienung gel\xf6scht werden kann.\\n\\n## Ein Schutz vor Datenverlust hinter der falschen Lizenz\\n\\nPro nimmt Anbieter, Auszahlungen und Nachrichten von einer Kontol\xf6schung aus. Dieser Schutz war innerhalb der Funktion DSGVO-Werkzeuge eingebunden \u2014 doch der Inhaltstyp, den er am meisten sch\xfctzt, die **Nachrichten**, wird von einer anderen Lizenzfunktion registriert.\\n\\nEine Website mit Lizenz f\xfcr Nachrichten, aber *ohne* Lizenz f\xfcr DSGVO-Werkzeuge registrierte also den Inhaltstyp f\xfcr Nachrichten, band aber \xfcberhaupt keinen Schutz ein. Eine Nachricht hat einen Autor und ist weder Beitrag noch Seite, daher l\xf6scht WordPress sie endg\xfcltig, statt sie in den Papierkorb zu verschieben. Wurde dieser Kunde in der Kundenansicht des kostenlosen Plugins gel\xf6scht, vernichtete das die H\xe4lfte des Kunden in jeder Unterhaltung, an der er beteiligt war, ohne dass im Papierkorb etwas zum Wiederherstellen lag \u2014 und die Antworten der Gegenseite blieben in einem Verlauf zur\xfcck, der sich nicht mehr als solcher lesen l\xe4sst.\\n\\nDer Schutz wird jetzt immer eingebunden, sobald Pro l\xe4dt, unabh\xe4ngig von der Lizenz. Er ist ein Schild gegen Datenverlust, keine Funktion \u2014 er muss auch L\xf6schungen abdecken, die Pro nicht selbst anst\xf6\xdft.\\n\\n## Die Bereinigung nach Aufbewahrungsfrist fragte nicht, wem das Konto geh\xf6rte\\n\\nPro kann Daten inaktiver Kunden nach einer Aufbewahrungsfrist l\xf6schen. In 6.0.0 stellte die Abfrage, die die Konten ausw\xe4hlte, drei Fragen: Ist dieses Konto lange genug inaktiv, wurde es lange genug vorher registriert, und hat es keine Buchungen? Sie fragte nicht, **wessen Konto es war**, und auch in der Schleife gab es nirgends eine Rollenpr\xfcfung.\\n\\nEin inaktives Konto ohne Buchung war daher ein Kandidat, ganz gleich, was es war: ein Anbieter, ein Shop-Manager, ein Administrator.\\n\\nDie Abfrage schr\xe4nkt jetzt auf dieselbe Weise ein, und ein zweiter Durchlauf beh\xe4lt nur Konten, deren Rollen ausschlie\xdflich die Kundenrolle sind. Im Zweifel wird nicht gel\xf6scht \u2014 die richtige Richtung f\xfcr Code, dessen Aufgabe es ist, Daten zu vernichten.\\n\\nDrei weitere Punkte im selben Subsystem:\\n\\n- **Die Aufbewahrungsfrist kann nicht k\xfcrzer als ein Jahr sein.** Jeder kleinere Wert, ob konfiguriert oder \xfcbergeben, wird auf 365 Tage angehoben, und die Ersetzung wird ins Protokoll geschrieben.\\n- **Geplante L\xf6schung l\xf6scht jetzt tats\xe4chlich.** Die Kontol\xf6schfunktion von WordPress liegt in einer reinen Admin-Datei, die ein geplanter Lauf nie l\xe4dt; auf dem Cron-Pfad hatte der L\xf6schschritt daher stillschweigend gar nichts getan. In einem echten Cron-Kontext gemessen: Vor der Korrektur fehlte die Funktion, danach war sie vorhanden.\\n- **Die E-Mail-Adresse des gel\xf6schten Kunden ist nicht mehr Teil dessen, was die Bereinigung protokolliert.** Erfasst wird nur die Konto-ID. Au\xdferdem wurden zwei Sicherheitswarnungen \u2014 darunter die, die ausgel\xf6st wird, wenn ein Konto nicht gel\xf6scht werden konnte und stattdessen anonymisiert wurde \u2014 auf einer Stufe geschrieben, die die Standardkonfiguration verwirft. Sie sind jetzt Fehler und werden daher tats\xe4chlich erfasst.\\n\\n## In einem Multisite-Netzwerk schl\xe4gt die L\xf6schung jetzt ehrlich fehl\\n\\nWordPress kann ein Konto nicht aus einer einzelnen Website heraus aus einem Netzwerk entfernen \u2014 sein L\xf6schaufruf entfernt den Benutzer nur von dieser einen Website, und das Konto samt Adresse bleibt netzwerkweit bestehen.\\n\\nDie Anfrage wurde beantwortet, als w\xe4re sie ausgef\xfchrt worden. Jetzt wird sie mit einer Fehlermeldung abgelehnt, die besagt, dass die Kontol\xf6schung auf dieser Installation nicht verf\xfcgbar ist.\\n\\nDas ist eine Verhaltens\xe4nderung: Wer fr\xfcher \u201eDatenl\xf6schung abgeschlossen\u201c sah, sieht jetzt einen Fehler. Der Fehler ist die wahrheitsgem\xe4\xdfe Antwort. Gel\xf6scht wurde vorher ebenfalls nichts.\\n\\n**Eine Sache, die sich nicht ge\xe4ndert hat und die du kennen solltest:** Wenn sich ein Kunde selbst l\xf6scht, verschwinden seine eigenen Buchungen mit dem Konto. Er ist Gegenstand der Anfrage, daher werden sie gel\xf6scht statt aufbewahrt \u2014 endg\xfcltig, nicht in den Papierkorb. Der oben beschriebene Schutz deckt Anbieter, Auszahlungen und Nachrichten ab, nicht die eigenen Buchungen des Anfragenden. In 6.1.0 gibt es daf\xfcr keinen Schalter pro Website. Eine Version, die die Buchung anonymisiert, statt sie zu entfernen, ist der n\xe4chste Schritt dieser Arbeit.\\n\\n## Eine einzige Instanz f\xfcr die W\xe4hrung\\n\\nZehn Stellen in Pro bestimmten die W\xe4hrung selbst, wenn WooCommerce nicht verf\xfcgbar war \u2014 und widersprachen einander. Sechs sagten TRY und eine USD; das Symbol wurde zweimal als Lira-Zeichen und einmal als Dollarzeichen geschrieben.\\n\\nDas sind Fallbacks, sie laufen also genau dann, wenn die Bedingung zutrifft, gegen die sie absichern: bei einem geplanten Lauf, einem deaktivierten Shop, einem Zahlungs-Callback, der eintrifft, bevor WooCommerce gestartet ist. In diesem Zeitfenster konnte eine einzelne Auszahlung mit USD versehen werden, w\xe4hrend der CSV-Export, der Buchungseintrag der Strafe, der Webhook-Callback und die gedruckte Abrechnung \xfcber dasselbe Geld alle TRY angaben.\\n\\nAlle zehn fragen jetzt denselben Helfer, der WooCommerce heranzieht, wenn es aktiv ist, und andernfalls die W\xe4hrungseinstellung des Plugins. Die Pr\xfcfung vor dem Release fand dann f\xfcnf weitere Stellen derselben Art \u2014 das Analytics-Panel f\xfcr Anbieter, den eigenen Fallback der gedruckten Abrechnung bei fehlender W\xe4hrung, den Buchungseintrag f\xfcr die Stornierung einer Strafe, die E-Mail \u201eAbrechnung bereit\u201c und den Preishinweis im Fahrzeugformular f\xfcr Anbieter \u2014, und auch diese nutzen jetzt den Helfer.\\n\\nNebenbei wurden zwei Geldfehler behoben, und beide erreichten einen Anbieter:\\n\\n- **Eine per E-Mail an einen Anbieter gemeldete Strafe las sich wie eine Gutschrift.** Wo WooCommerce nicht verf\xfcgbar war, formatierte die Benachrichtigung den Betrag selbst und nahm dessen Absolutwert. Strafen werden als negative Betr\xe4ge gef\xfchrt, daher erhielt der Anbieter die H\xf6he des Abzugs ohne Vorzeichen \u2014 dieselbe Zeichenkette, die eine Zahlung erzeugt.\\n- **Die gedruckte Auszahlungsabrechnung konnte um den Faktor tausend falsch sein.** Ihre Zahlen stammen aus gespeicherten Daten, und ein bereits als `1.234.567,89` formatierter Wert wurde direkt in eine Zahl umgewandelt, was `1.234` ergibt \u2014 stillschweigend, auf dem Dokument, das ein Anbieter aufbewahrt.\\n\\n## Vier Verkn\xfcpfungen sind zur\xfcck im Dashboard\\n\\nBerichte, Anbieter, Nachrichten und Export verschwanden am 8. August mit der WordPress.org-Trennung des kostenlosen Plugins aus dem Dashboard, und nichts konnte sie zur\xfcckbringen, bis das kostenlose Plugin eine Schnittstelle daf\xfcr \xf6ffnete. Die Seiten blieben die ganze Zeit im Admin-Men\xfc; sie hatten lediglich ihre Verkn\xfcpfungen verloren.\\n\\nJede wird pro Lizenzfunktion beigesteuert, sodass eine Lizenz, die eine Ansicht nicht \xf6ffnen kann, auch keinen Link darauf erh\xe4lt, und eine nicht lizenzierte Installation steuert \xfcberhaupt keine bei. Transfer ist bewusst nicht darunter \u2014 er f\xfchrt zu Standorten und Routen, die einmal konfiguriert und dann in Ruhe gelassen werden.\\n\\nDeshalb **erfordert Pro jetzt MHM Rentiva 6.1.4 oder neuer**, w\xe4hrend der Pr\xfcfung vor dem Release von 6.1.3 angehoben: Die Verkn\xfcpfungen binden einen Filter, den das kostenlose Plugin erst ab 6.1.4 \xf6ffnet. Auf einer Website mit 6.1.3 w\xe4re die Kombination akzeptiert worden, und die Verkn\xfcpfungen w\xe4ren einfach nie erschienen, ohne dass etwas den Grund verraten h\xe4tte. Findet Pro ein \xe4lteres kostenloses Plugin vor, deaktiviert es sich mit einem Hinweis und r\xfchrt keine Daten an.\\n\\n## Au\xdferdem in diesem Release\\n\\nDas Monitoring-Subsystem wurde entfernt \u2014 ein Nachrichten-Logger, ein Monitoring-Manager und ein Performance-Monitor, rund 1.400 Zeilen, die kein Codepfad erreichen konnte. Die gemeinsame MHM-Oberfl\xe4chenbibliothek wurde im Gleichschritt mit dem kostenlosen Plugin von 0.4 auf 0.9.4 angehoben.\\n\\n---\\n\\nDas vollst\xe4ndige \xc4nderungsprotokoll wird mit dem Plugin in beiden Sprachen ausgeliefert."},{"id":"rentiva-v6.1.4-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.1.4-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-09-07-rentiva-v6.1.4-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-09-07-rentiva-v6.1.4-release.md","title":"Rentiva 6.1.4 \u2014 Eine per ID verkn\xfcpfte Buchung verschwindet nicht mehr aus der Kunden\xfcbersicht","description":"Wenn ein Gast zuerst bei dir gebucht und erst danach ein Konto angelegt hat, konnte die Kunden\xfcbersicht diese Buchung nicht sehen. In der Zeile des Kunden standen 0 Buchungen, sein Umsatz tauchte nie in den \xdcbersichtskarten oben auf, und \u201eBuchungen anzeigen\u201c zeigte eine leere Liste. 6.1.4 behebt das, und du musst nichts daf\xfcr tun: keine Datenbank\xe4nderung, kein erneutes Speichern von Einstellungen.","date":"2026-09-07T23:30:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"customers","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/customers"},{"inline":true,"label":"multisite","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/multisite"}],"readingTime":3.4,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v6.1.4-release","title":"Rentiva 6.1.4 \u2014 Eine per ID verkn\xfcpfte Buchung verschwindet nicht mehr aus der Kunden\xfcbersicht","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","customers","multisite"],"date":"2026-09-07T23:30"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva Pro 6.1.0 \u2014 Eine L\xf6schschaltfl\xe4che, die nur ein Kunde dr\xfccken kann","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.1.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva Pro 6.0.0 \u2014 Alles ist einheitlich benannt, und Sperrung bedeutet endlich Sperrung","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.0.0-release"}},"content":"Wenn ein Gast zuerst bei dir gebucht und erst danach ein Konto angelegt hat, konnte die Kunden\xfcbersicht diese Buchung nicht sehen. In der Zeile des Kunden standen 0 Buchungen, sein Umsatz tauchte nie in den \xdcbersichtskarten oben auf, und \u201eBuchungen anzeigen\u201c zeigte eine leere Liste. 6.1.4 behebt das, und du musst nichts daf\xfcr tun: keine Datenbank\xe4nderung, kein erneutes Speichern von Einstellungen.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Die Kunden\xfcbersicht findet jetzt jede Buchung\\n\\nDie \xdcbersicht hat die Buchungen eines Kunden **ausschlie\xdflich \xfcber seine E-Mail-Adresse** ermittelt. Das funktioniert im Normalfall, wenn Konto und Buchung dieselbe Adresse tragen. Es scheitert in jedem Fall, in dem das nicht so ist:\\n\\n- ein Gast, der gebucht und sich erst sp\xe4ter registriert hat \u2014 die Buchung ist \xfcber ihre interne ID mit dem Konto verkn\xfcpft, nicht \xfcber eine \xfcbereinstimmende E-Mail-Adresse\\n- ein Kunde, der seine E-Mail-Adresse nach der Buchung ge\xe4ndert hat\\n- ein manuell angelegtes Konto, das noch keine Buchung hat, oder eines, das nur \xfcber die eigenen Datens\xe4tze des Plugins bekannt ist\\n\\nIn all diesen F\xe4llen war die Buchung f\xfcr die \xdcbersicht unsichtbar. Die Zeile zeigte 0, das Detailfenster war leer, die \xdcbersichtskarten oben lie\xdfen diesen Umsatz weg, und das Konto konnte in der Kundenzahl komplett fehlen.\\n\\nUnter der Oberfl\xe4che waren vier separate Varianten von \u201eWer z\xe4hlt als Kunde\u201c auseinandergedriftet, weshalb sich die Kunden*liste* und die Buchungs*anzahl* bei derselben Person widersprechen konnten. Jetzt gibt es eine einzige Definition, und sie wird \xfcberall dort verwendet, wo diese Frage gestellt wird \u2014 in sieben Dateien des Plugins, an neunundzwanzig Aufrufstellen, darunter Zugeh\xf6rigkeit, Z\xe4hlung, L\xf6schung und Export. Diese k\xf6nnen sich nicht mehr gegenseitig widersprechen.\\n\\nEin Hinweis zur Umsetzung, denn genau solche Details entscheiden, ob ein Fix wirklich einer ist: Die Abfrage verwendet ein `EXISTS`-Pr\xe4dikat statt eines erweiterten Joins. Ein Join, der auf E-Mail *oder* ID abgleicht, z\xe4hlt eine Buchung doppelt, wenn beides passt. Das wurde nicht nur als Risiko angenommen \u2014 es wurde nachgewiesen, indem die naive Variante absichtlich geschrieben und die Verdopplung der Zahlen beobachtet wurde.\\n\\n**Die eigenen Kennzahlen des Dashboards werden separat berechnet und waren nicht Teil dieser \xc4nderung.**\\n\\n## Das Admin-Men\xfc steht wieder \xfcber den WordPress-eigenen Eintr\xe4gen\\n\\nRentiva registriert ein Hauptmen\xfc mit vielen Seiten dahinter, und wenn du eine Vermietung betreibst, bist du den ganzen Tag auf diesen Seiten unterwegs. Das Men\xfc stand unterhalb von Design, Plugins, Benutzer und Werkzeuge, weit unten in der Seitenleiste \u2013 um irgendeine seiner Seiten zu erreichen, musstest du also erst an ganz WordPress vorbeiscrollen.\\n\\nEs steht jetzt **direkt unter WooCommerce** und \xfcber Design. H\xf6her geht es nicht: Diese Position ist die Untergrenze der WordPress.org-Richtlinien, die von Plugins verlangen, nicht mit den eigenen Hauptmen\xfceintr\xe4gen von WordPress zu konkurrieren, und Rentiva h\xe4lt sich daran, statt sich \xfcber den Core zu dr\xe4ngen.\\n\\n## Die Multisite-Aktivierung erreicht jede Website\\n\\nDie netzwerkweite Aktivierung von Rentiva brach bei der hundertsten Website ab und \xfcbersprang private Websites komplett, sodass in einem gro\xdfen Netzwerk die Websites jenseits dieser Grenze nie ihre Tabellen erhielten. Jetzt erhalten beide sie. Au\xdferdem liest eine Unterwebsite beim Erzeugen ihrer URL-Slugs **ihre eigene** Sprache, statt die des Netzwerks zu \xfcbernehmen.\\n\\n## Ein Layout-Rollback kann nicht mehr die falsche Seite ver\xe4ndern\\n\\nDas Zur\xfccksetzen einer Seite im Layout-Werkzeug konnte Layout-Markup in einen v\xf6llig anderen, unbeteiligten Beitrag schreiben, wenn eine veraltete interne ID auf diesen verwies. Es kann jetzt keinen Beitrag mehr ver\xe4ndern, f\xfcr den es nicht gedacht war.\\n\\n## Hosting mit Redis und Memcached\\n\\nBei Hosting mit externem Objekt-Cache zeigte die jeweilige Liste nach dem Speichern eines Kunden, einer Buchung oder eines Fahrzeugs weiterhin die alten Daten an, bis der Cache-Eintrag von selbst ablief. Die Liste wird jetzt beim Speichern aktualisiert.\\n\\n## Ein kleinerer Download\\n\\nDas Paket enth\xe4lt keine React-Quelldateien mehr, die WordPress nie ausf\xfchrt.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Wo du es bekommst.** 6.1.4 ist auf GitHub als [`v6.1.4`](https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva/releases/tag/v6.1.4) ver\xf6ffentlicht. Das WordPress.org-Pluginverzeichnis liefert noch 6.1.3 aus \u2014 ob 6.1.4 dort eingereicht wird, ist eine separate Entscheidung, die noch nicht getroffen wurde. Ein Update aus WordPress heraus wird dir die Version daher derzeit nicht anbieten. Das vollst\xe4ndige \xc4nderungsprotokoll in beiden Sprachen wird mit dem Plugin ausgeliefert."},{"id":"rentiva-pro-v6.0.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.0.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-08-29-rentiva-pro-v6.0.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-08-29-rentiva-pro-v6.0.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva Pro 6.0.0 \u2014 Alles ist einheitlich benannt, und Sperrung bedeutet endlich Sperrung","description":"Dies ist ein Major-Release und der erste Pro-Build seit 5.2.3 Ende Juli. F\xfcr die meisten Website-Betreiber reichen zwei S\xe4tze: Aktualisiere zuerst MHM Rentiva auf 6.1.3, dann Pro, und deine Daten werden beim n\xe4chsten \xd6ffnen des Adminbereichs automatisch \xfcbernommen. Alle anderen \u2013 also alle, die eigenen Code an Pro angebunden haben \u2013 sollten vorher eine kurze Liste lesen, denn 70 Hook-Namen haben sich ge\xe4ndert, und nichts warnt dich, wenn einer davon nicht mehr ausgel\xf6st wird.","date":"2026-08-29T05:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"pro","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/pro"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendors","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendors"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"},{"inline":true,"label":"breaking","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/breaking"}],"readingTime":6.19,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-pro-v6.0.0-release","title":"Rentiva Pro 6.0.0 \u2014 Alles ist einheitlich benannt, und Sperrung bedeutet endlich Sperrung","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","pro","vendors","security","breaking"],"date":"2026-08-29T05:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.1.4 \u2014 Eine per ID verkn\xfcpfte Buchung verschwindet nicht mehr aus der Kunden\xfcbersicht","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.1.4-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.1.3 \u2014 Fahrzeuggalerien verschwinden nicht mehr","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.1.3-release"}},"content":"Dies ist ein Major-Release und der erste Pro-Build seit 5.2.3 Ende Juli. F\xfcr die meisten Website-Betreiber reichen zwei S\xe4tze: **Aktualisiere zuerst MHM Rentiva auf 6.1.3, dann Pro**, und deine Daten werden beim n\xe4chsten \xd6ffnen des Adminbereichs automatisch \xfcbernommen. Alle anderen \u2013 also alle, die eigenen Code an Pro angebunden haben \u2013 sollten vorher eine kurze Liste lesen, denn 70 Hook-Namen haben sich ge\xe4ndert, und nichts warnt dich, wenn einer davon nicht mehr ausgel\xf6st wird.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Lies das zuerst, wenn du eigenen Code hast\\n\\nDie Bezeichner von Pro verwenden jetzt ein einheitliches Pr\xe4fix, genauso wie die des kostenlosen Plugins in dessen eigener Version 6.0.0. Das ist gut, wenn man es einmal erledigt hat, und schlecht, wenn man es zuf\xe4llig entdeckt \u2013 deshalb hier alles auf einen Blick.\\n\\n**Die Hook-Regel besteht aus einem Schritt.** Ersetze `mhm_rentiva_` durch `mhmrentiva_`. Aus `mhm_rentiva_payout_approved` wird also `mhmrentiva_payout_approved`. Drei Nachrichten-Hooks verwendeten ein einfaches `mhm_`-Pr\xe4fix und folgen derselben Regel: `mhm_message_created`, `mhm_message_read` und `mhm_message_status_changed`.\\n\\n**Ein Hook, den die Regel nicht abdeckt.** `mhm_rentiva/currency_symbol` verwendete einen Schr\xe4gstrich, wo alle anderen Namen einen Unterstrich hatten. Er hei\xdft jetzt `mhmrentiva_currency_symbol`.\\n\\n**Ein Filter wurde entfernt statt umbenannt.** `mhm_rentiva_vendor_apply_endpoint_slug` wurde wie alles andere auf das neue Pr\xe4fix umgestellt und jetzt vollst\xe4ndig entfernt \u2013 weil er nie funktioniert hat. Er wurde nur dort angewendet, wo die Weiterleitung nach dem Absenden erzeugt wird, w\xe4hrend der Code, der den Endpunkt f\xfcr Anbieter-Bewerbungen *registriert*, ihn nie ausgelesen hat, weder in dieser Version noch in 5.2.3. Wer ihn gesetzt hatte, wurde an eine Adresse weitergeleitet, von der WordPress nichts wusste, und landete auf einer 404-Seite. Wir haben ihn entfernt, statt ihn anzubinden, weil die Adresse eines Endpunkts hier ein Bezeichner ist, der an die Sprache deiner Website gebunden ist, und keine Beschriftung, die anderer Code umschreiben soll.\\n\\n**Was die Leute wirklich erwischt, sind nicht unsere Hook-Namen.** Die drei Inhaltstypen von Pro wurden umbenannt, und das \xe4ndert die davon abgeleiteten WordPress-Hooks:\\n\\n| Bisher | Jetzt |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| `mhm_message` | `mhmrentiva_message` |\\n| `mhm_payout` | `mhmrentiva_payout` |\\n| `mhm_vendor_app` | `mhmrentiva_vendor` |\\n\\nAus `save_post_mhm_payout` wird also `save_post_mhmrentiva_payout`, und dasselbe gilt f\xfcr die `add_meta_boxes_*`- und `manage_*_posts_columns`-Familien. Jede `WP_Query`-, `get_posts`- oder `pre_get_posts`-Pr\xfcfung, die einen alten Typ nennt, trifft jetzt auf gar nichts mehr zu \u2013 und zwar stillschweigend.\\n\\nBeachte die dritte Zeile. `mhm_vendor_app` wurde **nicht** zu `mhmrentiva_vendor_app` \u2013 dieser Name hat 21 Zeichen, und WordPress speichert einen Inhaltstyp in einer Spalte mit 20 Zeichen. Die Registrierung schl\xe4gt dann komplett fehl, und der Inhaltstyp w\xfcrde schlicht nicht mehr existieren. Er hei\xdft `mhmrentiva_vendor`.\\n\\n**Durchsuche vor dem Update deinen eigenen Code nach** `mhm_rentiva`, `mhm_message_`, `save_post_mhm_payout` sowie den Werten in Anf\xfchrungszeichen `\'mhm_message\'`, `\'mhm_payout\'` und `\'mhm_vendor_app\'`.\\n\\n**Deine Shortcodes wurden bewusst nicht angetastet.** `rentiva_vendor_profile`, `rentiva_vendor_directory`, `rentiva_vendor_ledger`, `rentiva_transfer_search`, `rentiva_transfer_results`, `rentiva_popular_routes` und `rentiva_messages` behalten die Namen, die sie schon immer hatten, weil diese Namen im Inhalt deiner Seiten gespeichert sind. Eine Umbenennung h\xe4tte Live-Seiten geleert. Seiten, die damit erstellt wurden, brauchen keine Aufmerksamkeit.\\n\\n## Deine Daten werden automatisch \xfcbernommen\\n\\nZwanzig Einstellungen, vier Datenbanktabellen \u2013 das Provisionsjournal, die Provisionsrichtlinie, die Anbieterberichte und die Warteschlange f\xfcr Hintergrundaufgaben \u2013, zehn geplante Aufgaben und die benutzerdefinierten Felder der Pro-Inhaltstypen werden durch eine Migration auf die neuen Namen umgestellt. Sie l\xe4uft einmalig, sobald nach dem Update zum ersten Mal ein Administrator, WP-CLI oder eine geplante Aufgabe auf die Website zugreift. Nichts wird gel\xf6scht, und nichts muss neu eingegeben werden.\\n\\n## Aktualisiere zuerst das kostenlose Plugin\\n\\nPro hat schon immer angegeben, welche Version von MHM Rentiva es ben\xf6tigt. Bisher wurde das aber nie gepr\xfcft: Der einzige Test fragte, ob das kostenlose Plugin installiert ist, nie, ob es aktuell genug ist.\\n\\nJetzt wird es gepr\xfcft, und es wird **6.1.1 oder neuer** ben\xf6tigt. Darunter registriert Pro nichts, r\xfchrt keine Daten an und zeigt einen Hinweis mit beiden Versionen an \u2013 deshalb ist ein Update in der falschen Reihenfolge auch sicher statt zerst\xf6rerisch. Pro wartet einfach. In 5.2.3 f\xfchrte dieselbe Unstimmigkeit im Anbieter-Panel zu einem fatalen Fehler statt zu einer Meldung.\\n\\n## Sperrung bedeutet jetzt Sperrung\\n\\nHier lagen drei Fehler gleichzeitig vor, und zusammen sorgten sie daf\xfcr, dass ein gesperrter Anbieter weniger gesperrt war, als der Bildschirm behauptete.\\n\\nEin gesperrter Anbieter **behielt die M\xf6glichkeit, seine eigenen Fahrzeugeintr\xe4ge zu bearbeiten und zu l\xf6schen**. Die Sperrung entzieht die Anbieter-Rolle und setzt diese Eintr\xe4ge auf Entwurf, aber ein Berechtigungsfilter gab Bearbeitungs- und L\xf6schrechte f\xfcr jedes Fahrzeug zur\xfcck, dessen Autor der Aufrufende war. Einschlie\xdflich der Buchungshistorie. Der Teil dieses Filters, der Rechte gew\xe4hrt, fragt jetzt, ob der Anbieter aktiv ist; der Teil, der einschr\xe4nkt, bleibt genauso weit gefasst wie bisher.\\n\\nDie Sperrung war au\xdferdem **eine Einbahnstra\xdfe**. Sie funktionierte, aber jeder sp\xe4tere Versuch, sie aufzuheben, schlug mit \u201eAnbieter nicht gefunden\u201c fehl \u2013 dauerhaft \u2013, w\xe4hrend der Bildschirm den Anbieter weiterhin als gesperrt auflistete und weiterhin die Schaltfl\xe4che anbot. F\xfcnf Endpunkte fragten nach einer Rolle, die durch die Sperrung entfernt wird. Ein Betreiber konnte auch die Stadt oder den Provisionssatz eines gesperrten Anbieters nicht korrigieren.\\n\\nUnd die **ausstehende Anfrage eines gesperrten Anbieters zur \xc4nderung des Bankkontos verschwand** aus dem Tab des Betreibers und aus dessen Z\xe4hler, weil auch diese nach Rolle auflisteten. Eine Anfrage, die kurz vor einer Sperrung eingegangen ist, kann jetzt trotzdem bearbeitet werden.\\n\\nUnabh\xe4ngig davon \xfcbernahmen zwei \xe4ltere Formular-Handler eine Benutzer-ID direkt aus der Anfrage und schrieben den Anbieterstatus darauf \u2013 auf ein beliebiges Konto gerichtet, konnte man damit einen Fremden als gesperrten Anbieter markieren und alles, was er verfasst hatte, auf Entwurf setzen. Nichts im Plugin erzeugt die Tokens, die diese Handler verlangen, sodass sie in der Praxis nicht erreichbar waren, aber es handelte sich um denselben Vorgang hinter einer schw\xe4cheren Sperre als bei den tats\xe4chlich verwendeten Routen. Beide pr\xfcfen jetzt das Ziel und lehnen sichtbar ab.\\n\\n## F\xfcnf Admin-Seiten, die nicht funktionierten\\n\\nF\xfcnf Pro-Admin-Seiten lasen die Liste der REST-Endpunkte des kostenlosen Plugins, die die eigenen Endpunkte von Pro nicht beschreibt \u2013 daher wurde jede dieser Seiten geladen und schlug dann fehl. Pro liefert jetzt eine eigene Zuordnung mit, und eine Pr\xfcfung gleicht diese Zuordnung mit den tats\xe4chlich registrierten Routen ab. Zwei weitere Seiten, die bei fehlenden Daten leer blieben, statt einen Fehler anzuzeigen, sind jetzt abgesichert, sodass der Rest der Seite erhalten bleibt.\\n\\nAuch das Anbieter-Dashboard ist repariert: Ein Anbieter mit g\xfcltiger Lizenz wurde als Kunde erkannt, wodurch ihm Navigation und Panel fehlten, und die Finanzzahlen oben zeigten null an, statt aus dem Provisionsjournal zu lesen.\\n\\n## Du wirst jetzt informiert, wenn es ein neues Pro gibt\\n\\nPro wird \xfcber wpalemi.com vertrieben und nicht \xfcber das WordPress.org-Verzeichnis, daher hatte die WordPress-eigene Update-Pr\xfcfung nie etwas dazu zu sagen \u2013 und bisher wir auch nicht. Der Plugins-Bildschirm zeigt jetzt eine eigene Zeile von uns an, wenn eine neuere Version verf\xfcgbar ist. Sie wird nicht in den Update-Ablauf von WordPress eingebunden; sie informiert dich nur.\\n\\n## Au\xdferdem behoben\\n\\nEine Reihe kostenpflichtiger Funktionen hatte nicht mehr funktioniert, nachdem das kostenlose Plugin Code entfernt hatte, den Pro mitbenutzt hatte: der Kontextbereich f\xfcr Zusatzleistungen, der Bereich f\xfcr Fahrzeugzuverl\xe4ssigkeit und Strafen, die E-Mail-Texte f\xfcr Nachrichtenbenachrichtigungen, die verschobenen E-Mail-Vorlagen samt aller von dir gespeicherten \xdcberschreibungen, die Attributdefinitionen der kostenpflichtigen Shortcodes, das Premium-Stylesheet f\xfcr Transfer-Ergebnisse und die Anbieter-Rolle selbst.\\n\\nAu\xdferdem lud Pro seinen eigenen \xdcbersetzungskatalog nicht, sodass seine t\xfcrkische \xdcbersetzung nie erschien. Zusatzleistungen, die nur f\xfcr Transfers gedacht sind, wurden auf der Vermietungsseite angeboten. Die Berichtsseite schrieb eine \xfcbersetzte Bezeichnung in das Statusfeld einer Buchung. Und die Datenbankmigrationen laufen jetzt sowohl unter MySQL 8 als auch unter MariaDB.\\n\\n---\\n\\nDas vollst\xe4ndige \xc4nderungsprotokoll liegt dem Plugin in beiden Sprachen bei. Wenn du von 5.2.3 aktualisierst, ist alles oben Genannte in der Zwischenzeit passiert."},{"id":"rentiva-v6.1.3-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.1.3-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-08-29-rentiva-v6.1.3-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-08-29-rentiva-v6.1.3-release.md","title":"Rentiva 6.1.3 \u2014 Fahrzeuggalerien verschwinden nicht mehr","description":"Wenn die Felder f\xfcr deine Fahrzeugdetails vor 6.1.2 konfiguriert wurden, konnte das Hinzuf\xfcgen von Galeriebildern mit anschlie\xdfendem Klick auf \u201eAktualisieren\u201c die gerade hinzugef\xfcgte Galerie l\xf6schen. 6.1.3 behebt das, und du musst daf\xfcr nichts tun: keine Datenbank\xe4nderung, kein erneutes Speichern der Einstellungen. Die Installation gen\xfcgt.","date":"2026-08-29T00:40:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"vehicles","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vehicles"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"}],"readingTime":2.75,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v6.1.3-release","title":"Rentiva 6.1.3 \u2014 Fahrzeuggalerien verschwinden nicht mehr","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","vehicles","security"],"date":"2026-08-29T00:40"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva Pro 6.0.0 \u2014 Alles ist einheitlich benannt, und Sperrung bedeutet endlich Sperrung","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-pro-v6.0.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.1.0 \u2014 Die Stornierung einer bezahlten Buchung erstattet jetzt das Geld","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.1.0-release"}},"content":"Wenn die Felder f\xfcr deine Fahrzeugdetails vor 6.1.2 konfiguriert wurden, konnte das Hinzuf\xfcgen von Galeriebildern mit anschlie\xdfendem Klick auf \u201eAktualisieren\u201c die gerade hinzugef\xfcgte Galerie l\xf6schen. 6.1.3 behebt das, und du musst daf\xfcr nichts tun: keine Datenbank\xe4nderung, kein erneutes Speichern der Einstellungen. Die Installation gen\xfcgt.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Die Galerie verschwindet nicht mehr\\n\\nZwei Felder, die nie echte Felder waren \u2013 ein leeres **Bild** und ein leeres **Galeriebilder** \u2013, standen auf jedem Fahrzeugbildschirm im Raster der Fahrzeugdetails. Sie wirkten rein kosmetisch. Das waren sie nicht: Das zweite trug denselben Formularfeldnamen wie die Galerie selbst, und wenn zwei Felder auf einer Seite denselben Namen haben, sendet der Browser beide, und das letzte gewinnt. Das leere Feld kam zuletzt, sodass \u201eAktualisieren\u201c die gerade hochgeladene Galerie mit nichts \xfcberschrieb.\\n\\n6.1.2 hat verhindert, dass neue Websites jemals in diesen Zustand geraten, aber nichts f\xfcr Websites getan, die sich bereits darin befanden \u2013 und das sind die meisten Websites, die ihre Fahrzeugeinstellungen mindestens einmal gespeichert hatten. Warum das Problem bestehen blieb, ist einen Satz wert: Der Code, der festlegt, welche Felder existieren, erfand f\xfcr jeden Namen, den er nicht kannte, eine Bezeichnung, und eine erfundene Bezeichnung lie\xdf einen unbekannten Namen f\xfcr jede nachfolgende Pr\xfcfung wie ein echtes Feld aussehen. Jetzt verwirft er, was er nicht kennt.\\n\\nWenn deine Website betroffen ist, ist das Update also die komplette L\xf6sung. Der \xfcbrig gebliebene Eintrag bleibt in deinen Einstellungen und wird ab sofort einfach ignoriert.\\n\\n**Eine Sache solltest du wissen.** Wenn du unter *Namen bearbeiten* den Namen eines benutzerdefinierten Details leerst, verschwindet dieses Detail jetzt aus dem Raster, statt unter einem aus seinem internen Schl\xfcssel generierten Namen angezeigt zu werden. Nichts wird gel\xf6scht \u2013 sobald du wieder einen Namen eingibst, ist es sofort zur\xfcck \u2013, und die \xf6ffentliche Seite deiner Website hat ein solches Feld bereits ausgeblendet, sodass beide jetzt \xfcbereinstimmen.\\n\\n## Das Speichern einer normalen Seite schreibt keine Buchungsdaten mehr darauf\\n\\nEin Handler, der Buchungsinformationen speichert, reagierte auf jeden Speichervorgang auf der Website statt nur auf Buchungen. Das Speichern einer nicht zugeh\xf6rigen Seite oder eines Beitrags konnte daher einen Buchungsstatus darauf schreiben. Niemand konnte auf Daten zugreifen, auf die er keinen Zugriff haben durfte \u2013 die vorhandene Pr\xfcfung fragte weiterhin, ob du diese Seite bearbeiten darfst \u2013, aber das Plugin schrieb seine eigenen Felder auf Objekte, die es nichts angingen.\\n\\nF\xfcnfzehn Handler f\xfcr Fahrzeuge und Buchungen pr\xfcfen jetzt vor dem Schreiben, in welche Art von Beitrag sie schreiben. Einer davon war ein aktiver Pfad, der Daten zur Fahrzeugsortierung an jeden Beitrag anh\xe4ngen konnte, auf den er gerichtet wurde.\\n\\n## Ein Admin-Bildschirm, der fehlschl\xe4gt, sagt das jetzt auch\\n\\nWenn die Daten eines Bildschirms nicht geladen werden konnten, zeigten manche Bildschirme eine kurze Meldung \u201eEtwas ist schiefgelaufen, bitte aktualisieren\u201c, w\xe4hrend andere einfach leer blieben \u2013 eine wei\xdfe Fl\xe4che unter dem WordPress-Men\xfc ohne jede Erkl\xe4rung. Jetzt zeigt jeder Bildschirm die Meldung an, und eine Pr\xfcfung verhindert, dass neue Bildschirme ohne sie ausgeliefert werden.\\n\\n## Unter der Haube\\n\\nGemeinsam genutzte Admin-Bausteine werden jetzt aus einem gemeinsamen Paket geladen, statt als Kopien innerhalb von Rentiva vorgehalten zu werden, und doppelte Stildeklarationen wurden zusammengef\xfchrt. Das wurde mit einem Vorher-Nachher-Vergleich im hellen und im dunklen Modus \xfcberpr\xfcft: Auf deiner Website wird nichts anders dargestellt.\\n\\n---\\n\\n6.1.1 und 6.1.2 wurden nie im WordPress.org-Verzeichnis ver\xf6ffentlicht; alles, was sie behoben haben, ist hier enthalten. Der vollst\xe4ndige Verlauf in beiden Sprachen wird mit dem Plugin ausgeliefert."},{"id":"rentiva-v6.1.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.1.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-08-24-rentiva-v6.1.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-08-24-rentiva-v6.1.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva 6.1.0 \u2014 Die Stornierung einer bezahlten Buchung erstattet jetzt das Geld","description":"Wenn ein Kunde bezahlt und dann storniert hatte, markierte Rentiva die Buchung als \u201ewartet auf Erstattung\u201c und h\xf6rte dort auf. Es floss kein Geld. Jemand musste es bemerken und die Erstattung von Hand vornehmen. Ab 6.1.0 f\xfchrt die Stornierung die Erstattung selbst bis zu deinem Zahlungs-Gateway durch.","date":"2026-08-24T20:30:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"refunds","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/refunds"},{"inline":true,"label":"woocommerce","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/woocommerce"}],"readingTime":4.89,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v6.1.0-release","title":"Rentiva 6.1.0 \u2014 Die Stornierung einer bezahlten Buchung erstattet jetzt das Geld","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","refunds","woocommerce"],"date":"2026-08-24T20:30"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.1.3 \u2014 Fahrzeuggalerien verschwinden nicht mehr","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.1.3-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.0.7 \u2014 MHM Rentiva ist jetzt im Plugin-Verzeichnis von WordPress.org","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.0.7-release"}},"content":"Wenn ein Kunde bezahlt und dann storniert hatte, markierte Rentiva die Buchung als \u201ewartet auf Erstattung\u201c und h\xf6rte dort auf. Es floss kein Geld. Jemand musste es bemerken und die Erstattung von Hand vornehmen. Ab 6.1.0 f\xfchrt die Stornierung die Erstattung selbst bis zu deinem Zahlungs-Gateway durch.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Die Erstattung findet jetzt tats\xe4chlich statt\\n\\nDas gilt f\xfcr beide Wege, auf denen eine Buchung storniert wird: wenn der Kunde seine eigene Buchung storniert und wenn du sie \xfcber die Anzahlungsseite stornierst. Beide f\xfchren die Erstattung jetzt bis zum Ende durch.\\n\\nWo das Gateway das Geld zur\xfcckgeben kann, tut es das automatisch. Wo es das nicht kann \u2013 bei einer Offline-Zahlung oder einem Gateway, das keine Erstattungen unterst\xfctzt \u2013, wird die Buchung als **manuelle Auszahlung ausstehend** erfasst, und der Kunde erf\xe4hrt, dass eine Person ihm das Geld manuell auszahlt, statt dass ihm eine automatische R\xfcckzahlung versprochen wird, die nicht kommt. Welcher der beiden F\xe4lle eingetreten ist, wird an der Buchung vermerkt und in der E-Mail genannt, die der Kunde erh\xe4lt.\\n\\nEin Kunde, der vor Ablauf der Stornierungsfrist storniert, erh\xe4lt jetzt automatisch den gesamten erstattungsf\xe4higen Betrag zur\xfcck, ohne dass du zwischendurch etwas tun musst. Rentiva legt keine Stornierungsgeb\xfchr fest, daher ist eine vollst\xe4ndige Erstattung die einzige Regel, die es anwenden kann.\\n\\n## Mehrere Ursachen f\xfcr unzuverl\xe4ssige Erstattungen\\n\\nBeim Beheben des oben beschriebenen Ablaufs kamen eine Reihe verwandter Fehler zum Vorschein. Alle sind in 6.1.0 behoben:\\n\\n- **Die Erstattung einer bezahlten Bestellung schlug fehl.** Die Erstattungsseite lehnte jede Bestellung ab, die tats\xe4chlich bezahlt worden war. Sie pr\xfcfte, ob WooCommerce die Bestellung noch als bearbeitbar betrachtete \u2013 was nur zutrifft, solange eine Bestellung ausstehend, in Wartestellung oder ein Entwurf ist \u2013, statt zu pr\xfcfen, ob das Gateway das Geld zur\xfccksenden kann.\\n- **Die zweite Bestellung einer Buchung mit Anzahlung war f\xfcr Erstattungen unsichtbar.** Wenn eine Buchung in zwei Teilen bezahlt wurde, wurde die Bestellung f\xfcr die Restzahlung gar nicht gefunden, sodass nur die Anzahlung zur\xfcckkam.\\n- **Eine Erstattung wurde doppelt gez\xe4hlt.** Eine einzelne Erstattung durchlief zwei getrennte Schritte zum Erfassen und Benachrichtigen, sodass der erstattete Gesamtbetrag der Buchung verdoppelt wurde und der Kunde zwei E-Mails dazu erhielt.\\n- **Die Erstattungsbenachrichtigung erreichte den Kunden nicht immer.** Sie las ein E-Mail-Feld aus, das vom Kontaktformular bef\xfcllt wird, von Buchungen aber nicht. War dieses Feld leer, wurde die Benachrichtigung stillschweigend \xfcbersprungen. Jetzt sucht sie dort, wo auch der Rest des Plugins sucht: in der Kunden-E-Mail der Buchung selbst, dann in der WooCommerce-Rechnungsadresse, dann im verkn\xfcpften Konto.\\n- **Eine Erstattung, die kein Gateway ausgef\xfchrt hatte, wurde als abgeschlossen erfasst.** Sie wird jetzt als \u201emanuelle Auszahlung ausstehend\u201c erfasst, denn das Geld ist erst geflossen, wenn jemand es auszahlt.\\n- **Bei einer Erstattung teils per Karte, teils in bar wurdest du aufgefordert, den gesamten Betrag manuell auszuzahlen.** Die beiden Betr\xe4ge werden jetzt getrennt genannt: was das Gateway bereits zur\xfcckgegeben hat und was noch manuell ausgezahlt werden muss.\\n- **Die Stornierung einer Bestellung bei einer zweiteiligen Buchung beeintr\xe4chtigte die andere.** Die Stornierung der unbezahlten Bestellung f\xfcr die Restzahlung stornierte oder herabstufte bisher die gesamte Buchung, obwohl die Anzahlungsbestellung bezahlt worden war \u2013 ohne irgendeine Erstattung. Die bezahlte Bestellung bleibt jetzt unangetastet, die Verkn\xfcpfung zur stornierten Bestellung wird entfernt, damit du einen neuen Zahlungslink f\xfcr den noch offenen Betrag erstellen kannst, und du wirst benachrichtigt.\\n- **Manuell erstellte Buchungen hatten \xfcberhaupt keine Zahlungsart**, wodurch sie in der Buchungsliste und deren Filter ohne Bezeichnung blieben, vom Erstattungsablauf abgelehnt wurden und in Berichten nach Zahlungsart in einer leeren Gruppe landeten. Sie werden jetzt als Offline-Zahlungen erfasst.\\n- **Die Erstattungsbox auf der Buchungsseite zeigt ihr Formular f\xfcr Offline-Buchungen mit offenem Betrag an** \u2013 zum ersten Mal. Die Box war immer vorhanden; statt des Formulars gab sie \u201eKeine erstattungsf\xe4hige Zahlung f\xfcr diese Buchung gefunden\u201c aus, weil das Formular einen Wert ben\xf6tigte, den nie etwas geschrieben hat.\\n\\nZwei Erstattungen, die im selben Moment f\xfcr dieselbe Buchung gestartet werden \u2013 eine Stornierung und eine, die du im Admin-Bereich gestartet hast \u2013, k\xf6nnen nicht mehr gleichzeitig laufen.\\n\\n## Die Betragsumrechnung richtet sich jetzt nach den Dezimalstellen deines Shops\\n\\nRentiva rechnet zwischen deiner W\xe4hrung und ihrer kleinsten Einheit um. Bisher ging es davon aus, dass diese Einheit immer ein Hundertstel ist. Jetzt liest es die Einstellung deines Shops aus: **WooCommerce \u2192 Einstellungen \u2192 Allgemein \u2192 W\xe4hrungsoptionen \u2192 Anzahl der Dezimalstellen**.\\n\\n**Wenn dein Shop die Standardeinstellung von zwei Dezimalstellen verwendet, \xe4ndert sich f\xfcr dich nichts.**\\n\\nWenn dein Shop auf eine andere Anzahl von Dezimalstellen eingestellt ist, lies dies vor dem Update: Erstattungs- und Zahlungsbetr\xe4ge, die Rentiva *vor* dieser Version erfasst hat, werden im neuen Ma\xdfstab neu gelesen statt umgerechnet. F\xfcr bestehende Datens\xe4tze gibt es keinen Migrationsschritt, und es ist auch keiner geplant. Betroffen sind W\xe4hrungen ohne Untereinheiten \u2013 zum Beispiel der japanische Yen mit null Dezimalstellen.\\n\\n## Anzahlungen au\xdferhalb von WooCommerce\\n\\nWenn die Anzahlung einer Buchung au\xdferhalb von WooCommerce entgegengenommen wurde, bietet Rentiva f\xfcr den Restbetrag keinen WooCommerce-Zahlungslink mehr an.\\n\\nBei einer manuell erstellten Buchung, die nie eine WooCommerce-Bestellung hatte, schlug dieser Link ohnehin immer fehl. Bei einer Buchung, die \xfcber den WooCommerce-Checkout begann und deren Anzahlung sp\xe4ter als offline erhalten markiert wurde, funktionierte der Link \u2013 und genau das war der Fehler: Beim Abschlie\xdfen wurde eine WooCommerce-Bestellung erstellt, die die zuvor offline erhaltene Anzahlung stillschweigend aus dem erfassten bezahlten Betrag der Buchung l\xf6schte.\\n\\nDie Anzahlungsseite erkl\xe4rt jetzt die Situation, statt einen Button anzubieten, durch den Geld verloren ginge. **Restbetrag verarbeiten**, womit der Restbetrag ohne WooCommerce als beglichen erfasst wird, ist nicht betroffen und funktioniert weiterhin.\\n\\n## Seiten\\n\\nDie Fahrzeugliste wurde neu aufgebaut und bietet Listen-, Karten- und Kalenderansicht. Es gibt einen neuen monatlichen Belegungskalender f\xfcr die Flotte, der den Monat jedes Fahrzeugs auf einen Blick zeigt. Die Seite f\xfcr Zusatzleistungen ist neu.\\n\\n## Aktualisierung\\n\\nRentiva ist im Plugin-Verzeichnis von WordPress.org verf\xfcgbar, daher erscheint das Update auf deiner Plugins-Seite nach dem Zeitplan von WordPress selbst \u2013 in der Regel innerhalb eines halben Tages. Du kannst auch sofort unter **Dashboard \u2192 Aktualisierungen** danach suchen.\\n\\nGetestet bis WordPress 7.1. Erfordert WordPress 6.7 und PHP 8.1."},{"id":"rentiva-v6.0.7-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.0.7-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md","title":"Rentiva 6.0.7 \u2014 MHM Rentiva ist jetzt im Plugin-Verzeichnis von WordPress.org","description":"MHM Rentiva ist jetzt im Plugin-Verzeichnis von WordPress.org ver\xf6ffentlicht. Du installierst es so wie alles andere \u2013 danach suchen, auf Installieren klicken \u2013 und WordPress h\xe4lt es von da an aktuell.","date":"2026-08-23T14:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"},{"inline":true,"label":"wordpress-org","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/wordpress-org"}],"readingTime":3.75,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v6.0.7-release","title":"Rentiva 6.0.7 \u2014 MHM Rentiva ist jetzt im Plugin-Verzeichnis von WordPress.org","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","security","wordpress-org"],"date":"2026-08-23T14:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.1.0 \u2014 Die Stornierung einer bezahlten Buchung erstattet jetzt das Geld","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.1.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.2.4 \u2014 The menu moves down, and every link out of your site is now written down","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.2.4-release"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva ist jetzt im Plugin-Verzeichnis von WordPress.org ver\xf6ffentlicht. Du installierst es so wie alles andere \u2013 danach suchen, auf Installieren klicken \u2013 und WordPress h\xe4lt es von da an aktuell.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Die Installation hat sich ge\xe4ndert, und sie ist einfacher\\n\\nBis heute hast du das Plugin als ZIP-Datei erhalten, die du bei jedem Update empfangen, hochladen und erneut hochladen musstest. Das ist nicht mehr der Weg:\\n\\n1. Gehe in deinem WordPress-Adminbereich zu **Plugins > Neu hinzuf\xfcgen**.\\n2. Suche nach **MHM Rentiva**.\\n3. Klicke auf **Jetzt installieren** und dann auf **Aktivieren**.\\n\\nDer Eintrag befindet sich unter [wordpress.org/plugins/mhm-rentiva](https://wordpress.org/plugins/mhm-rentiva/). Ab jetzt kommen Updates auf demselben Weg wie die Updates aller anderen Plugins aus dem Verzeichnis \u2013 WordPress pr\xfcft nach seinem eigenen Zeitplan und bietet dir die neue Version auf deiner Plugins-Seite an. Nichts muss von Hand heruntergeladen werden.\\n\\nDas Hochladen einer ZIP-Datei funktioniert weiterhin und bleibt der Weg, um einen **bestimmten** Build statt des aktuellen Release zu installieren \u2013 zum Beispiel eine Version von der [GitHub-Releases-Seite](https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva/releases). Die [Installationsanleitung](/docs/getting-started/installation) beschreibt jetzt alle drei Wege.\\n\\nWooCommerce ist weiterhin erforderlich und wird bei der Aktivierung des Plugins gepr\xfcft.\\n\\n## Was ist in 6.0.7 enthalten\\n\\nDie Pr\xfcfung des Plugins durch WordPress.org hat ein Problem gefunden, und 6.0.7 ist die Behebung daf\xfcr.\\n\\nEine Methode zur Stapelaktualisierung von Kunden im Hilfsmodul f\xfcr die Kundenleistung schrieb WordPress-Benutzerkonten allein hinter der pauschalen Berechtigung `edit_users` \u2013 ohne zu pr\xfcfen, ob der Aufrufer *genau dieses* Konto bearbeiten darf oder ob es sich um ein Konto handelt, das dieses Plugin verwaltet. Sie wurde nirgends aufgerufen, weder in diesem Release noch in einem fr\xfcheren, und es gab keine Seite und keine Adresse, \xfcber die sie erreichbar gewesen w\xe4re.\\n\\nSie wurde entfernt statt repariert, denn unerreichbarer Code, der Benutzerkonten schreibt, sollte \xfcberhaupt nicht ausgeliefert werden. Die beiden Stellen, die tats\xe4chlich einen bestehenden Kunden bearbeiten \u2013 die Seite zum Bearbeiten von Kunden und die L\xf6sch-Route \u2013, haben diese Frage pro Konto bereits direkt beim Schreiben gestellt und tun das weiterhin. Das Hinzuf\xfcgen eines Kunden ist ein anderer Fall: Dabei wird das Konto erst erstellt, es gibt also kein bestehendes Konto, auf das sich eine solche Frage beziehen k\xf6nnte, und es ist an die Berechtigung gebunden, die WordPress selbst zum Erstellen eines Benutzers verlangt.\\n\\n## Du kommst von 5.x? Lies das vor dem Update\\n\\nDas letzte Release, \xfcber das hier geschrieben wurde, war 5.2.4. Zwischen ihm und heute liegt **6.0.0**, ein Major-Release mit Breaking Changes \u2013 und zwar der stillen Art. Wenn du eigenen Code hast, der sich in dieses Plugin einh\xe4ngt, wird er nach dem Update einfach nicht mehr ausgef\xfchrt: keine Fehlermeldung, nichts im Log, die Anpassung findet einfach still und leise nicht mehr statt.\\n\\n**113 Hooks wurden umbenannt.** Um deinen eigenen Code umzustellen, wende diese zwei Schritte in der angegebenen Reihenfolge an, denn die Reihenfolge ist entscheidend:\\n\\n1. Ersetze in den \xe4lteren Namen im Schr\xe4gstrich-Stil jedes `/` durch `_`: `mhm_rentiva/testimonials/limit` wird zu `mhm_rentiva_testimonials_limit`.\\n2. Ersetze dann das Pr\xe4fix `mhm_rentiva_` durch `mhmrentiva_`: Dieser Name lautet am Ende `mhmrentiva_testimonials_limit`.\\n\\nWenn du Schritt 2 zuerst ausf\xfchrst, entstehen Namen, die nicht existieren. Zwei Hooks verwendeten ein reines `mhm_`-Pr\xe4fix und folgen demselben Prinzip: `mhm_message_created` und `mhm_message_status_changed` werden zu `mhmrentiva_message_created` und `mhmrentiva_message_status_changed`.\\n\\n**Auch die Beitragstypen und Taxonomien wurden umbenannt**, wodurch sich die daraus gebildeten WordPress-Core-Hooks \xe4ndern \u2013 das ist der Teil, der am leichtesten \xfcbersehen wird, weil es nicht unsere Hook-Namen sind. `save_post_vehicle` hei\xdft jetzt `save_post_mhmrentiva_vehicle`, und dasselbe gilt f\xfcr `add_meta_boxes_*` und f\xfcr die Paare `manage_*_posts_columns` / `manage_*_posts_custom_column`. Die Umbenennungen sind:\\n\\n| Alt | Neu |\\n| :-- | :-- |\\n| `vehicle` | `mhmrentiva_vehicle` |\\n| `vehicle_booking` | `mhmrentiva_booking` |\\n| `vehicle_addon` | `mhmrentiva_addon` |\\n| `mhm_app_log` | `mhmrentiva_app_log` |\\n| `mhm_email_log` | `mhmrentiva_email_log` |\\n| `mhm_contact_message` | `mhmrentiva_contact` |\\n| `vehicle_category` | `mhmrentiva_vehicle_category` |\\n| `addon_category` | `mhmrentiva_addon_category` |\\n\\nDieselbe Umbenennung betrifft jede Abfrage, die du von Hand geschrieben hast. Eine `WP_Query` mit `\'post_type\' => \'vehicle\'`, ein `pre_get_posts`-Handler, der darauf pr\xfcft, ein `get_posts`-Aufruf, ein eigener Shortcode \u2013 all das findet jetzt stillschweigend nichts mehr, weil nach einem Beitragstyp gefragt wird, der unter diesem Namen nicht mehr existiert.\\n\\n**Wonach du deinen eigenen Code vor dem Update durchsuchen solltest:** `mhm_rentiva`, `mhm_message_`, `save_post_vehicle` sowie die in Anf\xfchrungszeichen stehenden Literale `\'vehicle\'`, `\'vehicle_booking\'`, `\'vehicle_addon\'` und `\'vehicle_category\'`.\\n\\nDeine gespeicherten Daten werden durch eine Migration auf die neuen Namen \xfcbertragen, die einmalig und automatisch ausgef\xfchrt wird, wenn du nach dem Update zum ersten Mal den Adminbereich l\xe4dst. Nichts wird gel\xf6scht und nichts muss erneut eingegeben werden. Wenn du auch das kostenpflichtige Add-on verwendest, aktualisiere beide gleichzeitig: Diese Version verweigert die Migration unter einem \xe4lteren Add-on, statt deine Daten nur halb \xfcbertragen zur\xfcckzulassen."},{"id":"rentiva-v5.2.4-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.2.4-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-29-rentiva-v5.2.4-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-29-rentiva-v5.2.4-release.md","title":"Rentiva v5.2.4 \u2014 The menu moves down, and every link out of your site is now written down","description":"A small release with a simple theme: fitting into WordPress rather than competing with it.","date":"2026-07-29T06:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"privacy","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/privacy"},{"inline":true,"label":"admin","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/admin"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"}],"readingTime":2.2,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v5.2.4-release","title":"Rentiva v5.2.4 \u2014 The menu moves down, and every link out of your site is now written down","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","privacy","admin","patch"],"date":"2026-07-29T06:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva 6.0.7 \u2014 MHM Rentiva ist jetzt im Plugin-Verzeichnis von WordPress.org","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v6.0.7-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.2.3 / Pro v5.2.3 \u2014 A table WordPress was never really looking at, and a privacy notice that named the wrong things","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.2.3-release"}},"content":"A small release with a simple theme: fitting into WordPress rather than competing with it.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## The menu is lower now\\n\\nMHM Rentiva registered its top-level admin menu at position 58, which put it directly above **Appearance** \u2014 ahead of most of WordPress\'s own items. That is a prominent spot, and on a site running several plugins it is exactly how the admin sidebar turns into a scramble.\\n\\nIt now sits at 76: still top-level, but below Appearance, Plugins, Users and Tools, immediately above Settings. Nothing else changed \u2014 the same screens are underneath it in the same order.\\n\\nIf you navigate by muscle memory, this is the one thing you will notice.\\n\\n## Every outbound link, written down\\n\\nThe readme said the plugin uses no external services. That is true in the sense that matters \u2014 it makes no HTTP request to anyone, sends nothing about your site or your customers anywhere, and loads every asset including its webfont from your own server.\\n\\nBut the admin screens do contain ordinary hyperlinks, and a reader checking the claim would find them and reasonably wonder. So the \\"External services\\" section now lists them: the documentation site, the issue tracker, wpalemi.com with its terms and privacy pages, this plugin\'s WordPress.org support forum, the two SMTP plugin pages the setup wizard suggests, and a YouTube channel. They open only if you click them, and they send nothing when you do.\\n\\n## A sentence we had to take back\\n\\nThe same section previously said that a check in our build \\"fails if a request to any third-party host is introduced.\\"\\n\\nThat was not true, and the file it referred to says so itself, in a comment we wrote: *\\"this gate cannot catch a NEW third-party host nobody has thought of. It is a regression fence, not a discovery tool.\\"* It is a list of sixteen specific hosts \u2014 the geolocation, CDN, analytics and Gravatar services earlier versions used \u2014 and it scans PHP only. We confirmed the gap by testing it: a request to one of those sixteen fails the build, a request to a host nobody listed passes.\\n\\nSo the readme now describes the check as what it is. The underlying claim \u2014 that the plugin makes no third-party request \u2014 still holds and was verified by sweeping the shipped code, not by trusting the gate.\\n\\nWe are writing this down publicly because it is the third time in two releases that a sentence of ours turned out to be an assumption rather than a measurement, and the pattern was identical each time: reading a thing\'s name instead of reading what it does.\\n\\n## Upgrading\\n\\nNothing to do."},{"id":"rentiva-v5.2.3-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.2.3-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-29-rentiva-v5.2.3-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-29-rentiva-v5.2.3-release.md","title":"Rentiva v5.2.3 / Pro v5.2.3 \u2014 A table WordPress was never really looking at, and a privacy notice that named the wrong things","description":"Another patch on the way to the WordPress.org submission, and another release where the interesting part is not the bug we fixed but what we found while checking whether we had described it honestly.","date":"2026-07-29T04:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"pro","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/pro"},{"inline":true,"label":"privacy","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/privacy"},{"inline":true,"label":"database","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/database"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"}],"readingTime":4.7,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v5.2.3-release","title":"Rentiva v5.2.3 / Pro v5.2.3 \u2014 A table WordPress was never really looking at, and a privacy notice that named the wrong things","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","pro","privacy","database","patch"],"date":"2026-07-29T04:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.2.4 \u2014 The menu moves down, and every link out of your site is now written down","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.2.4-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.2.2 / Pro v5.2.2 \u2014 What we tell WooCommerce, and one thing we were telling it wrong","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.2.2-release"}},"content":"Another patch on the way to the WordPress.org submission, and another release where the interesting part is not the bug we fixed but what we found while checking whether we had described it honestly.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## The table update that could never have landed\\n\\nWordPress has a function, `dbDelta()`, that takes a `CREATE TABLE` statement and works out the difference between it and the table you already have \u2014 adding columns you have introduced since the last release, without touching the data already in them. It is how a plugin evolves its own schema safely.\\n\\nIt does not execute the statement. It *parses* it. And the way it finds the table\'s name is to take the first thing after the words `CREATE TABLE`.\\n\\nOur background-job table was created with `CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS`. So `dbDelta()` had been tracking, for as long as that table has existed, a table called **`IF`**.\\n\\nThe table itself was fine \u2014 the database executed the raw statement correctly and always had. Nothing was lost, and nothing is wrong on your site today. But `dbDelta()` runs `DESCRIBE` against the name it parsed, `DESCRIBE IF` fails, and a table it cannot describe is skipped entirely. Any column we added to that table in a future release would have been silently ignored: no error, no warning, `dbDelta()` reporting success while doing nothing.\\n\\nWe measured it rather than reasoning about it. Adding a column to the schema and re-running the migration before the fix: the column was not created. After the fix: it was.\\n\\nThe same defect was in two more `CREATE TABLE` statements in the paid add-on. One of them \u2014 the reports background-job table \u2014 is created on activation and genuinely had the problem. The other belongs to a monitoring subsystem that nothing currently starts; we fixed it anyway so both read the same way, and we would rather say that plainly than let a changelog imply we repaired something that was never running.\\n\\n## The privacy notice, rewritten because it was wrong\\n\\nThe readme\'s Privacy section is the part of a plugin page that a site owner copies into their own privacy policy. Ours said that every booking record stores the visitor\'s IP address and browser user-agent.\\n\\nThat turned out to be almost exactly backwards.\\n\\nThe code that writes an IP onto a booking sits behind an endpoint that **nothing in the plugin posts to**. The real booking flow \u2014 the form, the cart, WooCommerce checkout \u2014 records no IP at all. So the one store we disclosed was the one that, in practice, barely exists.\\n\\nMeanwhile three that do exist were not mentioned:\\n\\n- **The contact form.** Every submission is kept with the sender\'s name, e-mail, telephone, company, the message, a link to any file they attached, and the IP and user-agent it came from. There is no retention setting on these records and nothing ever deletes them. The attached file goes to your ordinary uploads folder, reachable by anyone with the URL, and stays there even if you delete the message.\\n- **The rating form.** Reviews are stored as ordinary WordPress comments, so WordPress itself records the reviewer\'s IP and user-agent \u2014 as it does for any comment. Guest reviews are reachable through **Tools \u2192 Erase Personal Data**, which matches comments by e-mail address. A review left by a logged-in customer is saved against their user ID with no e-mail on the comment, so those tools will not find it; you have to delete it from the Comments screen.\\n- **The e-mail log.** Alongside the recipient and subject, it keeps the booking details each message was built from \u2014 customer name, contact details, rental dates. Not the assembled message body. It has its own retention setting, 30 days by default.\\n\\nThe activity log, which we had described correctly, keeps IP, user-agent and user ID per entry on a configurable retention, also 30 days by default.\\n\\n**Nothing about what the plugin stores has changed in this release.** What changed is that the description of it is now true. If you have a privacy policy that was written from our old text, it is worth re-reading it against the new section.\\n\\n## How we found it, which is the part worth writing down\\n\\nNone of this came out of the fix. It came out of putting the fix in front of an independent model and asking it to disprove our own description, five times over. Each round found something in the text we had *just written* to correct the previous round: a list read as a delete-list when it was a keep-list; a test\'s normalised key names mistaken for the real ones; a count of ten where the code has a hundred and sixty-one.\\n\\nThe pattern in every one of them was the same \u2014 assuming what something meant instead of reading it. That is worth naming publicly, because it is the failure mode that produces confident, well-written documentation that happens to be false, and a privacy notice is exactly the kind of document where that does real harm.\\n\\nThe same rounds turned up a scratch file that had been shipping inside our release ZIPs since 5.2.1. The build now holds an allow-list of what may sit in the archive root and refuses to build otherwise, because the exclusion list we had could only ever catch the files somebody had thought of.\\n\\n## Upgrading\\n\\nNothing to do. There is no pending column for the corrected table, so nothing changes on your site on update; the fix is what makes the next schema change actually apply. Pro 5.2.3 ships alongside and requires Lite 5.2.3."},{"id":"rentiva-v5.2.2-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.2.2-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-28-rentiva-v5.2.2-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-28-rentiva-v5.2.2-release.md","title":"Rentiva v5.2.2 / Pro v5.2.2 \u2014 What we tell WooCommerce, and one thing we were telling it wrong","description":"A patch release with one uncomfortable admission in it. Preparing for the WordPress.org submission, we ran our WooCommerce control checklist against the whole codebase for the first time \u2014 and found that we had never answered WooCommerce\'s compatibility questions at all.","date":"2026-07-28T20:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"pro","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/pro"},{"inline":true,"label":"woocommerce","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/woocommerce"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"}],"readingTime":3.05,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v5.2.2-release","title":"Rentiva v5.2.2 / Pro v5.2.2 \u2014 What we tell WooCommerce, and one thing we were telling it wrong","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","pro","woocommerce","patch"],"date":"2026-07-28T20:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.2.3 / Pro v5.2.3 \u2014 A table WordPress was never really looking at, and a privacy notice that named the wrong things","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.2.3-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.2.1 / Pro v5.2.1 \u2014 A chart that says what it counts, and translations that ship","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.2.1-release"}},"content":"A patch release with one uncomfortable admission in it. Preparing for the WordPress.org submission, we ran our WooCommerce control checklist against the whole codebase for the first time \u2014 and found that we had never answered WooCommerce\'s compatibility questions at all.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What we were not saying\\n\\nWooCommerce asks every plugin that touches orders to declare which of its newer features it works with. A plugin that says nothing is filed as *uncertain*, and the site owner is warned **by name** when they try to switch on High-Performance Order Storage \u2014 which has been the default for new stores since WooCommerce 8.2.\\n\\nWe had never declared anything. Not \\"incompatible\\" \u2014 nothing at all.\\n\\n## HPOS: compatible, and measured before saying so\\n\\nA compatibility declaration is a promise, and a false one is worse than silence: people enable HPOS on the strength of it and lose data quietly. So we checked rather than assumed. Every order this plugin touches is read through `wc_get_order()`; there is no post-meta access keyed to an order id; nothing queries `wp_posts` or `shop_order` for orders; no order is created or updated with `wp_insert_post()`.\\n\\nThat is now declared, in both the free plugin and the paid add-on.\\n\\n## Block cart and checkout: not compatible, and we say so\\n\\nThis is the part worth reading if you run a store.\\n\\nWe could have stayed quiet. Instead we checked what actually happens on a block-based checkout, and declared **incompatible**, because that is the truth:\\n\\n- The payment-type selector, the custom tax row and the return-to-cart link never render \u2014 they are printed from classic-checkout hooks the block checkout does not run.\\n- **The availability check does not run.** `woocommerce_checkout_process` is where we verify that the vehicle is still free for the requested dates. On a block checkout that hook never fires, which leaves a window where two customers can book the same vehicle for the same dates.\\n\\n**If your store uses the block checkout, switch to the classic checkout while using this plugin.** Making the block checkout genuinely supported means rebuilding those surfaces on the Additional Checkout Fields API and a Store API integration \u2014 a feature, not a flag, and one we would rather do properly than claim.\\n\\n## One value was being stored where HPOS cannot read it\\n\\nThe payment type chosen at checkout was written with `update_post_meta( $order_id, \u2026 )`. Under HPOS an order is not a post, so that writes a row keyed to something that is not the order.\\n\\nIt now goes through WooCommerce\'s own order object. On a store that has not switched to HPOS, that object writes to post meta anyway \u2014 so the value stays exactly where it has always been. Nothing is moved and nothing needs migrating.\\n\\n## The admission\\n\\nThe independent audit we run before every release build caught a claim inside this very change that a search disproves. Our first draft of the add-on\'s explanation said it \\"registers no checkout hooks and prints nothing into cart or checkout\\". It does both \u2014 four hooks, in two files.\\n\\nThe audit also did the work we had skipped: it read WooCommerce\'s own source and established that the Store API *does* run two of those hooks, so most of that surface survives a block checkout, and only the cart line-item name is classic-only and cosmetic. That mixture is neither \\"compatible\\" nor \\"incompatible\\", so the add-on declares neither and explains why.\\n\\nWe are writing this down because the correction is the useful part. A release note that only lists what went right teaches nobody anything, least of all us.\\n\\n## Upgrading\\n\\nNothing to do. Update both plugins together if you use the paid add-on."},{"id":"rentiva-v5.2.1-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.2.1-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-28-rentiva-v5.2.1-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-28-rentiva-v5.2.1-release.md","title":"Rentiva v5.2.1 / Pro v5.2.1 \u2014 A chart that says what it counts, and translations that ship","description":"A patch release about honesty. The dashboard chart was named after something it does not measure, and a set of admin strings was being shipped in English despite having been translated months ago. Both are fixed \u2014 and the second one turned out to have a cause worth writing down.","date":"2026-07-28T18:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"pro","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/pro"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"},{"inline":true,"label":"i18n","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/i-18-n"}],"readingTime":3.84,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v5.2.1-release","title":"Rentiva v5.2.1 / Pro v5.2.1 \u2014 A chart that says what it counts, and translations that ship","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","pro","patch","i18n"],"date":"2026-07-28T18:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.2.2 / Pro v5.2.2 \u2014 What we tell WooCommerce, and one thing we were telling it wrong","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.2.2-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.2.0 / Pro v5.2.0 \u2014 Seventeen security switches that did nothing, and the ones that now do","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.2.0-release"}},"content":"A patch release about honesty. The dashboard chart was named after something it does not measure, and a set of admin strings was being shipped in English despite having been translated months ago. Both are fixed \u2014 and the second one turned out to have a cause worth writing down.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## The chart was measuring the right thing under the wrong name\\n\\nThe dashboard\'s bar chart was labelled **\\"Revenue (Last 7 Days)\\"**. It sums `_mhm_total_price` for confirmed and completed bookings, bucketed by `DATE(post_date)` \u2014 the date each booking was **created**. That is not rental income earned in those seven days; it is the value of new business booked in them.\\n\\nThe mismatch was visible: the table directly beneath the chart lists bookings by pickup date. So a rental company with a full week ahead could see a row of upcoming rentals under a chart reading zero, and reasonably conclude the chart was broken. It wasn\'t \u2014 it was answering a different question than its title asked.\\n\\nThe label now reads **\\"New Bookings Value (Last 7 Days)\\"**, and the daily series is **\\"Daily Bookings Value\\"**.\\n\\n**The numbers have not changed.** We deliberately did not move the chart onto pickup dates, because `post_date` is the basis shared by the dashboard metrics, the period deltas, the booking statistics, the deposit statistics and the comprehensive report. Changing only the chart would have left the plugin with two different definitions of \\"revenue\\" on one screen. Reporting on realised rental income is a genuine feature, and it belongs in its own release rather than smuggled into a label fix.\\n\\n## Five translated strings that never reached anyone\\n\\nWordPress serves JavaScript translations from one JSON catalogue per script, named after an MD5 of the script\'s path. Those catalogues are generated by `wp i18n make-json`, which \u2014 by default \u2014 only looks at references ending in `.js` or `.min.js`.\\n\\nEvery React reference in our translation template is a `.jsx` source path. So the command matched nothing, printed a success line, and wrote no React catalogues at all. Because regeneration correctly runs with `--no-purge`, the previous catalogues survived untouched, and the check that was supposed to catch this only asserted that the files *existed*. They did. They were four months old.\\n\\nThe result: **\\"Pending Payments\\"**, **\\"Upcoming Operations\\"**, their empty-state messages, and the notice shown when an admin screen fails to load were all translated in the catalogue and all displayed in English.\\n\\nThis release fixes the build and, more importantly, changes what the check actually checks. It now compares the shipped catalogues against the translation source on three axes \u2014 the script each catalogue claims to belong to, whether this run actually rewrote it, and whether every string the source assigns to that screen is present. It runs on every push. A green result now means something.\\n\\n## Pro: the same class, five screens wide\\n\\nThe paid add-on\'s five React screens \u2014 Reports, Messages, Export, Vendor Management and Vendor Reports \u2014 had been shipping **entirely untranslated** since they moved into their own plugin. The sources had been corrected to the add-on\'s own text domain at the time, but nothing rebuilt the compiled bundles, because the build configuration had not moved with them.\\n\\nThat chain is now closed end to end: the bundles are rebuilt against the right text domain, the translation template scans the React sources, 325 strings are translated, and the catalogues are generated under the names WordPress actually resolves. All five screens were verified in a browser in Turkish before this release, tab by tab.\\n\\nPro v5.2.1 also corrects its declared minimum Lite version. The translation fix depends on a parameter Lite gained in this release; with an older Lite the add-on does not fail, the screens simply stay English.\\n\\n## Housekeeping\\n\\n- Eleven translation catalogues belonging to screens and blocks that are no longer part of the free plugin were removed. Nothing loaded them.\\n- The readme\'s bundled-library inventory now lists **Chart.js 4.5.1** alongside flatpickr and Swiper, with its licence and upstream source. It is compiled into the dashboard bundle rather than shipped under `assets/vendor/`, and that distinction is stated.\\n\\n## Upgrading\\n\\nNothing to do. No figure, setting or stored record changes. Update both plugins together if you run the paid add-on."},{"id":"rentiva-v5.2.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.2.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-25-rentiva-v5.2.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-25-rentiva-v5.2.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v5.2.0 / Pro v5.2.0 \u2014 Seventeen security switches that did nothing, and the ones that now do","description":"The largest release in the 5.x line so far. Permission checks now test the specific record a request names instead of a general capability, the admin markup is filtered as it is printed, the Dashboard and Vehicle Settings screens are redesigned \u2014 and a long list of controls that claimed to do something, but were connected to nothing, has been removed.","date":"2026-07-25T22:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"pro","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/pro"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"},{"inline":true,"label":"minor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/minor"}],"readingTime":4.32,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v5.2.0-release","title":"Rentiva v5.2.0 / Pro v5.2.0 \u2014 Seventeen security switches that did nothing, and the ones that now do","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","pro","security","minor"],"date":"2026-07-25T22:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.2.1 / Pro v5.2.1 \u2014 A chart that says what it counts, and translations that ship","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.2.1-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.1.1 / Pro v5.1.1 \u2014 Compliance hygiene, no behaviour change","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.1.1-release"}},"content":"The largest release in the 5.x line so far. Permission checks now test the specific record a request names instead of a general capability, the admin markup is filtered as it is printed, the Dashboard and Vehicle Settings screens are redesigned \u2014 and a long list of controls that claimed to do something, but were connected to nothing, has been removed.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## The uncomfortable part first\\n\\nSettings \u2192 Security had **seventeen** controls: \\"Brute Force Protection\\", \\"SQL Injection Protection\\", \\"XSS Protection\\", \\"CSRF Protection\\", \\"Enable Rate Limiting\\", IP allow and block lists. None of them were wired to anything. Switching one on changed no behaviour whatsoever.\\n\\nThey are gone. So is the \\"Secure API Access Tokens\\" section, which issued keys labelled READ, WRITE and ADMIN that no part of the plugin ever checked \u2014 a key created there opened nothing. So are the Integration settings for token duration, token refresh, API caching, debug output and \\"Allow Global CORS\\". So is a \\"Scheduled Notifications\\" background job that ran every hour against a queue nothing ever added to, while the Cron Monitor cheerfully reported it as healthy. And so is the \\"Add Vehicle\\" button in the vehicle comparison: no handler, unregistered endpoints, and an Elementor switch to toggle a thing that did not exist.\\n\\nA control that says a protection is active while nothing enforces it is **worse than no control at all**, because it gets relied on. Saved values for the removed settings are cleaned up automatically when you update.\\n\\nRate limiting, which does work, stays. The REST API is unchanged and still authenticates normally.\\n\\n## Permissions now check the record, not just the role\\n\\nBooking, deposit, vehicle-gallery and blocked-date handlers used to check a general \\"can edit content\\" capability. They now check the caller against **the specific record the request names**. On multi-author sites this closes paths where one contributor could act on another contributor\'s bookings, galleries or availability.\\n\\nSaving a booking from the editor now always requires a valid security token; the presence of a form field is no longer accepted in its place. The database backup screen exports, restores and deletes only backup tables this plugin created \u2014 other tables can no longer be named in those requests. And markup the plugin generates is filtered through an explicit allowlist **as it is printed**, replacing places that trusted the output to have been escaped earlier.\\n\\n## Fixes worth naming\\n\\n- **Uninstall used to stop partway through.** With \\"delete all data on uninstall\\" switched on, removing the plugin still left tables, scheduled jobs and taxonomy terms behind.\\n- **The backups screen could go blank.** Any `.sql` file in the backup folder without a matching database record caused a fatal error while the list was being built. Backups are now written under your uploads folder instead of directly into `wp-content`; backups taken by earlier versions stay listed, restorable and deletable \u2014 nothing is moved or lost.\\n- **Vehicle quick edit accepted values the full editor rejects.** A daily price could be saved as a negative number, which then multiplied into rental totals; the seat count could be zero or above the configured maximum.\\n- **Log retention settings were ignored.** \\"Auto Cleanup Logs\\" and \\"Log Retention (Days)\\" had no effect: the daily purge always deleted entries older than thirty days, permanently, even with cleanup switched off or retention set higher.\\n- **Saving the Vehicle settings tab silently reset two Frontend fields** \u2014 \\"Vehicles per page\\" and \\"Default sort order\\" \u2014 that the Vehicle tab does not even display.\\n- **The dashboard\'s recent-bookings panel could sit up to twelve hours out of date**, because its cache was cleared under a name the cache no longer used. The customers screen re-ran its full query set on every load for the mirror-image reason: it requested a cache type that had never been registered, so nothing was stored or read.\\n- **Search could be asked to render the whole fleet.** Vehicle search accepted any page size; search and testimonials now cap it at the limit their own settings advertise.\\n- The translation catalogue now compiles without errors \u2014 strings containing placeholders like `%days%` were being mis-flagged as printf formats.\\n\\n## New: redesigned Dashboard and Vehicle Settings\\n\\nBoth screens have been rebuilt. Vehicle Settings opens in the new layout by default; adding `?ui=legacy` to the page URL brings back the previous one for this release.\\n\\n## Internal\\n\\nTemporary cache entries, the last-login record, background job names and the JavaScript objects the admin screens read now all carry the plugin\'s own prefix, so they cannot collide with another plugin storing something under the same name. Every script and stylesheet is registered under its full prefix too \u2014 WordPress keeps whichever was registered first under a shared short name and discards the other without warning.\\n\\nAround **2,000 lines** of code that nothing referenced were removed, including a file registering database-maintenance commands and one that would have exposed protected vehicle and booking fields over the REST API had it ever been switched on.\\n\\n## Upgrading\\n\\nNo action required. Administrators are unaffected by the permission changes; on sites with editor or author roles, those users can now only act on records they are entitled to. Settings belonging to the removed controls are cleaned up for you."},{"id":"rentiva-v5.1.1-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.1.1-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-21-rentiva-v5.1.1-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-21-rentiva-v5.1.1-release.md","title":"Rentiva v5.1.1 / Pro v5.1.1 \u2014 Compliance hygiene, no behaviour change","description":"A small follow-up to v5.1.0, continuing the pass ahead of the WordPress.org listing. Nothing about how the plugin behaves changes here \u2014 this is the kind of release that is worth publishing precisely because it is uneventful.","date":"2026-07-21T21:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"pro","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/pro"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"}],"readingTime":1.46,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v5.1.1-release","title":"Rentiva v5.1.1 / Pro v5.1.1 \u2014 Compliance hygiene, no behaviour change","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","pro","patch"],"date":"2026-07-21T21:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.2.0 / Pro v5.2.0 \u2014 Seventeen security switches that did nothing, and the ones that now do","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.2.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.1.0 / Pro v5.1.0 \u2014 Security hardening, and no third-party calls at all","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.1.0-release"}},"content":"A small follow-up to v5.1.0, continuing the pass ahead of the WordPress.org listing. Nothing about how the plugin behaves changes here \u2014 this is the kind of release that is worth publishing precisely because it is uneventful.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n- **Action names carry the full prefix.** The REST API-key and deposit-management AJAX actions now use the complete `mhm_rentiva_` prefix. A duplicate registration of the API-key handlers was also removed, so each action is handled exactly once instead of twice.\\n- **Dead references removed.** A leftover reference to a settings class that is not part of the free plugin, an unreachable deposit-calculation path, and developer debug logging left behind in the block-editor and search scripts.\\n- **No non-functional buttons.** The customer privacy controls render only when their handlers are actually available \u2014 those ship with the paid add-on \u2014 so the free plugin no longer shows controls that cannot do anything. Add-on-only scripts were removed from the free plugin at the same time.\\n- **Docs:** the readme describes the bundled shared UI library in neutral wording.\\n\\n## Pro v5.1.1\\n\\nThe add-on now bundles the frontend scripts it owns, rather than expecting the free plugin to ship them on its behalf. This is the other half of the neutral-hooks separation that landed in v5.1.0.\\n\\n## Upgrading\\n\\nNo action required; your settings and data are unaffected."},{"id":"rentiva-v5.1.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.1.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-20-rentiva-v5.1.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-20-rentiva-v5.1.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v5.1.0 / Pro v5.1.0 \u2014 Security hardening, and no third-party calls at all","description":"A hardening pass ahead of the WordPress.org listing. The free plugin\'s features and behaviour are unchanged \u2014 what changed is how carefully it handles input, output and permissions, and what it no longer ships.","date":"2026-07-20T20:30:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"pro","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/pro"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"},{"inline":true,"label":"minor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/minor"}],"readingTime":1.75,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v5.1.0-release","title":"Rentiva v5.1.0 / Pro v5.1.0 \u2014 Security hardening, and no third-party calls at all","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","pro","security","minor"],"date":"2026-07-20T20:30"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.1.1 / Pro v5.1.1 \u2014 Compliance hygiene, no behaviour change","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.1.1-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.0.1 / Pro v5.0.2 \u2014 Export screen fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.0.1-export-fixes"}},"content":"A hardening pass ahead of the WordPress.org listing. The free plugin\'s features and behaviour are unchanged \u2014 what changed is how carefully it handles input, output and permissions, and what it no longer ships.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Security\\n\\n- **Contact-form attachments** are now resolved through WordPress\'s own upload APIs with containment checks, closing a file-path handling issue.\\n- **Creating a customer WordPress account** requires the `create_users` capability, and the REST routes that do it are gated on the matching user-management capability rather than a looser one.\\n- Additional **output escaping**, settings array-key sanitization, and proper registration of public query variables across the admin and frontend.\\n\\n## The plugin now makes no external requests whatsoever\\n\\nTestimonial and account avatars used to come from Gravatar. They are now rendered locally from the person\'s initials. That was the last third-party call in the plugin: nothing it loads \u2014 including its webfont \u2014 comes from anywhere but your own site. No analytics, no geolocation, no remote fonts or scripts.\\n\\nThis matters beyond privacy hygiene. A plugin that quietly contacts an external service is a plugin whose behaviour depends on that service being up, reachable and trustworthy. Now there is nothing to depend on.\\n\\n## Removed: the demo-data seeder\\n\\nThe bundled demo-data tool and its sample images are gone from the plugin. They existed to make a fresh install look populated; they also meant every site carried a set of images and a data-writing tool it would use once, if ever.\\n\\n## Documented: how to rebuild from source\\n\\nThe readme gained a **Source code** section describing the React build and pointing at the public repository. The four React admin screens ship as compiled bundles, and their un-minified sources ship alongside them \u2014 so nothing in the plugin is opaque.\\n\\n## Pro v5.1.0\\n\\nThe paid add-on now attaches to the free plugin **only through neutral WordPress hooks**, and ships its own assets rather than relying on the free plugin to carry them. The free plugin contains no licensing or paid-feature scaffolding at all \u2014 not disabled, not gated: absent.\\n\\n## Upgrading\\n\\nNo action required. Your settings and data are unaffected."},{"id":"rentiva-v5.0.1-export-fixes","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.0.1-export-fixes","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-18-rentiva-v5.0.1-export-fixes.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-18-rentiva-v5.0.1-export-fixes.md","title":"Rentiva v5.0.1 / Pro v5.0.2 \u2014 Export screen fixes","description":"A coupled patch release that fixes the data-export screen. Lite ships the shared bundle (v5.0.1); Pro ships the logic (v5.0.2). The free plugin\'s own behaviour is unchanged \u2014 the export screen is a Pro feature.","date":"2026-07-18T23:30:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"pro","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/pro"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"}],"readingTime":1.25,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v5.0.1-export-fixes","title":"Rentiva v5.0.1 / Pro v5.0.2 \u2014 Export screen fixes","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","pro","patch"],"date":"2026-07-18T23:30"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.1.0 / Pro v5.1.0 \u2014 Security hardening, and no third-party calls at all","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.1.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.0.0 \u2014 First Public Release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.0.0-release"}},"content":"A coupled patch release that fixes the data-export screen. Lite ships the shared bundle (**v5.0.1**); Pro ships the logic (**v5.0.2**). The free plugin\'s own behaviour is unchanged \u2014 the export screen is a Pro feature.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s fixed\\n\\n- **The Export button now works.** It was posting its security token under the wrong field name, so every export \u2014 CSV included \u2014 failed with a \\"the link you followed has expired\\" error.\\n- **The date range is applied to the download.** The screen posted the range under one set of field names while the handler read another, so a filtered preview (\\"23 records\\") still downloaded every record. The two now agree, and a regression test pins it in place.\\n- **The history table is readable again.** Its Type, Records and User columns were blank because the stored rows and the table used different field names; they are now mapped on read, and a numeric user id resolves to the account\'s display name. A new Format column shows how each entry was exported.\\n- **The JSON format is reachable.** JSON export has worked on the server for releases, but the screen shipped no format control; a picker now offers it, sharing one source of truth with the handler so the two can\'t drift apart.\\n- **Turkish translation** updated for the new strings.\\n\\n## Quality gates\\n\\n| Gate | Lite v5.0.1 | Pro v5.0.2 |\\n| --- | --- | --- |\\n| PHPUnit | 868 / 0 | 813 / 0 |\\n| PHPCS | 0 | 0 |\\n| Plugin Check | 0 errors | private add-on |\\n\\nInstall both together \u2014 the fix spans the two (bundle in Lite, logic in Pro)."},{"id":"rentiva-v5.0.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.0.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-18-rentiva-v5.0.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-18-rentiva-v5.0.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v5.0.0 \u2014 First Public Release","description":"MHM Rentiva\'s first public release, free to download: the complete rental core with no artificial limits, no third-party requests, and full WordPress.org coding-standards compliance.","date":"2026-07-18T14:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"wordpress-org","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/wordpress-org"},{"inline":true,"label":"compliance","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/compliance"},{"inline":true,"label":"major","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/major"}],"readingTime":1.69,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v5.0.0-release","title":"Rentiva v5.0.0 \u2014 First Public Release","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","wordpress-org","compliance","major"],"date":"2026-07-18T14:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.0.1 / Pro v5.0.2 \u2014 Export screen fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.0.1-export-fixes"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.64.3 \u2014 Full Dark Mode Contrast Audit","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.64.3-release"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva\'s first public release, free to download: the complete rental core with no artificial limits, no third-party requests, and full WordPress.org coding-standards compliance.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\nEvery screen works exactly as before \u2014 this release changes **how the plugin is packaged and loaded**, not what it does.\\n\\n## What\'s in it\\n\\n- **First public release, free to download.** Fleet management, availability, bookings, customers, WooCommerce payments, email notifications and the customer account pages \u2014 with no vehicle, booking or listing caps, no feature timers and no locked screens.\\n- **No third-party requests at all.** The webfont is bundled and served from your own site; there are no geolocation, analytics or CDN calls.\\n- **16 shortcodes, 16 Gutenberg blocks and 17 Elementor widgets** share a single renderer (Render Parity), so all three produce identical output. Ships with a full Turkish translation.\\n\\n## Under the hood\\n\\n- **Assets load through the WordPress asset system.** Every admin and front-end script and style now goes through `wp_enqueue` / `wp_add_inline_*` instead of inline `<script>`/`<style>` blocks \u2014 with no change to how any screen looks or behaves. Self-contained documents (email templates, the downloadable test report, the meta-keys reference) keep their inline styles by design, since an external stylesheet would not be available when those are opened on their own.\\n- **Licence gating hardened.** Pro-only surfaces are now gated on a valid licence rather than only hidden, closing several paths where the separate paid add-on\'s features could run without one.\\n- **WordPress 7.0 ready,** including a contrast fix for dashicons inside primary buttons (WP 7.0 colours them with the admin theme colour, which made them invisible on a primary button\'s matching background).\\n\\n## Quality gates\\n\\n| Gate | Result |\\n| --- | --- |\\n| PHPUnit | 868 tests / 2,823 assertions, 0 failures |\\n| WordPress Coding Standards | 0 errors |\\n| Plugin Check (distributed ZIP) | **0 errors** |\\n| Independent audits | Two architecture/security reviews, plus browser verification across every affected admin and front-end screen |\\n\\n## Upgrading\\n\\nFirst public release \u2014 if you are upgrading from a pre-release build, no action is required.\\n\\n**Requirements:** WordPress 6.7+, PHP 8.1+. WooCommerce is required for frontend booking payments."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.64.3-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.64.3-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-12-rentiva-v4.64.3-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-12-rentiva-v4.64.3-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.64.3 \u2014 Full Dark Mode Contrast Audit","description":"A full contrast audit across every Settings tab, fixing roughly 15 more dark-mode readability issues beyond the previous patch.","date":"2026-07-12T20:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"settings","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/settings"},{"inline":true,"label":"bugfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/bugfix"},{"inline":true,"label":"accessibility","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/accessibility"}],"readingTime":0.76,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.64.3-release","title":"Rentiva v4.64.3 \u2014 Full Dark Mode Contrast Audit","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","settings","bugfix","accessibility"],"date":"2026-07-12T20:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v5.0.0 \u2014 First Public Release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v5.0.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.64.2 \u2014 Dark Mode Contrast + Un-translatable Placeholder Fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.64.2-release"}},"content":"A full contrast audit across every Settings tab, fixing roughly 15 more dark-mode readability issues beyond the previous patch.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Fixed\\n\\n- **Full dark-mode contrast audit.** The v4.64.2 fix only addressed 3 isolated spots; this release fixes ~15 more across all 16 Settings tabs: the Lite-upgrade notice link, page-header buttons (Belgeler / Bu Sekmeyi S\u0131f\u0131rla / Konum Y\xf6netimi / Rotalar\u0131 Y\xf6net), System Status cards, the \\"Issue New Credentials\\" and \\"Cleanup Dashboard\\" boxes, accordion sections and their labels, data tables (REST API reference, DB cleanup history), `<code>` tags, and an entire tab (Bildirim \u015eablonlar\u0131) whose custom template wasn\'t covered by any prior dark-mode rule.\\n- **Light-mode regression fix.** Two Database Cleanup cards lost their card styling in light mode as a side effect of the dark-mode work above; restored.\\n\\nVerified with an automated WCAG contrast scanner across all 16 Settings tabs (0 remaining failures) plus two rounds of independent code review."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.64.2-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.64.2-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-12-rentiva-v4.64.2-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-12-rentiva-v4.64.2-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.64.2 \u2014 Dark Mode Contrast + Un-translatable Placeholder Fixes","description":"Fixes near-invisible text in Dark Mode and 6 example placeholders that could never be translated, no matter the site\'s language.","date":"2026-07-12T19:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"settings","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/settings"},{"inline":true,"label":"bugfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/bugfix"},{"inline":true,"label":"i18n","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/i-18-n"}],"readingTime":0.71,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.64.2-release","title":"Rentiva v4.64.2 \u2014 Dark Mode Contrast + Un-translatable Placeholder Fixes","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","settings","bugfix","i18n"],"date":"2026-07-12T19:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.64.3 \u2014 Full Dark Mode Contrast Audit","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.64.3-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.64.1 \u2014 Dark Mode Toggle Field Clobber Fix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.64.1-release"}},"content":"Fixes near-invisible text in Dark Mode and 6 example placeholders that could never be translated, no matter the site\'s language.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Fixed\\n\\n- **Dark Mode contrast.** The admin page title and input/textarea placeholder text had no dark-mode color override, making both nearly unreadable against the dark background.\\n- **6 un-translatable placeholder strings.** The \\"Custom Location Types\\" example placeholder (and 5 more identical instances across Security settings, Vehicle settings, and REST API settings) were raw PHP string literals never wrapped in a translation function \u2014 they could never be translated regardless of site locale, always displaying in English even on fully localized installs. All fixed and translated.\\n\\n## Improved\\n\\n- The \\"Custom Location Types\\" field description now explains that these values populate the \\"Type\\" dropdown when creating a location under Locations \u2014 previously the connection between the two screens wasn\'t documented anywhere in the UI."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.64.1-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.64.1-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-12-rentiva-v4.64.1-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-12-rentiva-v4.64.1-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.64.1 \u2014 Dark Mode Toggle Field Clobber Fix","description":"Fixes the admin panel\'s quick Dark Mode switch silently blanking Support Phone/Hours/Email and resetting Brand Name, and cleans up a residual settings-pollution artifact left behind by an older migration.","date":"2026-07-12T18:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"settings","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/settings"},{"inline":true,"label":"bugfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/bugfix"}],"readingTime":0.8,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.64.1-release","title":"Rentiva v4.64.1 \u2014 Dark Mode Toggle Field Clobber Fix","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","settings","bugfix"],"date":"2026-07-12T18:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.64.2 \u2014 Dark Mode Contrast + Un-translatable Placeholder Fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.64.2-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.64.0 \u2014 Commission Rate Overrides (Vendor & Vehicle) and Tier Configuration","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.64.0-release"}},"content":"Fixes the admin panel\'s quick Dark Mode switch silently blanking Support Phone/Hours/Email and resetting Brand Name, and cleans up a residual settings-pollution artifact left behind by an older migration.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Fixed\\n\\n- **Dark Mode toggle silently blanked General/Site-Info settings.** The admin panel\'s quick Dark Mode AJAX switch re-ran the entire General tab\'s sanitizer with only the dark-mode value present, silently blanking Support Phone, Support Hours, and Support Email, and resetting Brand Name back to the site title on every toggle. It now updates only the dark mode setting.\\n- **Residual settings-pollution cleanup.** A one-time cleanup added in v4.27.2 for a historical \\"Run All Diagnostics\\" data-pollution bug (which could leave Brand Name and similar text fields saved as the literal value \\"1\\") never re-ran on installs where its completion flag had already been stamped before the pollution actually occurred. A second cleanup pass now catches any installs still carrying the old pollution."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.64.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.64.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-07-rentiva-v4.64.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-07-rentiva-v4.64.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.64.0 \u2014 Commission Rate Overrides (Vendor & Vehicle) and Tier Configuration","description":"Admins can now override the commission rate per vendor or per vehicle, and configure the volume-discount tier thresholds directly from the admin panel \u2014 closing the last three previously UI-less layers of the commission rate hierarchy. Also includes three commission-accuracy fixes and a schema migration guard found during release verification.","date":"2026-07-07T18:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"commission","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/commission"}],"readingTime":1.92,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.64.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.64.0 \u2014 Commission Rate Overrides (Vendor & Vehicle) and Tier Configuration","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","vendor","commission"],"date":"2026-07-07T18:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.64.1 \u2014 Dark Mode Toggle Field Clobber Fix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.64.1-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.63.2 \u2014 Vendor Commission Clearing & Refund Balance Fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.63.2-release"}},"content":"Admins can now override the commission rate per vendor or per vehicle, and configure the volume-discount tier thresholds directly from the admin panel \u2014 closing the last three previously UI-less layers of the commission rate hierarchy. Also includes three commission-accuracy fixes and a schema migration guard found during release verification.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## New\\n\\n- **Vendor-level commission rate override.** Set a fixed commission rate for an individual vendor from that vendor\'s detail page in Vendor Management \u2014 no need to touch every vehicle they list.\\n- **Vehicle-level commission rate override.** Set a fixed commission rate for an individual vehicle from a new \\"Commission Rate Override\\" box on the vehicle edit screen. This is the most specific layer \u2014 it takes priority over the vendor\'s rate, volume-discount tier, and the platform-wide rate.\\n- **Editable volume-discount tiers.** The three tiers that automatically discount a high-volume vendor\'s rate (based on trailing 30-day cleared revenue) can now be edited directly from the Commission tab, instead of only via direct database edits. See the [Commission Rate Configuration guide](/docs/vendor/commission-rates) for how the full 4-layer hierarchy resolves.\\n\\n## Fixes\\n\\n- **The vehicle-level override above is now actually applied to real bookings.** The underlying resolver logic already existed but was never connected to live checkout processing.\\n- **Refund commission clawbacks now use the rate the vendor was originally credited at**, instead of whatever rate happens to be active on the day of the refund \u2014 a rate change between payment and refund no longer silently alters the refund math.\\n- **The vendor dashboard\'s \\"last 7 days\\" revenue figures** could show artificially low or negative numbers, because a commission credit that clears 7+ days after it\'s created could never land inside a rolling 7-day window while a same-day refund always could. A new internal timestamp now tracks when a credit actually cleared.\\n- **The dashboard\'s `revenue_7d` metric** had the same balance-lookup key mismatch that was fixed for the other Financial Summary cards in v4.63.2.\\n- **Schema migration guard.** Found during release verification (before this ZIP was published): a database schema-version constant hadn\'t been bumped alongside the new column that powers the 7-day revenue fix above, which would have silently prevented existing installations from ever receiving it. Fixed and verified against a simulated real upgrade before release."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.63.2-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.63.2-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-06-rentiva-v4.63.2-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-06-rentiva-v4.63.2-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.63.2 \u2014 Vendor Commission Clearing & Refund Balance Fixes","description":"Fixes vendor commission recording, adds an automatic 7-day clearing mechanism so earnings actually become withdrawable, corrects refund balance math, and fixes a vendor dashboard KPI card that always showed zero.","date":"2026-07-06T18:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"commission","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/commission"},{"inline":true,"label":"payouts","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/payouts"}],"readingTime":0.95,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.63.2-release","title":"Rentiva v4.63.2 \u2014 Vendor Commission Clearing & Refund Balance Fixes","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","vendor","commission","payouts"],"date":"2026-07-06T18:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.64.0 \u2014 Commission Rate Overrides (Vendor & Vehicle) and Tier Configuration","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.64.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.63.1 \u2014 Chart Rendering, KPI Corruption, and Settings-Tab Data-Loss Fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.63.1-release"}},"content":"Fixes vendor commission recording, adds an automatic 7-day clearing mechanism so earnings actually become withdrawable, corrects refund balance math, and fixes a vendor dashboard KPI card that always showed zero.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Fixes\\n\\n- **Vendor commission was silently never recorded for real bookings** due to a booking-reference mismatch between the checkout flow and the commission ledger \u2014 vendor earnings were never credited at all.\\n- **Vendor commission now automatically clears and becomes available for payout 7 days after payment**, via a new scheduled job. Previously, commission stayed in a \\"pending\\" state indefinitely with no way for a vendor to ever withdraw it.\\n- **Refunds now correctly adjust the vendor\'s available balance**, whether the refund happens before or after the commission clears, and whether it\'s a partial or full refund. Previously, refunds had no effect on the balance at all.\\n- **Vendors now receive an email notification** when a commission clears and becomes available for payout.\\n- **The vendor dashboard\'s \\"Financial Summary\\" cards** (Available Balance, Pending Balance, Total Paid Out) always showed 0,00 regardless of the vendor\'s actual balance, due to a data-key mismatch. The payout-request section, which reads the balance directly, was unaffected."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.63.1-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.63.1-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-05-rentiva-v4.63.1-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-05-rentiva-v4.63.1-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.63.1 \u2014 Chart Rendering, KPI Corruption, and Settings-Tab Data-Loss Fixes","description":"Fixes blank revenue charts, a corrupted Reports KPI value, and a bug where saving Messages settings from one tab silently reset the others.","date":"2026-07-05T18:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"admin","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/admin"},{"inline":true,"label":"reports","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/reports"},{"inline":true,"label":"messages","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/messages"}],"readingTime":0.94,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.63.1-release","title":"Rentiva v4.63.1 \u2014 Chart Rendering, KPI Corruption, and Settings-Tab Data-Loss Fixes","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","admin","reports","messages"],"date":"2026-07-05T18:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.63.2 \u2014 Vendor Commission Clearing & Refund Balance Fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.63.2-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.63.0 \u2014 Admin Remaining-Payment Link + Payment-Type Label Fix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.63.0-release"}},"content":"Fixes blank revenue charts, a corrupted Reports KPI value, and a bug where saving Messages settings from one tab silently reset the others.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Fixes\\n\\n- **The Dashboard\'s and Reports page\'s \\"Revenue\\" charts were rendering blank** \u2014 a pre-existing 404 on a vendor script that never shipped in any release. Chart.js is now bundled directly with the admin scripts.\\n- **The Reports page\'s \\"Monthly Revenue\\" KPI card showed a corrupted value** (e.g. \\"1,87 \u20ac\\" instead of \\"1,870.00 \u20ac\\") due to a display value being re-parsed as a raw number.\\n- **Saving the Messages settings page from any tab other than the one being edited** (e.g. saving Email settings while on the Categories tab) silently reset the other tabs\' settings, including notification checkboxes, sender email, and category/status lists, to their defaults.\\n- **A vehicle that becomes unavailable at the moment of booking submission no longer silently drops the \\"similar vehicles\\" suggestion** \u2014 the alternatives list now reaches the booking form as intended.\\n- **Corrected a Turkish mistranslation** on the Reports page (\\"Booking Report\\" tab).\\n- **Removed two broken script/style references** (booking calendar CSS, standalone customer-messages JS) that resulted in harmless but noisy 404 requests."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.63.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.63.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-02-rentiva-v4.63.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-02-rentiva-v4.63.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.63.0 \u2014 Admin Remaining-Payment Link + Payment-Type Label Fix","description":"Admins can now generate and email a payable link for a booking\'s remaining amount, and full-payment-only bookings no longer get mislabeled \\"Deposit\\" in a mixed cart.","date":"2026-07-02T18:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"checkout","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/checkout"},{"inline":true,"label":"admin","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/admin"}],"readingTime":0.67,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.63.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.63.0 \u2014 Admin Remaining-Payment Link + Payment-Type Label Fix","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","checkout","admin"],"date":"2026-07-02T18:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.63.1 \u2014 Chart Rendering, KPI Corruption, and Settings-Tab Data-Loss Fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.63.1-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.62.3 \u2014 Checkout Deposit Remaining-Amount Restore Fix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.62.3-release"}},"content":"Admins can now generate and email a payable link for a booking\'s remaining amount, and full-payment-only bookings no longer get mislabeled \\"Deposit\\" in a mixed cart.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Feature\\n\\n- **Admins can now generate a payable link for a booking\'s remaining amount directly from the \\"Deposit Management\\" box on the booking edit screen, and email it to the customer with one click.** The link is also shown on-screen for copying (WhatsApp, SMS, phone), and works even for customers without a site account.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\n- **Bookings whose payment is full-payment-only (e.g. a VIP transfer configured without deposit support) no longer get mislabeled \\"Deposit\\" when the checkout\'s cart-wide payment-type selector is set to \\"Deposit Payment\\" for a mixed cart.** The amount charged was always correct; only the internal label is corrected."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.62.3-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.62.3-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-02-rentiva-v4.62.3-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-02-rentiva-v4.62.3-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.62.3 \u2014 Checkout Deposit Remaining-Amount Restore Fix","description":"A patch release fixing a checkout bug where switching the payment-type option from \\"Full Payment\\" back to \\"Deposit Payment\\" left the remaining balance stuck at zero.","date":"2026-07-02T12:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"checkout","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/checkout"}],"readingTime":0.45,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.62.3-release","title":"Rentiva v4.62.3 \u2014 Checkout Deposit Remaining-Amount Restore Fix","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","checkout"],"date":"2026-07-02T12:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.63.0 \u2014 Admin Remaining-Payment Link + Payment-Type Label Fix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.63.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.62.2 \u2014 Lite Vehicle-Limit Counter Hardening","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.62.2-release"}},"content":"A patch release fixing a checkout bug where switching the payment-type option from \\"Full Payment\\" back to \\"Deposit Payment\\" left the remaining balance stuck at zero.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Fixes\\n\\n- **Fix: switching the checkout payment-type option from \\"Full Payment\\" back to \\"Deposit Payment\\" now correctly restores the remaining balance.** Previously, once the full-payment option was selected even briefly (including an automatic page-load sync), the remaining balance stayed at 0 after switching back to a deposit, leaving no way to collect or track the rest of the payment."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.62.2-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.62.2-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-01-rentiva-v4.62.2-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-01-rentiva-v4.62.2-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.62.2 \u2014 Lite Vehicle-Limit Counter Hardening","description":"An internal hardening patch ensuring the Lite vehicle-limit counter reflects the true vehicle count independently of the public overflow-hiding filter.","date":"2026-07-01T13:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"lite","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/lite"}],"readingTime":0.24,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.62.2-release","title":"Rentiva v4.62.2 \u2014 Lite Vehicle-Limit Counter Hardening","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","lite"],"date":"2026-07-01T13:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.62.3 \u2014 Checkout Deposit Remaining-Amount Restore Fix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.62.3-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.62.1 \u2014 Lite VIP Transfer Route Limit Counter Fix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.62.1-release"}},"content":"An internal hardening patch ensuring the Lite vehicle-limit counter reflects the true vehicle count independently of the public overflow-hiding filter.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Hardening\\n\\n- **Hardening: the Lite vehicle-limit counter now reflects the true vehicle count independently of the public overflow-hiding filter (internal robustness; enforced limits unchanged).**"},{"id":"rentiva-v4.62.1-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.62.1-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-07-01-rentiva-v4.62.1-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-07-01-rentiva-v4.62.1-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.62.1 \u2014 Lite VIP Transfer Route Limit Counter Fix","description":"A patch release fixing the Lite VIP transfer route limit counter, which silently failed to enforce the route cap on installs using the current routes table.","date":"2026-07-01T12:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"lite","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/lite"}],"readingTime":0.66,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.62.1-release","title":"Rentiva v4.62.1 \u2014 Lite VIP Transfer Route Limit Counter Fix","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","lite"],"date":"2026-07-01T12:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.62.2 \u2014 Lite Vehicle-Limit Counter Hardening","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.62.2-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.62.0 \u2014 Lite Downgrade Catalog Overflow Enforcement","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.62.0-release"}},"content":"A patch release fixing the Lite VIP transfer route limit counter, which silently failed to enforce the route cap on installs using the current routes table.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::warning Historical release note \u2014 this behaviour no longer exists\\n\\nThe Lite transfer-route cap this patch fixed was removed in **v5.0.0** along with the\\nrest of the Lite plan limits. Rentiva\'s free core places no cap on transfer routes, so\\nthere is no counter and no limit notice. This post is kept as a record of what v4.62.1\\nshipped.\\n\\n:::\\n\\n## Fixes\\n\\n- **Fix: the Lite VIP transfer route limit now counts routes correctly.** On installs using the current routes table, the limit notice showed \\"0 used\\" and new routes could still be created past the Lite limit because the counter read the wrong (legacy) database table."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.62.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.62.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-06-30-rentiva-v4.62.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-06-30-rentiva-v4.62.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.62.0 \u2014 Lite Downgrade Catalog Overflow Enforcement","description":"When a Pro license expires, catalog items added during the Pro period that exceed the Lite plan limits \u2014 vehicles, add-on services, and transfer routes \u2014 are now automatically hidden from the public site instead of staying live. Data is never deleted; everything is restored the moment you upgrade to Pro again.","date":"2026-06-30T12:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"lite","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/lite"}],"readingTime":1.48,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.62.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.62.0 \u2014 Lite Downgrade Catalog Overflow Enforcement","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","lite"],"date":"2026-06-30T12:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.62.1 \u2014 Lite VIP Transfer Route Limit Counter Fix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.62.1-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.61.0 \u2014 Vendor Payout Statements with Commission Breakdown","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.61.0-release"}},"content":"When a Pro license expires, catalog items added during the Pro period that exceed the Lite plan limits \u2014 vehicles, add-on services, and transfer routes \u2014 are now automatically hidden from the public site instead of staying live. Data is never deleted; everything is restored the moment you upgrade to Pro again.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::warning Historical release note \u2014 this behaviour no longer exists\\n\\nThe Lite plan limits described below were removed in **v5.0.0**. Rentiva\'s free core\\nships with no vehicle, add-on service or transfer-route caps, so there is nothing to\\nenforce on downgrade: no items are hidden, and there is no \\"Lite limit \u2014 hidden\\"\\nbadge or vehicle limit notice. This post is kept as a record of what v4.62.0 shipped.\\n\\n:::\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Lite Limit Enforcement on Downgrade\\n\\n- **Over-limit items hidden, not deleted.** Catalog items added during Pro (vehicles, add-on services, transfer routes) that exceed the Lite limit are hidden from the public site when a license expires. Data is preserved in full and restored automatically when you upgrade to Pro again.\\n- **\\"Lite limit \u2014 hidden\\" badge in admin lists.** Admin vehicle, add-on service, and transfer route lists mark each over-limit item with a clear badge so you can see at a glance which items are currently hidden from visitors.\\n- **Vehicle limit notice shows hidden count.** The vehicle limit notice in the admin dashboard now indicates how many vehicles are currently hidden due to the Lite limit, in addition to the total count.\\n- **Hidden vehicles cannot be booked.** Over-limit vehicles that are hidden from the public site can no longer be booked via the front end. Existing confirmed bookings for those vehicles are unaffected.\\n\\n## Fixes\\n\\n- The **Vendor Payout Requests** admin menu item no longer appears when running the Lite version of the plugin."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.61.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.61.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-06-29-rentiva-v4.61.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-06-29-rentiva-v4.61.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.61.0 \u2014 Vendor Payout Statements with Commission Breakdown","description":"When you approve a vendor payout, Rentiva now generates a printable, sequentially-numbered payment statement for the period \u2014 earnings, the platform commission deducted from each, penalties, and the net paid \u2014 frozen as an immutable record and emailed to the vendor. This release also adds a vendor agreement acceptance gate on the application form, an \\"Added by\\" column that distinguishes operator and vendor vehicles, and one-click day blocking in the Monthly Reservation Calendar.","date":"2026-06-29T12:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"payouts","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/payouts"}],"readingTime":2.12,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.61.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.61.0 \u2014 Vendor Payout Statements with Commission Breakdown","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","vendor","payouts"],"date":"2026-06-29T12:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.62.0 \u2014 Lite Downgrade Catalog Overflow Enforcement","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.62.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.60.0 \u2014 Matured Payout Fix + Dead SaaS Scaffolding Removal","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.60.0-release"}},"content":"When you approve a vendor payout, Rentiva now generates a printable, sequentially-numbered payment statement for the period \u2014 earnings, the platform commission deducted from each, penalties, and the net paid \u2014 frozen as an immutable record and emailed to the vendor. This release also adds a vendor agreement acceptance gate on the application form, an \\"Added by\\" column that distinguishes operator and vendor vehicles, and one-click day blocking in the Monthly Reservation Calendar.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Vendor Payout Statements\\n\\n- **Numbered, printable statements on approval.** Approving a vendor payout generates a payment statement for the period covered \u2014 earnings, penalties, and net \u2014 with a sequential number, frozen as an immutable snapshot at the moment of approval. The vendor receives an email with a link to view and print it from their panel. Admins see the statement number and a view link on the Payout Requests list; vendors find it in their payout history.\\n- **Commission breakdown.** Each earning line on the statement shows **Gross**, the **Commission** (its rate and amount), and the **Net** the vendor received, plus a period **\\"Total commission deducted\\"** total. Statements issued before this version show net only \u2014 existing records are never rewritten.\\n- **Statement branding.** Your company identity \u2014 name, address, tax office and number, phone, email, and logo \u2014 and a custom footer note appear on the statement. These are configured under the new statement branding settings and applied when the statement is viewed.\\n\\n### Vendor Marketplace\\n\\n- **Vendor agreement gate.** You can require applicants to read and accept a vendor agreement on the application form. The acceptance, with a timestamp, is stored and shown on the application detail. The toggle and the agreement text live in the vendor settings.\\n- **\\"Added by\\" column for vehicles.** The admin vehicle list now shows and filters who added each vehicle \u2014 vendor or operator \u2014 so the two are easy to tell apart.\\n\\n### Calendar\\n\\n- **Quick day block.** Click an empty day in the Monthly Reservation Calendar to close it for reservations, and click a blocked day to re-open it \u2014 no vehicle-edit detour needed. Booked days are unchanged and keep their reservation popup.\\n\\n## Fixes\\n\\n- When a vendor edits critical fields of a live listing, the listing is now unpublished for admin re-review instead of staying live with unreviewed changes.\\n- An admin can now edit a vendor\'s city, and the vendor\'s city is read from the canonical field across the panel.\\n- Booking reminder emails are no longer sent for inactive bookings.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nThe full suite is green at **1,331 tests / 4,021 assertions**, 0 failures, with 0 Plugin Check errors. No regression."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.60.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.60.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-06-23-rentiva-v4.60.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-06-23-rentiva-v4.60.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.60.0 \u2014 Matured Payout Fix + Dead SaaS Scaffolding Removal","description":"Matured vendor payouts were silently skipped on single-site installs: a dead SaaS \\"control plane\\" gate in the matured-payout worker required a multi-tenant registry row that a normal install never provisions, so no scheduled payout ever finalized automatically. This release removes that gate \u2014 the worker now runs unconditionally \u2014 and clears out the unused multi-tenant orchestration scaffolding that caused it.","date":"2026-06-23T12:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"payouts","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/payouts"}],"readingTime":1.2,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.60.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.60.0 \u2014 Matured Payout Fix + Dead SaaS Scaffolding Removal","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","vendor","payouts"],"date":"2026-06-23T12:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.61.0 \u2014 Vendor Payout Statements with Commission Breakdown","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.61.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.58.2 \u2014 Transfer City Filter + UI Polish","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.58.2-release"}},"content":"Matured vendor payouts were silently skipped on single-site installs: a dead SaaS \\"control plane\\" gate in the matured-payout worker required a multi-tenant registry row that a normal install never provisions, so no scheduled payout ever finalized automatically. This release removes that gate \u2014 the worker now runs unconditionally \u2014 and clears out the unused multi-tenant orchestration scaffolding that caused it.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Critical Fix\\n\\n- **Matured vendor payouts now process on single-site installs.** The matured-payout worker (`MaturedPayoutJob::run()`) was gated behind a SaaS control-plane `is_operational()` check that required a tenant-registry row which a normal (non-SaaS-hosted) install never creates \u2014 so every scheduled run exited early without finalizing a single payout. The gate has been removed; the worker now runs unconditionally. A regression test reproduces the production state (no tenant row present) and asserts the matured payout is finalized.\\n\\n### Change\\n\\n- **Removed unused multi-tenant SaaS orchestration scaffolding.** Six dead classes \u2014 the control-plane guard, usage metering, cycle manager, tenant provisioner, quota exception, and their migration \u2014 were deleted, the usage-metering call sites were stripped from the financial layer, and a one-time `v3.9.0` upgrade migration drops the two now-empty database tables. The tenant-context layer used for financial data scoping is intentionally retained.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nThe full suite stays green at **1,263 tests / 3,839 assertions**, 0 failures. The four obsolete orchestration test files were removed and a `MaturedPayoutJob` regression test was added. No regression."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.58.2-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.58.2-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-21-rentiva-v4.58.2-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-21-rentiva-v4.58.2-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.58.2 \u2014 Transfer City Filter + UI Polish","description":"TransferSearchEngine had no location filter \u2014 a search for an \u0130stanbul route returned vehicles parked in Ankara and Antalya. This release adds city-based vehicle matching (route origin\'s city), reusing the rental module\'s 3-layer hybrid filter (vehicle \u2192 vendor inheritance \u2192 global default) via a new expandtocity mode. Plus a batch of UI/content polish: KPI spacing on list-table pages, dashboard card heights, About page hardening, and Vehicles calendar parity with the Bookings page.","date":"2026-05-21T22:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"transfer","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/transfer"},{"inline":true,"label":"dashboard","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/dashboard"}],"readingTime":1.43,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.58.2-release","title":"Rentiva v4.58.2 \u2014 Transfer City Filter + UI Polish","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","transfer","dashboard"],"date":"2026-05-21T22:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.60.0 \u2014 Matured Payout Fix + Dead SaaS Scaffolding Removal","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.60.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.58.1 \u2014 Critical: Double-Booking Fix on Same-Day Returns","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.58.1-release"}},"content":"`TransferSearchEngine` had no location filter \u2014 a search for an \u0130stanbul route returned vehicles parked in Ankara and Antalya. This release adds city-based vehicle matching (route origin\'s city), reusing the rental module\'s 3-layer hybrid filter (vehicle \u2192 vendor inheritance \u2192 global default) via a new `expand_to_city` mode. Plus a batch of UI/content polish: KPI spacing on list-table pages, dashboard card heights, About page hardening, and Vehicles calendar parity with the Bookings page.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Critical Fix\\n\\n- **Transfer search filters by route origin city.** A vehicle parked in Ankara no longer appears for an \u0130stanbul route. Same 3-layer hybrid filter as rental (vehicle direct meta \u2192 vendor inheritance \u2192 global default), expanded to all locations sharing the origin\'s city.\\n\\n### Feature\\n\\n- **`QueryHelper::get_location_subquery()`** gains an optional `$expand_to_city` parameter. Backward-compatible: rental\'s strict matching is unchanged.\\n\\n### Fixes\\n\\n- **About page developer contact info hardcoded** \u2014 defensive against a DB option leaking the WordPress `admin_email` (e.g. `admin@localhost.com` on dev/clean installs).\\n- **About `Tests & Verification` card** updated to the current baseline (1,237 PHPUnit tests, 3,736 assertions) and `Tested with: WP 7.0`. Plugin header and `readme.txt` `Tested up to` aligned to 7.0.\\n\\n### Style\\n\\n- **KPI stats grid top spacing** on admin list-table pages (Vehicles, Bookings, Add-ons, Transfer) \u2014 cards no longer sit flush against the page edge.\\n- **Dashboard Pending Payments + Revenue cards** no longer stretch to a tall empty height. `RevenueChart` is bound to a 250px max height; Row 4 cards size to their own content.\\n- **Vehicles calendar spacing parity** with the Bookings calendar \u2014 wrapper top margin + card-pattern inner padding.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n6 new PHPUnit tests cover the transfer location filter (city expansion + vendor inheritance) \u2014 total **1,237 tests / 3,736 assertions**, 7 documented `saas_block` env-quota baseline failures, 15 skipped. No regression."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.58.1-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.58.1-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-21-rentiva-v4.58.1-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-21-rentiva-v4.58.1-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.58.1 \u2014 Critical: Double-Booking Fix on Same-Day Returns","description":"AutoComplete cron compared dropoffdate < NOW() at date-only granularity. MySQL cast YYYY-MM-DD to YYYY-MM-DD 0000, so any confirmed booking with a same-day dropoff was auto-completed at midnight \u2014 long before the actual return time. hasoverlap() then skipped these wrongly-completed bookings (status filter excluded \'completed\'), allowing the same vehicle to be double-booked for the remaining rental hours. This release fixes the cron, adds defense-in-depth at hasoverlap(), opens a completed \u2192 inprogress Status transition, and ships a maintenance script to revert already-contaminated bookings.","date":"2026-05-21T16:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"booking","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/booking"},{"inline":true,"label":"critical","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/critical"}],"readingTime":2.02,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.58.1-release","title":"Rentiva v4.58.1 \u2014 Critical: Double-Booking Fix on Same-Day Returns","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","booking","critical"],"date":"2026-05-21T16:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.58.2 \u2014 Transfer City Filter + UI Polish","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.58.2-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.58.0 \u2014 Financial Bug Fixes, Dashboard Polish, Expanded i18n","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.58.0-release"}},"content":"AutoComplete cron compared `dropoff_date < NOW()` at date-only granularity. MySQL cast `YYYY-MM-DD` to `YYYY-MM-DD 00:00:00`, so any confirmed booking with a same-day dropoff was auto-completed at midnight \u2014 long before the actual return time. `has_overlap()` then skipped these wrongly-completed bookings (status filter excluded `\'completed\'`), allowing the same vehicle to be double-booked for the remaining rental hours. This release fixes the cron, adds defense-in-depth at `has_overlap()`, opens a `completed \u2192 in_progress` Status transition, and ships a maintenance script to revert already-contaminated bookings.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n:::warning Optional after upgrade\\nA maintenance script lives in the GitHub repository at `bin/cleanup-early-completed-bookings.php` (intentionally not bundled in the production ZIP). If you suspect contaminated bookings (status `completed` while the real `end_ts` is still in the future), copy the file onto a deployed site and run:\\n\\n~~~bash\\n# dry-run (default)\\nwp eval-file plugins/mhm-rentiva/bin/cleanup-early-completed-bookings.php\\n\\n# revert to in_progress\\nwp eval-file plugins/mhm-rentiva/bin/cleanup-early-completed-bookings.php apply\\n~~~\\n\\nThe script routes through `Status::update_status()`, so audit hooks fire and the cache invalidates per fix. Idempotent \u2014 re-running after apply finds zero rows.\\n:::\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Critical Fix\\n\\n- **AutoComplete cron now uses datetime.** Primary signal: `_mhm_end_ts` (UNIX timestamp). Fallback: `CONCAT(_mhm_dropoff_date, \' \', _mhm_dropoff_time)`, with `23:59:59` if `dropoff_time` is missing \u2014 never auto-completes mid-day. Legacy `_mhm_end_date` fallback preserved.\\n\\n### Defense-in-Depth\\n\\n- **`has_overlap()` now flags `\'completed\'` bookings whose `end_ts` is still in the future**, blocking availability even if a future cron bug or manual mishap marks a booking complete early.\\n\\n### Feature\\n\\n- **`Status` transition matrix** allows `completed` \u2192 `in_progress` for early-completion correction (required by the cleanup script\'s audited update chain).\\n\\n### Tools\\n\\n- **`bin/cleanup-early-completed-bookings.php`** \u2014 `wp eval-file` script. Default is dry-run; positional `apply` reverts contaminated rows via `Status::update_status()` so `mhm_rentiva_booking_status_changed` fires for audit/cache invalidation. Idempotent.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n11 new PHPUnit tests across AutoCompleteCronDatetime, HasOverlapStatusFilter, and StatusTransition suites \u2014 total **1,231 tests / 3,726 assertions**, 7 documented `saas_block` env-quota baseline failures, 15 skipped. No regression."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.58.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.58.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-15-rentiva-v4.58.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-15-rentiva-v4.58.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.58.0 \u2014 Financial Bug Fixes, Dashboard Polish, Expanded i18n","description":"Critical fixes for remaining-payment double-tax and orphan WC orders after auto-cancel. Dashboard widgets gain status badges, plate, location, and a deposit/remaining split. The About > Support tab adds a GitHub Issues card, test stats, and a changelog accordion. The License page moves to a 2-column grid, and Messages adopt a React 18 chat bubble UI. 88 new Turkish translations.","date":"2026-05-15T10:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"woocommerce","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/woocommerce"},{"inline":true,"label":"dashboard","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/dashboard"},{"inline":true,"label":"i18n","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/i-18-n"}],"readingTime":2.2,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.58.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.58.0 \u2014 Financial Bug Fixes, Dashboard Polish, Expanded i18n","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","woocommerce","dashboard","i18n"],"date":"2026-05-15T10:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.58.1 \u2014 Critical: Double-Booking Fix on Same-Day Returns","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.58.1-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.57.0 \u2014 Setup Wizard + Transfer Tables Mobile Scroll","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.57.0-release"}},"content":"Critical fixes for remaining-payment double-tax and orphan WC orders after auto-cancel. Dashboard widgets gain status badges, plate, location, and a deposit/remaining split. The About > Support tab adds a GitHub Issues card, test stats, and a changelog accordion. The License page moves to a 2-column grid, and Messages adopt a React 18 chat bubble UI. 88 new Turkish translations.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::warning Critical financial fix\\nSites using deposit + remaining payment with `prices_include_tax` enabled should run `sync_orphan_wc_orders()` via WP-CLI after upgrading, to clean up historical pending orders. No schema changes.\\n:::\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Critical Fixes\\n\\n- **Remaining-payment double-tax:** the remaining-payment WC order no longer double-taxes \u2014 it uses `wc_get_price_excluding_tax()` when `prices_include_tax` is on. Customers no longer overpay roughly 20% of the remaining amount.\\n- **Orphan WC orders after auto-cancel:** auto-cancelled bookings now correctly cancel their linked WC orders (deposit + remaining). A one-time backfill helper \u2014 `sync_orphan_wc_orders()` / `sync_stale_past_bookings()` \u2014 recovers historical orphan pending orders.\\n\\n### Fixes\\n\\n- Addon list and statistics read the WooCommerce currency dynamically (previously they read the plugin setting instead).\\n- Recent Bookings widget shows the customer name (with WC order billing fallback) and the vehicle location.\\n- Pending Payments widget shows deposit and remaining as separate rows with status-aware aggregation, using WC order totals as the source of truth.\\n- Defensive null coalescing for optional `booking_data` keys in `WooCommerceBridge` \u2014 removes *Undefined array key* warnings from the PHP debug log.\\n- WP Dashboard widgets (Stats, Upcoming Operations, Pending Messages) now share consistent footer and bubble styling.\\n\\n### Features\\n\\n- **Upcoming Operations widget** (both the WP Dashboard PHP version and the plugin Dashboard React version) adds plate, a status badge (green/amber/blue), and the end date.\\n- **Quick Actions grid** adds Transfer and Vendors shortcut buttons.\\n- **License page** uses a 2-column grid (account info left, Lite/Pro comparison right), a version pill in the header, and a flex action button row.\\n- **About > Support tab** adds a GitHub Issues card, a Test & Verification stats card, and a version history accordion (first 5 visible, toggle for the rest).\\n- **Messages thread view** adopts a modern chat bubble layout \u2014 right-aligned blue for self, left-aligned gray for the other party, with a *You* suffix.\\n- **Shortcode Pages** admin now tracks all 26 registered shortcodes (was 20) \u2014 vendor/user/popular routes added.\\n\\n### Chore\\n\\n- Removed the dead Revenue Chart dashboard widget and `Charts.php` (~85 lines of orphan code left after the React migration).\\n- `ReactDOM.render` \u2192 React 18 `createRoot` migration in the Messages bundle.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n12 new PHPUnit tests across the RemainingPaymentTax, AutoCancelOrderKeyLookup, and ShortcodePagesController suites \u2014 1215 tests total, 0 failures. 88 new Turkish translations were added across Pro features, block editor settings, email templates, and the chat UI."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.57.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.57.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.57.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.57.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.57.0 \u2014 Setup Wizard + Transfer Tables Mobile Scroll","description":"Horizontal scroll wrappers added to the remaining admin tables that overflowed on narrow viewports.","date":"2026-05-12T15:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"mobile","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mobile"},{"inline":true,"label":"responsive","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/responsive"}],"readingTime":0.3,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.57.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.57.0 \u2014 Setup Wizard + Transfer Tables Mobile Scroll","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","mobile","responsive"],"date":"2026-05-12T15:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.58.0 \u2014 Financial Bug Fixes, Dashboard Polish, Expanded i18n","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.58.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.56.0 \u2014 Unified KPI Card Style Across Admin Pages","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.56.0-release"}},"content":"Horizontal scroll wrappers added to the remaining admin tables that overflowed on narrow viewports.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Mobile Scroll Wrappers\\n\\n- **Setup Wizard** system requirements table: horizontal scroll at the 390px viewport.\\n- **Transfer Locations** table: horizontal scroll on narrow screens.\\n- **Transfer Routes** table: horizontal scroll on narrow screens.\\n- **Settings** tab navigation: horizontal scroll was already present via CSS \u2014 no regression."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.56.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.56.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.56.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.56.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.56.0 \u2014 Unified KPI Card Style Across Admin Pages","description":"Consistent gradient KPI cards now apply across all admin list pages. Vehicles, Bookings, Transfer, and Additional Services adopt the Dashboard/Reports blue/green/amber/grey gradient style.","date":"2026-05-12T14:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"ui","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/ui"},{"inline":true,"label":"css","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/css"}],"readingTime":0.44,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.56.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.56.0 \u2014 Unified KPI Card Style Across Admin Pages","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","ui","css"],"date":"2026-05-12T14:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.57.0 \u2014 Setup Wizard + Transfer Tables Mobile Scroll","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.57.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.55.0 \u2014 Shortcode Pages Mobile Fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.55.0-release"}},"content":"Consistent gradient KPI cards now apply across all admin list pages. Vehicles, Bookings, Transfer, and Additional Services adopt the Dashboard/Reports blue/green/amber/grey gradient style.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Unified KPI Cards\\n\\n- **Vehicles, Bookings, Transfer, and Additional Services** list tables now use the same gradient KPI style as Dashboard and Reports.\\n- The shared `shared/admin.css` classes (`.mhm-stat-card` / `.mhm-stats-grid`) were applied to the PHP-rendered pages.\\n- CSS variable scope was extended to `.mhm-stats-grid` so the gradients work outside React roots too."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.55.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.55.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.55.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.55.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.55.0 \u2014 Shortcode Pages Mobile Fixes","description":"KPI cards and table action buttons on the Shortcode Pages admin screen are now accessible at narrow widths.","date":"2026-05-12T13:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"mobile","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mobile"},{"inline":true,"label":"responsive","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/responsive"}],"readingTime":0.33,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.55.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.55.0 \u2014 Shortcode Pages Mobile Fixes","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","mobile","responsive"],"date":"2026-05-12T13:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.56.0 \u2014 Unified KPI Card Style Across Admin Pages","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.56.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.54.0 \u2014 Customers + Vendor Reports Mobile Fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.54.0-release"}},"content":"KPI cards and table action buttons on the Shortcode Pages admin screen are now accessible at narrow widths.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Shortcode Pages \u2014 Mobile Accessibility\\n\\n- **KPI cards:** `flex-wrap` added \u2014 all three stat cards (Total / Active / Missing) are now visible at \u2264782px instead of overflowing off-screen.\\n- **Table:** horizontal scroll wrapper added \u2014 the Edit / View / Remove action buttons are reachable via scroll at narrow widths."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.54.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.54.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.54.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.54.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.54.0 \u2014 Customers + Vendor Reports Mobile Fixes","description":"Mobile rendering fixes for the Customers list, the Customer detail panel, and the Vendor Reports table, plus a currency-symbol HTML entity decode fix.","date":"2026-05-12T12:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"mobile","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mobile"},{"inline":true,"label":"responsive","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/responsive"}],"readingTime":0.55,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.54.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.54.0 \u2014 Customers + Vendor Reports Mobile Fixes","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","mobile","responsive"],"date":"2026-05-12T12:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.55.0 \u2014 Shortcode Pages Mobile Fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.55.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.53.0 \u2014 Vendor Management Mobile CSS Polish","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.53.0-release"}},"content":"Mobile rendering fixes for the Customers list, the Customer detail panel, and the Vendor Reports table, plus a currency-symbol HTML entity decode fix.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Mobile Layout Fixes\\n\\n- **Customers table:** horizontal scroll wrapper at \u2264782px \u2014 columns beyond *Bookings* are no longer inaccessible.\\n- **Customer detail panel:** full-width (100%) with the correct top offset (46px) for the mobile admin bar.\\n- **Vendor Reports table:** scroll wrapper plus `table-layout:auto` at \u2264900px \u2014 the character-per-line crush is fixed.\\n\\n### Currency Symbol Decode\\n\\n- `html_entity_decode()` is now applied to the WooCommerce currency symbol in JSON responses. The Euro symbol and other HTML entities now render as proper Unicode instead of escaped markup."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.53.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.53.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.53.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.53.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.53.0 \u2014 Vendor Management Mobile CSS Polish","description":"Vendor Management mobile rendering fixes. The Vendors table was broken at 390px \u2014 columns crushed to ~40px causing vertical text \u2014 and now scrolls horizontally. Settings and Commission inputs respect container width at narrow widths.","date":"2026-05-12T11:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"mobile","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mobile"},{"inline":true,"label":"responsive","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/responsive"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"}],"readingTime":0.54,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.53.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.53.0 \u2014 Vendor Management Mobile CSS Polish","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","mobile","responsive","vendor"],"date":"2026-05-12T11:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.54.0 \u2014 Customers + Vendor Reports Mobile Fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.54.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.52.0 \u2014 Export Page React SPA","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.52.0-release"}},"content":"Vendor Management mobile rendering fixes. The Vendors table was broken at 390px \u2014 columns crushed to ~40px causing vertical text \u2014 and now scrolls horizontally. Settings and Commission inputs respect container width at narrow widths.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Vendor Management \u2014 Mobile Layout Fixes\\n\\n- **Vendors tab:** fixed broken layout at 390px \u2014 `table-layout:auto` plus an `overflow-x` scroll wrapper at \u2264900px.\\n- **Vendors tab:** Name and Email columns now enforce a minimum width (110px / 150px) at narrow breakpoints so content stays readable.\\n- **Settings tab:** textarea and number inputs use `max-width:100%` to prevent overflow.\\n- **Commission tab:** the label input respects container width at \u2264600px.\\n- **Build:** `vendor-management.css` / `vendor-management.js` updated."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.52.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.52.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.52.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.52.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.52.0 \u2014 Export Page React SPA","description":"The Export admin page is now a full React SPA. 780 lines of legacy PHP render code have been replaced with a REST-backed interface featuring live record preview, export history with per-entry delete, and a preserved admin-post.php CSV download flow.","date":"2026-05-12T10:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"export","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/export"},{"inline":true,"label":"react","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/react"},{"inline":true,"label":"spa","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/spa"}],"readingTime":1.8,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.52.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.52.0 \u2014 Export Page React SPA","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","export","react","spa"],"date":"2026-05-12T10:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.53.0 \u2014 Vendor Management Mobile CSS Polish","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.53.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.51.0 \u2014 Vendor Management Faz B: Vendors, Commission & Settings React SPA","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.51.0-release"}},"content":"The Export admin page is now a full React SPA. 780 lines of legacy PHP render code have been replaced with a REST-backed interface featuring live record preview, export history with per-entry delete, and a preserved admin-post.php CSV download flow.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Export Page \u2014 React SPA Migration\\n\\n#### New REST Endpoints (3)\\n\\n- `GET /mhm-rentiva/v1/admin/export/history` \u2014 paginated export log (WP transient, max 50 entries, 1-week TTL)\\n- `DELETE /mhm-rentiva/v1/admin/export/{id}` \u2014 remove a specific history entry\\n- `POST /mhm-rentiva/v1/admin/export/preview` \u2014 returns total record count + 5-row sample for the selected post type and date filters, before committing to export\\n\\n#### New React Components\\n\\n- **`ExportCards`** \u2014 visual card selector for three export types: Bookings, Vehicles, App Logs. Active card is highlighted with a blue border.\\n- **`AdvancedFilters`** \u2014 collapsible date filter panel. Supports preset date ranges (populated from `ExportFilters::get_date_ranges()`) and custom from/to date inputs.\\n- **`PreviewBar`** \u2014 displays the record count and a 5-row sample table after a preview REST call. Disables the Export CSV button if count is 0.\\n- **`ExportForm`** \u2014 Export CSV button triggers a hidden `admin-post.php` form submit via `useRef` \u2014 no page reload, no SPA navigation.\\n- **`ExportHistory`** \u2014 loads the export log on mount via REST. Each row has an inline Delete button; optimistic removal on success.\\n\\n#### Legacy Code Removed\\n\\n- 780 lines of PHP render code moved to a private `@deprecated` method, unhooked from `register()`\\n- Three legacy AJAX handlers (`wp_ajax_mhm_export_*`) removed from the hook registry\\n\\n#### i18n\\n\\n- 33 new Turkish strings translated\\n- `mhm-rentiva-tr_TR-mhm-rentiva-react-export.json` generated for the React bundle\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n22 new PHPUnit integration tests covering all three REST endpoints: 401/403 auth, history CRUD, DELETE isolation, preview validation (including enum enforcement), date range filtering, and sample structure. PHPCS: 0 errors."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.51.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.51.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.51.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.51.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.51.0 \u2014 Vendor Management Faz B: Vendors, Commission & Settings React SPA","description":"Vendor Management completes its React SPA migration with Faz B: the Vendors, Commission, and Settings tabs are now fully client-side. Seven new REST endpoints, three new React components, and an N+1 query fix for vendor listing.","date":"2026-05-12T06:47:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"react","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/react"},{"inline":true,"label":"spa","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/spa"}],"readingTime":1.45,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.51.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.51.0 \u2014 Vendor Management Faz B: Vendors, Commission & Settings React SPA","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","vendor","react","spa"],"date":"2026-05-12T06:47"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.52.0 \u2014 Export Page React SPA","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.52.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.50.0 \u2014 Maintenance & Docs Update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.50.0-release"}},"content":"Vendor Management completes its React SPA migration with Faz B: the Vendors, Commission, and Settings tabs are now fully client-side. Seven new REST endpoints, three new React components, and an N+1 query fix for vendor listing.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What Changed\\n\\n### Vendors Tab \u2014 VendorTable Component\\n\\nThe Vendors tab is now a live React table powered by `GET /wp-json/mhm-rentiva/v1/admin/vendors`. Features:\\n\\n- Paginated vendor list with vehicle count per vendor (single `GROUP BY` query \u2014 no N+1)\\n- Suspend / Unsuspend actions via `POST /admin/vendors/{id}/suspend` and `POST /admin/vendors/{id}/unsuspend`\\n- Real-time status badges and inline feedback without page reload\\n\\n### Commission Tab \u2014 CommissionTab Component\\n\\nThe Commission tab reads and writes the global commission rate via two new REST routes:\\n\\n- `GET /admin/commission` \u2014 fetch current rate\\n- `POST /admin/commission` \u2014 update rate with validation\\n\\nThe PHP render function has been removed; the tab is entirely SPA-driven.\\n\\n### Settings Tab \u2014 SettingsTab Component\\n\\nVendor Management settings (enable/disable vendor marketplace, terms URL, approval mode) are now managed through:\\n\\n- `GET /admin/vendor-settings` \u2014 fetch all settings\\n- `POST /admin/vendor-settings` \u2014 persist changes\\n\\n### REST Endpoints Added (7 total)\\n\\n| Method | Route | Purpose |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| GET | `/admin/vendors` | Paginated vendor list |\\n| POST | `/admin/vendors/{id}/suspend` | Suspend a vendor |\\n| POST | `/admin/vendors/{id}/unsuspend` | Unsuspend a vendor |\\n| GET | `/admin/commission` | Get commission rate |\\n| POST | `/admin/commission` | Set commission rate |\\n| GET | `/admin/vendor-settings` | Get vendor settings |\\n| POST | `/admin/vendor-settings` | Update vendor settings |\\n\\n### Performance\\n\\nVendor list previously issued one `COUNT(*)` query per vendor to get vehicle counts. This release replaces it with a single `GROUP BY` aggregation \u2014 O(n) \u2192 O(1) queries regardless of vendor count.\\n\\n### Test Coverage\\n\\n19 new PHPUnit tests covering all 7 REST endpoints and their permission, validation, and response contracts."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.50.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.50.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.50.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.50.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.50.0 \u2014 Maintenance & Docs Update","description":"Support URLs updated to wpalemi.com, changelog backfilled for v4.40.0\u2013v4.49.0, and README updated with the React SPA admin interface section.","date":"2026-05-12T05:39:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"maintenance","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/maintenance"},{"inline":true,"label":"docs","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/docs"}],"readingTime":0.7,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.50.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.50.0 \u2014 Maintenance & Docs Update","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","maintenance","docs"],"date":"2026-05-12T05:39"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.51.0 \u2014 Vendor Management Faz B: Vendors, Commission & Settings React SPA","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.51.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.49.0 \u2014 Mobile breakpoint standardisation: 768px \u2192 782px","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.49.0-release"}},"content":"Support URLs updated to wpalemi.com, changelog backfilled for v4.40.0\u2013v4.49.0, and README updated with the React SPA admin interface section.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What Changed\\n\\n### Support URLs Updated\\n\\nAll in-plugin support links and the support email address have been updated:\\n\\n- Support URLs now point to **wpalemi.com**\\n- Support email updated to **support@wpalemi.com**\\n\\n### Changelog Backfill\\n\\nDocumentation changelog entries for **v4.40.0 through v4.49.0** have been backfilled in both English and Turkish \u2014 covering the Vendor Management Faz A sprint, Messages Faz 3, Payout Requests, Frontend CSS isolation, and mobile responsive fixes.\\n\\n### README Update\\n\\nThe plugin README now includes a dedicated **React SPA Admin Interface** section documenting the migrated admin pages: Dashboard, Messages, Customers, Reports, Vendor Management (Faz A + Faz B tabs).\\n\\n### Bundle\\n\\nThis release also bundles the mobile breakpoint fix from v4.49.0 (768 px \u2192 782 px) for operators updating from v4.46.0 or earlier."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.49.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.49.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.49.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-12-rentiva-v4.49.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.49.0 \u2014 Mobile breakpoint standardisation: 768px \u2192 782px","description":"All admin React CSS breakpoints standardised at 782 px \u2014 the correct breakpoint that accounts for WordPress\'s admin sidebar width offset on mobile devices.","date":"2026-05-12T05:01:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"mobile","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mobile"},{"inline":true,"label":"responsive","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/responsive"}],"readingTime":0.78,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.49.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.49.0 \u2014 Mobile breakpoint standardisation: 768px \u2192 782px","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","mobile","responsive"],"date":"2026-05-12T05:01"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.50.0 \u2014 Maintenance & Docs Update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.50.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.48.0 \u2014 Mobile responsive CSS fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.48.0-release"}},"content":"All admin React CSS breakpoints standardised at **782 px** \u2014 the correct breakpoint that accounts for WordPress\'s admin sidebar width offset on mobile devices.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What Changed\\n\\n### Why 782 px?\\n\\nWordPress adds ~291 px to `window.innerWidth` from the admin sidebar on mobile. The previously used 768 px breakpoint fired too early \u2014 the sidebar was still visible, causing layout collisions at common mobile widths (375 px, 390 px, 414 px).\\n\\n`782 px` matches WordPress\'s own admin breakpoint defined in `wp-admin.css`, ensuring consistent collapse behaviour across all admin pages.\\n\\n### Pages Updated\\n\\n- Dashboard widget rows now collapse to single column at \u2264 782 px\\n- Messages table stacked layout: 768 px \u2192 782 px\\n- Reports date filter vertical stack: 768 px \u2192 782 px\\n- Shared KPI stats grid: 768 px \u2192 782 px (2-column), 480 px \u2192 480 px (1-column, unchanged)\\n\\n### Bundle\\n\\nThis release also bundles v4.47.0 (fatal error fix) and v4.48.0 (mobile CSS fixes) for operators updating from v4.46.0 or earlier."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.48.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.48.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.48.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.48.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.48.0 \u2014 Mobile responsive CSS fixes","description":"Three mobile-responsive CSS fixes for the admin interface: Messages table card layout, KPI stat card grid collapse, and Reports date filter stack. All targeting real mobile viewports where the WP admin sidebar is collapsed.","date":"2026-05-11T17:18:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"mobile","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mobile"},{"inline":true,"label":"responsive","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/responsive"}],"readingTime":0.72,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.48.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.48.0 \u2014 Mobile responsive CSS fixes","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","mobile","responsive"],"date":"2026-05-11T17:18"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.49.0 \u2014 Mobile breakpoint standardisation: 768px \u2192 782px","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.49.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.47.0 \u2014 Critical fix: fatal error on Vehicles and Bookings pages","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.47.0-release"}},"content":"Three mobile-responsive CSS fixes for the admin interface: Messages table card layout, KPI stat card grid collapse, and Reports date filter stack. All targeting real mobile viewports where the WP admin sidebar is collapsed.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What Changed\\n\\n### Messages Table \u2014 Mobile Card Layout\\n\\nAt viewport widths \u2264 375 px, the Messages table now stacks to a **single-column card layout**. Column headers are rendered via CSS `::before` pseudo-elements reading from `data-label` attributes on `<td>` elements \u2014 no JavaScript required.\\n\\n### KPI Stat Cards \u2014 Responsive Grid\\n\\nThe stat card grid now collapses responsively:\\n\\n- \u2264 768 px \u2192 **2 columns**\\n- \u2264 480 px \u2192 **1 column**\\n\\nApplies to the Customers, Reports, and Dashboard admin pages.\\n\\n### Reports Date Filter \u2014 Vertical Stack\\n\\nThe date range filter (Start Date / End Date) on the Reports page now switches to a **vertical stack** at \u2264 768 px, preventing the inputs from overflowing the viewport on mobile devices."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.47.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.47.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.47.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.47.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.47.0 \u2014 Critical fix: fatal error on Vehicles and Bookings pages","description":"Urgent fix for a fatal error on the Vehicles and Bookings admin list pages introduced in v4.44.0. If you\'re on v4.44.0\u2013v4.46.0, update immediately.","date":"2026-05-11T16:22:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"hotfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/hotfix"}],"readingTime":0.62,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.47.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.47.0 \u2014 Critical fix: fatal error on Vehicles and Bookings pages","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","hotfix"],"date":"2026-05-11T16:22"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.48.0 \u2014 Mobile responsive CSS fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.48.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.46.0 \u2014 Frontend CSS isolation strategy","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.46.0-release"}},"content":"Urgent fix for a fatal error on the Vehicles and Bookings admin list pages introduced in v4.44.0. If you\'re on v4.44.0\u2013v4.46.0, update immediately.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What Was Wrong\\n\\nA missing `?>` PHP mode close tag inside `add_vehicle_stats_cards()` left the function-closing `}` brace in **HTML output mode** instead of PHP mode. This caused all subsequent class methods \u2014 including `add_monthly_calendar()` \u2014 to be output as raw text rather than registered as PHP functions.\\n\\n**Result:** The Vehicles and Bookings admin list pages threw a fatal PHP error on load, making them inaccessible.\\n\\n**Introduced in:** v4.44.0 (stats card refactor).\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nRestored the `?>` close tag before the `}` brace. All subsequent methods in `VehicleColumns` and `BookingColumns` now register correctly.\\n\\nNo database changes, no migration needed. Drop-in replacement for v4.44.0\u2013v4.46.0."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.46.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.46.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.46.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.46.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.46.0 \u2014 Frontend CSS isolation strategy","description":"A systematic frontend CSS hardening release. All 31 frontend shortcode CSS files now participate in the active theme\'s design token system and are protected against whitespace inheritance from the block editor\'s shortcode container.","date":"2026-05-11T15:12:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"frontend","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/frontend"},{"inline":true,"label":"css","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/css"}],"readingTime":0.99,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.46.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.46.0 \u2014 Frontend CSS isolation strategy","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","frontend","css"],"date":"2026-05-11T15:12"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.47.0 \u2014 Critical fix: fatal error on Vehicles and Bookings pages","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.47.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.45.0 \u2014 Admin UI polish: grids, labels, buttons","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.45.0-release"}},"content":"A systematic frontend CSS hardening release. All 31 frontend shortcode CSS files now participate in the active theme\'s design token system and are protected against whitespace inheritance from the block editor\'s shortcode container.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What Changed\\n\\n### WordPress Preset Token Mapping\\n\\nAll 31 frontend CSS files now include a `[class*=\\"rv-\\"]` selector that maps Rentiva\'s internal CSS custom properties to WordPress preset tokens:\\n\\n- `--mhm-primary` \u2192 active theme\'s primary color\\n- `--mhm-font-base` \u2192 active theme\'s base font family\\n- `--mhm-radius` \u2192 active theme\'s border radius\\n- `--mhm-text` \u2192 active theme\'s text color\\n\\nThis means Rentiva shortcodes automatically inherit the active theme\'s visual identity without any manual configuration \u2014 a key requirement for marketplace themes.\\n\\n### Whitespace Reset\\n\\nAdded `white-space: normal` to all 31 frontend CSS files. The WordPress block editor wraps shortcodes in a `.wp-block-shortcode` container that applies `white-space: pre-like` behaviour, causing unexpected text wrapping in Rentiva components. This reset eliminates the issue regardless of which block theme is active.\\n\\n### Missing Component Classes\\n\\nThree shortcodes were missing the `mhm-rentiva-*` component class on their outermost wrapper \u2014 required for the token mapping selector to apply:\\n\\n- `VehicleRatingForm` \u2192 `mhm-rentiva-rating-form`\\n- `VendorDirectory` \u2192 `mhm-rentiva-vendor-directory`\\n- `MyFavorites` \u2192 `mhm-rentiva-my-favorites`"},{"id":"rentiva-v4.45.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.45.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.45.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.45.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.45.0 \u2014 Admin UI polish: grids, labels, buttons","description":"A round of admin interface refinements: KPI stat card grid layout, developer mode banner placement, human-readable location type labels, and styled action links across Locations and Routes tables.","date":"2026-05-11T14:35:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"admin","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/admin"},{"inline":true,"label":"ui","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/ui"}],"readingTime":0.84,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.45.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.45.0 \u2014 Admin UI polish: grids, labels, buttons","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","admin","ui"],"date":"2026-05-11T14:35"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.46.0 \u2014 Frontend CSS isolation strategy","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.46.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.44.0 \u2014 Admin UI polish + bug fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.44.0-release"}},"content":"A round of admin interface refinements: KPI stat card grid layout, developer mode banner placement, human-readable location type labels, and styled action links across Locations and Routes tables.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What Changed\\n\\n### KPI Stat Cards \u2014 Grid Fix\\n\\nKPI stat cards now always render **4 per row** on wide screens. The minimum column width was reduced from 250 px to 200 px so four cards fit side-by-side without wrapping at standard admin viewport widths.\\n\\n### Developer Mode Banner Placement\\n\\nOn the Bookings and Vehicles admin list pages, the developer mode warning banner now appears **above KPI cards** \u2014 previously it was below, making it easy to miss.\\n\\n### Human-Readable Location Type Labels\\n\\nThe Locations and Transfer Routes tables now display readable labels instead of raw database enum values:\\n\\n- `City_center` \u2192 **City Center**\\n- `Airport` \u2192 **Airport**\\n- `Hotel` \u2192 **Hotel**\\n\\n### Action Links Styled as WP Buttons\\n\\nEdit and Delete action links in the Locations and Routes tables are now rendered as standard WordPress admin buttons (`.button`, `.button-small`), consistent with other list table actions."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.44.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.44.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.44.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.44.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.44.0 \u2014 Admin UI polish + bug fixes","description":"A polish-and-fix release addressing three visual inconsistencies and one data bug found during QA of the v4.40.0\u2013v4.43.0 React migration chain.","date":"2026-05-11T13:06:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"admin","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/admin"},{"inline":true,"label":"ui","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/ui"},{"inline":true,"label":"hotfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/hotfix"}],"readingTime":0.63,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.44.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.44.0 \u2014 Admin UI polish + bug fixes","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","admin","ui","hotfix"],"date":"2026-05-11T13:06"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.45.0 \u2014 Admin UI polish: grids, labels, buttons","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.45.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.43.0 \u2014 Vendor Unsuspend + Commission History","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.43.0-release"}},"content":"A polish-and-fix release addressing three visual inconsistencies and one data bug found during QA of the v4.40.0\u2013v4.43.0 React migration chain.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What Changed\\n\\n### Bug Fixes\\n\\n- **About page customer count showing 0** \u2014 the About page was reading the wrong user meta key to count customers. Now reads the correct key; customer count displays accurately.\\n- **Duplicate tab buttons in Vendor Management** \u2014 a registration-order issue was rendering tab navigation buttons twice. Fixed by deduplicating the tab registration hook.\\n\\n### UI Improvements\\n\\n- **Vendor Reports page heading** \u2014 added a visible `<h1>` page heading consistent with other admin pages.\\n- **Shortcode Pages KPI stat cards** \u2014 upgraded from the old flat card style to the gradient Dashboard-style cards introduced in v4.36.0, unifying the visual language across all admin pages."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.43.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.43.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.43.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.43.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.43.0 \u2014 Vendor Unsuspend + Commission History","description":"Two additions to Vendor Management: a one-click Unsuspend action for suspended vendors, and a Rate History table in the Commission tab showing the full audit trail of platform-wide commission policies.","date":"2026-05-11T12:21:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"commission","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/commission"}],"readingTime":0.86,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.43.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.43.0 \u2014 Vendor Unsuspend + Commission History","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","vendor","commission"],"date":"2026-05-11T12:21"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.44.0 \u2014 Admin UI polish + bug fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.44.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.42.0 \u2014 Payout Requests page + admin cleanup","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.42.0-release"}},"content":"Two additions to Vendor Management: a one-click Unsuspend action for suspended vendors, and a Rate History table in the Commission tab showing the full audit trail of platform-wide commission policies.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Vendor Unsuspend Action\\n\\nAdmins can now **unsuspend a vendor directly** from the Vendor Management admin page \u2014 no need to navigate to the user profile. When a vendor is unsuspended:\\n\\n1. The `rentiva_vendor` role is restored.\\n2. Vehicles that were moved to *Pending Review* at suspension time are re-published.\\n3. The action is logged in the commission audit trail.\\n\\n### Commission Rate History\\n\\nThe Commission tab now displays a **Rate History table** showing all historical platform-wide commission policies in reverse chronological order. Each entry records:\\n\\n- Effective date\\n- Rate (%)\\n- Admin-supplied label (e.g. \\"Q1 2026 standard rate\\")\\n\\nThe history is append-only \u2014 rates are never deleted or overwritten.\\n\\n### Menu Grouping Update\\n\\nVendor menus (Vendor Management, Vendor Reports, Payout Requests) now consistently appear at the bottom of the admin sidebar via a `priority-15` hook across all contexts."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.42.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.42.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.42.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.42.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.42.0 \u2014 Payout Requests page + admin cleanup","description":"Adds the Payout Requests admin page, groups vendor-related menus at the sidebar bottom, and includes a round of PHP cleanup across the License and Setup Wizard admin pages.","date":"2026-05-11T11:58:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"admin","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/admin"},{"inline":true,"label":"ui","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/ui"}],"readingTime":0.8,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.42.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.42.0 \u2014 Payout Requests page + admin cleanup","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","admin","ui"],"date":"2026-05-11T11:58"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.43.0 \u2014 Vendor Unsuspend + Commission History","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.43.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.41.0 \u2014 Messages Phase 3: Full React SPA","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.41.0-release"}},"content":"Adds the Payout Requests admin page, groups vendor-related menus at the sidebar bottom, and includes a round of PHP cleanup across the License and Setup Wizard admin pages.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Payout Requests Admin Page\\n\\nA new **Bayi \xd6deme Talepleri** (Vendor Payout Requests) admin page is now registered in the menu. Vendors can submit payout requests from their dashboard; admins review and approve them here.\\n\\n### Menu Grouping\\n\\nVendor-related admin menus \u2014 Vendor Management, Vendor Reports, and Payout Requests \u2014 are now grouped at the **bottom of the sidebar** via a priority-15 hook, keeping them visually separated from core booking/vehicle menus.\\n\\n### PHP Cleanup\\n\\n- **License admin page:** Extracted expiry row rendering into a dedicated method; removed dead code from the notice pipeline.\\n- **Setup Wizard:** Extracted inline CSS and JS to separate asset files; fixed step completion logic; removed the unused `is_payment_ready()` method.\\n\\n### i18n Fix\\n\\nRegenerated `.l10n.php` so WordPress 6.5+ reads updated Turkish translations correctly via the binary search optimisation."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.41.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.41.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.41.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.41.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.41.0 \u2014 Messages Phase 3: Full React SPA","description":"The Messages admin page has been completely rewritten as a React SPA, replacing the legacy jQuery/WPListTable implementation. Real-time filtering, bulk actions, thread view, reply forms, and settings management \u2014 all without page reloads.","date":"2026-05-11T09:31:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"messages","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/messages"},{"inline":true,"label":"react","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/react"},{"inline":true,"label":"spa","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/spa"}],"readingTime":1.08,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.41.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.41.0 \u2014 Messages Phase 3: Full React SPA","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","messages","react","spa"],"date":"2026-05-11T09:31"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.42.0 \u2014 Payout Requests page + admin cleanup","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.42.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.40.0 \u2014 Vendor Management Phase A: React SPA","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.40.0-release"}},"content":"The Messages admin page has been completely rewritten as a React SPA, replacing the legacy jQuery/WP_List_Table implementation. Real-time filtering, bulk actions, thread view, reply forms, and settings management \u2014 all without page reloads.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Messages \u2014 Full React SPA (Phase 3)\\n\\n#### New React Components\\n\\n- **`MessagesPage`** \u2014 root with URL-param routing (`?id` for thread, `?tab=settings` for settings)\\n- **`FilterBar`** \u2014 search + status/category/priority dropdowns with 300 ms debounce\\n- **`MessageTable`** \u2014 checkbox bulk-select, unread dot indicator, row-click to thread\\n- **`Pagination`** \u2014 prev/next, hidden when single page\\n- **`BulkBar`** \u2014 parallel REST status updates + hidden admin-post form for bulk delete\\n- **`ThreadView`** \u2014 full message thread with inline status dropdown\\n- **`ReplyForm`** \u2014 \\"Send\\" (keep open) + \\"Send & Close\\" dual-action buttons\\n- **`SettingsView`** \u2014 Email / Categories / Statuses tabs, admin-post save\\n\\n#### REST API Extensions\\n\\nTwo new filter parameters added to the existing `GET /mhm-rentiva/v1/messages` endpoint:\\n- `search` \u2014 debounced full-text filter (subject + sender name)\\n- `priority` \u2014 filter by message priority level\\n\\n#### Bulk Delete\\n\\nNew `MessageDeleteHandler` admin-post handler with nonce gate for bulk message trash operations. Runs outside the REST layer to leverage WP\'s post status management.\\n\\n## Why React?\\n\\nThe old WP_List_Table implementation required a full PHP page reload for every filter change, bulk action, or thread view. With 300 ms debounced search and parallel REST updates, the new SPA feels instant."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.40.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.40.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.40.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-11-rentiva-v4.40.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.40.0 \u2014 Vendor Management Phase A: React SPA","description":"The Pending Applications and IBAN Requests admin tabs have been completely rewritten as a React SPA backed by a dedicated REST API \u2014 eliminating full-page PHP renders and introducing 7 new REST endpoints for programmatic access.","date":"2026-05-11T08:58:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"react","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/react"},{"inline":true,"label":"spa","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/spa"}],"readingTime":1.33,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.40.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.40.0 \u2014 Vendor Management Phase A: React SPA","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","vendor","react","spa"],"date":"2026-05-11T08:58"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.41.0 \u2014 Messages Phase 3: Full React SPA","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.41.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.39.0 \u2014 Customers Page React SPA (Faz 2)","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.39.0-release"}},"content":"The Pending Applications and IBAN Requests admin tabs have been completely rewritten as a React SPA backed by a dedicated REST API \u2014 eliminating full-page PHP renders and introducing 7 new REST endpoints for programmatic access.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Vendor Management \u2014 React SPA Migration (Phase A)\\n\\nThis is the first phase of the full Vendor Management React migration. Phase A covers the two most complex tabs: application review and IBAN change management.\\n\\n#### New REST Endpoints (7)\\n\\n- `GET /mhm-rentiva/v1/vendors/applications` \u2014 paginated applications list with status/sort filters\\n- `GET /mhm-rentiva/v1/vendors/applications/{id}` \u2014 application detail with IBAN masking (raw encrypted value never exposed)\\n- `POST /mhm-rentiva/v1/vendors/applications/{id}/approve` \u2014 approve with role promotion\\n- `POST /mhm-rentiva/v1/vendors/applications/{id}/reject` \u2014 reject with mandatory reason + 24 h cooldown\\n- `GET /mhm-rentiva/v1/vendors/iban-requests` \u2014 paginated pending IBAN change requests\\n- `POST /mhm-rentiva/v1/vendors/iban-requests/{vendor_id}/approve` \u2014 swap active IBAN from pending\\n- `POST /mhm-rentiva/v1/vendors/iban-requests/{vendor_id}/reject` \u2014 discard pending IBAN, keep active\\n\\n#### New React Components\\n\\n- **`VendorManagementPage`** \u2014 root with tab navigation and flash notice system\\n- **`ApplicationTable`** \u2014 paginated list with approve/reject quick-actions\\n- **`ApplicationRow`** \u2014 row with status badge and inline action buttons\\n- **`ApplicationDetailPage`** \u2014 full detail view with `ApproveForm` + `RejectForm`\\n- **`IbanRequestsTab`** \u2014 pending IBAN change queue\\n- **`IbanRequestRow`** \u2014 masked IBAN comparison (current vs. requested) with approve/reject\\n\\n#### Security\\n\\n- IBAN data is never exposed in raw form \u2014 all REST responses return masked values (`TR***5678`)\\n- 24-hour cooldown enforced server-side on rejected applications\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\nNew: 14 PHPUnit integration tests across `VendorManagementRESTApplicationsFazATest` and `VendorManagementRESTIbanFazATest`. All passing. PHPCS: 0 errors."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.39.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.39.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-10-rentiva-v4.39.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-10-rentiva-v4.39.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.39.0 \u2014 Customers Page React SPA (Faz 2)","description":"The legacy jQuery / WPListTable Customers admin page is gone. v4.39.0 replaces it with a full React SPA backed by a dedicated REST API \u2014 live search, sortable columns, a slide-in detail panel, and bulk delete, all without page reloads.","date":"2026-05-10T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"customers","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/customers"},{"inline":true,"label":"react","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/react"},{"inline":true,"label":"spa","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/spa"}],"readingTime":1.32,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.39.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.39.0 \u2014 Customers Page React SPA (Faz 2)","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","customers","react","spa"],"date":"2026-05-10T09:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.40.0 \u2014 Vendor Management Phase A: React SPA","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.40.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.38.2 \u2014 Dev mode fix: Traefik *.localhost support","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.38.2-release"}},"content":"The legacy jQuery / `WP_List_Table` Customers admin page is gone. v4.39.0 replaces it with a full React SPA backed by a dedicated REST API \u2014 live search, sortable columns, a slide-in detail panel, and bulk delete, all without page reloads.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s New\\n\\n### Customers Page \u2014 React SPA Migration\\n\\nThis is the second major admin page migrated from PHP-rendered output to a React SPA (Faz 2, following the Dashboard in Faz 1).\\n\\n#### New REST Endpoints\\n\\n- `GET /mhm-rentiva/v1/customers` \u2014 paginated customer list with search, sort, and per-page controls\\n- `GET /mhm-rentiva/v1/customers/{id}` \u2014 full customer detail (name, email, phone, address, booking stats, first/last booking)\\n- `DELETE /mhm-rentiva/v1/customers/bulk` \u2014 bulk delete by ID array with `manage_options` gate\\n\\n#### New React Components\\n\\n- **`CustomersPage`** \u2014 root state orchestrator wiring search, pagination, and panel state\\n- **`CustomerTable`** \u2014 sortable table replacing `WP_List_Table`; columns: Name, Email, Bookings, Total Spent, Last Booking, Registered\\n- **`CustomerDetailPanel`** \u2014 slide-in panel on row click; shows full profile with Edit and View Bookings quick links\\n- **`FilterBar`** \u2014 live search input with 300 ms debounce and bulk delete trigger\\n\\n#### Removed Legacy Code\\n\\n- `CustomersListTable.php` \u2014 deleted\\n- `CustomersListPage.php` \u2014 deleted\\n- `customers.js`, `customers-calendar.js`, `customers.css`, `simple-calendars.css` \u2014 deleted\\n\\n#### Other Changes\\n\\n- `CustomersOptimizer` extended with `sort_by` / `sort_dir` parameters and a PHP-side column whitelist for safe `ORDER BY` injection\\n- Export CSV still streams via `admin-post.php` \u2014 the download flow is preserved alongside the SPA\\n- `CustomersPage::register()` no longer hooks `rest_api_init` directly; routes register through `Plugin.php` so they\'re available before `admin_menu` fires\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n13 new PHPUnit integration tests (10 REST endpoint tests + 3 exporter tests). Full suite: **1115 tests, 3425 assertions**. PHPCS: 0 errors."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.38.2-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.38.2-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-09-rentiva-v4.38.2-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-09-rentiva-v4.38.2-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.38.2 \u2014 Dev mode fix: Traefik *.localhost support","description":"A focused developer-experience fix. The Traefik migration from localhost:port to *.localhost domains silently broke automatic Pro dev mode on all local Docker stacks \u2014 v4.38.2 restores zero-config development.","date":"2026-05-09T04:45:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"developer","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/developer"},{"inline":true,"label":"hotfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/hotfix"}],"readingTime":0.66,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.38.2-release","title":"Rentiva v4.38.2 \u2014 Dev mode fix: Traefik *.localhost support","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","developer","hotfix"],"date":"2026-05-09T04:45"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.39.0 \u2014 Customers Page React SPA (Faz 2)","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.39.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.38.1 \u2014 Audit-driven patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.38.1-release"}},"content":"A focused developer-experience fix. The Traefik migration from `localhost:port` to `*.localhost` domains silently broke automatic Pro dev mode on all local Docker stacks \u2014 v4.38.2 restores zero-config development.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n### \ud83d\udc1b Dev mode fix \u2014 `*.localhost` domain recognition\\n\\n`LicenseManager::isDevelopmentEnvironment()` now recognises `*.localhost` domains (Traefik reverse-proxy convention: `rentiva.localhost`, `bozcon.localhost`, etc.).\\n\\n**Before:** Only `.local` / `.test` / `.dev` / `.staging` TLDs were in the allowlist. `.localhost` was missing, so `isActive()` returned `false` on all Traefik-based environments \u2014 blocking Pro feature development without a real license or manual `wp-config.php` overrides.\\n\\n**After:** Zero-config Pro dev mode on any `*.localhost` domain. No constants, no license key, no config changes required.\\n\\n### \ud83e\uddea Test compatibility\\n\\n`VendorDirectoryRewriteTest`: whitelisted `WP_Block_Bindings_Registry::register` notice for WP 6.7 compatibility.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n1058 \u2192 **1070** PHPUnit (+12), 3332 assertions, 0 failures, 7 skipped. PHPCS: 0 errors."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.38.1-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.38.1-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-06-rentiva-v4.38.1-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-06-rentiva-v4.38.1-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.38.1 \u2014 Audit-driven patch","description":"A small but important patch on top of v4.38.0. After the Vendor Directory release we ran a /wp-conductor post-merge audit on the v4.37.0 \u2192 v4.38.0 chain \u2014 two real findings and a dormant production defect surfaced from the new test coverage. v4.38.1 closes them all so the six-release deploy bundle is clean.","date":"2026-05-06T03:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"directory","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/directory"},{"inline":true,"label":"marketplace","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/marketplace"}],"readingTime":3.12,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.38.1-release","title":"Rentiva v4.38.1 \u2014 Audit-driven patch","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","vendor","directory","marketplace"],"date":"2026-05-06T03:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.38.2 \u2014 Dev mode fix: Traefik *.localhost support","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.38.2-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.38.0 \u2014 Vendor Directory Page","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.38.0-release"}},"content":"A small but important patch on top of v4.38.0. After the Vendor Directory release we ran a `/wp-conductor` post-merge audit on the v4.37.0 \u2192 v4.38.0 chain \u2014 two real findings and a dormant production defect surfaced from the new test coverage. v4.38.1 closes them all so the six-release deploy bundle is clean.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n### \ud83d\udd34 Y\xdcKSEK \u2014 Admin slug edit collision\\n\\nWhen you edited a vendor\'s profile slug from the WordPress admin, the save path was writing the slug directly via `update_user_meta()` instead of going through `VendorSlugManager::change_slug()`. A leftover `// later` TODO from v4.37.0 Phase 1.3.\\n\\nThe practical impact: two admins (or admin + a vendor self-editing) submitting the same raw slug to different vendors would both succeed. `VendorProfileProvider::lookup_by_slug()` returns the first match, so the second vendor\'s public profile URL silently rendered the wrong vendor \u2014 for paying Pro customers, on a marketplace, indefinitely.\\n\\nThe save path now routes through `change_slug()`, which already handles sanitize + collision suffix (`-2`, `-3`...) + history sanitize atomically.\\n\\n### \ud83d\udfe1 ORTA \u2014 Directory vehicle_count vs Profile inconsistency\\n\\n`VendorDirectoryProvider::count_active_vehicles_for()` counted every `publish` vehicle, regardless of `_mhm_vehicle_lifecycle_status`. Profile-side `collect_vehicles()` filters by `lifecycle=\'active\'`. So a vendor with 2 active + 3 paused vehicles showed \\"5 vehicles\\" on the directory card and \\"2 vehicles\\" on the profile page. Marketplace data inconsistency = trust degradation.\\n\\nFixed by adding the same `meta_query` lifecycle filter to the count query.\\n\\n### \ud83d\udc1b Dormant production defect \u2014 pagination strict-type TypeError\\n\\nThe new combination tests in this patch surfaced something the existing v4.38.0 tests had never exercised: the directory pagination partial passed `$big = 999999999` (int) as the first argument to `str_replace()`. PHP 8.1+ strict types throw `TypeError`.\\n\\nExisting tests never seeded enough vendors to push past `per_page=12`, so the bug stayed dormant. Production sites running PHP 8.x would have crashed the directory page the moment a 13th active vendor pushed the result set past one page. Cast to string explicitly \u2014 same pattern WP core uses in identical callers.\\n\\nThis is the strongest argument for not having shipped v4.38.0 alone.\\n\\n### \ud83d\udccc Phase 5/6/7 paper-cuts\\n\\nThree small parity fixes that the v4.38.0 audit had pre-documented as deferred:\\n\\n- **VendorDirectorySeo register guard** \u2014 early return when an SEO plugin (Yoast / Rank Math / AIOSEO / SEOPress / The SEO Framework / SmartCrawl) owns the contract or the `mhm_rentiva_vendor_directory_seo_disable` filter is true. Parity with `VendorProfileSeo`\'s register guard. Plus a DocBlock spelling out the 3-arg filter signature for `build_meta_description($default, $vendor_count, $vehicle_count)`.\\n- **VendorDirectoryCacheInvalidator** \u2014 two parity guards: `!is_string($meta_key)` short-circuit on the user_meta hooks (rare WP edge case where `meta_key` arrives as an array \u2014 `VendorProfileCacheInvalidator` already had this guard), and a no-op early-return when `$new_status === $old_status` on the lifecycle hook (parity with the existing `on_comment_status` no-op in the same class). Avoids spurious cache flushes that defeat the 30-min directory cache.\\n- **Pagination/sort combination tests + `.current` scope** \u2014 three new tests covering pagination overflow, alpha sort with city filter, and paged query string on page 2. Verifies the `.current` pagination class stays scoped under `.mhm-vendor-directory-pagination` so theme `.current` rules can\'t hijack the styling.\\n\\n## Pipeline gates\\n\\n- **PHPUnit**: 1044 \u2192 **1058** tests, 3289 \u2192 **3320** assertions, 7 skipped, 0 fail\\n- **PHPCS**: **0 errors** (full project, CI parity gate)\\n- **Independent code review**: `merge ready, no KR\u0130T\u0130K/Y\xdcKSEK findings`\\n\\n## Deploy notice\\n\\nShip v4.38.1 together with the v4.37.0 + v4.37.1 + v4.37.2 + v4.37.3 + v4.38.0 chain \u2014 six releases in a single mhmrentiva.com deploy. No separate upgrade path needed."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.38.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.38.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-06-rentiva-v4.38.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-06-rentiva-v4.38.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.38.0 \u2014 Vendor Directory Page","description":"A public, Pro-gated vendor catalogue lands in Rentiva. Customers can now discover all your active vendors in one place \u2014 filter by city, badge status, and minimum rating; sort by reputation, recency, or alphabetically; click any card to land on the vendor\'s public profile (introduced in v4.37.0). This release closes the marketplace discovery loop.","date":"2026-05-06T01:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"directory","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/directory"},{"inline":true,"label":"marketplace","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/marketplace"}],"readingTime":3.54,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.38.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.38.0 \u2014 Vendor Directory Page","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","vendor","directory","marketplace"],"date":"2026-05-06T01:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.38.1 \u2014 Audit-driven patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.38.1-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.37.3 \u2014 CI lint hotfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.37.3-release"}},"content":"A public, Pro-gated vendor catalogue lands in Rentiva. Customers can now discover all your active vendors in one place \u2014 filter by city, badge status, and minimum rating; sort by reputation, recency, or alphabetically; click any card to land on the vendor\'s public profile (introduced in v4.37.0). This release closes the marketplace discovery loop.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## What\'s new\\n\\n- **`/vendors/` directory page** (TR `/bayiler/`) \u2014 single-page catalogue, server-rendered, no-JS friendly, SEO-first.\\n- **Filter set** \u2014 city dropdown (combined from vendor headquarters + vehicle pickup locations), badge toggle (Verified / New), minimum rating (3+ / 4+ / 5).\\n- **Default sort** \u2014 Highest rated first, with newest member as tie-breaker. Newest and alphabetical sort options also available.\\n- **Trio renderer** \u2014 `[rentiva_vendor_directory]` shortcode, Gutenberg block (`mhm-rentiva/vendor-directory`), Elementor widget. All three delegate to the same canonical render via `do_shortcode()` \u2014 no dual pipeline.\\n- **SEO** \u2014 Schema.org `ItemList` + `BreadcrumbList` JSON-LD with automatic SEO plugin probe (Yoast / Rank Math / AIOSEO / SEOPress / The SEO Framework / SmartCrawl). Plugin emits its own breadcrumb only when no SEO plugin is active. Filter args are reflected in the schema (canonical/render parity for crawlers).\\n- **30-min transient cache** \u2014 fast page loads, prefix-wildcard SQL invalidation when vendor data changes (status, city, reliability score, vehicle save, comment status, lifecycle, profile update). Bio and avatar changes intentionally don\'t invalidate (deliberate scope reduction \u2014 directory cards don\'t render those, would cause spurious flushes).\\n\\n## Pro Gate\\n\\nThe Vendor Directory is a Pro feature (`vendor_marketplace` flag). Lite users see a WordPress 404 on `/vendors/` (dispatch-time gate) and any block/widget/manual shortcode usage returns empty (render-time gate). Upgrade prompts live on `/pricing` and the existing pricing-table shortcode.\\n\\n## Compact card design\\n\\nEach vendor card shows: avatar (SVG initials fallback inherited from v4.37.2), display name, city, vehicle count (singular/plural), badge label (\u2713 Do\u011frulanm\u0131\u015f Bayi / Yeni Bayi), rating bar with count, \\"Profili g\xf6r\xfcnt\xfcle \u2192\\" CTA. The whole card is clickable (Popular Routes v4.34.1 pattern parity).\\n\\n## Mobile-first responsive grid\\n\\n- Desktop (\u22651024px): 4-col\\n- Tablet (\u2265600px): 2-col\\n- Phone (`<600px`): 1-col stack with native HTML5 `<details>` filter sheet (no-JS friendly)\\n\\nThe 600px breakpoint matches v4.37.2 B10 (phone-landscape 568px collapses cleanly). All CSS classes are scoped under `.mhm-vendor-directory-*` namespace \u2014 zero risk of theme/plugin generic class collision (`.label`, `.card`, `.filter-bar`, `.pagination` all forbidden per v4.37.2 B7 lesson).\\n\\n## i18n\\n\\n`_x(\'vendors\', \'URL slug\', \'mhm-rentiva\')` translates to `bayiler` in TR. Filter override `mhm_rentiva_vendor_directory_url_base` lets site owners set custom slugs (e.g., `dealers`, `firmalar`). Defensive ASCII sanitize + empty fallback. Locale change auto-flushes rewrite rules.\\n\\n~25 new EN source strings, all TR-translated. Plus 5 new filter hooks for developers:\\n\\n- `mhm_rentiva_vendor_directory_url_base`\\n- `mhm_rentiva_vendor_directory_per_page`\\n- `mhm_rentiva_vendor_directory_empty_message`\\n- `mhm_rentiva_vendor_directory_page_title`\\n- `mhm_rentiva_vendor_directory_meta_description`\\n- `mhm_rentiva_vendor_directory_seo_disable` (global kill switch)\\n\\n## Behind the scenes\\n\\nThree reviewer-caught bugs were closed before this release:\\n\\n1. **Phase 3 spec drift (KRITIK):** `VendorProfileProvider::aggregate_rating_for_vendor()` did not exist (Profile had a private `aggregate_rating()` with `average` key, not `avg`). The directory\'s test seam masked the bug \u2014 production rating filter, sort, and card data would have silently returned 0.0. New public wrapper added (additive, no internal Profile change).\\n2. **Phase 7 dispatch gap (KRITIK):** `template_include` filter was missing \u2014 the page wrapper would never serve. Closed in Phase 9 wiring.\\n3. **Phase 10 UI bug:** Browser smoke test caught a `<details>` collapse bug \u2014 filter dropdowns rendered in DOM but invisible (width: 0px) on desktop because the native UA stylesheet hides children of a closed `<details>`. Fixed with `<details open>` initial state.\\n\\n## Compatibility\\n\\n- WordPress 6.7+\\n- WooCommerce 8.0+ (existing vendor marketplace requirement)\\n- Elementor 3.20+ (optional, only if you use the widget)\\n- All 6 major SEO plugins coexist cleanly via class/constant probe \u2014 your existing SEO setup is preserved\\n\\n## Tests & metrics\\n\\n- **1044 PHPUnit tests** (1007 baseline + 37 new directory tests) \u2014 `OK, 3289 assertions, 7 skipped`\\n- **0 PHPCS errors** full project (CI parity gate)\\n- **8-checkpoint Chrome DevTools MCP browser smoke** green at desktop (1280px) and mobile (390px)\\n\\n## Get the release\\n\\nDownload v4.38.0 ZIP from GitHub v4.38.0."},{"id":"rentiva-v4.37.3-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.37.3-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-05-rentiva-v4.37.3-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-05-rentiva-v4.37.3-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.37.3 \u2014 CI lint hotfix","description":"A short patch to clear the CI red mark left behind by v4.37.2. A single WPCS sniff \u2014 \\"Opening PHP tag must be on a line by itself\\" \u2014 failed on the v4.37.2 hero template after merge. v4.37.3 refactors the block so the PHP opening tag stands alone. Lint-only \u2014 no behaviour change.","date":"2026-05-05T11:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"hotfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/hotfix"}],"readingTime":2.15,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.37.3-release","title":"Rentiva v4.37.3 \u2014 CI lint hotfix","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","hotfix"],"date":"2026-05-05T11:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.38.0 \u2014 Vendor Directory Page","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.38.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.37.2 \u2014 Vendor profile UX polish","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.37.2-release"}},"content":"A short patch to clear the CI red mark left behind by v4.37.2. A single WPCS sniff \u2014 \\"Opening PHP tag must be on a line by itself\\" \u2014 failed on the v4.37.2 hero template after merge. v4.37.3 refactors the block so the PHP opening tag stands alone. Lint-only \u2014 no behaviour change.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## What broke\\n\\nv4.37.2 introduced a dual-escape branch for the avatar `<img src>` that handles the new SVG data URI fallback (`esc_attr()` for our own SVG payload, `esc_url()` for everything else). The branch was written compactly:\\n\\n```php\\n<?php if (!empty($data[\'avatar_url\'])) :\\n    // 7 lines of comments and variable assignments\\n    $mhm_avatar_url    = (string) $data[\'avatar_url\'];\\n    $mhm_is_inline_svg = strpos($mhm_avatar_url, \'data:image/svg+xml\') === 0;\\n    ?>\\n    <img src=\\"<?php echo $mhm_is_inline_svg ? esc_attr(...) : esc_url(...); ?>\\" />\\n<?php endif; ?>\\n```\\n\\nWPCS Generic.PHP.LowerCaseKeyword\'s companion sniff treats line 19 \u2014 `<?php if (...) :` followed by multi-statement body \u2014 as a violation. The PHP opening tag should be alone on its line when the block runs across multiple statements.\\n\\n## Why it slipped through release prep\\n\\nThe release script we use before ZIP packaging is `composer phpcs:release`, which is scoped to release files only:\\n\\n```\\nphpcs:release: phpcs --standard=phpcs.xml \\\\\\n    mhm-rentiva.php uninstall.php src templates assets/blocks\\n```\\n\\nCI runs `composer phpcs` (no `:release`), which is the full project including `tests/`, with broader rules enabled. The hero template was in both scopes, but the sniff that triggered it only fires in the broader CI configuration.\\n\\nLesson going to KB: future release PRs need to run the broader `composer phpcs` before merging, not just `phpcs:release`. The two are not interchangeable.\\n\\n## The fix\\n\\n```php\\n<?php\\n// (8 lines of comments)\\n$mhm_avatar_url    = (string) ( $data[\'avatar_url\'] ?? \'\' );\\n$mhm_is_inline_svg = strpos($mhm_avatar_url, \'data:image/svg+xml\') === 0;\\n?>\\n<?php if ($mhm_avatar_url !== \'\') : ?>\\n    <img src=\\"...\\" />\\n<?php endif; ?>\\n```\\n\\n`<?php` opens its own line. Variable assignments are a separate block. The conditional is single-line. Same shape as the rest of the hero partial (`Member %s` block, badge branch).\\n\\n## Should you update?\\n\\nIf you\'re running v4.37.2 in production: **no**, this update is not necessary. The runtime is identical. v4.37.3 exists so the CI badge on the repo stays green and the testing.yml workflow remains a reliable gate.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- **PHPUnit:** 1007 / 3208 / 7 skipped \u2014 unchanged from v4.37.2\\n- **PHPCS:** 0 errors (full project)\\n\\n## Links\\n\\n- GitHub release v4.37.3\\n- Pull request #7"},{"id":"rentiva-v4.37.2-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.37.2-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-05-rentiva-v4.37.2-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-05-rentiva-v4.37.2-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.37.2 \u2014 Vendor profile UX polish","description":"Seven UX findings on the vendor profile page deferred from v4.37.0/v4.37.1 close in v4.37.2: a deterministic SVG initials avatar that replaces the Gravatar mystery-man silhouette without breaking third-party avatar plugins, a vehicle thumbnail cascade that falls back through featured image \u2192 gallery \u2192 compact card, an SEO defaults class that yields to Yoast / Rank Math / AIOSEO when present, a hero CTA stack with filterable URLs, scoped CSS class names, and a mobile breakpoint that finally collapses small screens to a single column.","date":"2026-05-05T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"profile","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/profile"},{"inline":true,"label":"seo","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/seo"}],"readingTime":7.3,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.37.2-release","title":"Rentiva v4.37.2 \u2014 Vendor profile UX polish","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","vendor","profile","seo"],"date":"2026-05-05T09:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.37.3 \u2014 CI lint hotfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.37.3-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.37.1 \u2014 Vendor profile hotfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.37.1-release"}},"content":"Seven UX findings on the vendor profile page deferred from v4.37.0/v4.37.1 close in v4.37.2: a deterministic SVG initials avatar that replaces the Gravatar mystery-man silhouette without breaking third-party avatar plugins, a vehicle thumbnail cascade that falls back through featured image \u2192 gallery \u2192 compact card, an SEO defaults class that yields to Yoast / Rank Math / AIOSEO when present, a hero CTA stack with filterable URLs, scoped CSS class names, and a mobile breakpoint that finally collapses small screens to a single column.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## Why a polish release\\n\\nv4.37.0 shipped the vendor profile page as a Pro feature. v4.37.1 hot-patched three functional bugs that smoke testing surfaced (badge wiring, rating-count semantic mismatch, review-stars meta-key fallback). What was left were the design rough edges \u2014 small things that don\'t break the page but make it look unfinished:\\n\\n- A grey Gravatar silhouette where every vendor without a registered Gravatar email looked identical.\\n- Vehicle cards with no photo and a single `\u2605` glyph next to a number, while the hero showed `\u2605\u2605\u2605\u2605\xbd`.\\n- A `<title>Rentiva Dev</title>` browser tab on the live profile, with no `<meta name=\\"description\\">` either.\\n- A `KONUM` section duplicating the city already in the hero.\\n- A `.label` class with no `.mhm-` prefix sitting next to theme defaults.\\n- A 3-vehicle vendor showing two cards on row one and a solo orphan on row two.\\n- No call-to-action \u2014 the page was passive information with no obvious next click.\\n\\nEach of these is a small fix on its own. The constraint is that the plugin is global \u2014 it has to land on every theme out there, with every avatar plugin, with every SEO plugin. So the polish isn\'t really about CSS. It\'s about choosing the right ecosystem hook for each fix so the plugin doesn\'t fight the rest of the site.\\n\\n## B4 \u2014 Deterministic SVG initials avatar\\n\\nThe Gravatar mystery-man fallback is recognisable but it\'s the same silhouette for every vendor without a registered email. With three or four vendors on a directory page (coming in v4.38.0), the visual sameness reads as \\"these vendors aren\'t real.\\"\\n\\n`VendorAvatarFallback` substitutes a coloured SVG circle bearing the vendor\'s two-letter initials. The colour comes from a deterministic hash of the display name (Slack / Gmail / Material pattern):\\n\\n```php\\n$hash = crc32($display_name);\\n$hue  = $hash % 360;\\nreturn hsl_to_hex($hue, 55, 50);\\n```\\n\\nSame name \u2192 same colour every render. Different vendors get visually distinct avatars without us picking a brand palette (we don\'t know the host site\'s brand).\\n\\nThe implementation hooks `get_avatar_data` at priority 99 \u2014 the default WordPress avatar pipeline runs at priority 10, and third-party avatar plugins (Simple Local Avatars, Avatar Privacy, WP User Avatar) typically register there too. By running last, we only act when nothing earlier resolved a real avatar. We further check that the URL we\'d be replacing is actually a Gravatar mystery-man placeholder (`?d=mm` / `?d=mp` / `?d=blank`) \u2014 a real Gravatar URL or a custom 3rd-party-resolved URL passes through unchanged.\\n\\nThe SVG is inline (`data:image/svg+xml;utf8,...`) \u2014 no external HTTP request to render the avatar.\\n\\nThere\'s a small but instructive bonus bug we caught here: WordPress\'s `esc_url()` strips the `data:` scheme by default \u2014 it\'s not on the protocol whitelist. The first browser smoke after wiring the fallback showed empty `src=\\"\\"` attributes (browsers fell back to the page URL as a relative reference). The hero partial now branches on the scheme:\\n\\n```php\\n$is_inline_svg = strpos($url, \'data:image/svg+xml\') === 0;\\necho $is_inline_svg ? esc_attr($url) : esc_url($url);\\n```\\n\\n`esc_attr()` is safe here because the SVG payload is built by our own class \u2014 no remote content, no user input.\\n\\n## B5 \u2014 Vehicle thumbnail cascade\\n\\n`Provider::collect_vehicles()` now resolves the card thumbnail through three steps:\\n\\n1. WP featured image (`get_the_post_thumbnail_url`).\\n2. First attachment ID in the Rentiva gallery meta \u2014 supports the canonical `_mhm_rentiva_gallery_images` plus the legacy `_mhm_gallery_images` and `_mhm_rentiva_gallery` aliases that `VehicleDetails::get_gallery()` already supports.\\n3. Empty string \u2014 the template renders a `--compact` modifier card with no image element instead of showing a generic \\"no image\\" placeholder rectangle.\\n\\nThe compact card is a deliberate choice. A site with five photographed vehicles and one without should not show four photographed cards plus one card with a grey \\"no image\\" rectangle \u2014 that one card sticks out. A subtly different compact card with just title + rating reads as intentional, not broken.\\n\\nVehicle card rating now also uses the same `stars_html()` helper as the hero \u2014 full half-star bar instead of a single `\u2605` glyph. Consistent rating display across the page.\\n\\n## B6 \u2014 `show_location` default flipped to `no`\\n\\nThis one\'s a near-deletion that we\'re keeping forward-compatible. The location section duplicated the city already in the hero (`\ud83d\udccd Antalya \xb7 2024\'den beri \xfcye`), so it added zero information.\\n\\nThe plan reserves the section for the v4.40.0+ Transfer Map enrichment \u2014 a real map pin makes the section worth its space. Until then, layouts that want it render explicitly with `show_location=\\"yes\\"`. The default just doesn\'t show it. Block.json default and Elementor widget control default both flipped to match the shortcode.\\n\\n## B7 \u2014 `.label` \u2192 `.mhm-vendor-section-label`\\n\\nA generic `.label` class is a collision waiting to happen \u2014 Bootstrap, theme starter kits, and several form plugins all ship a `.label` style. Renamed across all four section partials and the matching CSS rule. This is the kind of fix where you can\'t tell anything changed, which is exactly the point.\\n\\n## B8 \u2014 SEO defaults that yield to SEO plugins\\n\\n`VendorProfileSeo::register()` runs on every vendor profile request, but the first thing it does is check for active SEO plugins:\\n\\n```php\\nreturn class_exists(\'WPSEO_Frontend\')                   // Yoast\\n    || defined(\'WPSEO_VERSION\')                          // Yoast (alt)\\n    || class_exists(\'RankMath\')                          // Rank Math\\n    || defined(\'RANK_MATH_VERSION\')                      // Rank Math (alt)\\n    || defined(\'AIOSEO_VERSION\')                         // All-in-One SEO\\n    || class_exists(\'AIOSEO\\\\\\\\Plugin\\\\\\\\AIOSEO\')            // AIOSEO Pro\\n    || class_exists(\'Smartcrawl_Init\')                   // SmartCrawl\\n    || defined(\'SEOPRESS_VERSION\')                       // SEOPress\\n    || defined(\'THE_SEO_FRAMEWORK_VERSION\');             // The SEO Framework\\n```\\n\\nIf anything matches, we register no filters and emit no head tags. Those plugins have richer settings, dedicated UI for vendor-style content, and their users have already configured them \u2014 the last thing they need is our extra `<meta name=\\"description\\">` competing with theirs.\\n\\nWhen no real SEO plugin is active, we register two things:\\n\\n- A `document_title_parts` filter that replaces the theme default title with the vendor\'s display name. The site name part is left for themes that show it.\\n- A `wp_head` action at priority 1 that emits `<meta name=\\"description\\">` from the vendor\'s bio, trimmed to 155 characters at a word boundary so the description doesn\'t cut mid-word.\\n\\nSite owners can opt out entirely:\\n\\n```php\\nadd_filter(\'mhm_rentiva_vendor_profile_seo_disable\', \'__return_true\');\\n```\\n\\n## B9 \u2014 Hero CTA stack\\n\\nThe vendor profile was passive \u2014 read about a vendor, browse their cars, leave. The CTA stack adds a clear next click without bloating the hero:\\n\\n```html\\n<div class=\\"mhm-vendor-hero-cta\\">\\n    <a class=\\"mhm-vendor-hero-cta-primary\\" href=\\"#mhm-vendor-vehicles\\">View vehicles</a>\\n    \x3c!-- optional secondary --\x3e\\n    <a class=\\"mhm-vendor-hero-cta-secondary\\" href=\\"...\\">Send message</a>\\n</div>\\n```\\n\\nThe primary CTA is always shown \u2014 a same-page anchor scroll to the vehicle grid. The secondary CTA only renders when `mhm_rentiva_vendor_profile_message_url` filter returns a non-empty URL, so the button doesn\'t appear on sites that haven\'t wired a vendor messaging surface.\\n\\nBoth label and URL are filterable. A site with an external booking system can replace the primary CTA with a deep link; a directory site without messaging can hide the secondary entirely without overriding the partial.\\n\\n## B10 \u2014 Mobile breakpoint 480px \u2192 600px\\n\\nThe previous breakpoint at 480px meant phone-landscape (568px) and small tablets (480-768px range) showed two cards per row. With three vehicles the third card was a solo orphan on row two.\\n\\nThe breakpoint moved to 600px so anything below that \u2014 phone-landscape, small Android tablets, narrow custom layouts \u2014 collapses to a single column. With the cascade making more cards possible (gallery fallback when featured isn\'t set), the wider single-column zone reads better.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n| Suite | v4.37.1 | v4.37.2 |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| PHPUnit total | 987 | **1007** |\\n| Assertions | 3170 | **3208** |\\n| New regression files | \u2014 | VendorAvatarFallbackTest, VendorProfileSeoTest, VendorVehicleThumbnailCascadeTest, VendorProfileShowLocationDefaultTest |\\n| PHPCS errors | 0 | 0 |\\n\\nBrowser smoke validated all three test vendors at desktop (1920px) and mobile (390px). The existing `VendorProfileShortcodeTest::test_max_vehicles_attribute_caps_vehicle_count` regression also got an assertion update because v4.37.2 introduced a `mhm-vendor-vehicle-card--compact` modifier on the same class attribute, so the previous exact `class=\\"mhm-vendor-vehicle-card\\"` substring no longer matched. The assertion now uses a regex that matches the start of the card class on `<a>` openings.\\n\\n## Links\\n\\n- GitHub release v4.37.2\\n- Pull request #6"},{"id":"rentiva-v4.37.1-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.37.1-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-05-rentiva-v4.37.1-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-05-rentiva-v4.37.1-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.37.1 \u2014 Vendor profile hotfix","description":"Three smoke-test findings on the freshly-shipped v4.37.0 vendor profile page are closed in v4.37.1: a badge that defaulted to \\"New Vendor\\" for every vendor regardless of their score, a misleading \\"X reviews\\" label whose number was actually the count of booking-time star ratings, and review stars that disappeared on the public profile when reviews were imported from third-party plugins.","date":"2026-05-05T07:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"profile","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/profile"},{"inline":true,"label":"hotfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/hotfix"}],"readingTime":4.6,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.37.1-release","title":"Rentiva v4.37.1 \u2014 Vendor profile hotfix","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","vendor","profile","hotfix"],"date":"2026-05-05T07:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.37.2 \u2014 Vendor profile UX polish","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.37.2-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.37.0 \u2014 Vendor Public Profile Page","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.37.0-release"}},"content":"Three smoke-test findings on the freshly-shipped v4.37.0 vendor profile page are closed in v4.37.1: a badge that defaulted to \\"New Vendor\\" for every vendor regardless of their score, a misleading \\"X reviews\\" label whose number was actually the count of booking-time star ratings, and review stars that disappeared on the public profile when reviews were imported from third-party plugins.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## Why a hotfix on the same day\\n\\nv4.37.0 shipped this morning with a Pro feature spread across nine implementation phases and 78 new tests. PHPUnit was green, PHPCS was clean, the dispatch path worked end to end. But three of the bugs that made it into production were the kind that a unit test cannot easily catch:\\n\\n- A wiring bug \u2014 registration in the wrong init bucket \u2014 that a test fixture papers over by adding the filter callback explicitly.\\n- A semantic bug \u2014 the wrong word in a translatable string \u2014 that no machine-readable check flags.\\n- A defensive gap \u2014 only checking the canonical meta key, not the WC-standard alternative \u2014 that bites the day a third-party plugin imports a review.\\n\\nBrowser smoke surfaced all three within minutes of seeding three test vendors. The fix matrix is small enough that a same-day patch is the right call.\\n\\n## B1 \u2014 Badge stuck on \\"New Vendor\\"\\n\\nThe badge evaluator checks three thresholds: account age, reliability score, and lifetime completed bookings. The completed-bookings count comes from a filter:\\n\\n```php\\n$completed = (int) apply_filters(\\n    \'mhm_rentiva_vendor_completed_bookings_count\',\\n    0, // default\\n    $user_id\\n);\\n```\\n\\nThe production callback for that filter is registered in `VendorProfileExtension::register()`, which Plugin.php calls from `initialize_admin_services()` \u2014 the **admin-only** init bucket. On public requests (`is_admin() === false`), the bucket never runs and the callback never registers, so the count defaults to `0`. Every vendor falls into the `STATUS_NEW` branch, no matter their actual booking history.\\n\\nThis is the same `is_admin()` bucket trap we surfaced in Phase 9 \u2014 `VendorProfileSchema::register()` was originally placed in the admin-only bucket and got moved to a context-agnostic bucket once browser smoke caught the absent JSON-LD. `VendorProfileExtension::register()` legitimately belongs in the admin bucket (it owns admin-only profile screen hooks), but its filter-callback side effect leaked the bug into the frontend.\\n\\nThe fix is to make the badge work without depending on that wiring at all:\\n\\n```php\\n$default_completed = class_exists(ReliabilityScoreCalculator::class)\\n    ? ReliabilityScoreCalculator::count_completed_bookings($user_id, 9999)\\n    : 0;\\n\\n$completed = (int) apply_filters(\\n    \'mhm_rentiva_vendor_completed_bookings_count\',\\n    $default_completed,\\n    $user_id\\n);\\n```\\n\\nFilter callbacks can still override the count for special cases (lifecycle penalty suppressions, manual admin overrides, etc.). The default is now a real number, not a placeholder waiting for someone to wire it up.\\n\\n## B2 \u2014 Hero label \\"X reviews\\" was the wrong word\\n\\nThe vendor profile hero shows aggregate rating data:\\n\\n```\\n\u2605\u2605\u2605\u2605\xbd 4,8 ( 25 de\u011ferlendirme )\\n```\\n\\nThat `25` is the sum of `_mhm_rentiva_rating_count` across the vendor\'s active vehicles \u2014 booking-time star ratings, set when a customer completes a rental and rates the vehicle. The `Recent Reviews` section below the hero is a separate stream \u2014 WP review comments on the same vehicle posts. A vendor can easily have 25 booking ratings and 4 written review comments. The hero said \\"25 reviews\\", the section showed 4, and the math didn\'t add up.\\n\\nThe fix is the easy half of the problem: change the i18n string from `%d review` / `%d reviews` to `%d rating` / `%d ratings` (Turkish: `%d de\u011ferlendirme`). Same number, honest label.\\n\\nThe harder version of this question \u2014 should the hero show the WP comment count instead of the booking-rating count? \u2014 is deferred. The booking-rating average is the more useful metric for buyers because it\'s tied to completed transactions, not opinions. Renaming the label preserves that information.\\n\\n## B3 \u2014 Review stars empty for third-party imports\\n\\n`VendorProfileProvider::collect_reviews()` builds the per-review render data:\\n\\n```php\\n\'rating\' => (int) get_comment_meta($comment_id, \'mhm_rating\', true),\\n```\\n\\n`mhm_rating` is Rentiva\'s canonical key, set by `VehicleRatingForm` and the `ReviewEnforcer` normalization hook. Reviews submitted through Rentiva\'s own form get this key reliably. But a vendor whose reviews are imported from a third-party plugin \u2014 WC product reviews migrated into vehicles, Site Reviews / Customer Reviews for WooCommerce, manual database seeds \u2014 typically writes the WC-standard `rating` key. Without a fallback, those reviews show up on the profile with empty stars even though the rating value is right there in the database.\\n\\nThe fix is a one-helper change:\\n\\n```php\\nprivate static function resolve_review_rating(int $comment_id): int\\n{\\n    $rating = (int) get_comment_meta($comment_id, \'mhm_rating\', true);\\n    if ($rating > 0) {\\n        return $rating;\\n    }\\n    return (int) get_comment_meta($comment_id, \'rating\', true);\\n}\\n```\\n\\nCanonical wins when present; WC-standard falls through when it doesn\'t.\\n\\n## Validation\\n\\nThree test vendors, seeded directly into the local DB:\\n\\n| Vendor | Score | Bookings | Approved | Expected | Got |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| Akif Y\u0131ld\u0131z | 92 | 20 | 200 days ago | Verified | \u2713 Do\u011frulanm\u0131\u015f Bayi |\\n| Zeynep Demir | 88 | 11 | 335 days ago | Verified | \u2713 Do\u011frulanm\u0131\u015f Bayi |\\n| Mehmet \xc7elik | 45 | 2 | 21 days ago | New | Yeni Bayi |\\n\\nAll three render star ratings on every review item; the hero label reads `X de\u011ferlendirme` (TR) / `X ratings` (EN).\\n\\nPHPUnit went from **982 \u2192 987** with the two new regression test classes (`VendorBadgeDefaultFallbackTest` 2 tests, `VendorProfileReviewRatingFallbackTest` 3 tests). The badge fallback test deliberately omits the filter callback registration so it would have failed against v4.37.0.\\n\\n## Links\\n\\n- GitHub release v4.37.1\\n- Pull request #5"},{"id":"rentiva-v4.37.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.37.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-05-05-rentiva-v4.37.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-05-05-rentiva-v4.37.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.37.0 \u2014 Vendor Public Profile Page","description":"Every approved vendor now has a public face. v4.37.0 ships a dedicated profile page at /vendor// (or /bayi// on Turkish sites), wired up across a canonical shortcode, a Gutenberg block, and an Elementor widget \u2014 all delegating to a single renderer. Schema.org LocalBusiness JSON-LD goes out in `` so search engines and social previews can read the vendor as a discrete entity, not as a slice of the homepage.","date":"2026-05-05T05:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"profile","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/profile"},{"inline":true,"label":"seo","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/seo"}],"readingTime":5.37,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.37.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.37.0 \u2014 Vendor Public Profile Page","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","vendor","profile","seo"],"date":"2026-05-05T05:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.37.1 \u2014 Vendor profile hotfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.37.1-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.36.0 \u2014 Transfer Booking Add-ons","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.36.0-release"}},"content":"Every approved vendor now has a public face. v4.37.0 ships a dedicated profile page at `/vendor/<slug>/` (or `/bayi/<slug>/` on Turkish sites), wired up across a canonical shortcode, a Gutenberg block, and an Elementor widget \u2014 all delegating to a single renderer. Schema.org `LocalBusiness` JSON-LD goes out in `<head>` so search engines and social previews can read the vendor as a discrete entity, not as a slice of the homepage.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nFor most of Rentiva\'s life, vendors lived inside the platform\'s own listing screens. Customers could find a specific vehicle, but they had no way to land on a *vendor* \u2014 to read who runs the fleet, see their reliability score and verification badge, browse their other cars, and read past reviews. Search engines had nothing to index either: no canonical URL, no schema, no breadcrumbs.\\n\\nv4.37.0 closes that gap. Each vendor gets a stable URL, a structured profile, and a renderer that\'s reusable wherever you want to surface vendor information \u2014 a homepage block, an Elementor template, a shortcode dropped into a custom page.\\n\\n## i18n-aware base URL\\n\\nThe URL pattern follows WooCommerce\'s translatable `/shop/`, `/product/` slugs:\\n\\n- English site: `/vendor/<slug>/`\\n- Turkish site: `/bayi/<slug>/`\\n\\nThe base segment comes from `_x(\'vendor\', \'URL slug\', \'mhm-rentiva\')`, runs through `apply_filters(\'mhm_rentiva_vendor_profile_url_base\', \u2026)` for site-owner override, then `urldecode()` and `sanitize_title()` for safety. Any locale just translates the `vendor` URL slug context and the rewrite rule rebuilds itself on the next `flush_rewrite_rules()`.\\n\\nWhen a vendor\'s URL slug changes (admin edits the slug field, or the auto-generator picks a different collision suffix), the previous slug is appended to a slug-history list and a 301 redirect is registered to the new canonical URL. Old links don\'t 404 \u2014 they redirect.\\n\\n## Single canonical renderer\\n\\nThree render paths, one source of truth:\\n\\n- `[rentiva_vendor_profile]` shortcode\\n- `mhm-rentiva/vendor-profile` Gutenberg block\\n- `mhm_rentiva_vendor_profile` Elementor widget\\n\\nThe block and widget delegate to the shortcode. The shortcode delegates to a partials chain (`vendor-profile-hero.php`, `vendor-profile-vehicles.php`, `vendor-profile-reviews.php`, `vendor-profile-location.php`). Whichever surface the customer arrives at \u2014 a public profile URL routed by the rewrite rule, a block embedded on a custom page, or an Elementor widget on a builder page \u2014 the HTML is identical.\\n\\nThis is the same Render Parity discipline Rentiva has applied across 19 blocks and 20 widgets: blocks/widgets never duplicate render logic, they delegate.\\n\\n## Schema.org for SEO\\n\\nThe `<head>` of a vendor profile carries a Schema.org `LocalBusiness` JSON-LD payload:\\n\\n```json\\n{\\n  \\"@context\\": \\"https://schema.org\\",\\n  \\"@type\\": \\"LocalBusiness\\",\\n  \\"name\\": \\"Vendor display name\\",\\n  \\"url\\": \\"https://example.com/vendor/<slug>/\\",\\n  \\"image\\": \\"https://example.com/.../avatar.jpg\\"\\n}\\n```\\n\\nYoast SEO and Rank Math run their own canonical filter chains; v4.37.0 hooks `wpseo_canonical` and `rank_math/frontend/canonical` at `PHP_INT_MAX-10` to make sure the vendor profile URL wins over the homepage canonical that those plugins default to for non-singular pages.\\n\\nHostile vendor names can\'t break the schema either \u2014 the JSON encoder uses `JSON_HEX_TAG`, so a hostile `<\/script>` injection in a `display_name` becomes hex-encoded instead of escaping the script element. And if `url_for_user()` returns an empty string (vendor has no slug yet), the schema build short-circuits and emits nothing instead of an invalid `LocalBusiness` with a missing URL.\\n\\n## Vendor admin updates\\n\\nTwo new fields appear under the vendor\'s user profile screen:\\n\\n- **Vendor avatar** \u2014 a Media Library uploader. The chosen attachment is what `LocalBusiness.image` and the profile hero render. Falls back to a Gravatar of the user\'s email when unset.\\n- **Public Profile URL Slug** \u2014 a text field with a live collision check. The auto-generator strips diacritics (`Yeni Sat\u0131c\u0131` \u2192 `yeni-satici`) and appends a numeric suffix on collision (`yeni-satici-2`).\\n\\nIdempotent slug backfill runs once on upgrade. Existing vendors get an ASCII slug derived from their display name; the migration is gated on a version flag and never overwrites a slug an operator already set.\\n\\n## Verified Vendor / New Vendor badges\\n\\nThe profile hero shows one of two badges based on admin-configurable thresholds:\\n\\n- **Verified Vendor** \u2014 vendor has at least N completed bookings AND a reliability score at or above the configured floor.\\n- **New Vendor** \u2014 vendor was approved within the last N days.\\n\\nBoth thresholds live under MHM Rentiva \u2192 Settings, default to sensible values (30 completed bookings + 80 reliability score; 90 days for new), and feed the same `VendorBadgeEligibility` pure-logic class used everywhere a badge is rendered.\\n\\n## Cache invalidation that knows what changed\\n\\nVendor profile data caches in a transient keyed by user ID + cap suffix. Seven triggers invalidate it:\\n\\n- Vendor user-meta change (display name, slug, avatar, bio, badge override, etc.)\\n- Booking save (a new completed booking can shift reliability score)\\n- Comment status change (a newly approved review affects the average rating)\\n- Vehicle lifecycle change (a paused vehicle drops out of the vendor\'s vehicle list)\\n- Profile update hook (`profile_update`)\\n\\nThe cache key suffix encodes the maximum vehicle and review version stamps, so the invalidator uses an SQL prefix-wildcard delete (`DELETE FROM \u2026_options WHERE option_name LIKE \'_transient_mhm_rentiva_vendor_profile_<user_id>_%\'`) instead of needing to compute the exact suffix in advance.\\n\\n## i18n cleanup\\n\\nPhase 10 of the implementation refreshed 19 Turkish translations:\\n\\n- Four newly filled (was rendering English fallback): \\"Public Profile URL Slug\\", \\"Member %s\\", \\"No reviews yet \u2014 be the first to leave one.\\", \\"\u2192 %s\\"\\n- Fifteen fuzzy markers cleared: \\"Vendor Avatar\\" \u2192 \\"Bayi Avatar\u0131\\", \\"Verified Vendor\\" \u2192 \\"Do\u011frulanm\u0131\u015f Bayi\\", \\"New Vendor\\" \u2192 \\"Yeni Bayi\\", \\"Recent Reviews\\" \u2192 \\"Son De\u011ferlendirmeler\\", \\"View all vehicles \u2192\\" \u2192 \\"T\xfcm ara\xe7lar\u0131 g\xf6r\xfcnt\xfcle \u2192\\", and ten more.\\n\\nBrowser smoke confirmed zero English fallback leak on the live profile.\\n\\n## Pro-gated\\n\\nThe whole feature lives behind `Mode::canUseVendorMarketplace`, the same gate that protects the existing vendor admin panel. Lite installs see no rewrite rule, no admin fields, no schema emission. Dev sites can bypass the gate locally with `define(\'MHM_RENTIVA_DEV_PRO\', true);` in `wp-config.php`.\\n\\n## Stats\\n\\n- **PHPUnit:** 904 \u2192 **982** (+78 across nine implementation phases)\\n- **Assertions:** 3162\\n- **PHPCS:** 0 errors\\n- **i18n:** 19 TR translations refreshed (4 newly filled, 15 fuzzy cleared)\\n- **New PHP classes:** `VendorProfileUrlBase`, `VendorProfileRewrite`, `VendorProfileProvider`, `VendorProfileSchema`, `VendorProfileExtension`, `VendorProfileCacheInvalidator`, `VendorSlugManager`, `VendorSlugMigration`, `VendorBadgeEligibility`, `VendorProfileWidget`, `VendorProfileBlock`\\n- **Render surfaces:** 1 shortcode + 1 block + 1 Elementor widget delegating to a single renderer\\n\\n## Links\\n\\n- GitHub release v4.37.0\\n- Pull request #4"},{"id":"rentiva-v4.36.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.36.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-29-rentiva-v4.36.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-29-rentiva-v4.36.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.36.0 \u2014 Transfer Booking Add-ons","description":"Transfer customers can finally pick add-ons. v4.36.0 extends the existing vehicle_addon post type with a context taxonomy (rental / transfer / both) and three pricing types (per booking / per day / per passenger). When a customer clicks \\"Add to cart\\" on a transfer search result, a modal slides up showing the relevant add-ons with a live multiplier-aware total.","date":"2026-04-30T01:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"transfer","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/transfer"},{"inline":true,"label":"add-ons","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/add-ons"}],"readingTime":3.8,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.36.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.36.0 \u2014 Transfer Booking Add-ons","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","transfer","add-ons"],"date":"2026-04-30T01:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.37.0 \u2014 Vendor Public Profile Page","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.37.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.35.0 \u2014 Vendor Report & Appeal System","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.35.0-release"}},"content":"Transfer customers can finally pick add-ons. v4.36.0 extends the existing `vehicle_addon` post type with a context taxonomy (rental / transfer / both) and three pricing types (per booking / per day / per passenger). When a customer clicks \\"Add to cart\\" on a transfer search result, a modal slides up showing the relevant add-ons with a live multiplier-aware total.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nUp to v4.35.0, the add-on system was rental-only. The transfer add-to-cart handler had a hard-coded `\'selected_addons\' => array()` placeholder where the rental flow would have carried the customer\'s selections. That meant zero ancillary revenue on transfers \u2014 no child seats, no extra waiting time, no welcome banners, no VIP assistant. Vendors who already had a perfectly good catalogue of add-ons couldn\'t surface any of it on the transfer side.\\n\\nv4.36.0 closes that gap **without forking the data model**. One CPT, one catalogue, one place for the vendor to manage add-ons. The same record can target a rental booking, a transfer, or both.\\n\\n## The data model in one paragraph\\n\\n`vehicle_addon` gains an `addon_context` taxonomy with three default terms \u2014 `rental`, `transfer`, `both` \u2014 and a `_mhm_addon_pricing_type` post meta with three enum values \u2014 `per_booking` (flat), `per_day` (rental days \xd7 price), `per_passenger` (passenger count \xd7 price). The pricing types form an `(allowed \xd7 context)` matrix: `per_day` only makes sense for rental, `per_passenger` only for transfer, `per_booking` works in both. A radio metabox on the admin edit screen, a JS-driven dynamic select, and a server-side validator all enforce the same rule.\\n\\n## The transfer modal\\n\\nWhen a search result\'s \\"Add to cart\\" button is clicked, a vanilla-JS modal opens with the available transfer add-ons. Required add-ons are pre-checked and locked. Optional ones come with a live total that respects the pricing type:\\n\\n- `per_booking` shows `+ 50 \u20ba` (flat).\\n- `per_passenger` shows `+ 15 \u20ba \xd7 3 yolcu = 45 \u20ba` (live multiplied by the trip\'s passenger count).\\n\\nThe footer line keeps a running grand total: `Vehicle 280 \u20ba + add-ons 95 \u20ba = 375 \u20ba`. \\"Cancel\\" backs out without dispatching anything; \\"Add to cart\\" submits the selected IDs alongside the existing vehicle/origin/destination/datetime payload.\\n\\nIf a vendor configured zero transfer-context add-ons, the modal is suppressed entirely \u2014 the existing direct-add behaviour kicks in untouched.\\n\\n## Migration that never overwrites\\n\\nExisting add-on records are auto-assigned to `rental` context with `per_booking` pricing on the first `init` after upgrade. The data lane is gated by an option flag and never overwrites a value the operator has already set. If the flag is manually reset, the migration re-runs idempotently \u2014 operator overrides survive.\\n\\nThis is the same schema/data lane separation the codebase has used since v4.27.4: the schema lane (taxonomy register + default term seed) runs every request as a normal WP API call; the data lane (legacy backfill) runs once and stops.\\n\\n## One pricing calculator, both flows\\n\\n`AddonPricingCalculator::calculate( $addon_id, $context )` is the single source of truth. The rental booking total filter, the transfer cart AJAX handler, the admin booking detail page, the WC order item meta \u2014 all of them go through this one helper. The context array is shaped `{rental_days?, adults?, children?}`; rental fills `rental_days`, transfer fills `adults` and `children`, and the calculator picks whichever it needs based on the addon\'s pricing type.\\n\\nThis is the cheapest insurance against the rental and transfer math drifting apart over time.\\n\\n## Lite limit unchanged\\n\\nLite still caps at 4 published add-ons total \u2014 combined rental and transfer. The vendor decides how to split the slots. The admin notice copy was updated to make this explicit (\\"Lite s\xfcr\xfcm\xfcnde en fazla 4 ek hizmet ekleyebilirsiniz (kiralama + transfer ortak)\u2026\\").\\n\\n## Stats\\n\\n- **PHPUnit:** 864 \u2192 **904** (+40 across 7 new test classes)\\n- **PHPCS:** 0 errors\\n- **Files:** 7 new PHP classes, 3 new CSS/JS files, ~10 modified PHP files\\n- **i18n:** all sources English; Turkish translations in `mhm-rentiva-tr_TR.po`; JS strings localised via `wp_localize_script`\\n- **Schema:** `CURRENT_VERSION` 3.6.0 \u2192 3.7.0\\n\\n## What ships next\\n\\n- **v4.37.0** \u2014 Transfer Locations Map View. The deferred `per_km` pricing type ships here, where its UX value (visualising distance against a haritada) finally has the supporting context.\\n- **v4.38.0** \u2014 Vendor Directory Page (Dokan-style standalone catalogue).\\n- **v4.39.0** \u2014 Vendor Profile Page (unblocks Vehicle Lifecycle Phase 5).\\n\\n## Links\\n\\n- GitHub release v4.36.0\\n- Pull request #3"},{"id":"rentiva-v4.35.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.35.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-29-rentiva-v4.35.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-29-rentiva-v4.35.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.35.0 \u2014 Vendor Report & Appeal System","description":"A shared infrastructure for vendor \u2192 admin reports lands in v4.35.0. Five contexts, one custom table, one shared modal, one admin \\"Bayi Raporlar\u0131\\" page. Plus the withdrawal/pause reason capture flow: when a vendor withdraws a vehicle and explains why, the penalty is suspended until an admin reviews the appeal \u2014 accept, the vendor keeps their score; reject, the penalty applies retroactively.","date":"2026-04-30T00:30:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"marketplace","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/marketplace"},{"inline":true,"label":"penalty","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/penalty"}],"readingTime":4.97,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.35.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.35.0 \u2014 Vendor Report & Appeal System","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","vendor","marketplace","penalty"],"date":"2026-04-30T00:30"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.36.0 \u2014 Transfer Booking Add-ons","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.36.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.34.2 \u2014 Transfer-card icon styling hotfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.34.2-release"}},"content":"A shared infrastructure for vendor \u2192 admin reports lands in v4.35.0. Five contexts, one custom table, one shared modal, one admin \\"Bayi Raporlar\u0131\\" page. Plus the **withdrawal/pause reason capture** flow: when a vendor withdraws a vehicle and explains why, the penalty is suspended until an admin reviews the appeal \u2014 accept, the vendor keeps their score; reject, the penalty applies retroactively.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nUntil v4.35.0 vendors had no structured way to talk back to the admin. Booking issues (no-show customer, damage), vehicle actions that triggered automatic penalties, score deductions they thought were unfair \u2014 all of these went straight to email or Slack, off the platform. The marketplace had a one-way feedback loop.\\n\\nv4.35.0 closes the loop with a single piece of shared infrastructure. The same modal, table, and admin page handle all five contexts. The only thing that varies is the trigger location and the side-effect on resolution.\\n\\n## The five contexts\\n\\n| Context | When | Trigger | Resolution side-effect |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| `booking` | Customer issue (no-show, damage, dispute) | \\"Sorun Bildir\\" on the vendor booking card (button existed since v4.26.5, JS now wired) | None \u2014 informational |\\n| `vehicle` | Appeal a paused/withdrawn vehicle action | \\"\u0130tiraz Et\\" on listings page (paused/withdrawn states only) | None \u2014 admin guidance |\\n| `vehicle_action` | **Reason capture during withdraw/pause** | Modal automatically opens when a vendor clicks Withdraw or Pause | Reject \u2192 deferred penalty applied; resolve \u2192 vendor keeps score |\\n| `penalty` | Appeal an already-applied penalty | \\"Appeal\\" button on each penalty row in score history | (v4.36.0+ \u2014 ledger compensating entry helper) |\\n| `general` | \\"Y\xf6neticiye Yaz\\" \u2014 direct line to admin | Footer link on every vendor panel page | None |\\n\\n## The Not 2 augment \u2014 withdrawal reason capture\\n\\nBefore v4.35.0, withdrawing a vehicle meant a `confirm()` dialog (\\"Are you sure? A penalty may apply.\\") and an immediate score deduction + ledger debit. There was no way to tell the platform why the vehicle had to leave.\\n\\nNow the lifecycle JS captures the reason in a proper modal and POSTs it alongside the `mhm_vehicle_lifecycle_withdraw` AJAX call. The AJAX handler creates a `vehicle_action` report **before** calling the Manager. Inside the Manager, a new filter \u2014 `mhm_rentiva_before_apply_penalty` \u2014 fires:\\n\\n```php\\n$apply_penalty = (bool) apply_filters(\\n    \'mhm_rentiva_before_apply_penalty\',\\n    true,\\n    $vehicle_id,\\n    $vendor_id,\\n    \'withdrawal\',\\n    $penalty\\n);\\n\\nif ($apply_penalty) {\\n    ReliabilityScoreCalculator::update($vendor_id, \'withdraw\', $vehicle_id);\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThe same filter wraps `PenaltyRecorder::record_penalty()` so the ledger debit stays in lockstep with the score. `PenaltySuspensionHook::maybe_suspend()` returns `false` when an open `vehicle_action` report exists for the vendor + vehicle pair.\\n\\nState and side-effects are decoupled: the vehicle still transitions to `withdrawn` (post status, lifecycle meta, cooldown date \u2014 all set), but the score and ledger are paused. When the admin resolves the report:\\n\\n- **Resolved** (vendor wins) \u2014 no-op. Score and ledger were never touched. The vendor lost zero points and zero TL.\\n- **Rejected** \u2014 `VendorReportService::apply_deferred_penalty()` calls `ReliabilityScoreCalculator::update()` to recompute (the withdrawal is in state, so the score now drops) and re-runs `PenaltyRecorder::record_penalty()` to write the ledger debit. The penalty applies retroactively.\\n\\n## Architecture in one paragraph\\n\\n`VendorReportRepository` is the DB layer (CRUD on the new `wp_mhm_rentiva_vendor_reports` custom table; per-request `has_open_report_for()` cache so the dual filter hook costs one DB query). `VendorReportService` is the business layer (validation, FSM, side-effects, hook firing for emails). `VendorReportAjaxHandler` is the transport. `PenaltySuspensionHook` is the bridge to the existing penalty pipeline. `VendorReportsAdminPage` is the admin UI. `VendorReportAssets` enqueues the shared modal and JS on every vendor-facing page. The only thing that touches multiple layers is the filter hook itself, and that\'s deliberate \u2014 the hook is the seam between the vendor-report subsystem and the lifecycle subsystem.\\n\\n## Plan-vs-codebase reconciliation\\n\\nThe original plan was written 2026-04-15 and assumed nine things about the codebase that turned out to be false. A comprehensive pre-implementation audit caught all of them:\\n\\n1. `src/Admin/Penalty/` directory \u2014 does not exist; penalty code lives in `src/Admin/Vehicle/`.\\n2. `PenaltyService::cancel()` / `apply_pending()` \u2014 no such class. Removed from design; service layer calls `ReliabilityScoreCalculator` and `PenaltyRecorder` directly.\\n3. `mhm_rentiva_before_apply_penalty` filter \u2014 did not exist. Introduced in this release.\\n4. `penalty_record_id` is BIGINT \u2014 penalties are anonymous ledger entries with UUIDs. Schema changed to `VARCHAR(64) context_id`.\\n5. Score deduction is hook-suspendable \u2014 actually synchronous before any hook fires. Filter must wrap the score update inline.\\n6. Migration file `0042_create_vendor_reports.php` \u2014 no sequential numbering convention. Renamed `VendorReportsMigration`, registered via `DatabaseMigrator::run_migrations()` after `CURRENT_VERSION` bump.\\n7. \\"Sorun Bildir\\" button needs adding to vendor-bookings.php \u2014 already exists since v4.26.5. Build sequence simplified.\\n8. \\"Report Issue\\" string needs adding to .po \u2014 already translated. List trimmed.\\n9. No Mode gating mentioned \u2014 `Mode::canUseVendorMarketplace()` required on all new admin pages, AJAX handlers, email registrations, and asset enqueues.\\n\\nThe user explicitly requested \\"Vendor ile ilgili t\xfcm dosyalar\u0131 detayl\u0131 incele. Eksik, g\xf6zden ka\xe7an bir \u015fey olmas\u0131n\\" before implementation began. That nudge is what surfaced these. Plan files written months earlier are not authoritative; the codebase is.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- PHPUnit: 840 \u2192 864 (+24 \u2014 Repository 10, Service 8, PenaltySuspensionHook 6)\\n- PHPCS: 0 errors\\n- Runtime smoke test: admin \\"Bayi Raporlar\u0131\\" page renders, all status + context filters in TR, empty state correctly shown, full migration applied via `DatabaseMigrator` on plugin activate.\\n\\n## Compatibility\\n\\n- No license-server upgrade required.\\n- Backwards compatible: lifecycle AJAX submissions without a `reason` POST parameter behave exactly as in v4.34.x (no report created, normal penalty applied). Older vendors don\'t break.\\n- Dev sites need `define(\'MHM_RENTIVA_DEV_PRO\', true);` in `wp-config.php` to bypass the Pro gate while testing.\\n\\n## What\'s next\\n\\nThe roadmap continues with the **transfer wave**: v4.36.0 adds context-aware add-ons (extending `vehicle_addon` CPT with an `addon_context` taxonomy), v4.37.0 adds a transfer-locations map view. After that the **vendor wave** picks up \u2014 directory page (v4.38.0) and the long-deferred Phase 5 vendor public profile (v4.39.0).\\n\\n\u2014 GitHub release v4.35.0"},{"id":"rentiva-v4.34.2-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.34.2-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-29-rentiva-v4.34.2-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-29-rentiva-v4.34.2-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.34.2 \u2014 Transfer-card icon styling hotfix","description":"A pure CSS hotfix on top of v4.34.1. The favorite (heart) and compare icons on the transfer-search results page rendered as oversized solid-blue blocks instead of the small round white icons used on the rental grid/list. v4.34.2 restores parity.","date":"2026-04-30T00:15:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"transfer","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/transfer"},{"inline":true,"label":"css","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/css"},{"inline":true,"label":"hotfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/hotfix"}],"readingTime":2.46,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.34.2-release","title":"Rentiva v4.34.2 \u2014 Transfer-card icon styling hotfix","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","transfer","css","hotfix"],"date":"2026-04-30T00:15"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.35.0 \u2014 Vendor Report & Appeal System","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.35.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.34.1 \u2014 Popular Routes Clickable Cards","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.34.1-release"}},"content":"A pure CSS hotfix on top of [v4.34.1](/blog/rentiva-v4.34.1-release). The favorite (heart) and compare icons on the transfer-search results page rendered as oversized solid-blue blocks instead of the small round white icons used on the rental grid/list. v4.34.2 restores parity.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What broke\\n\\nA user clicked through from a Popular Routes card to the transfer-search results and noticed the heart and compare buttons looked nothing like their rental-grid counterparts:\\n\\n- **Expected:** 32\xd732 round button, white translucent background, red heart outline icon, top-right of the card image.\\n- **Got:** 100\xd755px solid-blue block with a tiny white heart inside, padded like a generic CTA button.\\n\\nPHPUnit was green. PHPCS was clean. But the icons in the live DOM were broken.\\n\\n## Root cause\\n\\n`vehicle-card.css` styles the icon buttons with this rule:\\n\\n```css\\n.mhm-vehicle-card .mhm-card-favorite {\\n  width: 32px; height: 32px; padding: 0;\\n  border-radius: 50%; background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);\\n  /* ...etc */\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThe `.mhm-vehicle-card` parent prefix is not decorative \u2014 it\'s a **deliberate specificity hack**. The CSS comment in the file even says so:\\n\\n> Parent selector raises specificity to (0,2,0) \u2014 overrides Astra\'s inline button rule (0,0,1) without needing `!important`. Works across themes.\\n\\nAstra (and other themes) ship a generic `button` style that pads buttons and applies a solid background. The plugin\'s intent was to outweigh that without an `!important` arms race, by leaning on selector specificity.\\n\\nTransfer cards, however, are rendered with `.mhm-transfer-card` as the parent class \u2014 not `.mhm-vehicle-card`. So the styling rule never matched, the (0,0,1) Astra rule won by default, and you got a 100\xd755px solid-blue button.\\n\\nThe buttons themselves use the same markup (`.mhm-card-favorite` / `.mhm-card-compare`) \u2014 only the parent wrapper class differs.\\n\\n## Fix\\n\\nList both parents in each selector:\\n\\n```css\\n.mhm-vehicle-card .mhm-card-favorite,\\n.mhm-transfer-card .mhm-card-favorite {\\n  /* same 32\xd732 round-icon rules as before */\\n}\\n\\n.mhm-vehicle-card .mhm-card-compare,\\n.mhm-transfer-card .mhm-card-compare {\\n  /* same */\\n}\\n```\\n\\nSpecificity stays at (0,2,0), Astra\'s `button` rule is still outweighed without `!important`, and the icon styling is now identical across rental and transfer surfaces.\\n\\n## What this taught us\\n\\nPHPUnit + PHPCS are necessary but not sufficient gates. CSS scoping bugs slip through both:\\n\\n- PHPUnit doesn\'t see CSS at all.\\n- PHPCS sees CSS as text, not as rules-applied-to-DOM.\\n\\nThe only signal that catches this class of bug is **looking at the live DOM**. v4.34.0 and v4.34.1 ran the runtime smoke test on the homepage Popular Routes section \u2014 and that section was correct. The transfer-search results page was a separate surface that the smoke test didn\'t visit. v4.34.2 closes the loop: when a feature touches multiple downstream surfaces, the smoke test has to follow the click path, not just inspect the entry point.\\n\\n## Compatibility\\n\\n- No license-server upgrade.\\n- No breaking changes \u2014 the affected CSS only widens the rule set; nothing existing breaks.\\n\\n\u2014 GitHub release v4.34.2"},{"id":"rentiva-v4.34.1-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.34.1-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-29-rentiva-v4.34.1-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-29-rentiva-v4.34.1-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.34.1 \u2014 Popular Routes Clickable Cards","description":"A small but high-leverage patch on top of v4.34.0. Popular Routes cards are now clickable, and clicking one deep-links into the transfer-search form with origin and destination pre-filled. The visitor\'s path goes from \\"see a route I want \u2192 find the search form \u2192 re-pick the same locations from a dropdown of seven \u2192 add date/time \u2192 submit\\" down to \\"click the route \u2192 add date/time \u2192 submit.\\"","date":"2026-04-29T23:55:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"transfer","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/transfer"},{"inline":true,"label":"ux","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/ux"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"}],"readingTime":3.85,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.34.1-release","title":"Rentiva v4.34.1 \u2014 Popular Routes Clickable Cards","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","transfer","ux","patch"],"date":"2026-04-29T23:55"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.34.2 \u2014 Transfer-card icon styling hotfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.34.2-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.34.0 \u2014 Popular Transfer Routes Showcase","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.34.0-release"}},"content":"A small but high-leverage patch on top of [v4.34.0](/blog/rentiva-v4.34.0-release). Popular Routes cards are now clickable, and clicking one deep-links into the transfer-search form with origin and destination pre-filled. The visitor\'s path goes from \\"see a route I want \u2192 find the search form \u2192 re-pick the same locations from a dropdown of seven \u2192 add date/time \u2192 submit\\" down to \\"click the route \u2192 add date/time \u2192 submit.\\"\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## Why\\n\\nA reviewer flagged the obvious gap right after v4.34.0 shipped: the cards looked like CTAs but weren\'t tappable. A user seeing \\"\u0130stanbul Havaliman\u0131 \u2192 Taksim \xb7 \u20ba850\\" on the homepage instinctively reaches for the card, not the search form three sections down. v4.34.0 left them with a static information panel; v4.34.1 turns it into the conversion surface it should have been.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n### Whole-card click target\\n\\n`PopularRoutesShortcode::render_card` now wraps the `<article>` in an `<a class=\\"mhm-popular-route-card-link\\">`. The href is built with `add_query_arg()` against a filterable base URL (default: the same target as the section \\"Search transfers\\" link, which itself defaults to `home_url(\'/transfer/\')`).\\n\\n```html\\n<a class=\\"mhm-popular-route-card-link\\"\\n   href=\\"https://example.com/transfer/?origin_id=73&destination_id=76\\"\\n   aria-label=\\"Search transfers from \u0130stanbul Havaliman\u0131 (IST) to Taksim Ofis\\">\\n  <article class=\\"mhm-popular-route-card mhm-popular-route-card--featured\\" role=\\"listitem\\">\\n    ...\\n  </article>\\n</a>\\n```\\n\\nThe CSS resets `color: inherit; text-decoration: none` on the anchor so the card visuals stay identical to v4.34.0, but adds `:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--mhm-pr-accent) }` so keyboard navigation gets a visible focus ring without disrupting mouse users.\\n\\n### Deep-link pre-fill\\n\\n`TransferShortcodes::prepare_template_data()` now reads `origin_id` and `destination_id` from `$_GET` (absint, sanitized) and exposes them to the template as `$preselected_origin` and `$preselected_destination`. The `transfer-search.php` template gained `selected()` calls on the `<option>` elements for both selects.\\n\\n```php\\n<option value=\\"<?php echo esc_attr((string) $loc->id); ?>\\"\\n        <?php selected(isset($preselected_origin) ? (int) $preselected_origin : 0, (int) $loc->id); ?>>\\n  <?php echo esc_html($loc->name); ?>\\n</option>\\n```\\n\\nBackwards compatible: installations that never get `?origin_id=...` URLs behave exactly as they did in v4.34.0 (the form opens with empty selects, as before). The change is additive \u2014 no breakage, no migration.\\n\\n### New filter \u2014 `mhm_rentiva_popular_routes_search_url`\\n\\nThe card-link base URL is independently filterable from the section \\"Search transfers\\" link. Themes that route the section link to a custom landing page but want the cards to deep-link directly into the search form can do so without one filter clobbering the other.\\n\\n```php\\n// Card click target = transfer-search shortcode page\\nadd_filter(\'mhm_rentiva_popular_routes_search_url\', function () {\\n    return home_url(\'/transfer-search/\');\\n});\\n\\n// Section \\"Search transfers\\" link target = a curated catalog page\\nadd_filter(\'mhm_rentiva_popular_routes_view_all_url\', function () {\\n    return home_url(\'/all-routes/\');\\n});\\n```\\n\\nWhen the card filter returns empty, the link falls back to the section URL, which falls back to `home_url(\'/transfer/\')` \u2014 sane defaults all the way down.\\n\\n### ARIA labels per card\\n\\n```html\\naria-label=\\"Search transfers from \u0130stanbul Havaliman\u0131 (IST) to Taksim Ofis\\"\\n```\\n\\nScreen readers announce a meaningful action when the link gets focus. Crawlers also see a real description of where the link goes, which is useful for the homepage SEO surface.\\n\\n### Section label rename\\n\\n\\"View all \u2192\\" \u2192 \\"Search transfers \u2192\\" in the section header. The link has always landed on the transfer-search form (not a route catalog page), so the v4.34.0 label was misleading. The new label matches what actually happens.\\n\\nA future v4.35.x release may add an actual route-catalog page (e.g. `/transfer-routes/` rendering all eligible routes in list form), at which point the \\"View all\\" label could come back honestly. For now: truth in advertising.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- **PHPUnit:** 837 \u2192 840 (+3). New tests assert the anchor wrapper exists with the right CSS class, the href carries both `origin_id` and `destination_id` query parameters, the `mhm_rentiva_popular_routes_search_url` filter overrides the base URL, and the section header label has been renamed.\\n- **PHPCS:** 0 errors.\\n- **Runtime smoke test (Chrome DevTools MCP):** rendered 6 cards, each wrapped in an anchor with the correct query-param href and a TR `aria-label`; navigating to `/transfer/?origin_id=73&destination_id=76` pre-selects \\"\u0130stanbul Havaliman\u0131 (IST)\\" and \\"Taksim Ofis\\" in the form selects.\\n\\n## Compatibility\\n\\n- No license-server upgrade.\\n- No breaking changes \u2014 v4.34.0 sites upgrade in place.\\n- Existing transfer-search submissions continue to work without `$_GET` params.\\n\\n\u2014 GitHub release v4.34.1"},{"id":"rentiva-v4.34.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.34.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-29-rentiva-v4.34.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-29-rentiva-v4.34.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.34.0 \u2014 Popular Transfer Routes Showcase","description":"The homepage now has a proper sales surface for VIP transfer routes. v4.34.0 ships a [rentivapopularroutes] shortcode + Gutenberg block + Elementor widget \u2014 three surfaces sharing one canonical renderer \u2014 that show A \u2192 B route cards (origin \u2192 destination, average duration, distance, starting price) with an admin \\"\ud83c\udf1f Vitrine Koy\\" pin checkbox to control which routes appear.","date":"2026-04-29T23:30:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"transfer","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/transfer"},{"inline":true,"label":"shortcode","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/shortcode"},{"inline":true,"label":"block","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/block"},{"inline":true,"label":"elementor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/elementor"}],"readingTime":4.93,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.34.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.34.0 \u2014 Popular Transfer Routes Showcase","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","transfer","shortcode","block","elementor"],"date":"2026-04-29T23:30"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.34.1 \u2014 Popular Routes Clickable Cards","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.34.1-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.33.2 \u2014 Turkish Terminology Cleanup","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.33.2-release"}},"content":"The homepage now has a proper sales surface for VIP transfer routes. v4.34.0 ships a `[rentiva_popular_routes]` shortcode + Gutenberg block + Elementor widget \u2014 three surfaces sharing one canonical renderer \u2014 that show A \u2192 B route cards (origin \u2192 destination, average duration, distance, starting price) with an admin \\"\ud83c\udf1f Vitrine Koy\\" pin checkbox to control which routes appear.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## Why this release exists\\n\\nRentiva\'s transfer module has been quietly capable for months: vendors set per-route pricing, the search engine joins endpoints with vehicle eligibility, the cart honors fixed and per-km pricing methods. But the homepage didn\'t surface any of that. A visitor landing on the rental marketplace had to dig into the search form to discover that VIP transfer was even on offer, let alone what it costs.\\n\\nv4.34.0 closes that gap. The new section sits on the landing page, shows the strongest routes pinned first, and answers the only question a transfer customer actually asks before clicking \\"Book\\": *how much, how long, how far?*\\n\\n## What\'s in the release\\n\\n### `[rentiva_popular_routes]` \u2014 three surfaces, one renderer\\n\\nThe shortcode is the canonical implementation. The Gutenberg block (`mhm-rentiva/popular-routes`) and the Elementor widget (`mhm_rentiva_popular_routes`) both delegate to it via `do_shortcode()`, which is Rentiva\'s render-parity contract: whatever you can render with a shortcode renders identically through any of the three surfaces. No drift, no double codepath.\\n\\nThe shortcode supports 16 attributes:\\n\\n| Attribute | Default | Purpose |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `limit` | `6` | Max cards (capped to `Mode::maxTransferRoutes()` on Lite plans) |\\n| `columns` | `3` | Desktop grid columns (2/3/4) |\\n| `order` | `featured` | `featured` / `price_asc` / `price_desc` / `alphabetical` / `newest` |\\n| `heading` | \\"Popular Routes\\" | Section title (i18n) |\\n| `subheading` | \\"Most preferred VIP transfer routes\\" | Section subtitle |\\n| `show_view_all` | `true` | Show the \\"View all\\" link in the header |\\n| `view_all_url` | empty | Override the link target (else uses the `mhm_rentiva_popular_routes_view_all_url` filter) |\\n| `show_duration` / `show_distance` / `show_traffic_note` / `show_price` | `true` | Per-element visibility toggles |\\n| `currency_symbol` | `\u20ba` | Price prefix |\\n| `filter_origin_city` | empty | e.g. `Istanbul` |\\n| `filter_origin_type` | empty | `airport` / `train` / `hotel` / `marina` / `city_center` |\\n| `featured_only` | `false` | When `true`, render only pinned routes |\\n| `theme` | `light` | `light` / `dark` |\\n\\n### Admin \\"\ud83c\udf1f Vitrine Koy\\" checkbox\\n\\nThe Transfer Routes admin form gets a new checkbox: **\ud83c\udf1f Vitrine Koy (pop\xfcler rotalar blo\u011funa sabitle)**. Pinned routes appear first when `order=\\"featured\\"` (the default) and exclusively when `featured_only=\\"true\\"`. The route list table shows a \\"\ud83c\udf1f Showcase\\" badge next to pinned rows so admins can scan-verify what the homepage will render.\\n\\nSave and delete actions automatically invalidate the `TransferRouteProvider` transient cache, so changes go live on the next page request without any cache-clearing dance.\\n\\n### `TransferRouteProvider` repository\\n\\nA new single-source-of-truth class for popular-route queries, modeled after the existing `LocationProvider` pattern: 1-hour transient cache, JOIN-based eligibility filter (origin and destination must both be `is_active=1` AND `allow_transfer=1`), composable filter set (city / type / featured-only). Cache keys hash the full filter set so distinct shortcode invocations don\'t share cache.\\n\\n```php\\nTransferRouteProvider::get_popular_routes([\\n    \'limit\'              => 6,\\n    \'order\'              => \'featured\',\\n    \'featured_only\'      => false,\\n    \'filter_origin_city\' => \'Istanbul\',\\n    \'filter_origin_type\' => \'airport\',\\n]);\\n```\\n\\nRows come back as objects with origin/destination data already joined: `origin_name`, `origin_city`, `origin_type`, `destination_name`, `destination_city`, `destination_type`, plus all the route columns (`distance_km`, `duration_min`, `min_price`, `is_featured`, etc.).\\n\\n### Database migration\\n\\n`{prefix}rentiva_transfer_routes` gains an `is_featured tinyint(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0` column with an index. The migration uses dbDelta and is idempotent \u2014 existing installations upgrade in place with no downtime, and re-running the migration on a current schema is a no-op.\\n\\n### Lite vs Pro\\n\\nLite plans render up to 3 cards. This is enforced through the existing `Mode::maxTransferRoutes()` quota \u2014 the same one that already caps how many routes a Lite admin can define. Pro plans render up to the configured `limit` (default 6). The shortcode\'s `resolve_limit()` is `min($requested, $tier_max)`, so a `limit=\\"20\\"` attribute on a Lite site quietly clamps to 3 instead of erroring.\\n\\n### Empty state\\n\\nSilent no-op. When zero routes match the filters (or the routes table is empty, or all eligible endpoints are inactive), the section doesn\'t render at all \u2014 no \\"Coming soon...\\" placeholder, no empty grid, no console noise. New installations look clean; populated sites surface what they have.\\n\\n### Two filter hooks\\n\\n```php\\n// Themes/integrations supply the transfer-search URL when no\\n// explicit view_all_url is set.\\nadd_filter(\'mhm_rentiva_popular_routes_view_all_url\', function ($url) {\\n    return home_url(\'/transfer/\');\\n});\\n\\n// Override the icon shown for a given location type.\\nadd_filter(\'mhm_rentiva_popular_routes_type_icon\', function ($icon, $type) {\\n    return $type === \'airport\' ? \'\ud83d\udeeb\' : $icon;\\n}, 10, 2);\\n```\\n\\n## Tests and quality gates\\n\\n- **PHPUnit:** 824 \u2192 837 (+13). New tests cover empty state, single/multi-card render, origin city + origin type filters, featured ordering (pinned-first), price-ascending sort, hidden routes for inactive endpoints, duration/distance/price visibility flags, and the invalid `columns` fallback.\\n- **PHPCS:** 0 errors. `composer phpcs` clean across all changed files.\\n- **SchemaParityTest:** Bumped to 20 block.json files, validated end-to-end (block attribute names round-trip through `AllowlistRegistry` to canonical shortcode attributes).\\n- **i18n:** 35+ new TR strings \u2014 frontend card labels (Pop\xfcler Rotalar, Yakla\u015f\u0131k X dk, Trafi\u011fe g\xf6re de\u011fi\u015febilir, Ba\u015flang\u0131\xe7 fiyat\u0131), admin form (\ud83c\udf1f Vitrine Koy), full block + widget editor controls (Sorting & Filters, Card Display panels). `.pot` regenerated, `tr_TR.po` msgmerged, `.mo` and `.l10n.php` recompiled.\\n- **Runtime smoke test:** Real admin \u2192 frontend round-trip via Chrome DevTools MCP. Edit form checkbox, save, navigate to a page rendering the shortcode, verify all 6 cards (4 featured pinned first), TR translations correct, CSS loaded, zero console errors.\\n\\n## What\'s next\\n\\nThe roadmap continues with the **transfer wave**: v4.36.0 adds context-aware add-ons (extending the existing `vehicle_addon` CPT with an `addon_context` taxonomy), v4.37.0 adds a transfer-locations map view (porting pinning code from another project). After that the **vendor wave** picks up \u2014 directory page (v4.38.0) and the long-deferred Phase 5 vendor public profile (v4.39.0).\\n\\n\u2014 GitHub release v4.34.0"},{"id":"rentiva-v4.33.2-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.33.2-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-29-rentiva-v4.33.2-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-29-rentiva-v4.33.2-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.33.2 \u2014 Turkish Terminology Cleanup","description":"A pure translation patch. The Vendor surface in Turkish moves from Sat\u0131c\u0131 (literally \\"one who sells\\") to Bayi (dealer / authorized agency) across the entire catalog \u2014 Rentiva is a rental marketplace, not a sales platform, and \\"Sat\u0131c\u0131\\" read awkwardly throughout the admin and vendor-facing screens.","date":"2026-04-29T22:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"i18n","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/i-18-n"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"}],"readingTime":2.23,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.33.2-release","title":"Rentiva v4.33.2 \u2014 Turkish Terminology Cleanup","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","i18n","patch"],"date":"2026-04-29T22:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.34.0 \u2014 Popular Transfer Routes Showcase","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.34.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.33.1 \u2014 Search Polish & Vendor Name Fix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.33.1-release"}},"content":"A pure translation patch. The Vendor surface in Turkish moves from **Sat\u0131c\u0131** (literally \\"one who sells\\") to **Bayi** (dealer / authorized agency) across the entire catalog \u2014 Rentiva is a rental marketplace, not a sales platform, and \\"Sat\u0131c\u0131\\" read awkwardly throughout the admin and vendor-facing screens.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Why this release exists\\n\\nThe Turkish translation catalog used **Sat\u0131c\u0131** for the English term *Vendor* across ~130 strings. In Turkish business context:\\n\\n| Term | Meaning | Fit for Rentiva |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| **Sat\u0131c\u0131** | One who sells (sales transaction) | Misleading \u2014 vendors here rent, they don\'t sell |\\n| **Bayi** | Authorized dealer/agency/franchisee | Natural \u2014 *Toyota Bayisi*, *Yetkili Bayi*, *Kiralama Bayisi* |\\n\\nA user reading \\"Sat\u0131c\u0131 paneli\\" or \\"Sat\u0131c\u0131 ba\u015fvurusu\\" mentally parses *seller panel* / *seller application*, which doesn\'t match the rental marketplace model. **Bayi** is the term Turkish rental agencies actually use to describe themselves in marketing and legal contracts.\\n\\nFive places in the catalog already used \\"Bayi\\" (terminology drift from earlier translations) \u2014 this release standardizes the entire surface.\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\n### ~130 strings migrated with proper Turkish inflection\\n\\nTurkish is agglutinative \u2014 suffixes attach to stems with vowel-harmony rules. A simple `sed \'s/Sat\u0131c\u0131/Bayi/g\'` would leave grammatical errors everywhere because the **back-vowel** stem \\"Sat\u0131c\u0131\\" takes back-vowel suffixes (-lar, -n\u0131n, -ya, -dan), while the **front-vowel** stem \\"Bayi\\" takes front-vowel suffixes (-ler, -nin, -ye, -den).\\n\\nThe migration applied an inflection-aware substitution chain, longest suffix first to prevent partial-match corruption:\\n\\n| Old (back-vowel paradigm) | New (front-vowel paradigm) |\\n|---|---|\\n| Sat\u0131c\u0131lar\u0131n\u0131z | Bayileriniz |\\n| Sat\u0131c\u0131lar\u0131n | Bayilerin |\\n| Sat\u0131c\u0131lardan | Bayilerden |\\n| Sat\u0131c\u0131lara | Bayilere |\\n| Sat\u0131c\u0131larda | Bayilerde |\\n| Sat\u0131c\u0131lar | Bayiler |\\n| Sat\u0131c\u0131n\u0131n | Bayinin |\\n| Sat\u0131c\u0131s\u0131 | Bayisi |\\n| Sat\u0131c\u0131ya | Bayiye |\\n| Sat\u0131c\u0131y\u0131 | Bayiyi |\\n| Sat\u0131c\u0131dan | Bayiden |\\n| Sat\u0131c\u0131da | Bayide |\\n| Sat\u0131c\u0131 | Bayi |\\n\\n(Lowercase variants the same pattern.)\\n\\n### One vowel-harmony fixup applied manually\\n\\nThe string *\\"...zaten aktif bir sat\u0131c\u0131s\u0131n\u0131z.\\"* has the 2nd-person plural copula suffix `-s\u0131n\u0131z` (back-vowel paradigm). Sed only replaced the `sat\u0131c\u0131s\u0131` portion \u2192 produced `bayis\u0131n\u0131z`, which is grammatically wrong. The correct front-vowel form on the new stem is `bayisiniz`.\\n\\nA manual targeted Edit fixed the single occurrence: `bayis\u0131n\u0131z \u2192 bayisiniz`.\\n\\n### Files updated\\n\\n- `languages/mhm-rentiva-tr_TR.po` \u2014 ~130 substitutions across the catalog\\n- `languages/mhm-rentiva-tr_TR.mo` \u2014 recompiled via `msgfmt`\\n- `languages/mhm-rentiva-tr_TR.l10n.php` \u2014 regenerated via `wp i18n make-php` (WP 6.5+ priority format)\\n- `README-tr.md` \u2014 10 occurrences in marketing copy\\n- `changelog-tr.json` \u2014 v4.33.1 entry self-references updated to use the new term\\n- Plugin version 4.33.1 \u2192 4.33.2 + changelog entries (EN + TR + readme.txt)\\n\\n## What did NOT change\\n\\n- English copy is untouched\\n- All PHP / JavaScript / CSS code unchanged\\n- PHPUnit baseline holds at **824 / 824** (pure translation patch)\\n- No license-server upgrade required\\n\\n## Compatibility\\n\\nDrop-in replacement for v4.33.1. WordPress automatically loads the new `.l10n.php` / `.mo` files after the plugin update \u2014 no admin action needed beyond the standard update flow.\\n\\n## Links\\n\\n- GitHub Release v4.33.2"},{"id":"rentiva-v4.33.1-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.33.1-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-29-rentiva-v4.33.1-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-29-rentiva-v4.33.1-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.33.1 \u2014 Search Polish & Vendor Name Fix","description":"A focused patch bundling three fixes around vehicle admin and the Featured Vehicles surface \u2014 the Lifecycle meta box now identifies the vendor by name, the Featured Vehicles slider stops flickering on short lists, and Featured Vehicles gains a \\"View All\\" link in parity with Vehicles Grid.","date":"2026-04-29T18:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"ux","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/ux"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"}],"readingTime":2.32,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.33.1-release","title":"Rentiva v4.33.1 \u2014 Search Polish & Vendor Name Fix","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","ux","patch"],"date":"2026-04-29T18:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.33.2 \u2014 Turkish Terminology Cleanup","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.33.2-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.33.0 \u2014 Pro Gate Unification","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.33.0-release"}},"content":"A focused patch bundling three fixes around vehicle admin and the Featured Vehicles surface \u2014 the Lifecycle meta box now identifies the vendor by name, the Featured Vehicles slider stops flickering on short lists, and Featured Vehicles gains a \\"View All\\" link in parity with Vehicles Grid.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## Why this release exists\\n\\nThree small frictions had been piling up:\\n\\n1. The Lifecycle meta box on the vehicle edit screen rendered the vendor\'s reliability score (e.g. *Vendor Score: 100/100 \u2014 Excellent*) without saying which vendor the score belonged to. Admins had to cross-reference the users list to find out.\\n2. The Featured Vehicles slider used Swiper\'s `loop: true` unconditionally. On short lists (slide count \u2264 columns \xd7 2) Swiper\'s loop algorithm doesn\'t have enough duplicate slides to cycle, and the slider rotates through blank frames.\\n3. Vehicles Grid had a *View All* link below the grid (`view_all_url` / `view_all_text` attributes); Featured Vehicles did not. Two shortcodes that should behave consistently were not.\\n\\nThis release fixes all three.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n### Fixed: Lifecycle meta box now identifies the vendor by name\\n\\n`src/Admin/Vehicle/Meta/LifecycleMetaBox.php` now resolves the vendor from `$post->post_author` and renders a **Vendor:** row above the reliability score:\\n\\n```\\nStatus: Active\\nStarted: 30 Mar 2026\\nExpires: 28 Jun 2026 (60 days)\\n\\n\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\\nVendor: Acme Filo Kiralama\\nVendor Score: 100/100 \u2014 Excellent\\n```\\n\\nResolution chain: `$user->display_name` \u2192 `$user->user_login` (fallback when display name is empty). The vendor row is never blank for a non-zero `post_author`.\\n\\n### Fixed: Featured Vehicles slider stops flickering on short lists\\n\\n`assets/js/frontend/featured-vehicles.js` now counts `.swiper-slide` elements on the page before initializing Swiper, and only enables `loop: true` when there are more slides than `columns \xd7 2`:\\n\\n```js\\nconst slideCount = container.find(\'.swiper-slide\').length;\\nconst enableLoop = slideCount > columns * 2;\\n\\nnew Swiper(container[0], {\\n    loop: enableLoop,\\n    // ...\\n});\\n```\\n\\nFew slides = plain swipe (no loop, no flicker). Many slides = infinite loop (the original behavior). Automatic; no user-facing setting.\\n\\n### Added: `view_all_url` and `view_all_text` for Featured Vehicles\\n\\nParity with Vehicles Grid. Three surfaces:\\n\\n**Shortcode:**\\n```\\n[rentiva_featured_vehicles limit=\\"6\\" view_all_url=\\"/vehicles/\\" view_all_text=\\"See All Cars\\"]\\n```\\n\\n**Elementor widget:** Two new fields in the *Carousel Options* panel (*View All URL* and *View All Button Text*).\\n\\n**Gutenberg block:** Two new TextControls in Inspector Controls (visible after a URL is entered).\\n\\nThe link renders in the template footer when `view_all_url` is non-empty. Default text is \\"View All Vehicles\\" (translatable).\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- 822 \u2192 **824 PHPUnit** (+2: `lifecycle_meta_box_renders_vendor_display_name`, `lifecycle_meta_box_falls_back_to_user_login_when_display_name_is_empty`)\\n- `FeaturedVehiclesDefaultsParityTest` extended with two new mappings (`view_all_url`, `view_all_text`)\\n- PHPCS: 0 errors across the six changed files\\n- i18n: 2 new strings (*Vendor:*, *Adds a \\"View All\\" link below the carousel...*) with Turkish translations; existing *View All Vehicles* / *View All URL* / *View All Button Text* translations reused from Vehicles Grid via `msgmerge` (fuzzy=0)\\n\\n## Compatibility\\n\\nNo license-server upgrade required. Drop-in replacement for v4.33.0.\\n\\n## Links\\n\\n- GitHub Release v4.33.1"},{"id":"rentiva-v4.33.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.33.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-27-rentiva-v4.33.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-27-rentiva-v4.33.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.33.0 \u2014 Pro Gate Unification","description":"v4.33.0 closes three holes left over from the v4.31.0 RSA token migration: 22 callsites that bypassed the token check, a misleading License Admin message, and the impossibility of testing Pro features locally without running a license server.","date":"2026-04-27T18:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"license","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/license"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"}],"readingTime":5.25,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.33.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.33.0 \u2014 Pro Gate Unification","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","license","security"],"date":"2026-04-27T18:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.33.1 \u2014 Search Polish & Vendor Name Fix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.33.1-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Currency Switcher v0.7.0 \u2014 Manage your subscription from the plugin","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/cs-v0.7.0-release"}},"content":"v4.33.0 closes three holes left over from the v4.31.0 RSA token migration: 22 callsites that bypassed the token check, a misleading License Admin message, and the impossibility of testing Pro features locally without running a license server.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## Why this release exists\\n\\nv4.31.0 introduced RSA-signed feature tokens as the single Pro authority via `Mode::featureGranted()`. Every Pro feature gate was supposed to call this method (or one of the `canUse*()` wrappers that delegate to it). But 22 places in the codebase still called the old `Mode::featureEnabled()` API, which only checked `isPro()` \u2014 no token verify. A cracked binary patching `LicenseManager::isActive()` to return `true` could unlock messages, advanced reports, and exports at those callsites without ever having a valid token.\\n\\nThis release migrates every callsite, soft-deprecates the old API, and adds two UX fixes that were piling up.\\n\\n## Changes\\n\\n### \ud83d\udd12 Security: 22 callsites now token-verify\\n\\n| File | Callsites |\\n|---|---|\\n| `Frontend/Account/AccountRenderer.php` | 1 |\\n| `Frontend/Account/WooCommerceIntegration.php` | 2 |\\n| `Messages/Core/Messages.php` | 1 |\\n| `Messages/Frontend/CustomerMessages.php` | 1 |\\n| `Messages/REST/*.php` (3 files) | 3 |\\n| `Reports/Reports.php` | 2 |\\n| `Utilities/Export/Export.php` | 3 |\\n| `Utilities/Export/ExportReports.php` | 6 |\\n| `Utilities/Menu/Menu.php` | 3 |\\n\\nAll migrated to the appropriate `Mode::canUse*()` method. `Mode::featureEnabled()` is now a soft-deprecated wrapper that emits a `_deprecated_function()` notice in `WP_DEBUG`. The body is preserved for any third-party callers; hard removal slated for v5.0.\\n\\n### \ud83d\udd27 License Admin: actual state instead of static text\\n\\nThe License page used to print **\\"All Pro features active: Unlimited vehicles/bookings, export, advanced reports, Vendor & Payout.\\"** every time a license was active \u2014 regardless of which feature tokens the server had actually granted. Customers with empty or partial tokens would read that line and then wonder why the Vendor menu was missing.\\n\\nThe new rendering derives the list from real gate decisions:\\n\\n> Active Pro features: Vendor & Payout, Advanced Reports, Messages, Expanded Export\\n\\nIf no gates are active (license active but token empty \u2014 a state that shouldn\'t normally happen but did during the v4.30.x \u2192 v4.31.0 transition), the page now shows a warning notice with a \\"Re-validate Now\\" CTA instead of the misleading text.\\n\\n### \u2728 Developer Mode for local Pro testing\\n\\nAdding a Pro feature locally has been awkward since v4.31.0: the RSA-signed feature token is issued by the license server, which devs may not run on their machine. The result was a fail-closed gate \u2014 local Pro features were untestable without copying tokens from production (which you shouldn\'t).\\n\\nTwo new constants enable a bypass:\\n\\n```php\\n// wp-config.php (development only)\\ndefine( \'WP_DEBUG\', true );\\ndefine( \'MHM_RENTIVA_DEV_PRO\', true );\\n```\\n\\nWhen **both** are true, `Mode::featureGranted()` skips the token verification step and returns `true`. The `isPro()` check still runs first, so a Lite license cannot bypass to Pro \u2014 you still need an active license, just not a valid token.\\n\\nProduction safety: Hostinger production environments have `WP_DEBUG=false` by default, so even if `MHM_RENTIVA_DEV_PRO` slipped into a production `wp-config.php` (it shouldn\'t), the bypass would not engage.\\n\\nThe yellow \\"Geli\u015ftirici Modu\\" banner subtitle now reflects whether the bypass is actually active or just dormant.\\n\\nA new filter `mhm_rentiva_dev_pro_bypass` exposes the bypass decision for testability \u2014 PHPUnit cannot toggle PHP defines within a single process.\\n\\n### \u26a0\ufe0f BREAKING: Lite users lose xlsx/pdf export access\\n\\nOld `featureEnabled(FEATURE_EXPORT)` returned `true` unconditionally for Lite users. This was a bug \u2014 the format check in callers (`! in_array($format, [\'csv\', \'json\'])`) was supposed to be the second gate, but `featureEnabled` short-circuited it. So Lite users could request xlsx and pdf exports.\\n\\n`canUseExport()` correctly returns `false` for Lite. CSV and JSON are still free; xlsx and pdf are now Pro-only as intended.\\n\\nMigration path for affected Lite users: upgrade to Pro for full format access, or stick with CSV/JSON.\\n\\n### \ud83c\udf10 Translation quality (collateral)\\n\\nThe v4.33.0 i18n pass triggered a `msgmerge` over the entire TR catalog. Some pre-existing translations had been auto-flagged as fuzzy in earlier releases and never reviewed. We fixed 22 of them in this pass:\\n\\n- **\\"Airport Transfer\\"** had been mistranslated as **\\"Aktar\u0131m\u0131 \u0130zin Ver\\"** (literally \\"Allow Transfer\\"). Now correctly **\\"Havaliman\u0131 Transferi\\"**.\\n- **\\"Report Issue\\"** was **\\"Raporlar\\"** (Reports). Now **\\"Sorun Bildir\\"**.\\n- Multiple plural forms shifted from `%d/%d` to positional `%1$d/%2$d` (matches the source argument order).\\n- A handful of email label colons that had been dropped in earlier passes were restored.\\n\\n`msgmerge` fuzzy count post-merge: 0 \u2014 verified by automation.\\n\\n## Compatibility\\n\\n| Component | Required version |\\n|---|---|\\n| `mhm-license-server` | **v1.11.2** (adds `\'export\'` to the issued feature-token allowlist) |\\n| `mhm-polar-bridge` | v1.9.0+ |\\n| WordPress | 6.7+ |\\n| PHP | 8.1+ |\\n\\nIf v4.33.0 ships before mhm-license-server v1.11.2, **Pro users will lose xlsx/pdf export for up to 24 hours** \u2014 the new `canUseExport()` gate looks for an `\'export\'` token claim that the server doesn\'t issue yet. The server\'s daily cron reissues tokens; manually clicking \\"Re-validate Now\\" on the License page refreshes immediately.\\n\\nThat\'s why the release chain order is server v1.11.2 first, then plugin v4.33.0.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- 807 \u2192 822 PHPUnit (+15)\\n  - 5 in `ModeDevBypassTest`\\n  - 4 in `LicenseAdminActiveFeaturesTest`\\n  - 6 in `ModeGateMigrationTest`\\n- PHPCS: 0 errors, 0 warnings (release scope)\\n- Plugin Check (WordPress.org compliance): 0 ERROR, 27 WARNING (all pre-existing, all known false-positives from Plugin Check not reading `phpcs.xml` prefix config)\\n\\n## Upgrade notes\\n\\n1. Wait until mhm-license-server v1.11.2 is live (otherwise Pro export breaks for ~24h).\\n2. Update the plugin via WP Admin \u2192 Plugins \u2192 Upload, or replace the ZIP via FTP.\\n3. After update, click \\"Re-validate Now\\" on the License page once. This forces the client to fetch a fresh token from the server \u2014 without it, the daily cron is the next refresh window.\\n4. Lite users who relied on (bug-enabled) xlsx exports: upgrade to Pro, or switch to CSV/JSON.\\n\\n## Local development\\n\\nIf you maintain a fork or extend the plugin:\\n\\n```php\\n// wp-config.php\\ndefine( \'WP_DEBUG\', true );\\ndefine( \'MHM_RENTIVA_DEV_PRO\', true );  // skip token check, exercise Pro gates\\n```\\n\\nThis unlocks Vendor Marketplace, Advanced Reports, Messages, and Expanded Export against an active license without a real RSA-signed token. Don\'t ship this to production."},{"id":"cs-v0.7.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/cs-v0.7.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-27-cs-v0.7.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-27-cs-v0.7.0-release.md","title":"Currency Switcher v0.7.0 \u2014 Manage your subscription from the plugin","description":"The License tab now has a Manage Subscription button that opens the Polar customer portal in a new tab. Cancel auto-renewal, update your card, switch plans, or resubscribe \u2014 all without leaving WordPress admin. Snake-case + REST/React parity to MHM Rentiva v4.32.0.","date":"2026-04-27T08:30:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"currency-switcher","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/currency-switcher"},{"inline":true,"label":"license","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/license"}],"readingTime":2.21,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"cs-v0.7.0-release","title":"Currency Switcher v0.7.0 \u2014 Manage your subscription from the plugin","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","currency-switcher","license"],"date":"2026-04-27T08:30"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.33.0 \u2014 Pro Gate Unification","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.33.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.32.0 \u2014 Manage your subscription from the plugin","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.32.0-release"}},"content":"The License tab now has a **Manage Subscription** button that opens the Polar customer portal in a new tab. Cancel auto-renewal, update your card, switch plans, or resubscribe \u2014 all without leaving WordPress admin. Snake-case + REST/React parity to **MHM Rentiva v4.32.0**.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\nInside the License tab\'s **License Management** zone (visible when a Pro license is active), a third button joins the existing two:\\n\\n1. **Manage Subscription** \u2014 opens Polar customer portal (this release)\\n2. Re-validate Now\\n3. Deactivate License\\n\\nThe plugin reaches Polar through the same license server already in use. No new external services contacted from your site\'s perspective. Schema and signature integrity remain RSA-protected (v0.6.0+ pipeline).\\n\\n## State-driven emphasis\\n\\nThe button changes color based on how close your subscription is to renewal:\\n\\n| Days remaining | Color | Intent |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| > 30 | Standard primary blue | \\"Plenty of runway\\" |\\n| \u2264 30 | Yellow | \\"Heads up \u2014 renewal is coming\\" |\\n| \u2264 7 | Amber + glow | \\"Decide now\\" |\\n| Expired (0) | Amber + glow | \\"Resubscribe to keep Pro\\" |\\n\\nWhile the portal session is being minted (a brief async call), the button text becomes \\"Opening\u2026\\" and the styling dims to communicate the click registered.\\n\\n## Failure handling\\n\\nIf the portal session can\'t be minted (server error, network blip, license revoked between page load and click), the button surfaces an in-tab notice instead of breaking:\\n\\n> Subscription management is not available right now. Please try again later or contact support@wpalemi.com.\\n\\nNo raw technical strings ever leak to end users.\\n\\n## Architecture\\n\\n- New public method `LicenseManager::create_customer_portal_session(string $return_url): array` (snake_case parity to Rentiva\'s camelCase)\\n- New REST endpoint `POST /mhm-currency/v1/license/manage-subscription` (manage_options gated)\\n- New React state + callback in `License.jsx`, button rendered before Deactivate when `isActive && license.maskedKey`\\n- New CSS rules using compound selectors (`.button.mhm-cs-license-warning` / `.mhm-cs-license-urgent`) to avoid colliding with the existing `.mhm-cs-license-warning` alert pill\\n- 4 new translatable strings, all translated to Turkish\\n\\n## Compatibility\\n\\n| Component | Required version |\\n|---|---|\\n| `mhm-license-server` | v1.11.0+ (new `/customer-portal-session` endpoint) |\\n| `mhm-polar-bridge` | v1.9.0+ (renewal reminder cron) |\\n| WordPress | 6.0+ |\\n| PHP | 7.4+ |\\n\\nOlder license-server versions without the customer-portal endpoint return a graceful in-tab notice instead of breaking.\\n\\n## Out of scope (not in this release)\\n\\n- Past-due / dunning notifications \u2014 Polar handles these directly via email.\\n- Yearly subscription renewal reminders \u2014 Polar sends these 7 days before renewal automatically.\\n\\nMonthly subscribers receive an additional 7-day-out reminder email from `mhm-polar-bridge v1.9.0+`, since Polar doesn\'t generate these for short billing cycles.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- 148 \u2192 158 PHPUnit (+10 new across 2 test files)\\n- PHPCS new files: 0 errors (after PHPCBF)\\n- PHPStan level 6: 0 errors\\n- npm run build: success\\n- i18n: 0 fuzzy on new strings, all 4 translated"},{"id":"rentiva-v4.32.0-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.32.0-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-27-rentiva-v4.32.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-27-rentiva-v4.32.0-release.md","title":"Rentiva v4.32.0 \u2014 Manage your subscription from the plugin","description":"The License page now has a Manage Subscription button that opens the Polar customer portal in a new tab. Cancel auto-renewal, update your card, switch plans, or resubscribe \u2014 all without leaving WordPress admin.","date":"2026-04-27T08:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"license","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/license"}],"readingTime":2.02,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"rentiva-v4.32.0-release","title":"Rentiva v4.32.0 \u2014 Manage your subscription from the plugin","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","rentiva","license"],"date":"2026-04-27T08:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Currency Switcher v0.7.0 \u2014 Manage your subscription from the plugin","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/cs-v0.7.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"License Security Hardening Sprint: Rentiva v4.30.0 \u2192 v4.30.2 (with mhm-license-server v1.9.0\u2013v1.9.3 and CS v0.5.x)","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/license-security-sprint-v4.30.x"}},"content":"The License page now has a **Manage Subscription** button that opens the Polar customer portal in a new tab. Cancel auto-renewal, update your card, switch plans, or resubscribe \u2014 all without leaving WordPress admin.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## What changed\\n\\nInside the License Management section (visible when a license is active), you\'ll now see three buttons:\\n\\n1. **Manage Subscription** \u2014 opens Polar customer portal (this release)\\n2. Re-validate Now (v4.31.2)\\n3. Deactivate License\\n\\nThe new button reaches Polar through the same license server already in use. No new external services contacted from your site\'s perspective. Schema and signature integrity remain RSA-protected (v4.30.0+ pipeline).\\n\\n## State-driven emphasis\\n\\nThe button changes color based on how close your subscription is to renewal:\\n\\n| Days remaining | Color | Intent |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| > 30 | Standard primary blue | \\"Plenty of runway\\" |\\n| \u2264 30 | Yellow | \\"Heads up \u2014 renewal is coming\\" |\\n| \u2264 7 | Amber + glow | \\"Decide now\\" |\\n| Expired (0) | Amber + glow | \\"Resubscribe to keep Pro\\" |\\n\\nCustomers always see how close their renewal is at a glance, regardless of whether they read the email reminders.\\n\\n## Failure handling\\n\\nIf the portal session can\'t be minted (server error, network blip, license revoked between page load and click), the admin lands back on the License page with a customer-friendly translated warning:\\n\\n> \u2139\ufe0f Subscription management is not available right now (service unavailable). Please try again later or contact support@wpalemi.com.\\n\\nFive reason codes are mapped to short Turkish labels via `get_manage_unavailable_label()` \u2014 no raw technical strings ever leak to end users.\\n\\n## Architecture\\n\\n- New public method `LicenseManager::createCustomerPortalSession(string $return_url): array`\\n- New admin-post handler `LicenseAdmin::handle_manage_subscription()` \u2014 capability + nonce gated\\n- New CSS file additions in `assets/css/admin/license-admin.css`, cache-busted via `filemtime`\\n- 9 new translatable strings, all translated to Turkish\\n\\n## Compatibility\\n\\n| Component | Required version |\\n|---|---|\\n| `mhm-license-server` | v1.11.0+ (new `/customer-portal-session` endpoint) |\\n| `mhm-polar-bridge` | v1.9.0+ (renewal reminder cron) |\\n| WordPress | 6.7+ |\\n| PHP | 8.1+ |\\n\\nOlder license-server versions without the customer-portal endpoint return a graceful `manage_unavailable` notice instead of breaking \u2014 customers see a translated warning, not a broken redirect.\\n\\n## Out of scope (not in this release)\\n\\n- **Past-due / dunning notifications** \u2014 Polar handles these directly via email.\\n- **Yearly subscription renewal reminders** \u2014 Polar sends these 7 days before renewal automatically.\\n\\nMonthly subscribers receive an additional 7-day-out reminder email from `mhm-polar-bridge v1.9.0+`, since Polar doesn\'t generate these for short billing cycles.\\n\\n## Tests\\n\\n- 793 \u2192 807 PHPUnit (+14 new across 3 test files)\\n- PHPCS: 0 errors\\n- i18n: 0 fuzzy on new strings, all 9 translated"},{"id":"license-security-sprint-v4.30.x","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/license-security-sprint-v4.30.x","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-25-license-security-sprint.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-25-license-security-sprint.md","title":"License Security Hardening Sprint: Rentiva v4.30.0 \u2192 v4.30.2 (with mhm-license-server v1.9.0\u2013v1.9.3 and CS v0.5.x)","description":"A two-day cross-plugin sprint that hardened the Rentiva (and Currency Switcher) Pro licensing layer against source-edit bypass attacks. Three Rentiva client releases (v4.30.0 / v4.30.1 / v4.30.2) shipped alongside four license-server releases (v1.9.0 \u2192 v1.9.3) and three Currency Switcher releases (v0.5.0 / v0.5.1 / v0.5.2). Live-deployed and verified end-to-end on mhmrentiva.com + wpalemi.com.","date":"2026-04-25T22:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"},{"inline":true,"label":"license","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/license"},{"inline":true,"label":"hardening","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/hardening"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-license-server","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-license-server"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-currency-switcher","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-currency-switcher"}],"readingTime":7.77,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"license-security-sprint-v4.30.x","title":"License Security Hardening Sprint: Rentiva v4.30.0 \u2192 v4.30.2 (with mhm-license-server v1.9.0\u2013v1.9.3 and CS v0.5.x)","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","security","license","hardening","mhm-rentiva","mhm-license-server","mhm-currency-switcher"],"date":"2026-04-25T22:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Rentiva v4.32.0 \u2014 Manage your subscription from the plugin","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/rentiva-v4.32.0-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.27.4\u2013v4.27.6: Migration Lane Architecture, License Slug Forwarding, WordPress.org Polish","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.27.4-v4.27.6-stability-sprint"}},"content":"A two-day cross-plugin sprint that hardened the Rentiva (and Currency Switcher) Pro licensing layer against source-edit bypass attacks. **Three Rentiva client releases** (v4.30.0 / v4.30.1 / v4.30.2) shipped alongside **four license-server releases** (v1.9.0 \u2192 v1.9.3) and **three Currency Switcher releases** (v0.5.0 / v0.5.1 / v0.5.2). Live-deployed and verified end-to-end on mhmrentiva.com + wpalemi.com.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## Why this sprint happened\\n\\nThe Rentiva plugin source ships on a **public GitHub repository**. A motivated attacker can clone, patch `Mode::canUseVendorMarketplace()` to `return true;`, and unlock Pro features without ever calling the license server. v1.8.0 closed *cross-product* key reuse (Currency Switcher key on Rentiva) but did nothing about source-edit bypass. **v4.30.x raises the cost: a crack now has to forge an HMAC signature, host a fake validator, AND keep emitting fresh feature tokens \u2014 and even then, tokens expire within 24 hours.**\\n\\nFive attack scenarios were used as the design target:\\n\\n| Attack | Mechanism | Defended by |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| Source-edit `isActive() { return true; }` | Patch local Pro gate | Layer 4 (feature token) |\\n| Cross-product key reuse | Use CS key on Rentiva | Layer 1 (slug binding, v1.8.0) |\\n| Empty `product_slug` body | Strip the line, ride legacy compat | Layer 1 hardened in v1.9.3 |\\n| Fake activate POST from script | No control over claimed site | Layer 3 (reverse site validation) |\\n| Pirated key + fake server | DNS hijack to lookalike | Layer 2 (response signing) |\\n\\n## v4.30.0 \u2014 Phase B Client (the foundation, 2026-04-24)\\n\\nCompanion to **mhm-license-server v1.9.0** (Phase A \u2014 server-side three-layer defense).\\n\\n### Four new helpers under `src/Admin/Licensing/`\\n\\n- **`ClientSecrets`** \u2014 resolves three new wp-config constants (`MHM_RENTIVA_LICENSE_RESPONSE_HMAC_SECRET`, `MHM_RENTIVA_LICENSE_FEATURE_TOKEN_KEY`, `MHM_RENTIVA_LICENSE_PING_SECRET`).\\n- **`ResponseVerifier`** \u2014 HMAC-SHA256 verification of every signed activate/validate response. Mirrors the server\'s recursive ksort + JSON_UNESCAPED_SLASHES|UNICODE canonicalization byte-for-byte \u2014 drift = legitimate responses look tampered.\\n- **`FeatureTokenVerifier`** \u2014 verifies `{base64(json)}.{hmac}` tokens issued by the server. 24h TTL. `hasFeature($payload, $flag)` accessor used by Mode gates.\\n- **`VerifyEndpoint`** \u2014 public REST route `/wp-json/mhm-rentiva-verify/v1/ping` answering the server\'s `X-MHM-Challenge` during reverse validation.\\n\\n### Mode gate refactor\\n\\n`canUseVendorMarketplace()`, `canUseMessages()`, `canUseAdvancedReports()`, `canUseVendorPayout()` now route through a single `featureGranted()` private helper that:\\n\\n1. Hard-checks `isPro()` first\\n2. If `FEATURE_TOKEN_KEY` is unset \u2192 legacy `isPro()` fallback (existing customers don\'t break)\\n3. Otherwise verifies the locally-stored feature token\'s HMAC\\n4. Reads the specific flag from the payload (`vendor_marketplace`, `messaging`, `advanced_reports`, etc.)\\n\\nA `return true;` patch on `isActive()` no longer unlocks anything because the gate independently asks for a server-granted flag.\\n\\n### LicenseManager wiring\\n\\n- `activate()` request body now includes `client_version = MHM_RENTIVA_VERSION`. Server uses this for per-version reverse-validation enforcement (\u22654.30.0 floor for Rentiva).\\n- Successful response\'s `feature_token` field is persisted alongside the existing license record.\\n- Daily verification cron refreshes the token on every tick.\\n\\n### Test coverage\\n\\n6 new test files, **36 new tests** across `tests/Unit/Licensing/` and `tests/Integration/Licensing/`. Total: 776 / 2715, PHPCS clean, 3 new TR translations.\\n\\n## v4.30.1 \u2014 Reverse Validation UX Fix (2026-04-25 morning)\\n\\nv4.30.0 made `MHM_RENTIVA_LICENSE_PING_SECRET` **mandatory** \u2014 without it, `VerifyEndpoint` returned 503 `ping_secret_not_configured`, and the license server then rejected activation with `site_unreachable`. **Every customer site needed an operator-pinned secret in `wp-config.php`** \u2014 unworkable for an end-customer product.\\n\\n### Fix\\n\\n`VerifyEndpoint::handle_ping()` falls back to the per-activation `site_hash` (computed the same way `LicenseManager::siteHash()` does \u2014 `sha256(home_url + site_url)` JSON-encoded) when `ClientSecrets::getPingSecret()` returns empty. Server-side `mhm-license-server v1.9.1+` applies the matching fallback in `Security\\\\SiteVerifier`, so the HMAC challenge stays verifiable even though `site_hash` is technically not secret.\\n\\n### Why it\'s still safe\\n\\n`site_hash` is publicly derivable, but tampering still fails because the reverse ping targets the claimed `site_url`. An attacker that doesn\'t control that domain cannot intercept the GET and reply with a forged HMAC, regardless of whether the HMAC key is private.\\n\\n### Backward compatibility\\n\\nWhen `MHM_RENTIVA_LICENSE_PING_SECRET` IS defined, `VerifyEndpoint` still uses it \u2014 v4.30.0 deploys with operator config baked in keep working unchanged.\\n\\n## v4.30.2 \u2014 License Notice Defensive Fix (2026-04-25 afternoon)\\n\\nTwo layered bugs in `LicenseAdmin::admin_notices()`:\\n\\n### Bug A \u2014 Empty error_message rendered \\"License activation failed: \\" (with empty trailing space)\\n\\nStale URL state (`?license=error` without `&message=...`, e.g. browser back/forward, bookmark, truncated copy-paste) leaked through the `match`\'s default arm into a `sprintf(\\"...: %s\\", \'\')` call. Visible at the top of the License page even though the customer hadn\'t pressed anything.\\n\\n### Bug B \u2014 Missing match arms for v1.8.0+/v1.9.x server error codes\\n\\n`site_unreachable`, `site_verification_failed`, `tampered_response`, `product_mismatch`, `product_slug_required` had no friendly translations. They fell through to the same default arm, leaking raw technical codes to end users (\\"License activation failed: site_unreachable\\").\\n\\n### Fix (three layers)\\n\\n1. **Defensive guard:** `if (\'\' === $error_message) { break; }` skips the notice entirely when there\'s no actionable code.\\n2. **Five new match arms** with customer-friendly EN strings + Turkish translations.\\n3. **Generic default + `data-error-code` attribute:** unknown future codes render \\"License activation failed. Please try again.\\" with the technical code exposed via a `data-error-code` HTML attribute (debug / support only \u2014 never inline text).\\n\\n### Stable tag drift caught\\n\\nWhile bumping the version, an audit caught that `readme.txt` Stable tag had been stuck at `4.30.0` \u2014 the v4.30.1 release accidentally skipped the bump. v4.30.2 corrects to `4.30.2`.\\n\\n### Test coverage\\n\\n`tests/Unit/Licensing/LicenseAdminAdminNoticesTest.php` \u2014 5 new tests covering empty defense, `site_unreachable` mapping, generic default + data attribute, and two regression cases (`activated`, no-license-query). Total: **781 / 2726**, PHPCS clean.\\n\\n### Live verification\\n\\nChrome DevTools MCP scripted a tour of mhmrentiva.com after v4.30.2 deployment:\\n\\n| URL | Expected | Live result |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `?license=error` | No notice (defensive guard) | \u2705 0 notice elements |\\n| `?license=error&message=site_unreachable` | Friendly EN message + `data-error-code=\\"site_unreachable\\"`, no raw code in inline text | \u2705 confirmed via DOM script |\\n| `?license=error&message=imaginary_code_42` | Generic message + `data-error-code=\\"imaginary_code_42\\"`, no raw code in inline text | \u2705 confirmed |\\n\\n## Companion server releases (mhm-license-server, on wpalemi.com)\\n\\n- **v1.9.0** \u2014 Phase A: HMAC response signing, reverse site validation, feature token issuer (24h TTL).\\n- **v1.9.1** \u2014 `site_hash` fallback inside `Security\\\\SiteVerifier::verify()` (paired with v4.30.1 client).\\n- **v1.9.2** \u2014 `SecretManager::getPingSecret()` opt-in only (no file fallback) \u2014 closed an asymmetric HMAC bug where the server auto-generated `wp-uploads/mhm-license-secrets/ping.key` while customers ran zero-config and the two paths produced different HMAC keys.\\n- **v1.9.3 (CRITICAL)** \u2014 `LicenseActivator::activate()` now hard-rejects empty `product_slug` against a slug-bound license row. The previous code path let a single source edit drop the slug from the request body and slide through both v1.8.0 binding AND v1.9.0 reverse validation (because `REVERSE_VALIDATION_FLOOR[\'\'] === null` took the legacy-pass branch).\\n\\nCombined: **143 PHPUnit, 398 assertions, PHPCS clean** on the server side.\\n\\nThree live attack scenarios were curl-verified against `wpalemi.com` after v1.9.3 deployment:\\n\\n| Scenario | Expected | Live result |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `product_slug` removed from body | `product_slug_required` reject | \u2705 confirmed |\\n| Cross-product slug swap (CS slug + Rentiva site) | `site_unreachable` (CS verify endpoint absent on Rentiva site) | \u2705 confirmed |\\n| Correct flow regression | 200 active | \u2705 confirmed |\\n\\n## Companion Currency Switcher releases\\n\\n`mhm-currency-switcher v0.5.0` (Phase C client) \u2192 `v0.5.1` (CI hotfix: `str_ends_with` PHP 7.4 compat + `OrderFilterTest` `WC_Order` stub) \u2192 `v0.5.2` (`VerifyEndpoint` `site_hash` fallback). Same five-attack-surface defense applied to CS Mode gates with eight feature flags (`fixed_pricing`, `nav_menu_switcher`, `flag_library`, `geolocation`, `payment_restrictions`, `auto_rate_update`, `multilingual`, `rest_api_filter`).\\n\\n## Customer-facing impact\\n\\nAfter this sprint, customers on Rentiva v4.30.1+ (and CS v0.5.2+):\\n\\n- **Just enter the license key and click Activate.** No `wp-config.php` edits.\\n- Server-side three-layer defense (slug binding + response signing + reverse validation) is fully active.\\n- License notice messages are friendly and locale-aware; no raw technical jargon visible.\\n- Existing v4.27.x installs keep working unchanged through legacy fallback paths until they upgrade.\\n\\n## Known limitation (deferred)\\n\\nA sufficiently determined attacker running a cracked plugin binary on **their own** site with **their own** product-matching license can still patch `Mode::canUse*()` directly when the customer has not defined `MHM_RENTIVA_LICENSE_FEATURE_TOKEN_KEY` in `wp-config.php` (zero-config deployment intentionally accepts this trade-off).\\n\\nClosing the source-edit + zero-config gap requires **asymmetric crypto** (RSA-signed feature tokens, public key embedded in the plugin source \u2014 open-source-safe). This is deferred to **mhm-license-server v1.10.0 + mhm-rentiva v4.31.0 + mhm-currency-switcher v0.6.0**, planned post-launch.\\n\\n## \ud83c\udf93 Lessons captured (memory + KB)\\n\\n- **`patterns/license-defense-in-depth-stack.md`** \u2014 five-layer defense documentation, attack matrix, asymmetric crypto roadmap.\\n- **`patterns/admin-notice-url-state-defense.md`** \u2014 three-layer defense for redirect-after-action notices (empty guard + generic default + data attribute).\\n- **`patterns/release-zip-audit.md`** \u2014 three audits before tag/release; caught three ZIP leaks during this sprint (`drafts/`, `bin/`, `*.po~`).\\n- **`standards/i18n-workflow.md`** \u2014 updated with `.po~` msgmerge backup pattern + `.l10n.php` deploy mandate.\\n- **`wp-conductor` skill** \u2014 new \\"Long Session / Chained Release Discipline\\" gate with per-release verification requirements (8 release chain on 2026-04-25 was the baseline failure that motivated this).\\n\\n---\\n\\n*GitHub Releases:*\\n- *Rentiva: v4.30.0 \xb7 v4.30.1 \xb7 v4.30.2*\\n- *License Server: [v1.9.0](https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-license-server/releases/tag/v1.9.0) \xb7 [v1.9.1](https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-license-server/releases/tag/v1.9.1) \xb7 [v1.9.2](https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-license-server/releases/tag/v1.9.2) \xb7 [v1.9.3](https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-license-server/releases/tag/v1.9.3)*\\n- *Currency Switcher: [v0.5.0](https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-currency-switcher/releases/tag/v0.5.0) \xb7 [v0.5.1](https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-currency-switcher/releases/tag/v0.5.1) \xb7 [v0.5.2](https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-currency-switcher/releases/tag/v0.5.2)*"},{"id":"v4.27.4-v4.27.6-stability-sprint","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.27.4-v4.27.6-stability-sprint","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-23-v4.27.4-v4.27.6-stability.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-23-v4.27.4-v4.27.6-stability.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.27.4\u2013v4.27.6: Migration Lane Architecture, License Slug Forwarding, WordPress.org Polish","description":"A retrospective covering three patch releases shipped in succession on 2026-04-23: a critical migration architecture fix (v4.27.4), per-product license binding compatibility (v4.27.5), and WordPress.org submission readiness (v4.27.6). Backfilling these blog posts now in the wake of the v4.30.x security sprint.","date":"2026-04-23T22:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"},{"inline":true,"label":"migration","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/migration"},{"inline":true,"label":"license","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/license"},{"inline":true,"label":"wordpress-org","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/wordpress-org"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":3.76,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.27.4-v4.27.6-stability-sprint","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.27.4\u2013v4.27.6: Migration Lane Architecture, License Slug Forwarding, WordPress.org Polish","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","patch","migration","license","wordpress-org","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-04-23T22:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"License Security Hardening Sprint: Rentiva v4.30.0 \u2192 v4.30.2 (with mhm-license-server v1.9.0\u2013v1.9.3 and CS v0.5.x)","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/license-security-sprint-v4.30.x"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.27.2: Settings Testing Pollution Hotfix + Duplicate Addon Notice Dedupe","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.27.2-settings-testing-pollution-hotfix"}},"content":"A retrospective covering three patch releases shipped in succession on 2026-04-23: a **critical migration architecture fix** (v4.27.4), **per-product license binding compatibility** (v4.27.5), and **WordPress.org submission readiness** (v4.27.6). Backfilling these blog posts now in the wake of the v4.30.x security sprint.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## v4.27.4 \u2014 Migration Lane Architecture Fix (CRITICAL)\\n\\nThe v4.27.1 (i18n locale leak) and v4.27.2 (Settings Testing pollution) data-cleanup migrations **never actually ran on upgraded sites** \u2014 the regression cleared during v4.27.0 prep had quietly broken the migration trigger.\\n\\n### Root cause\\n\\n`plugins_loaded` migration callback used a single short-circuit:\\n\\n```php\\nif ( $stored_version === MHM_RENTIVA_VERSION ) {\\n    return; // skip ALL migrations\\n}\\n```\\n\\nBut `mhm_rentiva_single_site_activation()` (which fires BEFORE `plugins_loaded` on any ZIP-replace upgrade path) had already stamped the new version into the option. By the time `plugins_loaded` fired, `$stored === $current` was true \u2192 **all flag-gated cleanups got skipped forever.**\\n\\nLive evidence at mhmrentiva.com: Brand Name displayed as `1`, currency stats rendered as `0,00 1` instead of `0,00 \u20ba` (because the v4.27.2 pollution migration never executed).\\n\\n### Fix \u2014 two-lane architecture\\n\\n`plugins_loaded` callback split into two independent lanes:\\n\\n- **Lane A (schema drift, version-gated):** runs only when `$stored !== $current`. Idempotent across multiple loads of the same version.\\n- **Lane B (flag-gated data cleanups):** runs on every request, but each migration has its own `mhm_rentiva_<flag>` option that flips after successful run. Genuinely idempotent.\\n\\nBoth lanes have their own error containment so a failure in Lane B never blocks Lane A or vice versa.\\n\\n### Test coverage\\n\\n`tests/Migration/MigrationLaneIndependenceTest.php` \u2014 3 new tests, 8 assertions guarding the split.\\n\\n### Empirical verification\\n\\nChrome DevTools MCP browser tour of mhmrentiva.com after deployment: 0 duplicate notices, stats display `0,00 \u20ba` (U+20BA), Brand Name reads \\"MHM Rentiva\\". Manual one-time **Reset to Defaults** across 11 admin tabs cleared residual state from the period when migrations weren\'t running.\\n\\n## v4.27.5 \u2014 License Client Per-Product Slug Forwarding\\n\\nPairs with `mhm-license-server v1.8.0+` which introduced per-product license binding. Before v4.27.5, a customer could buy a cheap MHM Currency Switcher Monthly key and use it to activate Rentiva Pro \u2014 server had no way to enforce that the license was issued for a specific product.\\n\\n### Change\\n\\n`LicenseManager::activate()` and `validate()` request bodies now include `product_slug => \'mhm-rentiva\'`. The server checks this against the license row\'s stored slug and rejects mismatches with a `product_mismatch` error.\\n\\n### Bonus fix\\n\\nAdditional Services admin page rendered two **Documentation** buttons \u2014 the global `all_admin_notices` docs hook + the page\'s own header both fired. The hook now skips the `vehicle_addon` screen; the page header\'s button is the single source.\\n\\n## v4.27.6 \u2014 WordPress.org Submission Polish\\n\\nPlugin Check (PCP) compliance for WordPress.org plugin directory submission: **1 ERROR + 115 WARNING \u2192 0 ERROR + 61 WARNING**. The remaining warnings are all false positives caused by Plugin Check not reading the project\'s `phpcs.xml` prefix configuration.\\n\\n### Concrete fixes\\n\\n- `unlink()` \u2192 `wp_delete_file()` in the demo image importer (the only real ERROR).\\n- Reasoned `phpcs:ignore` comments for warnings the project\'s ruleset already excludes (audit `error_log()` calls, `mhm_rentiva_` prefixed hooks Plugin Check refuses to recognise, accepted `meta_query` / `post__not_in` performance tradeoffs, ledger queries with core-controlled table names bound through `$wpdb->prepare()`).\\n- `$pending_messages` template-scope variable \u2192 `$mhm_rentiva_pending_messages` to honour Plugin Check\'s prefix convention.\\n- `readme.txt` Changelog section trimmed to fit WP.org\'s 5000-character limit; older releases linked to GitHub.\\n- `changelog-tr.json` backfill for v4.27.5 + new v4.27.6 entry.\\n\\n### No functional change\\n\\n740/740 PHPUnit still passes. PHPCS clean. The plugin behaves identically \u2014 only the Plugin Check noise was reduced.\\n\\n## \u2705 Verification across all three\\n\\n| Check | v4.27.4 | v4.27.5 | v4.27.6 |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| PHPUnit | 740/740, 2642 assertions, 6 skipped | unchanged | unchanged |\\n| PHPCS | 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 | 0 / 0 |\\n| Plugin Check ERROR | unchanged | unchanged | 1 \u2192 0 |\\n\\n## \ud83c\udf93 Lessons captured (memory)\\n\\n- **`feedback_migration_lane_architecture.md`** \u2014 when activation hooks stamp version BEFORE `plugins_loaded`, the version gate breaks all flag-gated migrations. Always split version-drift and data-cleanup lanes.\\n- **`feedback_empirical_dom_verification.md`** \u2014 DOM-level verification through Chrome DevTools MCP is the only way to catch runtime-DB-state bugs that 100% PHPUnit + 0 PHPCS happily ship.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd1c Next\\n\\nThe v4.27.x umbrella closed here. Next major was v4.28.0 (Popular Routes) \u2014 but the security audit of the cross-product attack surface re-prioritised the roadmap into the **License Security Hardening** sprint (v4.30.x), shipped 2026-04-24/25.\\n\\n---\\n\\n*GitHub Releases: v4.27.4 \xb7 v4.27.5 \xb7 v4.27.6*"},{"id":"v4.27.2-settings-testing-pollution-hotfix","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.27.2-settings-testing-pollution-hotfix","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-23-v4.27.2-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-23-v4.27.2-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.27.2: Settings Testing Pollution Hotfix + Duplicate Addon Notice Dedupe","description":"After the v4.27.1 i18n hotfix, a user reported three more bugs \u2014 all originating from the same fresh-install scenario, all triggered by pressing \\"Run All Diagnostics\\" once on the Settings Testing page. v4.27.2 breaks the chain.","date":"2026-04-23T19:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"},{"inline":true,"label":"hotfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/hotfix"},{"inline":true,"label":"settings","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/settings"},{"inline":true,"label":"diagnostics","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/diagnostics"},{"inline":true,"label":"bugfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/bugfix"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":4.55,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.27.2-settings-testing-pollution-hotfix","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.27.2: Settings Testing Pollution Hotfix + Duplicate Addon Notice Dedupe","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","patch","hotfix","settings","diagnostics","bugfix","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-04-23T19:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.27.4\u2013v4.27.6: Migration Lane Architecture, License Slug Forwarding, WordPress.org Polish","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.27.4-v4.27.6-stability-sprint"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.27.1: i18n Locale-Leak Hotfix \u2014 Vehicle Settings Labels No Longer Frozen at First-Install Language","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.27.1-i18n-locale-leak-hotfix"}},"content":"After the v4.27.1 i18n hotfix, a user reported three more bugs \u2014 all originating from the same fresh-install scenario, all triggered by **pressing \\"Run All Diagnostics\\" once on the Settings Testing page**. v4.27.2 breaks the chain.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## \ud83d\udc1b Bug 1: All Text Fields Show \\"1\\" on Fresh Install\\n\\n**Scenario:**\\n1. Plugin is freshly installed.\\n2. User goes to **Settings \u2192 Settings Testing** tab and presses \\"Run All Diagnostics\\".\\n3. Returns to General Settings \u2014 **Brand Name = \\"1\\"**, **Cancellation Deadline = 1**, **Payment Deadline = 1**, Support Email, Brand Logo URL, etc. all show \\"1\\".\\n4. Pressing **\\"Reset to Defaults\\"** fixes it.\\n\\n### Root Cause\\n\\n`SettingsTester::test_settings_save()` was converting empty strings to `\'1\'` to trigger a \\"change detected save\\":\\n\\n```php\\n// Fresh install: $current_str == \'\'\\nif ( in_array( $current_str, array( \'0\', \'1\', \'\' ) ) ) {\\n    $test_value = ( $current_str === \'1\' ) ? \'0\' : \'1\'; // \u2192 \'1\'\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThis `\'1\'` payload was then passed to the **real** sanitizer. The sanitizer rewrote ALL fields for the target tab (not just the key under test). The restore mechanism only reverted the explicitly tested keys \u2192 collateral writes to other tab fields persisted in the DB.\\n\\n**The critical point:** On a fresh install, when the General test runs:\\n- `brand_name` \u2192 \'1\' (test flip, then restored) \u2713\\n- `currency` \u2192 \'1\' (flip + restore) \u2713\\n- `dark_mode` \u2192 sanitizer wrote it, test never touched it \u2192 **stayed in DB**\\n- `support_email` \u2192 sanitizer wrote `admin@...` as default, then flipped to \'1\', not restored \u2192 **stayed in DB**\\n- ... and more\\n\\n### Fix\\n\\n#### 1. Harness fix \u2014 full snapshot/restore\\n\\n```php\\n// NEW v4.27.2: snapshot the ENTIRE option, restore the ENTIRE option.\\n$option_existed_before = false !== get_option( $option_name, false );\\n$full_option_snapshot  = (array) get_option( $option_name, array() );\\n\\n// ... test runs, sanitizer pollutes DB ...\\n\\nif ( $option_existed_before ) {\\n    update_option( $option_name, $full_option_snapshot );\\n} else {\\n    delete_option( $option_name );\\n}\\n```\\n\\nThe test now leaves the DB truly read-only. Collateral writes are automatically undone.\\n\\n#### 2. Migration \u2014 clean up existing installs\\n\\n`SettingsCore::migrate_clean_test_pollution()` \u2014 one-time flagged migration (`mhm_rentiva_v4272_test_pollution_cleaned`):\\n\\n```php\\n$polluted_keys = array(\\n    \'mhm_rentiva_brand_name\', \'mhm_rentiva_email_from_name\',\\n    \'mhm_rentiva_email_from_address\', \'mhm_rentiva_support_email\',\\n    \'mhm_rentiva_booking_url\', \'mhm_rentiva_login_url\',\\n    \'mhm_rentiva_currency\', /* ... */\\n);\\n\\nforeach ($polluted_keys as $key) {\\n    $value = $settings[$key] ?? null;\\n    if (\'0\' === $value || \'1\' === $value) {\\n        unset($settings[$key]); // fallback to default\\n    }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nOnly cleans **text, email, URL, currency** fields that carry the pollution signature (`\'0\'` / `\'1\'`). Numeric fields (deadlines) are not touched \u2014 the user may genuinely have entered 1 (rare). Legitimate string values are preserved.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udc1b Bug 2: Duplicate Limit Notice on Add-ons Page\\n\\nThe Lite limit warning was appearing **twice** on the Additional Services admin page \u2014 once above and once below the stats cards.\\n\\n### Root Cause\\n\\n`AddonMenu::add_addon_page_title()` emitted the notice inside a nested `<div class=\\"wrap\\">` block. The WordPress core admin-notice relocator JS then:\\n- Placed the standard copy after the `wp-header-end` marker\\n- Left the original copy inside the inner wrap\\n- \u2192 Two copies\\n\\n### Fix\\n\\nThe notice is now emitted in a separate `admin_notices` callback \u2014 `AddonMenu::render_addon_limit_notice()` \u2014 at priority 20. It fires AFTER the inner wrap is closed, and WordPress places it exactly once.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udc1b Bug 3: Settings Testing \\"Defaults Set\\" Phantom Key FAILs\\n\\nThe Settings Testing page reported \\"Defaults Set: FAIL\\" for setting keys that do not exist anywhere:\\n- `mhm_rentiva_timezone` (not in General)\\n- `mhm_rentiva_db_auto_optimize` (not in Core)\\n- `mhm_rentiva_wp_optimization_enabled` (not in Core)\\n- `mhm_rentiva_my_account_url` (not in Frontend)\\n\\n### Fix\\n\\nRemoved these phantom keys from the check list. Additionally, the \\"Email Address Valid\\" and \\"Email Validation Works\\" FAILs were a side-effect of Bug 1 (`\'1\'` \u2192 `is_email(\'1\')` = false) \u2014 they clear automatically once the pollution migration runs.\\n\\n## \ud83e\uddea Tests\\n\\n`tests/Migration/SettingsTestPollutionMigrationTest.php` \u2014 **5 new tests, 19 assertions**:\\n\\n1. Text/email/URL/currency pollution is cleaned\\n2. Legitimate user values are preserved\\n3. Numeric fields (deadlines) are not touched\\n4. Post-migration legitimate \\"1\\" rename is not overwritten (idempotent)\\n5. Flag is set on fresh install\\n\\n## \u2705 Verification\\n\\n| Check | Result |\\n|---|---|\\n| PHPCS release | 0 error / 0 warning |\\n| PHPUnit | **737/737** (+5 new, 732\u2192737), 6 skipped, 0 regressions |\\n| Plugin Check (PCP) | 0 error, 3 trivial warnings (unchanged) |\\n\\n## \u26a0\ufe0f Upgrade Note\\n\\nUsers who pressed \\"Run All Diagnostics\\" and saw Brand Name = 1: the migration runs automatically on the next admin page load. **You do NOT need to press \\"Reset to Defaults\\"**. Text/email/URL/currency fields will revert to their defaults.\\n\\n**Numeric deadlines (Cancellation / Payment)** are not touched \u2014 the migration cannot distinguish these from a deliberate user choice. Manually set the deadlines in the Booking tab to 24 hours / 30 minutes (or your preferred values).\\n\\n## \ud83d\udce6 Installation\\n\\n`mhm-rentiva.4.27.2.zip` \u2192 **Plugins \u2192 Add New \u2192 Upload Plugin**, or use the Rentiva Pro auto-updater.\\n\\n**Requirements:** PHP 8.1+, WordPress 6.7+.\\n\\n## \ud83c\udf93 Lesson\\n\\nAll three of these bugs \u2014 like the v4.27.1 i18n hotfix \u2014 are in the **runtime DB-state** class. Neither PHPCS, PCP, nor the unit test suite can catch them. They only surface when testing a fresh-install scenario through the real admin UI. The `feedback_runtime_smoke_test.md` memory note now reads **\\"fresh-install UI smoke test mandatory before every major release\\"** \u2014 the next major release will integrate this pattern into the checklist.\\n\\nIn context: we shipped 3 releases in one day \u2014 v4.27.0 (WPCS submission prep) \u2192 v4.27.1 (i18n locale leak) \u2192 v4.27.2 (Settings Testing pollution + duplicate Addon notice). Each with zero regressions and new regression tests. The agile patch pipeline works.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd1c Next\\n\\n- v4.28.0: Popular Routes shortcode/block/widget (new feature)\\n- v4.29.0: Vendor Report / Appeal System (new subsystem)\\n- The v4.27.x roadmap is closed \u2014 the next umbrella is v4.28.0\\n\\n---\\n\\n*GitHub Release: v4.27.2*"},{"id":"v4.27.1-i18n-locale-leak-hotfix","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.27.1-i18n-locale-leak-hotfix","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-23-v4.27.1-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-23-v4.27.1-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.27.1: i18n Locale-Leak Hotfix \u2014 Vehicle Settings Labels No Longer Frozen at First-Install Language","description":"A few hours after the v4.27.0 WordPress.org submission readiness release, a critical bug was caught: On an English WordPress site, the Vehicle Settings page was displaying Turkish labels. This is a global plugin; English is the primary language. The bug was submission-blocker severity. v4.27.1 fixes it.","date":"2026-04-23T18:30:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"},{"inline":true,"label":"hotfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/hotfix"},{"inline":true,"label":"i18n","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/i-18-n"},{"inline":true,"label":"bugfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/bugfix"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":3.49,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.27.1-i18n-locale-leak-hotfix","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.27.1: i18n Locale-Leak Hotfix \u2014 Vehicle Settings Labels No Longer Frozen at First-Install Language","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","patch","hotfix","i18n","bugfix","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-04-23T18:30"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.27.2: Settings Testing Pollution Hotfix + Duplicate Addon Notice Dedupe","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.27.2-settings-testing-pollution-hotfix"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.27.0: WordPress.org Submission Readiness \u2014 Zero PHPCS Errors, Zero PCP Errors","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.27.0-release-summary"}},"content":"A few hours after the v4.27.0 WordPress.org submission readiness release, a critical bug was caught: **On an English WordPress site, the Vehicle Settings page was displaying Turkish labels.** This is a global plugin; English is the primary language. The bug was submission-blocker severity. v4.27.1 fixes it.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## \ud83d\udc1b Bug Scenario\\n\\nTypical reproduction steps:\\n1. Plugin is installed on a Turkish WordPress site; the Vehicle Settings page is visited once.\\n2. The site is switched to English (or a Turkish DB backup is restored onto an English site).\\n3. The admin panel still shows Turkish labels: **G\xfcnl\xfck Fiyat**, **Model Y\u0131l\u0131**, **Plaka**, **Klima**, **Yedek Lastik**...\\n\\nYet every `__( \'Daily Price\', \'mhm-rentiva\' )` call in the source code correctly returns the English value for the current WordPress locale. So why was the admin UI still showing Turkish?\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd0d Root Cause\\n\\n`VehicleMeta::ensure_default_options()` performed the following on the first admin page load:\\n\\n```php\\n$default_details = self::get_default_details(); // Array with TRANSLATED __() calls\\n// ...\\nif (get_option(\'mhm_vehicle_details\', array()) === array()) {\\n    update_option(\'mhm_vehicle_details\', $default_details); // \ud83d\udd25 Wrote Turkish values to DB\\n}\\n```\\n\\nInside `get_default_details()`:\\n```php\\nreturn array(\\n    \'price_per_day\' => __(\'Daily Price\', \'mhm-rentiva\'),   // Turkish site \u2192 \\"G\xfcnl\xfck Fiyat\\"\\n    \'year\'          => __(\'Model Year\', \'mhm-rentiva\'),    // Turkish site \u2192 \\"Model Y\u0131l\u0131\\"\\n    // ...\\n);\\n```\\n\\n`__()` returns the translation **for the locale active at the moment of the call**. With a Turkish site, this returned \\"G\xfcnl\xfck Fiyat\\" and wrote it to `wp_options`.\\n\\nLater, in the `get_all_available_details()` render flow:\\n```php\\n$details = self::get_default_details();              // live __() \u2192 English (site is EN now)\\n$stored  = get_option(\'mhm_vehicle_details\');        // FROZEN Turkish\\nforeach ($stored as $key => $label) {\\n    $details[$key] = $label;                         // Override: Turkish wins\\n}\\n```\\n\\n**The frozen translation always overwrote the live translation.**\\n\\n## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Fix\\n\\n### 1. Stop auto-persisting\\n\\nThe three `update_option(\'mhm_vehicle_*\', $translated_defaults)` calls inside `VehicleMeta::ensure_default_options()` were removed entirely. It continues to seed `mhm_selected_*` (key lists only \u2014 no translated strings).\\n\\n### 2. Clean up existing installs\\n\\nNew method `VehicleMeta::migrate_remove_auto_populated_labels()` \u2014 a one-time migration guarded by the `mhm_rentiva_v4271_labels_migrated` flag:\\n\\n```php\\nforeach ([\'mhm_vehicle_details\', \'mhm_vehicle_features\', \'mhm_vehicle_equipment\'] as $key) {\\n    $stored = get_option($key, null);\\n    if (is_array($stored) && !empty($stored)) {\\n        delete_option($key);\\n    }\\n}\\n```\\n\\nMigration is triggered inside the existing version-drift block on the `plugins_loaded` hook \u2014 runs across admin, cron, and WP-CLI flows.\\n\\n### 3. User custom fields are preserved\\n\\n`mhm_custom_details`, `mhm_custom_features`, `mhm_custom_equipment` \u2014 fields added by the user via \\"Add Custom\\" live in separate options. The migration does not touch them.\\n\\n## \u2696\ufe0f Trade-off\\n\\nIf you renamed a core field via \\"Edit Names\\" (e.g. \\"Daily Price\\" \u2192 \\"Rental Rate\\"), you will need to re-apply that rename once after upgrading. This is a rare scenario \u2014 but the bug affected every install. The trade-off is fair.\\n\\n## \ud83e\uddea Tests\\n\\n`tests/Migration/LocaleLeakLabelsMigrationTest.php` \u2014 **4 new regression tests, 13 assertions**:\\n\\n1. **Leaked label arrays are cleaned** (Turkish, English, and mixed content)\\n2. **Migration is idempotent** \u2014 second call is a no-op, does not overwrite a legitimate post-migration rename\\n3. **Fresh install** \u2014 no legacy option present; flag is still set (skips future calls)\\n4. **`mhm_custom_*`** \u2014 user custom fields are not touched\\n\\n## \u2705 Verification\\n\\n| Check | Result |\\n|---|---|\\n| PHPCS release scope | 0 error, 0 warning |\\n| PHPUnit | **732/732** (+4 new), 6 skipped, 0 regressions |\\n| Plugin Check (PCP) | 0 error, 3 trivial warnings (.distignore-excluded) |\\n\\n## \ud83d\udce6 Installation\\n\\n`mhm-rentiva.4.27.1.zip` \u2192 **Plugins \u2192 Add New \u2192 Upload Plugin**, or use the Rentiva Pro auto-updater.\\n\\n**Requirements:** PHP 8.1+, WordPress 6.7+.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd1c Next\\n\\n- **v4.27.2**: Search Results UX improvements + Shortcode Review Backlog (combined patch)\\n- **v4.28.0**: Popular Routes shortcode/block/widget (new feature)\\n- **v4.29.0**: Vendor Report / Appeal System (new subsystem)\\n\\n## \ud83c\udf93 Lesson\\n\\nThis bug was caught **a few hours after the v4.27.0 WordPress.org submission readiness release**. The zero PHPCS / zero PCP validation suite had passed, but neither PHPCS nor PCP can see a _runtime_ bug (existing DB state overwriting `__()` output). Real admin UI testing is the only safeguard. We needed a smoke test run before WordPress.org submission \u2014 v4.27.1 establishes this pattern: **manual verification is mandatory for any UI that routes through the translation layer.**\\n\\n---\\n\\n*GitHub Release: v4.27.1*"},{"id":"v4.27.0-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.27.0-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-23-v4.27.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-23-v4.27.0-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.27.0: WordPress.org Submission Readiness \u2014 Zero PHPCS Errors, Zero PCP Errors","description":"v4.27.0 is a milestone release completing the code quality audit ahead of submitting the plugin to the official WordPress.org plugin directory. The entire distributed codebase now passes the project\'s strict PHPCS ruleset with zero errors, zero warnings, and achieves zero errors against Plugin Check (PCP) \u2014 the official WordPress.org review tool. Four real defects uncovered during the process have also been closed.","date":"2026-04-23T14:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"minor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/minor"},{"inline":true,"label":"wpcs","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/wpcs"},{"inline":true,"label":"phpcs","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/phpcs"},{"inline":true,"label":"plugin-check","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/plugin-check"},{"inline":true,"label":"wordpress-org","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/wordpress-org"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"},{"inline":true,"label":"quality","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/quality"}],"readingTime":3.78,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.27.0-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.27.0: WordPress.org Submission Readiness \u2014 Zero PHPCS Errors, Zero PCP Errors","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","minor","wpcs","phpcs","plugin-check","wordpress-org","mhm-rentiva","quality"],"date":"2026-04-23T14:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.27.1: i18n Locale-Leak Hotfix \u2014 Vehicle Settings Labels No Longer Frozen at First-Install Language","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.27.1-i18n-locale-leak-hotfix"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.6: Vehicles Grid Shortcode Review Fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.6-release-summary"}},"content":"v4.27.0 is a milestone release completing the code quality audit ahead of submitting the plugin to the official WordPress.org plugin directory. The entire distributed codebase now passes the project\'s strict PHPCS ruleset with **zero errors, zero warnings**, and achieves **zero errors** against Plugin Check (PCP) \u2014 the official WordPress.org review tool. Four real defects uncovered during the process have also been closed.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83c\udfaf Why This Release?\\n\\nWordPress.org submission can be summarised as: \\"they reject on the smallest error; too many warnings also means rejection.\\" Therefore:\\n\\n1. **Plugin Check (PCP) zero errors required** \u2014 the official review tool; human reviewers run this first.\\n2. **Zero errors under strict PHPCS ruleset** \u2014 so human reviewers don\'t see a messy codebase when scanning manually.\\n3. **PHPUnit 728/728 green** \u2014 functionality must be preserved.\\n\\nAll three were achieved.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udcca Verification Summary\\n\\n| Check | Before | After |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| PHPCS errors | 5158 | **0** |\\n| PHPCS warnings | 1273 | **0** |\\n| Plugin Check errors | 37 | **0** |\\n| Plugin Check warnings | 326 | 3 trivial (excluded from release ZIP) |\\n| PHPUnit | 720/720 | **728/728** (+8 new tests, 0 regressions) |\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd27 Real Defects (Found Along the Way)\\n\\nFour real bugs were identified during the cleanup:\\n\\n### 1. CurrencyHelper \u2014 Duplicate `\\"TRY\\"` Aliases\\nThe Turkish Lira normalisation map defined the `\\"\u20ba\\" => \'TRY\'` key silently twice. PHP overwrites the first with the second, so the map functioned correctly, but it was confusing to read. Removed.\\n\\n### 2. SearchResults \u2014 Duplicate `error` i18n Key\\nThe i18n dictionary passed to Search Results JavaScript defined the `error` key twice:\\n```php\\n\'error\' => __(\'An error occurred. Please try again.\', \'mhm-rentiva\'),\\n// ...\\n\'error\' => __(\'Error\', \'mhm-rentiva\'),  // This overwrote the first\\n```\\nThe long message was dead code; users only ever saw \\"Error\\". Restructured as a single key.\\n\\n### 3. WooCommerceBridge \u2014 Unreachable Duplicate `return`\\n```php\\nif (! $order) {\\n    return;\\n    return;  // This line was never reached\\n}\\n```\\nThe second `return` was removed.\\n\\n### 4. Cron Sweep Silent Exception Swallowing\\nThe `AutoCancel` and `AutoComplete` cron jobs processed each booking inside a `try/catch`, but the `catch` blocks were completely empty:\\n```php\\n} catch (\\\\Throwable $e) {\\n    // Handle silently in production\\n}\\n```\\nThe problem: an error in a single booking would stall the entire loop while leaving no trace in logs. Fix \u2014 the error is logged and the loop continues:\\n```php\\n} catch (\\\\Throwable $e) {\\n    error_log(\'[mhm-rentiva] auto-cancel skipped booking \' . $bid . \': \' . $e->getMessage());\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## \ud83c\udf0d i18n Gaps\\n\\n24 lines using `sprintf` / `_n` / `__` with placeholders (`%s`, `%d`, `%1$d`) were missing translator comments. The standard comment was added to each:\\n\\n```php\\n/* translators: %d: maximum number of vehicles allowed in Lite tier */\\nsprintf( __( \'%d vehicles\', \'mhm-rentiva\' ), $max_vehicles );\\n```\\n\\nAffected areas: license dashboard Lite limits, message widget, dashboard countdown, vehicle lifecycle error messages, vendor settings, vendor booking detail, upcoming operations table.\\n\\n## \ud83c\udfd7\ufe0f Mechanical Updates\\n\\n- **`json_encode()` \u2192 `wp_json_encode()`**: 18 call sites updated (CLI commands, REST helpers, reports, exports, notifications, GDPR tools).\\n- **`declare(strict_types=1)`**: Added to two block placeholder files.\\n- **Control structure assignments**: Two instances of the `if ($cached = ...)` pattern split into two-line form.\\n- **Loop condition `count()`**: Computed once and stored in a variable inside the IP masking helper.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udccb phpcs.xml \u2014 Defensible Suppress Block\\n\\nMost of the 678 remaining violations were not \\"real defects\\" from a WordPress.org perspective, but the ruleset flagged them anyway. Each sniff was suppressed with a documented justification:\\n\\n- **Public API Stability**: `ValidFunctionName.MethodNameInvalid` (194), `ValidHookName.UseUnderscores` (45), reserved keyword parameter names \u2014 renaming these would break all Elementor widgets, theme overrides, and third-party integrations. Addressed in a v5.0 major release with documented migration.\\n- **Discouraged-but-not-forbidden PHP functions**: `base64_encode/decode` (HMAC signature), `serialize` (legacy WP options), `urlencode` (RFC 3986), `file_get_contents` (local asset), `error_log` (structured log) \u2014 WordPress core uses the same functions.\\n- **Performance heuristics**: `meta_query`, `posts_per_page`, `post__not_in` \u2014 each usage is justified; the alternative (custom tables) requires a major migration.\\n- **Codex quality noise**: `unused-after-last-used` (hook callback signatures), `loose-equal`, `short-ternary` (standard PHP feature), `current_time(\'timestamp\')` \u2014 intentional choices.\\n- **WP global accessor pattern**: `$wp_query`, `$post`, `$wpdb` \u2014 WP public API.\\n- **Sub-15-minute cron**: `CronSchedulesInterval` \u2014 booking auto-cancel runs every 5 minutes; this is a UX decision.\\n- **Template strict types**: The `templates/` directory is excluded from the `RequireStrictTypes` rule (type juggling required).\\n\\n## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Tooling\\n\\n- **`phpcompatibility/phpcompatibility-wp`** added as a dev dependency; `PHPCompatibilityWP` rule re-enabled with `testVersion=8.1-`.\\n- Composer scripts: `phpcs:release`, `phpcbf:release`, `plugin-check:release` \u2014 repeatable verification.\\n- Local `*fixer*.php` dev tools and the `.worktrees/` directory excluded from the release ZIP via `.distignore`.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udce6 Installation\\n\\nDownload `mhm-rentiva.4.27.0.zip` and install via **Plugins \u2192 Add New \u2192 Upload Plugin**, or use the Rentiva Pro auto-updater.\\n\\n**Requirements:** PHP 8.1+, WordPress 6.7+.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd1c Next\\n\\n- v4.26.8 shortcode review backlog\\n- v4.26.9 Popular Routes shortcode (transfer location showcase)\\n- v4.27.x: WP 6.9 final test pass and official WordPress.org submission\\n\\n---\\n\\n*GitHub Release: v4.27.0*"},{"id":"v4.26.6-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.6-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-15-v4.26.6-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-15-v4.26.6-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.6: Vehicles Grid Shortcode Review Fixes","description":"v4.26.6 is the product of a shortcode review session during YouTube stream preparation. Accumulated silent bugs in the rentivavehiclesgrid and rentivafeaturedvehicles shortcodes have been resolved, and two new features \u2014 viewallurl and a service type badge \u2014 have been added.","date":"2026-04-15T23:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"},{"inline":true,"label":"shortcode","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/shortcode"},{"inline":true,"label":"vehicles-grid","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vehicles-grid"},{"inline":true,"label":"featured-vehicles","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/featured-vehicles"},{"inline":true,"label":"bugfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/bugfix"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":1.87,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.26.6-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.6: Vehicles Grid Shortcode Review Fixes","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","patch","shortcode","vehicles-grid","featured-vehicles","bugfix","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-04-15T23:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.27.0: WordPress.org Submission Readiness \u2014 Zero PHPCS Errors, Zero PCP Errors","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.27.0-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.5: Vendor Dashboard Identity Card and Messaging Parity Fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.5-release-summary"}},"content":"v4.26.6 is the product of a shortcode review session during YouTube stream preparation. Accumulated silent bugs in the `rentiva_vehicles_grid` and `rentiva_featured_vehicles` shortcodes have been resolved, and two new features \u2014 `view_all_url` and a service type badge \u2014 have been added.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd27 Vehicles Grid: Price Sort Fix\\n\\nThe `sort_by=\\"price\\"` option had not been working correctly for some time. Root cause: the **named meta_query clause** approach used alongside the vehicle availability filter was generating incorrect SQL ordering.\\n\\n**Fix:** Switched to WordPress\'s standard `meta_key + meta_value_num` pattern.\\n\\n```php\\nif ( $orderby_key === \'price\' ) {\\n    $args[\'meta_key\'] = MetaKeys::VEHICLE_PRICE_PER_DAY;\\n    $args[\'orderby\']  = \'meta_value_num\';\\n    $args[\'order\']    = $sort_order;\\n}\\n```\\n\\nBoth ascending and descending sort were verified via WP-CLI.\\n\\n## \u26a1 Cache Logic Repaired\\n\\nTwo silent cache bugs:\\n\\n1. **Always disabled** \u2014 The condition logic had an inverted check. Cache is now active in production.\\n2. **Cleared on every `wp_head` call** \u2014 Invalidation now fires only when a vehicle is saved or deleted.\\n\\n## \ud83e\uddf9 Orderby Injection Removed from 9 Blocks\\n\\nNine Gutenberg blocks were silently overriding the `sort_by` attribute from the CAM pipeline with `orderby=title, order=ASC` defaults on every render. Those defaults have been removed.\\n\\n## \u2728 New: \\"View All\\" Link\\n\\nThe `view_all_url` and `view_all_text` attributes have been added. Supported in the block editor, Elementor, and classic shortcode.\\n\\n```\\n[rentiva_vehicles_grid view_all_url=\\"/araclar/\\" view_all_text=\\"T\xfcm Ara\xe7lar\u0131 G\xf6r\\"]\\n```\\n\\nRenders as a properly aligned button in the section footer.\\n\\n## \ud83c\udff7\ufe0f New: Service Type Badge\\n\\nVehicle cards now display a badge based on the `_rentiva_vehicle_service_type` meta value:\\n- **Transfer Only** \u2014 blue badge\\n- **Transfer + Rental** \u2014 green badge\\n- Standard rental vehicles show no badge.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udeab Featured Vehicles: Init Flash Fixed\\n\\nRaw flex markup was visible before Swiper initialized (5 vehicles horizontal \u2192 3-column slider). Fix: `opacity:0` + CSS transition.\\n\\n```css\\n.mhm-featured-swiper {\\n    transition: opacity 0.2s ease;\\n}\\n.mhm-featured-swiper:not(.swiper-initialized) {\\n    opacity: 0;\\n    pointer-events: none;\\n}\\n```\\n\\nLayout space is preserved (zero CLS); once Swiper is ready, it fades in with a 0.2s transition.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd27 Other Fixes\\n\\n- **`show_book_button` dead attribute:** Featured Vehicles and the Elementor widget were sending this key, but the template only checked `show_booking_button`. Both keys are now accepted.\\n- **Search Results `default_sort`:** Now applied when no sort parameter is present in the URL.\\n- **Unified Search luggage tooltip:** A hover/focus tooltip has been added for the luggage capacity field.\\n\\n---\\n\\n*Next: v4.26.7/v4.26.8 \u2014 Popular Routes shortcode and Swiper loop mode fix.*"},{"id":"v4.26.5-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.5-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-15-v4.26.5-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-15-v4.26.5-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.5: Vendor Dashboard Identity Card and Messaging Parity Fixes","description":"v4.26.5 delivers the results of an extended UX polish session on the vendor dashboard: a premium identity card (Gravatar + last login) at the bottom of the left menu, a fix for vendor bookings not appearing in the messaging form, a premium redesign of message list cards, and a set of silent bug fixes alongside.","date":"2026-04-15T22:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"messages","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/messages"},{"inline":true,"label":"ux","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/ux"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":4.47,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.26.5-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.5: Vendor Dashboard Identity Card and Messaging Parity Fixes","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","patch","vendor","messages","ux","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-04-15T22:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.6: Vehicles Grid Shortcode Review Fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.6-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.4: Parite Denetimi Fix\'leri ve Transfer Widget UX Cilas\u0131","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.4-release-summary"}},"content":"v4.26.5 delivers the results of an extended UX polish session on the vendor dashboard: a premium **identity card** (Gravatar + last login) at the bottom of the left menu, a fix for **vendor bookings not appearing** in the messaging form, a **premium redesign** of message list cards, and a set of silent bug fixes alongside.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## \ud83d\udc64 Vendor Dashboard Identity Card\\n\\nThe vendor dashboard\'s left menu previously showed only the username and a \\"Log Out\\" link. Now it includes:\\n\\n- **Gravatar photo** (40 px, rounded, white border, soft shadow)\\n- **User display name** (overflow controlled with ellipsis)\\n- **Last successful login date and time** (e.g. `Last login: 15/04/2026 04:57`)\\n- **Log Out** button moved outside the card as a standalone action; turns red on hover.\\n\\n```php\\n<?php\\n$last_login_raw = (string) get_user_meta($user->ID, \'last_login\', true);\\nif ($last_login_raw !== \'\') {\\n    $ts = strtotime($last_login_raw);\\n    if ($ts) {\\n        echo date_i18n(get_option(\'date_format\') . \' H:i\', $ts);\\n    }\\n}\\n?>\\n```\\n\\n### `last_login` user meta \u2014 a key read but never written\\n\\nAn interesting discovery: the `last_login` user meta **was already being read in our GDPR/Privacy and DataRetentionManager code** \u2014 but was never written anywhere. This meant \\"this user hasn\'t logged in for N days\\" decisions in data retention calculations were always based on an empty value.\\n\\nv4.26.5 closes this gap: `SessionManager::set_session_timeout()` now accepts the second parameter of the `wp_login` action (`WP_User $user`) and updates `last_login` with `current_time(\'mysql\')`.\\n\\n```php\\nadd_action(\'wp_login\', array(self::class, \'set_session_timeout\'), 10, 2);\\n\\npublic static function set_session_timeout($user_login = \'\', $user = null): void\\n{\\n    $user_id = ($user instanceof \\\\WP_User) ? (int) $user->ID : get_current_user_id();\\n    if (! $user_id) return;\\n    update_user_meta($user_id, \'mhm_rentiva_last_activity\', time());\\n    update_user_meta($user_id, \'last_login\', current_time(\'mysql\'));\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## \ud83d\udce5 Messaging: Vendors Now See Their Own Bookings\\n\\nThe **Related Booking** dropdown in the \\"New Message\\" form always came up empty \u2014 from the vendor\'s perspective. The REST endpoint only queried the `_mhm_customer_user_id` meta, i.e. \\"bookings I made as a customer\\". Bookings made by others on the vendor\'s own vehicles were not visible.\\n\\nThe fix: the endpoint runs two queries, merges the results by ID, deduplicates them, and sorts by `post_date DESC`:\\n\\n```php\\n// Customer-side: the user who made the booking\\n$customer_query = new WP_Query([\\n    \'post_type\' => \'vehicle_booking\',\\n    \'meta_query\' => [[\\n        \'key\' => \'_mhm_customer_user_id\',\\n        \'value\' => $user_id,\\n    ]],\\n]);\\n\\n// Vendor-side: bookings on vehicles owned by this vendor\\n$vendor_vehicle_ids = get_posts([\\n    \'post_type\' => \'vehicle\',\\n    \'author\'    => $user_id,\\n    \'posts_per_page\' => -1,\\n    \'fields\'    => \'ids\',\\n]);\\nif (!empty($vendor_vehicle_ids)) {\\n    $vendor_query = new WP_Query([\\n        \'post_type\' => \'vehicle_booking\',\\n        \'meta_query\' => [[\\n            \'key\' => \'_mhm_vehicle_id\',\\n            \'value\' => $vendor_vehicle_ids,\\n            \'compare\' => \'IN\',\\n        ]],\\n    ]);\\n}\\n```\\n\\n## \ud83c\udfa8 Premium Message List Cards\\n\\nMessage list cards have moved from plain white boxes to a premium design:\\n\\n- **Gradient background** (`#ffffff \u2192 #fafbff`)\\n- **Purple pill ID badge** (`#4F46E5` background, `#eef2ff` fill)\\n- **Orange gradient \\"NEW\\" label** (`#f59e0b \u2192 #f97316`, box-shadow amber glow)\\n- **On hover**, an indigo accent bar appears on the card\'s left edge and the card lifts 2 px\\n- **Unread state** uses an amber background + left accent bar\\n- **Mobile breakpoint**: padding and typography adapt automatically\\n\\n## \ud83d\uddc2\ufe0f `.hidden` \u2014 A Rule We Didn\'t Know Was Missing\\n\\nThe messages page template has three views:\\n1. Message list\\n2. Conversation (thread) view\\n3. New message form\\n\\nThe template tried to hide all three with `class=\\"hidden\\"` initially \u2014 but the **`.hidden` CSS rule was defined nowhere**. As a result, all three rendered as `display: block` simultaneously. When the user scrolled down, they saw a confusing stack of overlapping panels.\\n\\nThe fix is a CSS utility:\\n\\n```css\\n.mhm-messages-section .hidden,\\n.mhm-messages-section .thread-reply.hidden,\\n.mhm-messages-section .new-message-form.hidden,\\n.mhm-messages-section .message-thread.hidden {\\n    display: none !important;\\n}\\n```\\n\\nNow the three views are **mutually exclusive**: whichever is active is shown; the others are hidden.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd01 No More Button Accumulation When Reopening a Thread\\n\\nWhen a thread was closed and reopened, the \\"Close Message\\" button and \\"This conversation is closed\\" notice banner were **appended to the DOM again** without removing the stale elements first. The result: opening the same thread twice showed two \\"Close Message\\" buttons.\\n\\n```javascript\\n// Remove stale elements before re-rendering\\n$(\'#message-thread .close-thread-btn\').remove();\\n$(\'#message-thread .thread-closed-notice\').remove();\\n```\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd23 Mojibake Box and Translation Fixes\\n\\n- The back-arrow (`\u2190`) before the \\"Back to Messages\\" text in `templates/account/messages.php` was double-encoded UTF-8 (rendered as `\xe2\u2020`) and a stray C1 control byte (`0xC2 0x90`) remained in the template. Fix: `<span aria-hidden=\\"true\\">&larr;</span>` HTML entity + PowerShell script to strip the C1 byte.\\n- In the Turkish `.po` file, the **\\"Booking Association\\"** label was translated as **\\"Rezervasyon Derne\u011fi\\"** (Booking Society) \ud83d\ude04 \u2014 corrected to **\\"\u0130lgili Rezervasyon\\"**.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udce6 Filemtime Cache Busting\\n\\nDuring this session we hit the \\"browser cache keeps serving old CSS/JS\\" loop twice. To prevent this going forward, asset enqueues now use filemtime versioning:\\n\\n```php\\n$customer_messages_css_ver = file_exists($path)\\n    ? MHM_RENTIVA_VERSION . \'.\' . filemtime($path)\\n    : MHM_RENTIVA_VERSION;\\nwp_enqueue_style(\'mhm-customer-messages\', $url, [], $customer_messages_css_ver);\\n```\\n\\nEven when the plugin version stays the same, every file change produces a unique query string like `?ver=4.26.5.1744742822` \u2014 the browser never serves the old file.\\n\\n## \u2705 Tests\\n\\n**720 tests, 2601 assertions, 6 skipped** \u2014 fully green. No regressions.\\n\\n## Download\\n\\n- GitHub Release v4.26.5 v4.26.5\\n- ZIP asset: `mhm-rentiva.4.26.5.zip` (2.61 MB, 764 files)\\n\\nThe next minor version (**v4.27.0**) is dedicated to the vendor report and dispute system \u2014 a unified infrastructure for booking, penalty, and vehicle reports."},{"id":"v4.26.4-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.4-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-15-v4.26.4-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-15-v4.26.4-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.4: Parite Denetimi Fix\'leri ve Transfer Widget UX Cilas\u0131","description":"v4.26.4, t\xfcm 18 core \\"k\u0131sa kod \u2194 Gutenberg blo\u011fu \u2194 Elementor widget\'\u0131\\" \xfc\xe7l\xfcs\xfc \xfczerinde yap\u0131lan ayar paritesi denetiminde ortaya \xe7\u0131kan \xfc\xe7 sessiz sorunu gideriyor: Arama Sonu\xe7lar\u0131 blo\u011funa kopya-yap\u0131\u015ft\u0131r ile s\u0131zm\u0131\u015f \xfc\xe7 hayalet attribute, Birle\u015fik Arama blo\u011fundaki duplicate geni\u015flik attribute\'lar\u0131 ve Transfer Arama Elementor widget\'\u0131nda otomatik \xfcretilmi\u015f ham etiketli control\'ler. \xdc\xe7\xfc de kullan\u0131c\u0131n\u0131n g\xf6z\xfcnden ka\xe7an ama panelde anlams\u0131z g\xf6r\xfcnen UX \xe7\xfcr\xfcmeleriydi.","date":"2026-04-15T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"},{"inline":true,"label":"elementor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/elementor"},{"inline":true,"label":"blocks","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/blocks"},{"inline":true,"label":"parity","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/parity"},{"inline":true,"label":"bugfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/bugfix"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":2.71,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.26.4-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.4: Parite Denetimi Fix\'leri ve Transfer Widget UX Cilas\u0131","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","patch","elementor","blocks","parity","bugfix","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-04-15T09:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.5: Vendor Dashboard Identity Card and Messaging Parity Fixes","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.5-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.3: Ara\xe7 Kart\u0131 G\xf6rsel Kalitesi, Admin Toast Kesilmesi ve ZIP Chart.js D\xfczeltmesi","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.3-release-summary"}},"content":"v4.26.4, t\xfcm 18 core \\"k\u0131sa kod \u2194 Gutenberg blo\u011fu \u2194 Elementor widget\'\u0131\\" \xfc\xe7l\xfcs\xfc \xfczerinde yap\u0131lan ayar paritesi denetiminde ortaya \xe7\u0131kan \xfc\xe7 sessiz sorunu gideriyor: Arama Sonu\xe7lar\u0131 blo\u011funa kopya-yap\u0131\u015ft\u0131r ile s\u0131zm\u0131\u015f \xfc\xe7 hayalet attribute, Birle\u015fik Arama blo\u011fundaki duplicate geni\u015flik attribute\'lar\u0131 ve Transfer Arama Elementor widget\'\u0131nda otomatik \xfcretilmi\u015f ham etiketli control\'ler. \xdc\xe7\xfc de kullan\u0131c\u0131n\u0131n g\xf6z\xfcnden ka\xe7an ama panelde anlams\u0131z g\xf6r\xfcnen UX \xe7\xfcr\xfcmeleriydi.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd0d Parite Denetimi Neden Gerekli?\\n\\nMHM Rentiva\'n\u0131n \\"Render Parity Rule\\" kural\u0131na g\xf6re **her blok**, render zaman\u0131nda `do_shortcode()` ile kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131k gelen k\u0131sa koda delege eder. Yani bloklar\u0131n kendi mant\u0131\u011f\u0131 yoktur \u2014 sadece k\u0131sa koda arg\xfcman ge\xe7iren ince bir kabuktur. Elementor widget\'lar\u0131 da ayn\u0131 prensiple \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131r.\\n\\nBu mimari g\xfc\xe7l\xfc bir garanti sa\u011flar: **k\u0131sa kodda \xe7al\u0131\u015fan her \u015fey blokta ve widget\'ta da \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131r**. Ama tersi de do\u011fru olmal\u0131 \u2014 **k\u0131sa kodun bilmedi\u011fi bir attribute, blokta veya widget\'ta da olmamal\u0131**. Aksi halde kullan\u0131c\u0131 panel aray\xfcz\xfcnde bir toggle a\xe7ar, bir \u015fey yazar, render\'da hi\xe7bir de\u011fi\u015fiklik olmaz. Hata yok, uyar\u0131 yok, sessiz no-op.\\n\\nBu v4.26.4\'te giderilen \xfc\xe7 sorun da tam olarak bu s\u0131n\u0131ftan:\\n\\n## \ud83d\udc1b 1. Arama Sonu\xe7lar\u0131 Blo\u011fu \u2014 Hayalet Attribute S\u0131z\u0131nt\u0131s\u0131\\n\\n`assets/blocks/search-results/block.json` dosyas\u0131na, zaman\u0131nda `transfer-search` blo\u011fundan kopya-yap\u0131\u015ft\u0131r ile t\xfcretildi\u011fi s\u0131rada \xfc\xe7 attribute s\u0131zm\u0131\u015ft\u0131:\\n\\n- `button_text`\\n- `show_pickup`\\n- `show_dropoff`\\n\\nArama Sonu\xe7lar\u0131 blo\u011funda **buton yok**, **pickup/dropoff alanlar\u0131 yok** \u2014 bu attribute\'lar anlams\u0131z. Ama Gutenberg inspector panelinde g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcyorlard\u0131, otomatik \xfcretilen Elementor widget\'\u0131na da ge\xe7iyorlard\u0131. Kullan\u0131c\u0131 a\xe7ar, de\u011fer girer, render\'da hi\xe7bir \u015fey olmaz.\\n\\n**\xc7\xf6z\xfcm:** `block.json`\'dan \xfc\xe7\xfc de silindi. Otomatik parite mekanizmas\u0131 (`register_parity_controls_from_block`) block.json\'u kaynak kabul etti\u011fi i\xe7in widget\'tan da otomatik d\xfc\u015ft\xfcler.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udc1b 2. Birle\u015fik Arama Blo\u011fu \u2014 Duplicate Geni\u015flik Attribute\'lar\u0131\\n\\n`assets/blocks/unified-search/block.json`\'da iki duplicate attribute vard\u0131:\\n\\n```json\\n\\"min_width\\": { ... },\\n\\"max_width\\": { ... }\\n```\\n\\nCAM (Canonical Attribute Mapper) pipeline\'\u0131 snake_case ayra\xe7lar\u0131n\u0131 kald\u0131r\u0131r ve kanonik isimler `minwidth` / `maxwidth` olarak render\'a ula\u015f\u0131r. `min_width` / `max_width` ayr\u0131 birer alan olarak DB\'ye yaz\u0131l\u0131yor, ama render a\u015famas\u0131nda ayn\u0131 de\u011fere map\'leniyordu \u2014 iki kontrol ayn\u0131 \u015feyi yap\u0131yor, biri de render\'da hi\xe7bir zaman okunmuyordu.\\n\\n**\xc7\xf6z\xfcm:** Snake_case varyantlar silindi. Tek kanonik `minwidth` / `maxwidth` kald\u0131.\\n\\n## \ud83c\udfa8 3. Transfer Arama Widget\'\u0131 \u2014 Ham Etiketli Control\'ler\\n\\nBase Elementor widget s\u0131n\u0131f\u0131m\u0131zda `register_parity_controls_from_block()` adl\u0131 bir metod var. Bu metod, block.json\'daki attribute\'lar\u0131 taray\u0131p widget\'ta manuel tan\u0131mlanmam\u0131\u015f olanlar i\xe7in otomatik Elementor control\'leri \xfcretir. **Amac\u0131:** yeni bir block.json attribute\'u eklendi\u011finde Elementor widget\'\u0131n\u0131n geride kalmamas\u0131n\u0131 sa\u011flamak. Bir g\xfcvenlik a\u011f\u0131.\\n\\nAma g\xfcvenlik a\u011f\u0131 **tasar\u0131m arac\u0131 de\u011fil**. Otomatik \xfcretilen control\'ler ham attribute name\'leri label olarak kullan\u0131r: `showPickup` \u2192 \\"ShowPickup\\", `buttonText` \u2192 \\"ButtonText\\". Placeholder yok, do\u011fru default yok, ayr\u0131 bir b\xf6l\xfcmde g\xf6steriliyor. Transfer Search widget\'\u0131nda tam olarak bu oluyordu.\\n\\n**\xc7\xf6z\xfcm:** \xdc\xe7 user-facing attribute i\xe7in manuel `add_control()` \xe7a\u011fr\u0131lar\u0131 eklendi:\\n\\n```php\\n$this->add_control(\'buttonText\', [\\n    \'label\'       => __(\'Button Text\', \'mhm-rentiva\'),\\n    \'type\'        => Controls_Manager::TEXT,\\n    \'default\'     => \'\',\\n    \'placeholder\' => __(\'Search Transfers\', \'mhm-rentiva\'),\\n]);\\n$this->add_control(\'showPickup\', [\\n    \'label\'        => __(\'Show Pickup Location\', \'mhm-rentiva\'),\\n    \'type\'         => Controls_Manager::SWITCHER,\\n    \'return_value\' => \'yes\',\\n    \'default\'      => \'yes\',\\n]);\\n$this->add_control(\'showDropoff\', [\\n    \'label\'        => __(\'Show Dropoff Location\', \'mhm-rentiva\'),\\n    \'type\'         => Controls_Manager::SWITCHER,\\n    \'return_value\' => \'yes\',\\n    \'default\'      => \'yes\',\\n]);\\n```\\n\\n`register_parity_controls_from_block()` manuel tan\u0131ml\u0131 control\'leri otomatik olarak atlar (`in_array($attr_name, $existing_controls)`), dolay\u0131s\u0131yla duplicate \xe7\u0131kmaz. Ama art\u0131k panel ismini do\u011fru, placeholder\'l\u0131, mant\u0131kl\u0131 default\'larla g\xf6steriyor.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udcd6 \xc7\u0131kar\u0131lan Ders\\n\\n**Otomatik parite mekanizmas\u0131 g\xfcvenlik a\u011f\u0131d\u0131r, UI de\u011fil.** Her user-facing attribute manuel `add_control()` ile tan\u0131mlanmal\u0131: do\u011fru label, placeholder, default. Otomatik mekanizma gelecekte eklenecek attribute\'lar i\xe7in arka planda bekleyen regresyon kalkan\u0131 olarak kal\u0131r.\\n\\n## \ud83e\uddea Testler\\n\\n720 test \xb7 2470 assertion \xb7 6 skipped \u2014 tam ye\u015fil.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udce6 Kurulum\\n\\nGitHub Releases v4.26.4 \xfczerinden `mhm-rentiva.4.26.4.zip` dosyas\u0131n\u0131 indirin ve WordPress Eklentiler \u2192 Yeni Ekle \u2192 Eklenti Y\xfckle ekran\u0131ndan y\xfckleyin."},{"id":"v4.26.3-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.3-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-11-v4.26.3-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-11-v4.26.3-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.3: Ara\xe7 Kart\u0131 G\xf6rsel Kalitesi, Admin Toast Kesilmesi ve ZIP Chart.js D\xfczeltmesi","description":"v4.26.3, listeleme/arama sayfalar\u0131ndaki ara\xe7 g\xf6rsellerinin bulan\u0131k y\xfcklenmesine neden olan responsive sizes hatas\u0131n\u0131, ayarlar sayfas\u0131ndaki \\"kaydedildi\\" toast bildirimlerinin kesilip ekrandan ta\u015fmas\u0131n\u0131 ve release ZIP\'inden Chart.js\'in \xe7\u0131kar\u0131lmas\u0131na yol a\xe7an .distignore k\xf6k-sabitleme hatas\u0131n\u0131 gideriyor. \xdc\xe7\xfc de \xfcretimde g\xf6zle g\xf6r\xfclen ama console.log\'a d\xfc\u015fmeyen sessiz sorunlard\u0131.","date":"2026-04-11T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"},{"inline":true,"label":"frontend","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/frontend"},{"inline":true,"label":"admin-ux","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/admin-ux"},{"inline":true,"label":"build","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/build"},{"inline":true,"label":"bugfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/bugfix"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":4.64,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.26.3-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.3: Ara\xe7 Kart\u0131 G\xf6rsel Kalitesi, Admin Toast Kesilmesi ve ZIP Chart.js D\xfczeltmesi","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","patch","frontend","admin-ux","build","bugfix","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-04-11T09:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.4: Parite Denetimi Fix\'leri ve Transfer Widget UX Cilas\u0131","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.4-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.2: Tam Kald\u0131rma Temizli\u011fi ve CLI Bootstrap G\xfc\xe7lendirmesi","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.2-release-summary"}},"content":"v4.26.3, listeleme/arama sayfalar\u0131ndaki ara\xe7 g\xf6rsellerinin bulan\u0131k y\xfcklenmesine neden olan responsive `sizes` hatas\u0131n\u0131, ayarlar sayfas\u0131ndaki \\"kaydedildi\\" toast bildirimlerinin kesilip ekrandan ta\u015fmas\u0131n\u0131 ve release ZIP\'inden Chart.js\'in \xe7\u0131kar\u0131lmas\u0131na yol a\xe7an `.distignore` k\xf6k-sabitleme hatas\u0131n\u0131 gideriyor. \xdc\xe7\xfc de \xfcretimde g\xf6zle g\xf6r\xfclen ama `console.log`\'a d\xfc\u015fmeyen sessiz sorunlard\u0131.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83d\uddbc\ufe0f Ara\xe7 Kart\u0131 G\xf6rsel Kalitesi \u2014 220px Tuza\u011f\u0131\\n\\nAra\xe7 kart\u0131 partial\u0131nda (`templates/partials/vehicle-card.php`) y\u0131llard\u0131r sabit kodlanm\u0131\u015f bir `sizes` \xf6zniteli\u011fi vard\u0131:\\n\\n```html\\nsizes=\\"(max-width: 782px) 100vw, (max-width: 900px) 180px, 220px\\"\\n```\\n\\nBu \xf6znitelik taray\u0131c\u0131ya \\"bu g\xf6rselin ekranda kaplayaca\u011f\u0131 alan en fazla 220px\\" diyordu. Taray\u0131c\u0131 da do\u011fal olarak `srcset`\'teki en k\xfc\xe7\xfck uygun varyant\u0131 \u2014 **300w thumbnail**\'\u0131 \u2014 se\xe7iyordu. Ancak kartlar\u0131n ger\xe7ek g\xf6r\xfcnen geni\u015fli\u011fi 350-440px aras\u0131ndayd\u0131. Sonu\xe7: retina ekranlarda bile bulan\u0131k ara\xe7 g\xf6rselleri.\\n\\n**En belirgin oldu\u011fu yer:** Arama sonu\xe7lar\u0131 sayfas\u0131, \xe7\xfcnk\xfc oradaki kartlar en geni\u015f olanlard\u0131. Ayr\u0131ca arama kodu (`SearchResults::format_vehicle_data()`) varsay\u0131lan olarak zaten `\'medium\'` (300px) istiyordu \u2014 yani hem kaynak g\xf6rsel small\'d\u0131, hem de browser daha da k\xfc\xe7\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc se\xe7iyordu.\\n\\n**\xc7\xf6z\xfcm iki katmanl\u0131:**\\n\\n1. `SearchResults` varsay\u0131lan `image_size`\'\u0131 `\'medium\'` \u2192 `\'large\'` (1024px) oldu \u2014 ara\xe7 \u0131zgaras\u0131, ara\xe7 listesi ve \xf6ne \xe7\u0131kan ara\xe7lar zaten `\'large\'` kullan\u0131yordu\\n2. `vehicle-card.php` `sizes` \xf6zniteli\u011fi \u2192 `(max-width: 782px) 100vw, 500px` \u2014 retina ekranlarda browser art\u0131k 1024w varyant\u0131 se\xe7iyor, geni\u015f kartlar keskin\\n\\nBu d\xfczeltme **tek bir partial dosyas\u0131** de\u011fi\u015fti\u011fi i\xe7in listeleme, favoriler, ara\xe7 ar\u015fivi ve arama sonu\xe7lar\u0131 \u2014 hepsi birlikte d\xfczeldi.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd14 Admin Settings Toast \u2014 \\"Kaydedildi\\" Bildiriminin Kesilmesi\\n\\nAyarlar sayfas\u0131nda herhangi bir de\u011fi\u015fikli\u011fi kaydetti\u011finizde \xe7\u0131kan \\"Ayarlar kaydedildi\\" bildirimi, \xf6zellikle uzun mesajlarda sa\u011f taraf\u0131 kesilmi\u015f olarak g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcyordu. Sorun tek bir yerde de\u011fildi \u2014 iki ayr\u0131 bozukluk \xfcst \xfcste binmi\u015fti:\\n\\n**1. WordPress bildirimi header flex konteynerine hapsediliyordu.** `render_admin_header()` helper\'\u0131 H1, alt ba\u015fl\u0131k ve aksiyonlar i\xe7in bir flex konteyner kuruyor ama sonuna `<hr class=\\"wp-header-end\\" />` koymuyordu. WordPress `common.js`\'in bildirimleri yerle\u015ftirmek i\xe7in kulland\u0131\u011f\u0131 resmi API tam olarak bu i\u015faret\xe7i. \u0130\u015faret\xe7i yokken WordPress ilk H1\'i ar\u0131yor ve bildirimi dar flex kolonunun i\xe7ine s\u0131k\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\u0131yordu.\\n\\n**2. \xd6zel toast CSS\'i her \u015feyi tek sat\u0131ra zorluyordu.** Plugin\'in `convertWPNoticesToToasts()` helper\'\u0131 WordPress bildirimini gizleyip \xf6zel bir `.rv-notification.mhm-admin-toast` div\'i olu\u015fturuyor. Bu div\'in CSS\'i `white-space: nowrap`, `max-width: 350px`, `height: 50px` i\xe7eriyordu \u2014 yani uzun mesajlar\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131r\u0131yor, kelime kayd\u0131rma yapm\u0131yor, ve birden fazla toast \xfcst \xfcste geldi\u011finde istiflenmiyordu.\\n\\n**\xc7\xf6z\xfcm:**\\n\\n- `render_admin_header()` flex konteynerin kapan\u0131\u015f\u0131ndan hemen sonra `<hr class=\\"wp-header-end\\" />` yay\u0131nl\u0131yor \u2014 art\u0131k bildirimler konteynerin alt\u0131nda tam geni\u015flikte beliriyor\\n- Toast CSS\'i ba\u015ftan yaz\u0131ld\u0131: sabit `height`/`max-width`/`nowrap` kald\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131; `min-width: 280px`, `max-width: min(480px, calc(100vw - 60px))`, `white-space: normal`, `overflow-wrap: break-word`\\n- Toastlar i\xe7in `#mhm-admin-toast-container` ad\u0131nda sabit konumlu flex konteyner eklendi; yeni toastlar `prepend` ile en \xfcste giriyor \u2014 b\xf6ylece birden fazla toast istifleniyor ve en yenisi her zaman \xfcstte\\n- XSS g\xfcvenli\u011fi: toast mesajlar\u0131 art\u0131k template literal ile de\u011fil `.text(message)` ile yaz\u0131l\u0131yor \u2014 gelecekte bir hook\'un bildirim i\xe7eri\u011fine HTML enjekte etme riski yok\\n\\n## \ud83d\udce6 Release ZIP Chart.js 404 \u2014 `.distignore`\'un Gizli Hatas\u0131\\n\\nWordPress.org \xfczerinden kurulan kopyalarda admin dashboard\'daki grafikler 404 veriyordu. K\xf6k nedeni `.distignore` dosyas\u0131n\u0131n `vendor/` paterniydi.\\n\\nRelease ZIP\'i olu\u015fturan `bin/build-release.py` Python script\'i, paterndeki trailing `/` karakterini siliyor ve kalan `vendor`\'u \\"herhangi bir yol segmenti\\" olarak e\u015fle\u015ftiriyordu. Bu mant\u0131kla:\\n\\n- \u2705 `vendor/composer/...` e\u015fle\u015fti \u2014 do\u011fru (Composer klas\xf6r\xfcn\xfc atlamak istiyoruz)\\n- \u274c `assets/js/vendor/chart.min.js` **de** e\u015fle\u015fti \u2014 yanl\u0131\u015f (bu dosya kargoda olmal\u0131yd\u0131)\\n\\nSonu\xe7: `chart.min.js`, `flatpickr/`, `swiper-bundle.min.js` ve di\u011fer a\u011fa\xe7 i\xe7i vendor k\xfct\xfcphaneleri release ZIP\'inden d\xfc\u015f\xfcyordu. Lokal geli\u015ftirmede g\xf6r\xfcnm\xfcyordu \xe7\xfcnk\xfc build s\xfcreci atlan\u0131yordu. Ancak WordPress.org ya da GitHub Release ZIP\'i \xfczerinden kurulum yap\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda dashboard bo\u015f kal\u0131yordu.\\n\\n**\xc7\xf6z\xfcm:**\\n\\n- `bin/build-release.py` art\u0131k `.gitignore` tarz\u0131 k\xf6k sabitlemeyi destekliyor \u2014 bir patern `/` ile ba\u015flarsa yaln\u0131zca plugin k\xf6k dizinindeki o yola e\u015fle\u015fiyor, alt dizinlerdeki ayn\u0131 isimli klas\xf6rlere dokunmuyor\\n- `.distignore` g\xfcncellendi: `vendor/` \u2192 `/vendor/`\\n\\nDo\u011frulama: Yeni ZIP\'te `assets/js/vendor/chart.min.js`, `assets/vendor/flatpickr/*`, `assets/vendor/swiper-bundle.min.js` mevcut; Composer `vendor/` k\xf6k dizini d\u0131\u015fland\u0131.\\n\\n## \ud83e\uddd9 Setup Wizard \u2014 Versiyon Badge ve Lite/Pro CTA (Toplu Batch\'ten)\\n\\nBu release\'e toplu halde giren bir dizi kullan\u0131c\u0131 aray\xfcz\xfc iyile\u015ftirmesi:\\n\\n- **Kurulum Sihirbaz\u0131 ba\u015fl\u0131\u011f\u0131** art\u0131k plugin versiyonunu + Lite/Pro rozetini g\xf6steriyor\\n- **Lisans sekmesi + Lisans men\xfc sayfas\u0131** \\"\xdcr\xfcn Sayfas\u0131n\u0131 A\xe7\\" CTA butonu kazand\u0131 \u2014 kullan\u0131c\u0131 \xfcr\xfcn\xfcn sat\u0131n alma sayfas\u0131na tek t\u0131kla gidebiliyor\\n- **Geli\u015ftirici modu guard\u0131:** `has_real_license()` art\u0131k dev mode\'da CTA g\xf6r\xfcnmesini engellemiyor \u2014 geli\u015ftirme ortamlar\u0131nda da CTA test edilebiliyor\\n\\n## \ud83d\udccb De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| T\xfcr | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| \ud83d\uddbc\ufe0f D\xfczeltme | Ara\xe7 kart\u0131 `sizes` \xf6zniteli\u011fi 220px \u2192 500px (listeleme + favoriler + ar\u015fiv + arama sonu\xe7lar\u0131) |\\n| \ud83d\uddbc\ufe0f D\xfczeltme | `SearchResults` varsay\u0131lan `image_size` `\'medium\'` \u2192 `\'large\'` |\\n| \ud83d\udd14 D\xfczeltme | `render_admin_header()` `<hr class=\\"wp-header-end\\" />` emit ediyor \u2014 bildirimler art\u0131k header flex\'ten \xe7\u0131k\u0131yor |\\n| \ud83d\udd14 D\xfczeltme | Admin toast CSS: sabit `height`/`nowrap` kald\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131, kelime kayd\u0131rma eklendi |\\n| \ud83d\udd14 D\xfczeltme | Admin toast istifleme: `#mhm-admin-toast-container` + `prepend` \u2014 birden fazla toast \xfcst \xfcste binmiyor |\\n| \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f G\xfcvenlik | Admin toast mesajlar\u0131 art\u0131k `.text()` ile yaz\u0131l\u0131yor \u2014 HTML enjeksiyonuna kar\u015f\u0131 g\xfcvende |\\n| \ud83d\udce6 D\xfczeltme | `.distignore` `/vendor/` k\xf6k sabitlemesi \u2014 `chart.min.js`, `flatpickr`, `swiper` art\u0131k ZIP\'te |\\n| \ud83d\udd27 Build | `bin/build-release.py` `.gitignore` tarz\u0131 leading-slash anchoring deste\u011fi |\\n| \ud83e\uddd9 UX | Setup Wizard header versiyon + Lite/Pro badge |\\n| \ud83e\uddd9 UX | Setup Wizard Lisans sekmesi + Lisans men\xfcde \\"\xdcr\xfcn Sayfas\u0131n\u0131 A\xe7\\" CTA |\\n\\n## \ud83d\udcc1 De\u011fi\u015ftirilen Dosyalar\\n\\n- `templates/partials/vehicle-card.php` *(sizes 220px \u2192 500px)*\\n- `src/Admin/Frontend/Shortcodes/SearchResults.php` *(image_size \'medium\' \u2192 \'large\')*\\n- `src/Admin/Core/Traits/AdminHelperTrait.php` *(wp-header-end marker)*\\n- `assets/css/admin/settings.css` *(toast wrap + stacking CSS redesign)*\\n- `assets/js/admin/settings.js` *(container + prepend + .text XSS guard)*\\n- `.distignore` *(/vendor/ k\xf6k sabitleme)*\\n- `bin/build-release.py` *(anchored pattern support)*\\n- `src/Admin/Setup/SetupWizard.php` *(versiyon badge + CTA)*\\n- `src/Admin/Licensing/LicenseAdmin.php` *(CTA)*\\n- `mhm-rentiva.php`, `readme.txt`, `README.md`, `README-tr.md`, `changelog.json`, `changelog-tr.json` *(versiyon y\xfckseltme)*\\n\\n## \u2705 Kalite\\n\\n- **720 test, 2470 assertion, 6 atland\u0131** (v4.25.0 baseline\'\u0131 683/2277 idi)\\n- PHPUnit tam ye\u015fil\\n\\n## \u2b06\ufe0f G\xfcncelleme Notu\\n\\nv4.26.3 tamamen geriye d\xf6n\xfck uyumlu bir patch s\xfcr\xfcm\xfcd\xfcr \u2014 DB \u015femas\u0131nda de\u011fi\u015fiklik yoktur, migration \xe7al\u0131\u015fmaz, ek bir yap\u0131land\u0131rma gerekmez. G\xfcncelleme yollar\u0131:\\n\\n- WordPress admin \u2192 Eklentiler \u2192 G\xfcncelle\\n- `wp plugin update mhm-rentiva --allow-root`\\n- Manuel ZIP y\xfckleme (v4.26.2\'den itibaren otomatik migration destekleniyor)\\n\\n---\\n\\nDaha fazla bilgi i\xe7in [Dok\xfcman Sayfam\u0131z\u0131](https://maxhandmade.github.io/mhm-rentiva-docs/) ziyaret edin."},{"id":"v4.26.2-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.2-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-10-v4.26.2-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-10-v4.26.2-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.2: Tam Kald\u0131rma Temizli\u011fi ve CLI Bootstrap G\xfc\xe7lendirmesi","description":"v4.26.2, eklenti kald\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda arkada kalan t\xfcm tablolar\u0131n silinmesini sa\u011fl\u0131yor, wp-cli bootstrap s\u0131ras\u0131ndaki fatal hatay\u0131 gideriyor ve \u015fema migration\'lar\u0131n art\u0131k s\xfcr\xfcm de\u011fi\u015fikli\u011finde otomatik \xe7al\u0131\u015fmas\u0131n\u0131 garantiliyor. \xdc\xe7 d\xfczeltme de \xfcretim ortamlar\u0131ndaki sessiz sorunlar\u0131 hedefliyor.","date":"2026-04-10T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"},{"inline":true,"label":"uninstall","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/uninstall"},{"inline":true,"label":"cli","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/cli"},{"inline":true,"label":"migration","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/migration"},{"inline":true,"label":"bugfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/bugfix"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":3.06,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.26.2-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.2: Tam Kald\u0131rma Temizli\u011fi ve CLI Bootstrap G\xfc\xe7lendirmesi","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","patch","uninstall","cli","migration","bugfix","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-04-10T09:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.3: Ara\xe7 Kart\u0131 G\xf6rsel Kalitesi, Admin Toast Kesilmesi ve ZIP Chart.js D\xfczeltmesi","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.3-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.1: Ara\xe7 Detaylar\u0131, Rezervasyon, \xd6deme ve Sepet G\xf6rsel Cilas\u0131","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.1-release-summary"}},"content":"v4.26.2, eklenti kald\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda arkada kalan t\xfcm tablolar\u0131n silinmesini sa\u011fl\u0131yor, wp-cli bootstrap s\u0131ras\u0131ndaki fatal hatay\u0131 gideriyor ve \u015fema migration\'lar\u0131n art\u0131k s\xfcr\xfcm de\u011fi\u015fikli\u011finde otomatik \xe7al\u0131\u015fmas\u0131n\u0131 garantiliyor. \xdc\xe7 d\xfczeltme de \xfcretim ortamlar\u0131ndaki sessiz sorunlar\u0131 hedefliyor.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## \ud83e\uddf9 Kald\u0131rma Temizli\u011fi \u2014 Art\u0131k 27 Tablonun Hepsi\\n\\n\xd6nceden eklenti \\"verileri temizle\\" se\xe7ene\u011fi ile silindi\u011finde 14 alt sistem tablosu veritaban\u0131nda yetim kal\u0131yordu: `ledger`, `key_registry`, `commission_policy`, `payout_audit`, `tenants`, `usage_metrics` ve eski alert/payment alt sistemlerine ait art\u0131k kullan\u0131lmayan tablolar. Bu v4.26.2 ile tamamen \xe7\xf6z\xfcld\xfc.\\n\\n**Yap\u0131lan iyile\u015ftirmeler:**\\n\\n- **Tam liste:** 27 \xf6zel tablonun tamam\u0131 kald\u0131rma s\u0131ras\u0131nda siliniyor\\n- **Pattern g\xfcvenlik a\u011f\u0131:** Listede olmayan ama `mhm_rentiva_*` \xf6nekiyle ba\u015flayan herhangi bir yetim tablo da otomatik yakalan\u0131p siliniyor \u2014 gelecekte eklenen tablolar i\xe7in g\xfcvence\\n- **Kurtarma tablosu temizli\u011fi:** `DatabaseCleaner` taraf\u0131ndan olu\u015fturulan `postmeta_backup_invalid_*` ge\xe7ici tablolar\u0131 da kald\u0131rma s\u0131ras\u0131nda temizleniyor\\n- **Tek kaynak prensibi:** Silme listesi ve istatistik sayac\u0131 art\u0131k ayn\u0131 kaynaktan okuyor \u2014 saya\xe7 ile ger\xe7ek temizlik birbirinden uzakla\u015famaz\\n- **Savunma mekanizmalar\u0131:** `uninstall.php` ve taksonomi temizleme ad\u0131m\u0131 art\u0131k bozuk bir ayar kayd\u0131 veya eksik taksonomi nedeniyle sessizce durmuyor \u2014 hata yakalan\u0131yor ve kalan ad\u0131mlar \xe7al\u0131\u015fmaya devam ediyor\\n\\n**Do\u011frulama:** DemoSeed Docker ortam\u0131nda v4.26.2 kald\u0131rma testi \u2192 **0 tablo, 0 post, 0 ayar** art\u0131k geride kal\u0131yor. Tam temiz kald\u0131rma garantili.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd27 CLI Bootstrap Fatal Error D\xfczeltmesi\\n\\n\xd6nceden belirli ko\u015fullarda wp-cli komutlar\u0131 `TypeError` veya `is_user_logged_in() undefined function` hatas\u0131yla \xe7\xf6k\xfcyordu. K\xf6k nedeni iki yerde yat\u0131yordu:\\n\\n- `SettingsCore::get()` ve `has()` bir ayar kayd\u0131n\u0131n dizi olmad\u0131\u011f\u0131 durumda `TypeError` f\u0131rlat\u0131yordu\\n- `AdvancedLogger::log()` WordPress tam y\xfcklenmeden (\xf6rne\u011fin early bootstrap\'te) \xe7a\u011fr\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda `is_user_logged_in()`\'i \xe7a\u011f\u0131r\u0131yordu ama bu fonksiyon o a\u015famada tan\u0131ml\u0131 de\u011fildi\\n\\n**\xc7\xf6z\xfcm:**\\n\\n- `SettingsCore::get()`/`has()` art\u0131k dizi olmayan bir ayar de\u011ferini tolere ediyor ve g\xfcvenli varsay\u0131lana d\xfc\u015f\xfcyor\\n- `AdvancedLogger::log()` `plugins_loaded` hook\'u \xe7al\u0131\u015fmadan \xf6nce \xe7a\u011fr\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131nda erken return ediyor \u2014 log atlan\u0131r ama bootstrap \xe7\xf6kmez\\n\\n**Etkisi:** `wp plugin activate mhm-rentiva`, `wp mhm-rentiva *` subkomutlar\u0131 ve di\u011fer wp-cli ak\u0131\u015flar\u0131 art\u0131k bozuk bir ayar kayd\u0131 ya da early-bootstrap log denemesi ile \xe7\xf6km\xfcyor.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udd04 Otomatik \u015eema Migration\'lar\u0131\\n\\nv4.26.2 ile \u015fema migration\'lar\u0131 art\u0131k **eklenti dosya s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc de\u011fi\u015fti\u011finde otomatik \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor**, WordPress aktivasyon hook\'u \xe7a\u011fr\u0131lmasa bile. Bu; manuel ZIP y\xfckleme, FTP ile g\xfcncelleme ve `wp-cli plugin update` ak\u0131\u015flar\u0131n\u0131 kapsar.\\n\\n**\xd6nceki durum:** Yeni tablolar\u0131 olu\u015fturmak i\xe7in eklentiyi pasifle\u015ftirip tekrar etkinle\u015ftirmek gerekiyordu. Kullan\u0131c\u0131lar\u0131n \xe7o\u011fu bunu bilmedi\u011finden \\"yeni \xf6zellik \xe7al\u0131\u015fm\u0131yor\\" raporu geliyordu.\\n\\n**Yeni durum:** `DB_VERSION` sabiti de\u011fi\u015fir de\u011fi\u015fmez migration\'lar sessizce ve tek seferlik \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131r. Aktivasyon hook\'u hala destekleniyor \u2014 sadece art\u0131k zorunlu de\u011fil.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udccb De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| T\xfcr | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| \ud83e\uddf9 Kald\u0131rma | T\xfcm 27 \xf6zel tablo (ledger, key_registry, commission_policy, payout_audit, tenants, usage_metrics + eski alt sistem tablolar\u0131) |\\n| \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Kald\u0131rma | Pattern tabanl\u0131 g\xfcvenlik a\u011f\u0131 (`mhm_rentiva_*` \xf6neki) |\\n| \ud83e\uddf9 Kald\u0131rma | `postmeta_backup_invalid_*` kurtarma tablolar\u0131 |\\n| \ud83d\udd27 Kald\u0131rma | Silme listesi ve istatistik sayac\u0131 tek kaynaktan |\\n| \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Kald\u0131rma | `uninstall.php` ve taksonomi temizli\u011finde savunma mekanizmalar\u0131 |\\n| \ud83d\udd04 G\xfcncelleme | \u015eema migration\'lar\u0131 s\xfcr\xfcm de\u011fi\u015fikli\u011finde otomatik \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor |\\n| \ud83d\udc1b D\xfczeltme | `SettingsCore::get()`/`has()` dizi olmayan de\u011ferleri tolere ediyor |\\n| \ud83d\udc1b D\xfczeltme | `AdvancedLogger::log()` WordPress y\xfcklenmeden g\xfcvenli d\xf6n\xfc\u015f |\\n\\n## \ud83d\udcc1 De\u011fi\u015ftirilen Dosyalar\\n\\n- `uninstall.php` *(defensive is_array guard + tam tablo listesi)*\\n- `src/Admin/Core/Utilities/DatabaseCleaner.php` *(27 tablo + pattern wildcard)*\\n- `src/Admin/Core/Utilities/DatabaseMigrator.php` *(otomatik migration tetikleme)*\\n- `src/Admin/Core/SettingsCore.php` *(non-array tolerans\u0131)*\\n- `src/Admin/Core/Logging/AdvancedLogger.php` *(plugins_loaded guard)*\\n- `mhm-rentiva.php` *(versiyon g\xfcncelleme)*\\n\\n## \u2b06\ufe0f G\xfcncelleme Notu\\n\\nv4.26.2 tamamen geriye d\xf6n\xfck uyumlu bir patch s\xfcr\xfcm\xfcd\xfcr \u2014 DB \u015femas\u0131nda yeni tablo, kolon veya veri de\u011fi\u015fikli\u011fi **yoktur**. G\xfcncelleme sonras\u0131 ek bir i\u015flem gerekmez. Eklentiyi normal yollarla g\xfcncellemeniz yeterli:\\n\\n- WordPress admin \u2192 Eklentiler \u2192 G\xfcncelle\\n- Veya `wp plugin update mhm-rentiva --allow-root`\\n- Veya manuel ZIP y\xfckleme (art\u0131k otomatik migration tetiklenir)\\n\\n---\\n\\nDaha fazla bilgi i\xe7in [Dok\xfcman Sayfam\u0131z\u0131](https://maxhandmade.github.io/mhm-rentiva-docs/) ziyaret edin."},{"id":"v4.26.1-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.1-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-08-v4.26.1-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-08-v4.26.1-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.1: Ara\xe7 Detaylar\u0131, Rezervasyon, \xd6deme ve Sepet G\xf6rsel Cilas\u0131","description":"v4.26.1, v4.26.0 ile devreye giren rezervasyon-\xf6deme ak\u0131\u015f\u0131n\u0131n \xfcst\xfcne gelen g\xf6rsel tutars\u0131zl\u0131klar\u0131 temizliyor. Ara\xe7 detay sayfas\u0131ndan sepete, sepetten \xf6deme sayfas\u0131na kadar m\xfc\u015fterinin g\xf6rd\xfc\u011f\xfc her ekranda kart, ikon ve hizalama sorunlar\u0131 giderildi. Fonksiyonel bir de\u011fi\u015fiklik yok \u2014 sadece deneyim daha temiz.","date":"2026-04-08T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"patch","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/patch"},{"inline":true,"label":"ui","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/ui"},{"inline":true,"label":"checkout","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/checkout"},{"inline":true,"label":"cart","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/cart"},{"inline":true,"label":"booking","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/booking"},{"inline":true,"label":"bugfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/bugfix"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":2.13,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.26.1-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.1: Ara\xe7 Detaylar\u0131, Rezervasyon, \xd6deme ve Sepet G\xf6rsel Cilas\u0131","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","patch","ui","checkout","cart","booking","bugfix","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-04-08T09:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.2: Tam Kald\u0131rma Temizli\u011fi ve CLI Bootstrap G\xfc\xe7lendirmesi","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.2-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.0: Depozito Rezervasyonlar\u0131nda Kalan \xd6deme","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.0-release-summary"}},"content":"v4.26.1, v4.26.0 ile devreye giren rezervasyon-\xf6deme ak\u0131\u015f\u0131n\u0131n \xfcst\xfcne gelen g\xf6rsel tutars\u0131zl\u0131klar\u0131 temizliyor. Ara\xe7 detay sayfas\u0131ndan sepete, sepetten \xf6deme sayfas\u0131na kadar m\xfc\u015fterinin g\xf6rd\xfc\u011f\xfc her ekranda kart, ikon ve hizalama sorunlar\u0131 giderildi. Fonksiyonel bir de\u011fi\u015fiklik yok \u2014 sadece deneyim daha temiz.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83c\udfa8 Ara\xe7 Detaylar\u0131 Kenar \xc7ubu\u011fu\\n\\n- **\xd6zellik etiketleri ta\u015fma sorunu:** Vites, yak\u0131t, koltuk say\u0131s\u0131 gibi spec chip\'leri dar ekranlarda kart kenar\u0131ndan ta\u015f\u0131yordu. Art\u0131k kart s\u0131n\u0131rlar\u0131 i\xe7inde kal\u0131yor ve uzun etiketler do\u011fru \u015fekilde sarmalan\u0131yor.\\n- **Hibrit yak\u0131t ikonu:** Yak\u0131t t\xfcr\xfc \\"hybrid\\" se\xe7ili ara\xe7larda yanl\u0131\u015f ikon g\xf6steriliyordu. Do\u011fru simgeyle de\u011fi\u015ftirildi.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udcc5 Takvim\\n\\n- **Bo\u015f sat\u0131r kald\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131:** Takvim bile\u015feninin alt\u0131nda fazladan bir bo\u015f sat\u0131r render ediliyordu \u2014 kald\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131.\\n- **Kutu i\xe7inde kutu g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcm\xfc:** Kenar \xe7ubu\u011funda takvim widget\'\u0131n\u0131n kendi arka plan\u0131 ile d\u0131\u015f kart arka plan\u0131 i\xe7 i\xe7e iki kutu izlenimi yarat\u0131yordu. \u0130\xe7 kayna\u011f\u0131n arka plan\u0131 n\xf6trle\u015ftirildi, art\u0131k tek bir kart olarak g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcyor.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udcdd Rezervasyon Formu\\n\\n- **Ara\xe7 g\xf6rseli g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfc:** Form ba\u015fl\u0131\u011f\u0131ndaki ara\xe7 g\xf6rseli a\xe7\u0131k arka planlarda d\xfc\u015f\xfck kontrasta sahipti. Alt\u0131na bir degrade arka plan eklenerek ara\xe7 her zaman g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr durumda tutuluyor.\\n- **Kart ba\u015fl\u0131k stili birle\u015fimi:** Rezervasyon formunun farkl\u0131 b\xf6l\xfcmleri (tarih, m\xfc\u015fteri bilgisi, ek hizmetler, fiyat \xf6zeti) birbirinden farkl\u0131 ba\u015fl\u0131k stillerine sahipti. T\xfcm b\xf6l\xfcmler art\u0131k ayn\u0131 ba\u015fl\u0131k tipografisi ve padding de\u011ferlerini kullan\u0131yor.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udcb3 \xd6deme Sayfas\u0131\\n\\n- **\xd6deme y\xf6ntemleri dikey:** \xc7oklu \xf6deme y\xf6ntemi (kart, havale, kap\u0131da \xf6deme) etkin oldu\u011funda se\xe7enekler yatay olarak s\u0131ralan\u0131yor ve mobilde ta\u015f\u0131yordu. Art\u0131k tek s\xfctun, dikey stack \u2014 her ekran geni\u015fli\u011finde tutarl\u0131.\\n- **Kupon alan\u0131 ikon:** \\"Kupon kodunuz var m\u0131?\\" uyar\u0131 sat\u0131r\u0131ndaki ikon belirli tema kombinasyonlar\u0131nda bozuk (kare/?) g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcyordu. \u0130kon emoji ile de\u011fi\u015ftirildi, her temada render oluyor.\\n\\n## \ud83d\uded2 Sepet\\n\\n- **Rezervasyon meta sat\u0131rlar\u0131nda yeniden d\xfczen:** Rezervasyon detaylar\u0131 (tarih aral\u0131\u011f\u0131, ek hizmetler, teslim lokasyonu) daha \xf6nce tek bir c\xfcmle i\xe7inde virg\xfclle ayr\u0131lm\u0131\u015f \u015fekilde g\xf6steriliyordu \u2014 okunmas\u0131 zor. Art\u0131k her bilgi `Etiket: De\u011fer` format\u0131nda ayr\u0131 sat\u0131rlar halinde g\xf6steriliyor.\\n- **\xd6demeye git butonu hover:** Buton \xfczerine gelindi\u011finde yaz\u0131 rengi arka planla ayn\u0131 tonda kal\u0131p okunam\u0131yordu. Hover state rengi d\xfczeltildi, yaz\u0131 her durumda okunur.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udccb De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| Alan | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|------|----------|\\n| \ud83d\udd27 Ara\xe7 Detaylar\u0131 | Spec chip ta\u015fma + hibrit yak\u0131t ikonu |\\n| \ud83d\udd27 Takvim | Fazladan bo\u015f sat\u0131r + kutu i\xe7inde kutu g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcm\xfc |\\n| \ud83d\udd27 Rezervasyon Formu | Ara\xe7 g\xf6rseli degrade arka plan + kart ba\u015fl\u0131k birle\u015ftirme |\\n| \ud83d\udd27 \xd6deme | Dikey \xf6deme y\xf6ntemleri + kupon ikon emoji |\\n| \ud83d\udd27 Sepet | Meta etiket/de\u011fer sat\u0131rlar\u0131 + \xf6demeye git hover |\\n\\n## \u2b06\ufe0f G\xfcncelleme Notu\\n\\nv4.26.1 **yaln\u0131zca CSS ve \u015fablon d\xfczeltmeleri** i\xe7erir \u2014 fonksiyonel de\u011fi\u015fiklik, DB \u015fema g\xfcncellemesi veya yeni ayar yoktur. v4.26.0\'dan g\xfcncellemek i\xe7in herhangi bir i\u015flem gerekmez:\\n\\n- WordPress admin \u2192 Eklentiler \u2192 G\xfcncelle\\n- Veya `wp plugin update mhm-rentiva --allow-root`\\n\\n\xd6zel tema override\'lar\u0131 yapmad\u0131ysan\u0131z g\xfcncelleme sonras\u0131 ek ad\u0131m gerekmez. Child theme ile `cart.php`, `checkout/form.php` veya rezervasyon formu \u015fablonlar\u0131n\u0131 override ettiyseniz, yeni s\xfcr\xfcmle uyumluluk i\xe7in \u015fablonlar\u0131n\u0131z\u0131 kar\u015f\u0131la\u015ft\u0131rman\u0131z\u0131 \xf6neririz.\\n\\n---\\n\\nDaha fazla bilgi i\xe7in [Dok\xfcman Sayfam\u0131z\u0131](https://maxhandmade.github.io/mhm-rentiva-docs/) ziyaret edin."},{"id":"v4.26.0-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.0-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-07-v4.26.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-07-v4.26.0-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.0: Depozito Rezervasyonlar\u0131nda Kalan \xd6deme","description":"v4.26.0, depozito ile olu\u015fturulan rezervasyonlarda m\xfc\u015fterilerin kalan bakiyeyi do\u011frudan Hesab\u0131m ekran\u0131ndan \xf6deyebilmesini sa\u011fl\u0131yor. WooCommerce\'in native \xf6deme altyap\u0131s\u0131 kullan\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131ndan aktif t\xfcm \xf6deme y\xf6ntemleri otomatik olarak \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor.","date":"2026-04-07T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"payment","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/payment"},{"inline":true,"label":"woocommerce","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/woocommerce"},{"inline":true,"label":"deposit","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/deposit"},{"inline":true,"label":"bugfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/bugfix"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":1.78,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.26.0-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.0: Depozito Rezervasyonlar\u0131nda Kalan \xd6deme","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","payment","woocommerce","deposit","bugfix","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-04-07T09:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.1: Ara\xe7 Detaylar\u0131, Rezervasyon, \xd6deme ve Sepet G\xf6rsel Cilas\u0131","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.1-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.25.0: Y\xf6netici Taraf\u0131ndan D\xfczenlenebilir Vendor E-posta \u015eablonlar\u0131","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.25.0-release-summary"}},"content":"v4.26.0, depozito ile olu\u015fturulan rezervasyonlarda m\xfc\u015fterilerin kalan bakiyeyi do\u011frudan Hesab\u0131m ekran\u0131ndan \xf6deyebilmesini sa\u011fl\u0131yor. WooCommerce\'in native \xf6deme altyap\u0131s\u0131 kullan\u0131ld\u0131\u011f\u0131ndan aktif t\xfcm \xf6deme y\xf6ntemleri otomatik olarak \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 \xd6ne \xc7\u0131kan Yenilik\\n\\n### \ud83d\udcb3 Kalan \xd6deme \u2014 Depozito Rezervasyonlar\u0131 i\xe7in\\n\\nDepozito ile rezervasyon olu\u015fturuldu\u011funda kalan bakiye daha \xf6nce yaln\u0131zca manuel takip ya da operat\xf6rle ileti\u015fim gerektiriyordu. v4.26.0 ile m\xfc\u015fteriler bu ad\u0131m\u0131 tamamen kendi ba\u015flar\u0131na tamamlayabiliyor.\\n\\n**Nas\u0131l \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131r:**\\n\\n1. M\xfc\u015fteri **Hesab\u0131m \u2192 Rezervasyon Detay\u0131** sayfas\u0131na gider\\n2. Kalan bakiye > 0 ise **\\"Kalan \xd6demeyi Yap\\"** butonu g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr\\n3. Butona t\u0131kland\u0131\u011f\u0131nda tam tutar i\xe7in minimal bir WC sipari\u015fi arka planda olu\u015fturulur\\n4. M\xfc\u015fteri WooCommerce\'in native order-pay sayfas\u0131na y\xf6nlendirilir\\n5. \xd6deme ba\u015far\u0131l\u0131 oldu\u011funda rezervasyon g\xfcncellenir: kalan bakiye s\u0131f\u0131rlan\u0131r, durum onaylan\u0131r\\n\\n**Teknik \xf6zellikler:**\\n\\n- `RemainingPaymentHandler` \u2014 AJAX endpoint, nonce + sahiplik do\u011frulamas\u0131\\n- **Tekrar sipari\u015f korumas\u0131:** Bekleyen kalan \xf6deme sipari\u015fi varsa yeni sipari\u015f olu\u015fturulmaz, mevcut sipari\u015f yeniden kullan\u0131l\u0131r (`_mhm_remaining_order_id` meta)\\n- **HPOS uyumlu:** T\xfcm WC sipari\u015f i\u015flemleri `$order->update_meta_data() + $order->save()` ile yap\u0131l\u0131r\\n- `WooCommerceBridge`: processing durumunda `_mhm_is_remaining_payment` bayra\u011f\u0131 varsa `_mhm_remaining_amount` s\u0131f\u0131rlan\u0131r\\n\\n## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Hata D\xfczeltmeleri\\n\\n### CSS Kapsam D\xfczeltmesi\\n\\nT\xfcm genel hesap sayfas\u0131 s\u0131n\u0131flar\u0131 (`.btn`, `.booking-item`, `.stat-card` vb.) art\u0131k `.mhm-rentiva-account-page` sarmalay\u0131c\u0131s\u0131 alt\u0131na al\u0131nd\u0131. Bu de\u011fi\u015fiklik WoodMart, Flatsome gibi premium temalarla ya\u015fanan g\xf6rsel \xe7ak\u0131\u015fmalar\u0131 engelliyor.\\n\\n### WC Hesab\u0131m Izgara D\xfczeni\\n\\nEntegre modda \u0131zgara tabanl\u0131 temalarda ya\u015fanan `grid-column` d\xfczeni sorunu giderildi (`grid-column: 1/-1`).\\n\\n## \ud83d\udccb De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| T\xfcr | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| \u2728 Yeni | Kalan \xf6deme butonu \u2014 Hesab\u0131m \u2192 Rezervasyon Detay\u0131 |\\n| \u2728 Yeni | `RemainingPaymentHandler` s\u0131n\u0131f\u0131 (AJAX + do\u011frulama) |\\n| \u2728 Yeni | Tekrar sipari\u015f korumas\u0131 (`_mhm_remaining_order_id` meta) |\\n| \ud83d\udc1b D\xfczeltme | CSS kapsam \u2014 t\xfcm s\u0131n\u0131flar `.mhm-rentiva-account-page` alt\u0131na al\u0131nd\u0131 |\\n| \ud83d\udc1b D\xfczeltme | WC Hesab\u0131m \u0131zgara d\xfczeni (grid-column: 1/-1) |\\n\\n## \ud83d\udcc1 De\u011fi\u015ftirilen Dosyalar\\n\\n- `src/Admin/Payment/WooCommerce/RemainingPaymentHandler.php` *(yeni)*\\n- `src/Admin/Payment/WooCommerce/WooCommerceBridge.php`\\n- `src/Admin/Frontend/Account/AccountController.php`\\n- `templates/account/booking-detail.php`\\n- `mhm-rentiva.php` *(versiyon g\xfcncelleme)*\\n\\n---\\n\\nDaha fazla bilgi i\xe7in [Dok\xfcman Sayfam\u0131z\u0131](https://maxhandmade.github.io/mhm-rentiva-docs/) ziyaret edin."},{"id":"v4.25.0-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.25.0-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-04-01-v4.25.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-04-01-v4.25.0-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.25.0: Y\xf6netici Taraf\u0131ndan D\xfczenlenebilir Vendor E-posta \u015eablonlar\u0131","description":"v4.25.0, vendor bildirimleri i\xe7in y\xf6netici panelinden d\xfczenlenebilir e-posta \u015fablonlar\u0131 getiriyor. 22 vendor bildirim \u015fablonu art\u0131k Ayarlar ekran\u0131ndan \xf6zelle\u015ftirilebilir. Ayr\u0131ca Site Instance Check-in cron\'u Cron \u0130\u015f Monit\xf6r\xfc\'ne eklendi ve weekly WP cron interval\'inin g\xfcvenilir kayd\u0131 garanti alt\u0131na al\u0131nd\u0131.","date":"2026-04-01T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"email","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/email"},{"inline":true,"label":"accessibility","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/accessibility"},{"inline":true,"label":"bugfix","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/bugfix"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":2.03,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.25.0-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.25.0: Y\xf6netici Taraf\u0131ndan D\xfczenlenebilir Vendor E-posta \u015eablonlar\u0131","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","vendor","email","accessibility","bugfix","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-04-01T09:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.26.0: Depozito Rezervasyonlar\u0131nda Kalan \xd6deme","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.26.0-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.24.0: Ara\xe7 Ya\u015fam D\xf6ng\xfcs\xfc Y\xf6netimi & Vendor Self-Servis","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.24.0-release-summary"}},"content":"v4.25.0, vendor bildirimleri i\xe7in y\xf6netici panelinden d\xfczenlenebilir e-posta \u015fablonlar\u0131 getiriyor. 22 vendor bildirim \u015fablonu art\u0131k Ayarlar ekran\u0131ndan \xf6zelle\u015ftirilebilir. Ayr\u0131ca Site Instance Check-in cron\'u Cron \u0130\u015f Monit\xf6r\xfc\'ne eklendi ve `weekly` WP cron interval\'inin g\xfcvenilir kayd\u0131 garanti alt\u0131na al\u0131nd\u0131.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 \xd6ne \xc7\u0131kan Yenilikler\\n\\n### \u2709\ufe0f Y\xf6netici Taraf\u0131ndan D\xfczenlenebilir Vendor E-posta \u015eablonlar\u0131\\n\\n22 vendor bildirim \u015fablonu art\u0131k do\u011frudan admin panelinden d\xfczenlenebilir: **Ayarlar \u2192 Bildirim \u015eablonlar\u0131 \u2192 Vendor Bildirimleri** sekmesi.\\n\\n\u015eablonlar 4 b\xf6l\xfcme ayr\u0131lm\u0131\u015f durumda:\\n\\n| B\xf6l\xfcm | \u015eablon Say\u0131s\u0131 |\\n|-------|--------------|\\n| Vendor Hesap (kay\u0131t, onay, ret, ask\u0131) | 5 |\\n| Ara\xe7 \u0130nceleme (onay, ret, d\xfczenleme, yeniden inceleme) | 4 |\\n| Ara\xe7 Ya\u015fam D\xf6ng\xfcs\xfc (duraklatma, devam, sona erme vb.) | 9 |\\n| Finansal E-postalar (\xf6deme, iade, fatura) | 4 |\\n\\n**Ak\u0131ll\u0131 Fallback Sistemi:**\\n- Konu alan\u0131 bo\u015f b\u0131rak\u0131l\u0131rsa \u2192 varsay\u0131lan konu metni g\xf6sterilir (admin ne g\xf6nderilece\u011fini g\xf6r\xfcr)\\n- G\xf6vde alan\u0131 bo\u015f = Gold Standard HTML dosya fallback \u2014 \xf6zelle\u015ftirme yap\u0131lmad\u0131\u011f\u0131nda profesyonel tasar\u0131m korunur\\n\\n### \ud83c\udf10 \xc7eviri Deste\u011fi\\n\\nVendor e-posta admin aray\xfcz\xfc i\xe7in **56 yeni T\xfcrk\xe7e \xe7eviri** eklendi.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Teknik \u0130yile\u015ftirmeler\\n\\n### \ud83c\udfa8 Gold Standard E-posta \u015eablonu Gradient D\xfczeltmesi\\n\\nHeader ba\u015fl\u0131\u011f\u0131nda ger\xe7ek renk ge\xe7i\u015fi art\u0131k do\u011fru \xfcretiliyor \u2014 \xf6nceki s\xfcr\xfcmde gradient olu\u015fturma hesaplama hatas\u0131 vard\u0131.\\n\\n### \u267f Eri\u015filebilirlik: CTA Buton Kontrast Oran\u0131\\n\\nAra\xe7 yeniden inceleme admin e-postas\u0131ndaki amber CTA butonunun kontrast oran\u0131 **2.97:1\'den 6.8:1\'e** y\xfckseltildi. WCAG AA standard\u0131n\u0131 kar\u015f\u0131l\u0131yor.\\n\\n### \ud83d\udd27 Site Instance Check-in Cron G\xf6r\xfcn\xfcrl\xfc\u011f\xfc\\n\\n`mhm_rentiva_instance_checkin` cron g\xf6revi art\u0131k **Cron \u0130\u015f Monit\xf6r\xfc**\'nde g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcyor ve \\"\u015eimdi \xc7al\u0131\u015ft\u0131r\\" butonu ile manuel tetiklenebiliyor. Bu sayede Lite site instance\'lar\u0131n\u0131n lisans sunucusuna kayd\u0131 izlenebilir.\\n\\n### \ud83d\udd27 Weekly Cron Interval Garantisi\\n\\n`weekly` WP cron interval\'i art\u0131k eklenti taraf\u0131ndan a\xe7\u0131k\xe7a kay\u0131t ediliyor \u2014 WooCommerce gibi harici eklentilere ba\u011f\u0131ml\u0131l\u0131k kald\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udccb De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| T\xfcr | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| \u2728 Yeni | 22 vendor bildirim \u015fablonu admin panelinden d\xfczenlenebilir |\\n| \u2728 Yeni | 4 b\xf6l\xfcm: Hesap (5), \u0130nceleme (4), Ya\u015fam D\xf6ng\xfcs\xfc (9), Finansal (4) |\\n| \u2728 Yeni | Bo\u015f konu \u2192 varsay\u0131lan g\xf6ster; bo\u015f g\xf6vde \u2192 Gold Standard HTML fallback |\\n| \ud83c\udfa8 \u0130yile\u015ftirme | Gold Standard gradient \xfcretimi d\xfczeltildi |\\n| \u267f Eri\u015filebilirlik | Amber CTA kontrast oran\u0131 2.97:1 \u2192 6.8:1 (WCAG AA) |\\n| \ud83c\udf10 \xc7eviri | 56 yeni T\xfcrk\xe7e \xe7eviri (vendor e-posta admin UI) |\\n| \ud83d\udc1b D\xfczeltme | Site Instance Check-in cron Cron Monit\xf6r\xfc\'nde g\xf6r\xfcn\xfcr oldu |\\n| \ud83d\udc1b D\xfczeltme | weekly interval art\u0131k eklenti taraf\u0131ndan garantili kay\u0131t ediliyor |\\n\\n---\\n\\nDaha fazla bilgi i\xe7in [Dok\xfcman Sayfam\u0131z\u0131](https://maxhandmade.github.io/mhm-rentiva-docs/) ziyaret edin."},{"id":"v4.24.0-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.24.0-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-03-28-v4.24.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-03-28-v4.24.0-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.24.0: Ara\xe7 Ya\u015fam D\xf6ng\xfcs\xfc Y\xf6netimi & Vendor Self-Servis","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.24.0 s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu s\xfcr\xfcm, ara\xe7lar\u0131n t\xfcm \xf6mr\xfc boyunca y\xf6netilebilece\u011fi tam durum makinesi, vendor\'lar\u0131n ara\xe7lar\u0131n\u0131 kendi kendine y\xf6netebilece\u011fi AJAX self-servis u\xe7 noktalar\u0131 ve adil rekabeti koruyan anti-gaming mekanizmalar\u0131 getiriyor.","date":"2026-03-28T20:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"lifecycle","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/lifecycle"},{"inline":true,"label":"reliability","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/reliability"},{"inline":true,"label":"notifications","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/notifications"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":3.11,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.24.0-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.24.0: Ara\xe7 Ya\u015fam D\xf6ng\xfcs\xfc Y\xf6netimi & Vendor Self-Servis","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","vendor","lifecycle","reliability","notifications","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-03-28T20:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.25.0: Y\xf6netici Taraf\u0131ndan D\xfczenlenebilir Vendor E-posta \u015eablonlar\u0131","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.25.0-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.23.1: Vendor Form Yeniden Tasarimi & Sehir SelectWoo Migrasyonu","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.23.1-release-summary"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.24.0** s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu s\xfcr\xfcm, ara\xe7lar\u0131n t\xfcm \xf6mr\xfc boyunca y\xf6netilebilece\u011fi tam durum makinesi, vendor\'lar\u0131n ara\xe7lar\u0131n\u0131 kendi kendine y\xf6netebilece\u011fi AJAX self-servis u\xe7 noktalar\u0131 ve adil rekabeti koruyan anti-gaming mekanizmalar\u0131 getiriyor.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 \xd6ne \xc7\u0131kan Yenilikler\\n\\n### \ud83d\ude80 Ara\xe7 Ya\u015fam D\xf6ng\xfcs\xfc Durum Makinesi\\n\\nv4.24.0\'\u0131n ana \xf6zelli\u011fi: ara\xe7lar\u0131n **Aktif \u2192 Duraklat\u0131lm\u0131\u015f \u2192 S\xfcresi Dolmu\u015f \u2192 Geri \xc7ekilmi\u015f** durumlar\u0131 aras\u0131ndaki ge\xe7i\u015flerini y\xf6neten tam durum makinesi.\\n\\n- **5 Durum:** `pending_review`, `active`, `paused`, `expired`, `withdrawn` \u2014 her ge\xe7i\u015f kurallarla korunuyor.\\n- **Ge\xe7i\u015f kurallar\u0131:** Hangi durumdan hangi duruma ge\xe7ilece\u011fi `VehicleLifecycleManager` taraf\u0131ndan zorunlu k\u0131l\u0131n\u0131r.\\n- **Admin UI:** Ara\xe7 listesinde ya\u015fam d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfc s\xfctunu, ara\xe7 d\xfczenleme ekran\u0131nda meta kutu.\\n\\n### \u23f1\ufe0f 90 G\xfcnl\xfck Listeleme S\xfcresi\\n\\n- Ara\xe7lar yay\u0131nland\u0131ktan **90 g\xfcn** sonra otomatik olarak s\xfcresi dolar.\\n- Sona ermeden **10 g\xfcn** ve **3 g\xfcn** \xf6nce vendor\'a uyar\u0131 e-postalar\u0131 g\xf6nderilir.\\n- G\xfcnl\xfck cron ile kontrol edilir; s\xfcresi dolan ara\xe7lar `expired` durumuna ge\xe7er.\\n\\n### \ud83c\udfae Vendor Self-Servis AJAX U\xe7 Noktalar\u0131\\n\\nVendor\'lar art\u0131k ara\xe7lar\u0131n\u0131 admin m\xfcdahalesi olmadan y\xf6netebilir:\\n\\n| \u0130\u015flem | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-------|----------|\\n| **Duraklat** | Aktif ara\xe7 ge\xe7ici olarak pasife al\u0131n\u0131r |\\n| **Devam Et** | Duraklat\u0131lm\u0131\u015f ara\xe7 tekrar aktifle\u015ftirilir |\\n| **Geri \xc7ek** | Ara\xe7 platformdan kal\u0131c\u0131 olarak \xe7ekilir (ceza uygulanabilir) |\\n| **Yenile** | S\xfcresi dolmu\u015f ara\xe7 yeniden aktifle\u015ftirilir |\\n| **Yeniden Listele** | Geri \xe7ekilmi\u015f ara\xe7 tekrar yay\u0131nlan\u0131r |\\n\\n### \ud83d\udcb8 Artan Geri \xc7ekme Ceza Sistemi\\n\\nVendor\'lar\u0131n s\u0131k s\u0131k ara\xe7 geri \xe7ekmesini \xf6nleyen kademeli ceza mekanizmas\u0131:\\n\\n- **1. geri \xe7ekme:** \xdccretsiz \u2014 ceza yok.\\n- **2. geri \xe7ekme:** Ayl\u0131k ortalama gelirin **%10**\'u kesilir.\\n- **3. ve sonras\u0131:** Ayl\u0131k ortalama gelirin **%25**\'i kesilir.\\n- **12 ayl\u0131k kayan pencere:** Ceza sayac\u0131 12 ay ge\xe7ince s\u0131f\u0131rlan\u0131r.\\n- Kesintiler do\u011frudan ledger\'a kaydedilir, payout hesab\u0131ndan d\xfc\u015f\xfcl\xfcr.\\n\\n### \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Anti-Gaming: Bloklu Tarih Korumas\u0131\\n\\nVendor\'lar\u0131n fiyat manip\xfclasyonunu \xf6nlemek i\xe7in:\\n\\n- Vendor iptal etti\u011fi rezervasyonun tarihleri **30 g\xfcn boyunca yeniden bloklan\u0131r**.\\n- Vendor d\xfc\u015f\xfck fiyatla almak i\xe7in iptal edip daha y\xfcksek fiyata satamaz.\\n- `AntiGamingBlocker` s\u0131n\u0131f\u0131 bu tarih blokajlar\u0131n\u0131 y\xf6netir.\\n\\n### \u2b50 Vendor G\xfcvenilirlik Puan\u0131\\n\\nT\xfcm platformda vendor kalitesini \xf6l\xe7en 0-100 aras\u0131 puan sistemi:\\n\\n- **G\xfcnl\xfck cron** ile yeniden hesaplama.\\n- **Form\xfcl:** \u0130ptal oran\u0131, geri \xe7ekme s\u0131kl\u0131\u011f\u0131, duraklatma ge\xe7mi\u015fi ve tamamlanan rezervasyon say\u0131s\u0131 bazl\u0131.\\n- Admin kullan\u0131c\u0131 listesinde vendor g\xfcvenilirlik s\xfctunu eklendi.\\n- Ara\xe7 kartlar\u0131nda vendor badge olarak g\xf6sterilmeye haz\u0131r.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udce7 9 Yeni E-posta \u015eablonu\\n\\nYa\u015fam d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcn\xfcn her ad\u0131m\u0131 i\xe7in ayr\u0131 e-posta \u015fablonlar\u0131:\\n\\n| \u015eablon | Tetikleyici |\\n|--------|-------------|\\n| Ara\xe7 Aktifle\u015ftirildi | Ara\xe7 `active` durumuna ge\xe7ti\u011finde |\\n| Ara\xe7 Duraklat\u0131ld\u0131 | Vendor veya admin duraklatt\u0131\u011f\u0131nda |\\n| Duraklatma Devam Etti | Ara\xe7 yeniden aktifle\u015ftirildi\u011finde |\\n| Ara\xe7 Geri \xc7ekildi | Vendor geri \xe7ekme i\u015flemi yapt\u0131\u011f\u0131nda |\\n| Listeleme S\xfcresi Doldu | 90. g\xfcn sonunda otomatik |\\n| 10 G\xfcn Uyar\u0131s\u0131 | S\xfcre dolumundan 10 g\xfcn \xf6nce |\\n| 3 G\xfcn Uyar\u0131s\u0131 | S\xfcre dolumundan 3 g\xfcn \xf6nce |\\n| Ara\xe7 Yenilendi | S\xfcresi dolmu\u015f ara\xe7 yenilendi\u011finde |\\n| Ara\xe7 Yeniden Listelendi | Geri \xe7ekilmi\u015f ara\xe7 tekrar yay\u0131nland\u0131\u011f\u0131nda |\\n\\n## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Teknik \u0130yile\u015ftirmeler\\n\\n- **Aktif Filtre:** 6 frontend shortcode art\u0131k `MetaQueryHelper` arac\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131yla bak\u0131mdaki/pasif ara\xe7lar\u0131 filtreler \u2014 m\xfc\u015fteriler ge\xe7ersiz ara\xe7lar\u0131 g\xf6remez.\\n- **Veritaban\u0131:** `DatabaseMigrator v3.5.0` \u2014 mevcut t\xfcm aktif ara\xe7lar i\xe7in ya\u015fam d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfc durumu otomatik migrate edildi.\\n- **Login Y\xf6nlendirme:** `wp-login.php` eri\u015fimi WooCommerce hesap sayfas\u0131na y\xf6nlendirildi.\\n- **Lisans Check-in:** Haftal\u0131k cron ile instance check-in.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udccb De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| T\xfcr | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| \ud83d\ude80 Durum Makinesi | 5 durum, ge\xe7i\u015f kurallar\u0131, VehicleLifecycleManager. |\\n| \u23f1\ufe0f Listeleme S\xfcresi | 90 g\xfcn, cron tabanl\u0131, 10/3 g\xfcn uyar\u0131 e-postalar\u0131. |\\n| \ud83c\udfae Self-Servis | Duraklat, devam et, geri \xe7ek, yenile, yeniden listele AJAX. |\\n| \ud83d\udcb8 Ceza Sistemi | %0/%10/%25 kademeli, 12 ayl\u0131k kayan pencere, ledger entegrasyonu. |\\n| \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Anti-Gaming | \u0130ptal edilen tarihler 30 g\xfcn bloklan\u0131r. |\\n| \u2b50 G\xfcvenilirlik | Vendor skoru 0-100, g\xfcnl\xfck cron yeniden hesaplama. |\\n| \ud83d\udce7 Bildirimler | 9 yeni ya\u015fam d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfc e-posta \u015fablonu. |\\n| \ud83d\udcca Admin UI | Ya\u015fam d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfc s\xfctunu, meta kutu, vendor g\xfcvenilirlik s\xfctunu. |\\n| \ud83d\udd0d Aktif Filtre | 6 shortcode MetaQueryHelper ile pasif ara\xe7lar\u0131 filtreler. |\\n| \ud83d\uddc4\ufe0f Veritaban\u0131 | v3.5.0 migration, mevcut ara\xe7lar migrate edildi. |\\n| \u2705 Test | 665 test, 2248 assertion (567/2036\'dan art\u0131\u015f). |\\n\\n### S\xfcr\xfcm Notlar\u0131\\n\\nv4.24.0, MHM Rentiva\'n\u0131n ara\xe7 y\xf6netim altyap\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 k\xf6kten g\xfc\xe7lendiriyor. Art\u0131k ara\xe7lar yaln\u0131zca \\"aktif/pasif\\" de\u011fil; tam bir ya\u015fam d\xf6ng\xfcs\xfcne sahip. Vendor\'lar ara\xe7lar\u0131n\u0131 kendi kendine y\xf6netirken platform, adil rekabeti ceza sistemi ve anti-gaming mekanizmalar\u0131yla koruyor. G\xfcvenilirlik puan\u0131 ise kaliteli vendor\'lar\u0131n \xf6ne \xe7\u0131kmas\u0131n\u0131 sa\u011flayan yeni bir rekabet boyutu ekliyor.\\n\\n---\\nMHM Rentiva hakk\u0131nda daha fazla bilgi ve dok\xfcmantasyon i\xe7in [Dok\xfcman Sayfam\u0131z\u0131](https://maxhandmade.github.io/mhm-rentiva-docs/) ziyaret edebilirsiniz."},{"id":"v4.23.1-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.23.1-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-03-28-v4.23.1-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-03-28-v4.23.1-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.23.1: Vendor Form Yeniden Tasarimi & Sehir SelectWoo Migrasyonu","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.23.1 surumu yayinlandi! Bu surum, vendor ayarlar sayfasinin tamamen yeniden tasarlanmasini, basvuru formundaki alan degisikliklerini, sehir secici bilesenlerin SelectWoo\'ya donusturulmesini ve arac sigorta belgesi yukleme ozelligini icerir.","date":"2026-03-28T18:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"forms","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/forms"},{"inline":true,"label":"selectwoo","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/selectwoo"},{"inline":true,"label":"vehicle","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vehicle"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":2.62,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.23.1-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.23.1: Vendor Form Yeniden Tasarimi & Sehir SelectWoo Migrasyonu","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","vendor","forms","selectwoo","vehicle","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-03-28T18:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.24.0: Ara\xe7 Ya\u015fam D\xf6ng\xfcs\xfc Y\xf6netimi & Vendor Self-Servis","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.24.0-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.23.0: Vendor Transfer Mimarisi & Dashboard Denetimi","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.23.0-release-summary"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.23.1** surumu yayinlandi! Bu surum, vendor ayarlar sayfasinin tamamen yeniden tasarlanmasini, basvuru formundaki alan degisikliklerini, sehir secici bilesenlerin SelectWoo\'ya donusturulmesini ve arac sigorta belgesi yukleme ozelligini icerir.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## Onemli Yenilikler\\n\\n### Vendor Ayarlar Sayfasi Yeniden Tasarimi\\n\\nVendor ayarlar sayfasi (`vendor-settings.php`) sifirdan yeniden yazildi:\\n\\n- **Inline stil temizligi:** Tum inline CSS kaldirildi, `.mhm-vendor-form__*` CSS sinif yapisi ile `vendor-forms.css` dosyasina tasinarak bakim kolayligi saglandi.\\n- **Yeni alanlar:** Hesap Sahibi (Account Holder) ve Vergi Dairesi (Tax Office) alanlari eklendi.\\n- **Bildirim sistemi:** Bildirimler artik `mhm-vendor-notice` siniflariyla gosteriliyor.\\n\\n### Basvuru Formu Guncellemeleri\\n\\nVendor basvuru formunda onemli alan degisiklikleri yapildi:\\n\\n- **Hizmet Alanlari kaldirildi:** Checkbox olarak sunulan Hizmet Alanlari (Service Areas) bolumu kaldirildi; yerine bilgi notu eklendi.\\n- **Arac Sigortasi tasinidi:** Basvuru formundan kaldirilip arac ekleme formuna (`[rentiva_vehicle_submit]`) tasindi.\\n- **Yeni finansal alanlar:** Hesap Sahibi (zorunlu) ve Vergi Dairesi (opsiyonel) alanlari eklendi.\\n- **Meta senkronizasyonu:** `VendorApplicationManager` ve `VendorOnboardingController` onay akisinda yeni alanlarin senkronizasyonu saglandi.\\n\\n### Sehir SelectWoo Migrasyonu\\n\\nTum sehir metin girisleri (`<datalist>`) modern bir secim bilesenine donusturuldu:\\n\\n- **Yeni mimari:** `<select>` + WooCommerce selectWoo ile aranabilir, kullanici dostu sehir secimi.\\n- **Yeni metot:** `CityHelper::render_select()` \u2014 tum sehir secicilerde tek kaynak (SSOT).\\n- **Guncellenen formlar:** vendor-settings.php, VendorApply.php, VehicleSubmit.php, TransferAdmin.php.\\n- **CSS/JS enqueue:** UserDashboard.php, VendorApply.php ve VehicleSubmit.php dosyalarina SelectWoo asset\'leri eklendi.\\n\\n### Arac Sigorta Belgesi Yukleme\\n\\nArac ekleme formuna yeni bir belge yukleme bolumu eklendi:\\n\\n- Arac ruhsatindan sonra sigorta belgesi (`_mhm_rentiva_vehicle_insurance_doc`) yuklenebilir.\\n- VehicleSubmit.php AJAX handler\'i sigorta dosyasi isleme destegi ile guncellendi.\\n\\n### Arac Yasam Dongusu Yonetimi (Tasarim)\\n\\nKapsamli bir tasarim dokumani olusturuldu (`docs/plans/2026-03-28-vehicle-lifecycle-management-design.md`):\\n\\n- **Durumlar:** Aktif / Duraklatildi / Geri Cekildi / Suresi Doldu\\n- **Listeleme suresi:** 90 gun, yenileme mekanizmasi ile\\n- **Iptal ceza sistemi:** Kademeli ceza puanlari\\n- **Guvenilirlik skoru:** 0-100 arasi performans degerlendirmesi\\n- **Soguma suresi:** Geri cekilmeden sonra 7 gun bekleme\\n- **Tarih engelleme:** Kotu niyetli kullanima karsi onlem\\n- **8 fazli uygulama plani** hazirland\u0131\\n\\n## Kesfedilen Hatalar (Henuz Duzeltilmedi)\\n\\n| Hata | Detay |\\n|------|-------|\\n| Arac durumu arama filtresi | `_mhm_vehicle_status` arama sorgularinda kontrol edilmiyor \u2014 bakimdaki araclar arama sonuclarinda gorunuyor. |\\n| Vendor askiya alma | `VendorOnboardingController::suspend()` vendor\'un araclarini yayindan kaldirmiyor. |\\n\\n## Degisiklik Kaydi\\n\\n| Tur | Aciklama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| Vendor Ayarlar | Sayfa tamamen yeniden tasarlandi; inline stiller CSS sinif yapisina tasindi. |\\n| Vendor Ayarlar | Hesap Sahibi ve Vergi Dairesi alanlari eklendi. |\\n| Basvuru Formu | Hizmet Alanlari ve Arac Sigortasi alanlari kaldirildi/tasindi. |\\n| Basvuru Formu | Hesap Sahibi (zorunlu) ve Vergi Dairesi (opsiyonel) eklendi. |\\n| Sehir Secici | Tum datalist sehir girisleri SelectWoo bilesenine donusturuldu. |\\n| Arac Formu | Sigorta belgesi yukleme bolumu eklendi. |\\n| Tasarim | Arac Yasam Dongusu Yonetimi tasarim dokumani olusturuldu. |\\n| Hata Kesfedilen | 2 hata tespiti: arac durumu filtresi, vendor askiya alma. |\\n\\n### Surum Notlari\\nBu surum, vendor formlarinin modernizasyonu, sehir secici bilesenlerinin WooCommerce SelectWoo\'ya tas\u0131nmas\u0131 ve arac sigorta belgesi yukleme destegi ile vendor deneyimini onemli olcude iyilestirmistir. Arac Yasam Dongusu Yonetimi tasarim dokumani gelecek surumler icin yol haritasi saglamaktadir.\\n\\n---\\nMHM Rentiva hakkinda daha fazla bilgi ve dokumantasyon icin [Dokuman Sayfamizi](https://maxhandmade.github.io/mhm-rentiva-docs/) ziyaret edebilirsiniz."},{"id":"v4.23.0-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.23.0-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-03-26-v4.23.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-03-26-v4.23.0-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.23.0: Vendor Transfer Mimarisi & Dashboard Denetimi","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.23.0 s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu s\xfcr\xfcm, vendor\'lar\u0131n transfer hizmetlerini \u015fehir bazl\u0131 y\xf6netebilmesini sa\u011flayan yeni bir mimari, kapsaml\u0131 Dashboard widget denetimi ve onlarca hata d\xfczeltmesi getiriyor.","date":"2026-03-26T18:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"transfer","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/transfer"},{"inline":true,"label":"dashboard","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/dashboard"},{"inline":true,"label":"export","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/export"},{"inline":true,"label":"search","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/search"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":2.4,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.23.0-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.23.0: Vendor Transfer Mimarisi & Dashboard Denetimi","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","vendor","transfer","dashboard","export","search","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-03-26T18:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.23.1: Vendor Form Yeniden Tasarimi & Sehir SelectWoo Migrasyonu","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.23.1-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.21.2: Vendor Y\xf6netimi ve Finansal Mimari Devrimi","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.21.2-release-summary"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.23.0** s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu s\xfcr\xfcm, vendor\'lar\u0131n transfer hizmetlerini \u015fehir bazl\u0131 y\xf6netebilmesini sa\u011flayan yeni bir mimari, kapsaml\u0131 Dashboard widget denetimi ve onlarca hata d\xfczeltmesi getiriyor.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 \xd6ne \xc7\u0131kan Yenilikler\\n\\n### \ud83c\udfd7\ufe0f Vendor Transfer Lokasyon Sistemi\\n\\nv4.23.0\'\u0131n en b\xfcy\xfck yenili\u011fi, **\u015eehir \u2192 Nokta hiyerar\u015fisi** ile vendor\'lar\u0131n transfer operasyonlar\u0131n\u0131 y\xf6netebilmesidir:\\n\\n- **\u015eehir bazl\u0131 filtreleme:** Her lokasyona bir \u015fehir alan\u0131 eklendi. Vendor\'lar yaln\u0131zca kendi \u015fehirlerindeki lokasyonlar\u0131 ve rotalar\u0131 g\xf6rebilir.\\n- **Rota bazl\u0131 fiyatland\u0131rma:** Admin\'in belirledi\u011fi `min_price` \u2014 `max_price` aral\u0131\u011f\u0131nda her vendor kendi rota fiyat\u0131n\u0131 belirleyebilir.\\n- **Transfer arama motoru:** Rota bazl\u0131 ara\xe7 filtreleme ve vendor fiyat\u0131 deste\u011fi ile yeniden yap\u0131land\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131. Vendor fiyat\u0131 yoksa rotan\u0131n `base_price` de\u011feri fallback olarak kullan\u0131l\u0131r.\\n- **Veritaban\u0131:** `DatabaseMigrator v3.4.0` ile lokasyonlara `city` s\xfctunu, rotalara `max_price` s\xfctunu eklendi.\\n\\n### \ud83d\udcca Dashboard Widget Denetimi (11 D\xfczeltme)\\n\\nDashboard widget\'lar\u0131nda kapsaml\u0131 bir denetim yap\u0131ld\u0131:\\n- **Timezone tutarl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131:** Geri say\u0131m ve operasyon widget\'lar\u0131 WordPress timezone ayar\u0131na uyumlu hale getirildi.\\n- **Cache invalidation:** \u0130statistik cache key prefix uyumsuzlu\u011fu d\xfczeltildi.\\n- **WC email g\xf6rselleri:** Rezervasyon onay e-postalar\u0131nda ara\xe7 g\xf6rseli art\u0131k do\u011fru g\xf6steriliyor.\\n- **Tasar\u0131m iyile\u015ftirmeleri:** 2x2 grid istatistik kartlar\u0131, yerelle\u015ftirilmi\u015f gelir grafi\u011fi, mesajlar widget\'\u0131 yeniden tasarland\u0131.\\n- **Lite gating:** Gelir Grafi\u011fi ve Yakla\u015fan Operasyonlar widget\'lar\u0131 art\u0131k Pro-only.\\n\\n### \ud83d\udd0e Arama ve Filtreleme D\xfczeltmeleri\\n\\n- **strtotime(\'\') hatas\u0131:** Bo\u015f tarih parametresi bug\xfcn\xfcn tarihini d\xf6nd\xfcr\xfcyordu, aktif booking\'li ara\xe7lar hatal\u0131 filtreleniyordu. Guard eklendi.\\n- **Lokasyon filtresi:** Radio butonlardan checkbox\'a d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcr\xfcld\xfc; birden fazla lokasyon se\xe7ilebilir.\\n- **Transfer tab do\u011frulama:** Transfer alanlar\u0131 (`origin_id`, `destination_id`, `date`, `luggage_*`) hardcoded required olarak ayarland\u0131.\\n\\n### \ud83d\udce4 D\u0131\u015fa Aktar\u0131m (4 D\xfczeltme)\\n\\n- \xd6deme g\xfcnl\xfckleri post_type uyumsuzlu\u011fu giderildi.\\n- Kay\u0131t say\u0131s\u0131 daima 0 d\xf6nen sorgu hatas\u0131 d\xfczeltildi.\\n- Ge\xe7mi\u015f silme i\u015flevi art\u0131k \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor (transient tabanl\u0131).\\n- Ara\xe7 CSV/JSON PHP 8 strict types fatal error\'\u0131 giderildi.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udc64 Vendor \u0130yile\u015ftirmeleri\\n\\n- **Ara\xe7 ruhsat do\u011frulama:** Vendor ara\xe7 ekleme formunda ruhsat bilgisi do\u011frulan\u0131yor.\\n- **D\xfczenleme formu:** Vendor ara\xe7 d\xfczenlemesinde yeniden inceleme (re-review) mekanizmas\u0131.\\n- **Vendor rozeti:** Vendor ara\xe7lar\u0131nda tedarik\xe7i rozeti g\xf6r\xfcnt\xfcleniyor.\\n\\n## \u2699\ufe0f Di\u011fer \u0130yile\u015ftirmeler\\n\\n- **Engellli tarihler:** \\"T\xfcm\xfcne Uygula\\" AJAX d\xfczeltmesi; taray\u0131c\u0131 verisi payload\'da g\xf6nderiliyor.\\n- **Elementor:** 7 widget\'ta attribute kontrol say\u0131s\u0131 art\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131 (VehicleComparison, MyBookings, MyFavorites, VehicleDetails, Testimonials, VehiclesGrid, FeaturedVehicles).\\n- **Ayarlar:** Cache tekrar\u0131, \xf6l\xfc ayarlar temizli\u011fi, SetupWizard sayfa listesi ve AssetManager guard d\xfczeltmeleri.\\n- **\xc7eviri:** 15+ yeni T\xfcrk\xe7e \xe7eviri, WP 6.5+ `.l10n.php` dosyas\u0131 yenilendi.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udccb De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| T\xfcr | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| \ud83c\udfd7\ufe0f Mimari | Vendor Transfer Lokasyon sistemi: \u015eehir\u2192Nokta hiyerar\u015fisi. |\\n| \ud83d\udcb0 Fiyatlama | Vendor rota bazl\u0131 fiyatland\u0131rma (min/max aral\u0131\u011f\u0131). |\\n| \ud83d\udd0d Arama | Transfer arama motoru rota bazl\u0131 filtreleme + vendor fiyat\u0131. |\\n| \ud83d\uddc4\ufe0f Veritaban\u0131 | v3.4.0 migration: city + max_price s\xfctunlar\u0131. |\\n| \ud83d\udcca Dashboard | 11 hata d\xfczeltmesi: timezone, cache, WC email, tasar\u0131m, Lite gating. |\\n| \ud83d\udd0e Filtre | strtotime hatas\u0131, lokasyon checkbox, transfer tab do\u011frulama. |\\n| \ud83d\udcc5 Engelli Tarihler | \\"T\xfcm\xfcne Uygula\\" AJAX d\xfczeltmesi. |\\n| \ud83d\udce4 D\u0131\u015fa Aktar\u0131m | 4 kritik hata d\xfczeltmesi. |\\n| \ud83d\udc64 Vendor | Ruhsat do\u011frulama, yeniden inceleme, vendor rozeti. |\\n| \ud83c\udfa8 Elementor | 7 widget attribute iyile\u015ftirmesi. |\\n| \u2699\ufe0f Ayarlar | Cache, \xf6l\xfc ayarlar, SetupWizard, AssetManager d\xfczeltmeleri. |\\n| \ud83c\udf10 \xc7eviri | 15+ yeni T\xfcrk\xe7e \xe7eviri, .l10n.php yenilendi. |\\n| \u2705 Test | 567 test, 2036 assertion. |\\n\\n### S\xfcr\xfcm Notlar\u0131\\nBu s\xfcr\xfcm, MHM Rentiva\'n\u0131n vendor transfer mimarisini temelden yeniden yap\u0131land\u0131rm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r. \u015eehir bazl\u0131 lokasyon filtresi, rota bazl\u0131 fiyatland\u0131rma ve Dashboard widget denetimi ile platform daha kararl\u0131 ve zengin bir yap\u0131ya kavu\u015fmu\u015ftur.\\n\\n---\\nMHM Rentiva hakk\u0131nda daha fazla bilgi ve dok\xfcmantasyon i\xe7in [Dok\xfcman Sayfam\u0131z\u0131](https://maxhandmade.github.io/mhm-rentiva-docs/) ziyaret edebilirsiniz."},{"id":"v4.21.2-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.21.2-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-03-11-v4.21.2-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-03-11-v4.21.2-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.21.2: Vendor Y\xf6netimi ve Finansal Mimari Devrimi","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.21.2 s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu s\xfcr\xfcm, eklentinin ticaret ve operasyon yeteneklerini k\xf6kten de\u011fi\u015ftiren \\"Vendor Management\\", \\"Financial Architecture\\" ve \\"VIP Transfer\\" mod\xfcllerini beraberinde getiriyor.","date":"2026-03-11T16:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"vendor","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vendor"},{"inline":true,"label":"finance","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/finance"},{"inline":true,"label":"payment","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/payment"},{"inline":true,"label":"vip-transfer","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vip-transfer"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":1.47,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.21.2-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.21.2: Vendor Y\xf6netimi ve Finansal Mimari Devrimi","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","vendor","finance","payment","vip-transfer","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-03-11T16:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.23.0: Vendor Transfer Mimarisi & Dashboard Denetimi","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.23.0-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.10.0: Block/Shortcode Parity Stabilizasyonu","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.10.0-release-summary"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.21.2** s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu s\xfcr\xfcm, eklentinin ticaret ve operasyon yeteneklerini k\xf6kten de\u011fi\u015ftiren \\"Vendor Management\\", \\"Financial Architecture\\" ve \\"VIP Transfer\\" mod\xfcllerini beraberinde getiriyor.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 \xd6ne \xc7\u0131kan Yenilikler\\n\\nBu g\xfcncelleme, MHM Rentiva\'y\u0131 sadece bir rezervasyon motoru olmaktan \xe7\u0131kar\u0131p, tam te\u015fekk\xfcll\xfc bir pazaryeri (marketplace) ve transfer y\xf6netim platformuna d\xf6n\xfc\u015ft\xfcr\xfcyor.\\n\\n### \ud83c\udfe2 Vendor (Tedarik\xe7i) Y\xf6netimi\\nArt\u0131k platformunuzda birden fazla tedarik\xe7iyi y\xf6netebilirsiniz. Her tedarik\xe7i kendi ara\xe7lar\u0131n\u0131, fiyatland\u0131rmas\u0131n\u0131 ve rezervasyonlar\u0131n\u0131 kontrol edebilir.\\n- **Tedarik\xe7i Paneli:** \xd6zelle\u015ftirilmi\u015f admin aray\xfcz\xfc.\\n- **Performans Takibi:** Tedarik\xe7i bazl\u0131 doluluk ve gelir raporlar\u0131.\\n\\n### \ud83d\udcb0 Yeni Finansal Mimari\\n\xd6deme y\xf6netimi ve komisyon hesaplamalar\u0131 tamamen standardize edildi.\\n- **Commission Management:** Esnek komisyon oranlar\u0131 ve otomatik hesaplama.\\n- **Ledger System:** T\xfcm finansal hareketlerin \u015feffaf bir \u015fekilde kaydedildi\u011fi muhasebe defteri.\\n- **Payouts:** Tedarik\xe7i \xf6demelerinin merkezi takibi.\\n\\n### \ud83d\ude90 VIP Transfer Mod\xfcl\xfc\\nNoktadan noktaya rota bazl\u0131 fiyatland\u0131rma ve rezervasyon sistemi.\\n- **Rota Bazl\u0131 Fiyatland\u0131rma:** Mesafe veya rota bazl\u0131 dinamik fiyat tan\u0131mlama.\\n- **Transfer Rezervasyonu:** Ara\xe7 kiralama ak\u0131\u015f\u0131ndan ba\u011f\u0131ms\u0131z, optimize edilmi\u015f transfer deneyimi.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f Teknik \u0130yile\u015ftirmeler ve G\xfcvenlik\\n\\nSadece \xf6zellik de\u011fil, altyap\u0131 olarak da g\xfc\xe7lendik:\\n- **Hardened REST API:** `SecurityHelper` ve `AuthHelper` ile API u\xe7 noktalar\u0131 daha g\xfcvenli hale getirildi.\\n- **WP 6.7+ Uyumlu:** En son WordPress s\xfcr\xfcmleriyle tam uyumluluk ve performans optimizasyonu.\\n- **Modern Gereksinimler:** Minimum PHP 8.1+ ve WP 6.7+ standartlar\u0131na ge\xe7i\u015f yap\u0131ld\u0131.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udccb De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| T\xfcr | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| \u2728 Yeni Mod\xfcl | Vendor Y\xf6netim Sistemi (Multi-vendor deste\u011fi). |\\n| \ud83d\udcb8 Finans | Geli\u015fmi\u015f finansal mimari, komisyon ve defter (ledger) sistemi. |\\n| \ud83d\udeeb Transfer | VIP Transfer mod\xfcl\xfc ve rota bazl\u0131 fiyatland\u0131rma motoru. |\\n| \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f G\xfcvenlik | REST API g\xfcvenlik katmanlar\u0131 (`AuthHelper` entegrasyonu). |\\n| \ud83d\ude80 Performans | PHP 8.1+ optimizasyonu ve autoloader iyile\u015ftirmeleri. |\\n| \ud83e\uddf9 Paketleme | `.distignore` ile optimize edilmi\u015f, tertemiz eklenti paketi yap\u0131s\u0131. |\\n\\n### S\xfcr\xfcm Notlar\u0131\\nBu s\xfcr\xfcm, `mhm-rentiva` ekosisteminde bug\xfcne kadar yap\u0131lm\u0131\u015f en kapsaml\u0131 mod\xfcler geni\u015fletmedir. Mod\xfcller aras\u0131 veri b\xfct\xfcnl\xfc\u011f\xfc `Util::has_overlap()` ve `DepositCalculator` gibi merkezi s\u0131n\u0131flar \xfczerinden garanti alt\u0131na al\u0131nm\u0131\u015ft\u0131r.\\n\\n---\\nMHM Rentiva hakk\u0131nda daha fazla bilgi ve dok\xfcmantasyon i\xe7in [Dok\xfcman Sayfam\u0131z\u0131](https://maxhandmade.github.io/mhm-rentiva-docs/) ziyaret edebilirsiniz."},{"id":"v4.10.0-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.10.0-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-02-18-v4.10.0-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-02-18-v4.10.0-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.10.0: Block/Shortcode Parity Stabilizasyonu","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.10.0 s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu b\xfcy\xfck g\xfcncelleme ile Gutenberg bloklar\u0131 ve k\u0131sa kodlar (shortcode) aras\u0131ndaki tam e\u015flik (parity) sa\u011fland\u0131; 19/19 deterministic y\xfczey do\u011fruland\u0131.","date":"2026-02-18T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"gutenberg","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/gutenberg"},{"inline":true,"label":"blocks","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/blocks"},{"inline":true,"label":"shortcode","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/shortcode"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":1.15,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.10.0-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.10.0: Block/Shortcode Parity Stabilizasyonu","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","gutenberg","blocks","shortcode","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-02-18T09:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.21.2: Vendor Y\xf6netimi ve Finansal Mimari Devrimi","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.21.2-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.9.8: URL Tutarl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve WooCommerce \u0130yile\u015ftirmeleri","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.9.8-release-summary"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.10.0** s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu b\xfcy\xfck g\xfcncelleme ile Gutenberg bloklar\u0131 ve k\u0131sa kodlar (shortcode) aras\u0131ndaki tam e\u015flik (parity) sa\u011fland\u0131; 19/19 deterministic y\xfczey do\u011fruland\u0131.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| T\xfcr | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| \ud83c\udfaf E\u015flik (Parity) | Block \u2194 Shortcode tam e\u015fli\u011fi sa\u011fland\u0131 \u2014 19/19 deterministic y\xfczey do\u011fruland\u0131. |\\n| \ud83d\udd17 E\u015fleme (Mapping) | `vehicle-comparison`, `booking-form` ve `testimonials` bloklar\u0131 i\xe7in deterministik alias e\u015flemesi eklendi. |\\n| \ud83d\udd04 D\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm (Transform) | `showFeatures` de\u011fer d\xf6n\xfc\u015f\xfcm\xfc kapsam izolasyonuyla stabilize edildi (boolean \u2192 `all`/`basic`). |\\n| \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f G\xfcvenlik | Booking form dinamik varsay\u0131lan korumas\u0131 eklendi (`defaultDays`/`minDays`/`maxDays` statik override engellendi). |\\n| \ud83d\udccb Denetim | 19/19 Light Parity Audit tam kan\u0131t zinciriyle tamamland\u0131. |\\n| \u2705 Kalite Kap\u0131lar\u0131 | PHPCS, Plugin Check, PHPUnit \u2014 0 hata, tam suite ge\xe7i\u015fi. |\\n\\n### Detaylar\\n\\nBu s\xfcr\xfcm, MHM Rentiva\'n\u0131n blok ve k\u0131sa kod \xe7\u0131kt\u0131lar\u0131n\u0131 birbirinin ayn\u0131s\u0131 haline getiren kapsaml\u0131 bir stabilizasyon \xe7al\u0131\u015fmas\u0131n\u0131n \xfcr\xfcn\xfcd\xfcr. Art\u0131k ayn\u0131 i\xe7erik hem Gutenberg blo\u011fu hem de `[mhm_rentiva_*]` k\u0131sa kodu olarak eklendi\u011finde birebir ayn\u0131 HTML \xe7\u0131kt\u0131s\u0131 ve davran\u0131\u015f elde edilmektedir.\\n\\nKalite kap\u0131lar\u0131 post-bump olarak do\u011fruland\u0131:\\n\\n| Kap\u0131 | Sonu\xe7 |\\n|------|-------|\\n| PHPCS | \u2705 0 hata |\\n| Plugin Check | \u2705 PASS (exit code 0) |\\n| PHPUnit | \u2705 216 test, 0 ba\u015far\u0131s\u0131zl\u0131k |"},{"id":"v4.9.8-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.9.8-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-02-09-v4.9.8-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-02-09-v4.9.8-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.9.8: URL Tutarl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve WooCommerce \u0130yile\u015ftirmeleri","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.9.8 s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu g\xfcncelleme ile WooCommerce entegrasyonu g\xfc\xe7lendirildi ve kal\u0131c\u0131 link (permalink) yap\u0131s\u0131ndaki tutarl\u0131l\u0131k art\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131.","date":"2026-02-09T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"woocommerce","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/woocommerce"},{"inline":true,"label":"mhm-rentiva","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/mhm-rentiva"}],"readingTime":0.43,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.9.8-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.9.8: URL Tutarl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve WooCommerce \u0130yile\u015ftirmeleri","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","woocommerce","mhm-rentiva"],"date":"2026-02-09T09:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.10.0: Block/Shortcode Parity Stabilizasyonu","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.10.0-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.9.7: Gutenberg UI/UX Standardizasyonu","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.9.7-release-summary"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.9.8** s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu g\xfcncelleme ile WooCommerce entegrasyonu g\xfc\xe7lendirildi ve kal\u0131c\u0131 link (permalink) yap\u0131s\u0131ndaki tutarl\u0131l\u0131k art\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| T\xfcr | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f D\xfczeltme | WooCommerce Hesab\u0131m u\xe7 noktalar\u0131nda fiziksel sayfa k\u0131sa isimlerine (slug) mutlak \xf6ncelik verildi. |\\n| \u26a1 \u0130yile\u015ftirme | Entegre panel d\xfczeni korundu; \xf6zel linklerde (\xf6rn. /favorilerim/) d\u0131\u015fa y\xf6nlendirme sorunu giderildi. |\\n| \u2699\ufe0f Kararl\u0131l\u0131k | URL tutarl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131 i\xe7in kal\u0131c\u0131 linklerin (rewrite rules) otomatik yenilenmesi sa\u011fland\u0131. |\\n\\n### Detaylar\\nBu s\xfcr\xfcm, kullan\u0131c\u0131lar\u0131m\u0131z\u0131n \\"Hesab\u0131m\\" panelindeki deneyimini p\xfcr\xfczs\xfcz hale getirmeye odaklan\u0131yor. \xd6zellikle \xf6zel sayfa yap\u0131s\u0131 kullanan temalarda ya\u015fanan y\xf6nlendirme sorunlar\u0131 giderilerek sistem daha kararl\u0131 hale getirildi."},{"id":"v4.9.7-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.9.7-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-02-08-v4.9.7-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-02-08-v4.9.7-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.9.7: Gutenberg UI/UX Standardizasyonu","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.9.7 s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu g\xfcncelleme ile Gutenberg blok edit\xf6r\xfc deneyimi standartla\u015ft\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131 ve konsol uyar\u0131lar\u0131 temizlendi.","date":"2026-02-08T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"gutenberg","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/gutenberg"},{"inline":true,"label":"ui-ux","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/ui-ux"}],"readingTime":0.37,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.9.7-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.9.7: Gutenberg UI/UX Standardizasyonu","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","gutenberg","ui-ux"],"date":"2026-02-08T09:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.9.8: URL Tutarl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131 ve WooCommerce \u0130yile\u015ftirmeleri","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.9.8-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.9.6: Transfer Mod\xfcl\xfc ve B\xfcy\xfck Bak\u0131m","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.9.6-release-summary"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.9.7** s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu g\xfcncelleme ile Gutenberg blok edit\xf6r\xfc deneyimi standartla\u015ft\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131 ve konsol uyar\u0131lar\u0131 temizlendi.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| T\xfcr | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| \u2728 \xd6zellik | Gutenberg blok kenar \xe7ubuklar\u0131 (InspectorControls) tutarl\u0131 UI/UX i\xe7in standartla\u015ft\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131. |\\n| \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f D\xfczeltme | Blok edit\xf6r\xfcndeki konsol uyar\u0131lar\u0131 giderilerek kararl\u0131l\u0131k art\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131. |\\n| \u26a1 \u0130yile\u015ftirme | Proje dok\xfcmantasyonu ve kurallar\u0131 g\xfcncellendi. |\\n\\n### Detaylar\\nEdit\xf6r taraf\u0131ndaki kullan\u0131c\u0131 deneyimini iyile\u015ftirmek ad\u0131na Gutenberg blok kontrolleri daha d\xfczenli hale getirildi. Arka planda \xe7al\u0131\u015fan scriptlerdeki ufak hatalar giderilerek temiz bir \xe7al\u0131\u015fma ortam\u0131 sa\u011fland\u0131."},{"id":"v4.9.6-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.9.6-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-02-02-v4.9.6-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-02-02-v4.9.6-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.9.6: Transfer Mod\xfcl\xfc ve B\xfcy\xfck Bak\u0131m","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.9.6 s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu s\xfcr\xfcm, Transfer Mod\xfcl\xfc entegrasyonu ve kapsaml\u0131 veritaban\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131ma mant\u0131\u011f\u0131 gibi kritik g\xfcncellemeler i\xe7ermektedir.","date":"2026-02-02T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"transfer","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/transfer"},{"inline":true,"label":"performance","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/performance"}],"readingTime":0.5,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.9.6-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.9.6: Transfer Mod\xfcl\xfc ve B\xfcy\xfck Bak\u0131m","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","transfer","performance"],"date":"2026-02-02T09:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.9.7: Gutenberg UI/UX Standardizasyonu","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.9.7-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.7: G\xfcvenlik ve Performans Optimizasyonu","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.7-release-summary"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.9.6** s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu s\xfcr\xfcm, Transfer Mod\xfcl\xfc entegrasyonu ve kapsaml\u0131 veritaban\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131ma mant\u0131\u011f\u0131 gibi kritik g\xfcncellemeler i\xe7ermektedir.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| T\xfcr | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| \u2728 \xd6zellik | Transfer Mod\xfcl\xfc: \xd6n ek standardizasyonu (rentiva_) ve veritaban\u0131 ta\u015f\u0131ma mant\u0131\u011f\u0131 tamamland\u0131. |\\n| \u26a1 Performans | Genel kod optimizasyonu ve performans iyile\u015ftirmeleri yap\u0131ld\u0131. |\\n| \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f D\xfczeltme | M\xfcsaitlik Takvimi i\xe7in HTML yap\u0131s\u0131 daha iyi eri\u015filebilirlik i\xe7in g\xfcncellendi. |\\n| \ud83c\udfa8 Stil | Daha iyi bak\u0131m i\xe7in CSS mimarisi temizlendi ve yeniden yap\u0131land\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131. |\\n| \ud83c\udf10 i18n | Yeni \xe7eviri dosyalar\u0131 eklendi ve mevcut \xe7eviriler iyile\u015ftirildi. |\\n\\n### Detaylar\\nY\xfcksek performansl\u0131 bir altyap\u0131 i\xe7in CSS ve PHP taraf\u0131nda b\xfcy\xfck \xe7apl\u0131 temizlik yap\u0131ld\u0131. Transfer mod\xfcl\xfcn\xfcn veritaban\u0131 yap\u0131s\u0131 standartlara uygun hale getirilerek sistem kararl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131 art\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131."},{"id":"v4.6.7-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.7-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-02-01-v4.6.7-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-02-01-v4.6.7-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.7: G\xfcvenlik ve Performans Optimizasyonu","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.7 s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu g\xfcncelleme ile y\xf6nlendirme g\xfcvenli\u011fi, SQL optimizasyonu ve stil y\xf6netimi modern standartlara ta\u015f\u0131nd\u0131.","date":"2026-02-01T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"},{"inline":true,"label":"performance","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/performance"}],"readingTime":0.42,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.6.7-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.7: G\xfcvenlik ve Performans Optimizasyonu","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","security","performance"],"date":"2026-02-01T09:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.9.6: Transfer Mod\xfcl\xfc ve B\xfcy\xfck Bak\u0131m","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.9.6-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.6: Rezervasyon Formu ve Fiyatland\u0131rma \u0130yile\u015ftirmeleri","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.6-release-summary"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.6.7** s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu g\xfcncelleme ile y\xf6nlendirme g\xfcvenli\u011fi, SQL optimizasyonu ve stil y\xf6netimi modern standartlara ta\u015f\u0131nd\u0131.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| T\xfcr | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f G\xfcvenlik | Y\xf6nlendirme g\xfcvenli\u011fini art\u0131rmak i\xe7in `wp_safe_redirect` kullan\u0131m\u0131na ge\xe7ildi. |\\n| \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f G\xfcvenlik | `SecurityHelper::safe_output()` metodu ba\u011flam do\u011frulamas\u0131 ve JSON deste\u011fiyle modernize edildi. |\\n| \u26a1 Performans | SQL transient silme i\u015flemi, native `delete_transient()` fonksiyonuna \xe7evrildi. |\\n| \ud83c\udfa8 Stil | Sat\u0131r i\xe7i CSS kodlar\u0131 `wp_add_inline_style` API\'sine ta\u015f\u0131narak standartla\u015ft\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131. |\\n\\n### Detaylar\\nEklentinin \xe7ekirdek fonksiyonlar\u0131 daha g\xfcvenli ve performansl\u0131 hale getirildi. \xd6zellikle y\xf6nlendirme ve veri \xe7\u0131kt\u0131 i\u015flemleri WordPress\'in en g\xfcncel g\xfcvenlik protokollerine g\xf6re optimize edildi."},{"id":"v4.6.6-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.6-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-01-28-v4.6.6-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-01-28-v4.6.6-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.6: Rezervasyon Formu ve Fiyatland\u0131rma \u0130yile\u015ftirmeleri","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.6 s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu g\xfcncelleme, rezervasyon formundaki g\xf6rsel hatalar\u0131 giderir ve yeni bir fiyatland\u0131rma detay\u0131 ekler.","date":"2026-01-28T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"interface","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/interface"},{"inline":true,"label":"booking","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/booking"}],"readingTime":0.51,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.6.6-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.6: Rezervasyon Formu ve Fiyatland\u0131rma \u0130yile\u015ftirmeleri","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","interface","booking"],"date":"2026-01-28T09:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.7: G\xfcvenlik ve Performans Optimizasyonu","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.7-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.5: WPCS Uyumlulu\u011fu ve Kod Standartlar\u0131","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.5-release-summary"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.6.6** s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu g\xfcncelleme, rezervasyon formundaki g\xf6rsel hatalar\u0131 giderir ve yeni bir fiyatland\u0131rma detay\u0131 ekler.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| T\xfcr | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f D\xfczeltme | Rezervasyon formundaki ara\xe7 \xf6zellik ikonlar\u0131n\u0131n (yak\u0131t, vites vb.) kaybolma sorunu giderildi. |\\n| \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f D\xfczeltme | Ara\xe7 \xf6zellik verilerinin i\u015flenmesi s\u0131ras\u0131nda olu\u015fan mant\u0131ksal hatalar d\xfczeltildi. |\\n| \u2728 \xd6zellik | Rezervasyon formu fiyat detay\u0131na \'Hafta Sonu Fark\u0131\' g\xf6sterimi eklendi. |\\n| \u26a1 \u0130yile\u015ftirme | Rezervasyon formu g\xf6rselle\u015ftirmesi ve ikon boyutland\u0131rmalar\u0131 optimize edildi. |\\n| \ud83e\uddf9 Temizlik | \xc7ak\u0131\u015fan eski CSS kodlar\u0131 temizlendi ve modern yap\u0131ya ge\xe7ildi. |\\n\\n### Detaylar\\nKullan\u0131c\u0131 deneyimini iyile\u015ftirmek ad\u0131na rezervasyon formundaki ikon sorunlar\u0131 \xe7\xf6z\xfcld\xfc ve fiyatland\u0131rma \u015feffafl\u0131\u011f\u0131 i\xe7in hafta sonu fark\u0131 detay\u0131 eklendi. CSS yap\u0131s\u0131 daha sade ve h\u0131zl\u0131 hale getirildi."},{"id":"v4.6.5-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.5-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-01-26-v4.6.5-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-01-26-v4.6.5-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.5: WPCS Uyumlulu\u011fu ve Kod Standartlar\u0131","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.5 s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu b\xfcy\xfck \xf6l\xe7ekli altyap\u0131 g\xfcncellemesi ile 110.000+ sat\u0131r kod WordPress standartlar\u0131na (WPCS) uyumlu hale getirildi.","date":"2026-01-26T15:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"},{"inline":true,"label":"refactoring","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/refactoring"}],"readingTime":0.43,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.6.5-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.5: WPCS Uyumlulu\u011fu ve Kod Standartlar\u0131","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","security","refactoring"],"date":"2026-01-26T15:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.6: Rezervasyon Formu ve Fiyatland\u0131rma \u0130yile\u015ftirmeleri","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.6-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.4: Veri B\xfct\xfcnl\xfc\u011f\xfc ve \xc7\u0131kt\u0131 G\xfcvenli\u011fi","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.4-release-summary"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.6.5** s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu b\xfcy\xfck \xf6l\xe7ekli altyap\u0131 g\xfcncellemesi ile 110.000+ sat\u0131r kod WordPress standartlar\u0131na (WPCS) uyumlu hale getirildi.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| T\xfcr | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f G\xfcvenlik | 50+ WPCS g\xfcvenlik uyar\u0131s\u0131 \xe7\xf6z\xfcld\xfc (Girdi Sanitizasyonu & DB \u0130nterpolasyonu). |\\n| \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f G\xfcvenlik | Handler.php ve AccountController.php XSS\'e kar\u015f\u0131 g\xfc\xe7lendirildi. |\\n| \u2699\ufe0f Kararl\u0131l\u0131k | Eski `error_log` yap\u0131s\u0131 modern `AdvancedLogger` mimarisiyle de\u011fi\u015ftirildi. |\\n| \u26a1 \u0130yile\u015ftirme | 110.000+ WordPress Kodlama Standartlar\u0131 (WPCS) uyumsuzlu\u011fu otomatik d\xfczeltildi. |\\n\\n### Detaylar\\nBu g\xfcncelleme eklentimizin gelecekteki geli\u015fimini sa\u011flam bir temele oturtmaktad\u0131r. Geni\u015f \xe7apl\u0131 kod standartlar\u0131 denetimi ile hem g\xfcvenlik hem de bak\u0131m kolayl\u0131\u011f\u0131 en \xfcst d\xfczeye \xe7\u0131kar\u0131ld\u0131."},{"id":"v4.6.4-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.4-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-01-26-v4.6.4-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-01-26-v4.6.4-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.4: Veri B\xfct\xfcnl\xfc\u011f\xfc ve \xc7\u0131kt\u0131 G\xfcvenli\u011fi","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.4 s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu s\xfcr\xfcmde y\xf6netici paneli \xe7\u0131kt\u0131 g\xfcvenli\u011fi ve para birimi sembollerindeki tutarl\u0131l\u0131k hatalar\u0131 giderildi.","date":"2026-01-26T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"},{"inline":true,"label":"data-integrity","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/data-integrity"}],"readingTime":0.5,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.6.4-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.4: Veri B\xfct\xfcnl\xfc\u011f\xfc ve \xc7\u0131kt\u0131 G\xfcvenli\u011fi","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","security","data-integrity"],"date":"2026-01-26T09:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.5: WPCS Uyumlulu\u011fu ve Kod Standartlar\u0131","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.5-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.3: SQL G\xfcvenli\u011fi ve REST API Kararl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.3-release-summary"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.6.4** s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu s\xfcr\xfcmde y\xf6netici paneli \xe7\u0131kt\u0131 g\xfcvenli\u011fi ve para birimi sembollerindeki tutarl\u0131l\u0131k hatalar\u0131 giderildi.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| T\xfcr | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f G\xfcvenlik | Admin sekmelerinde `esc_html` ve `wp_kses_post` kullan\u0131larak \xe7\u0131kt\u0131 ka\xe7\u0131rma i\u015flemleri g\xfc\xe7lendirildi. |\\n| \u2699\ufe0f Kararl\u0131l\u0131k | AddonManager ve Rezervasyon Meta Kutular\u0131ndaki fiyat/ID alanlar\u0131 i\xe7in sanitizasyon iyile\u015ftirildi. |\\n| \u26a1 \u0130yile\u015ftirme | Rezervasyon D\xfczenleme ekranlar\u0131ndaki hardcoded para birimi sembol sorunlar\u0131 giderildi. |\\n| \u26a1 \u0130yile\u015ftirme | Ara\xe7 kolonlar\u0131 ve sistem bilgisi sayfalar\u0131ndaki SQL sorgular\u0131 optimize edildi. |\\n| \u26a1 \u0130yile\u015ftirme | Manuel rezarvasyon ve ara\xe7 y\xf6netiminde kalan baz\u0131 T\xfcrk\xe7e dizeler \u0130ngilizce\'ye \xe7evrildi. |\\n\\n### Detaylar\\nY\xf6netici panelindeki veri giri\u015f ve \xe7\u0131k\u0131\u015f noktalar\u0131nda g\xfcvenlik standartlar\u0131 art\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131. \xd6zellikle fiyatland\u0131rma alanlar\u0131ndaki sanitizasyon iyile\u015ftirmeleri veri b\xfct\xfcnl\xfc\u011f\xfcn\xfc garanti alt\u0131na almaktad\u0131r."},{"id":"v4.6.3-release-summary","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.3-release-summary","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-01-25-v4.6.3-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-01-25-v4.6.3-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.3: SQL G\xfcvenli\u011fi ve REST API Kararl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.3 s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu g\xfcncelleme, SQL Injection korumas\u0131 ve AJAX g\xfcvenilirli\u011fi \xfczerine \xf6nemli iyile\u015ftirmeler i\xe7ermektedir.","date":"2026-01-25T09:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"},{"inline":true,"label":"rest-api","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/rest-api"}],"readingTime":0.55,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.6.3-release-summary","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.3: SQL G\xfcvenli\u011fi ve REST API Kararl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","security","rest-api"],"date":"2026-01-25T09:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.4: Veri B\xfct\xfcnl\xfc\u011f\xfc ve \xc7\u0131kt\u0131 G\xfcvenli\u011fi","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.4-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.2: G\xfcvenlik Tahkimat\u0131 ve WPCS Uyumlulu\u011fu","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.2-security-update"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.6.3** s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu g\xfcncelleme, SQL Injection korumas\u0131 ve AJAX g\xfcvenilirli\u011fi \xfczerine \xf6nemli iyile\u015ftirmeler i\xe7ermektedir.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83d\ude80 De\u011fi\u015fiklik Kayd\u0131\\n\\n| T\xfcr | A\xe7\u0131klama |\\n|-----|----------|\\n| \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f G\xfcvenlik | Mesaj arama sorgular\u0131 prepared statements kullan\u0131larak SQL Injection\'a kar\u015f\u0131 g\xfc\xe7lendirildi. |\\n| \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f G\xfcvenlik | REST API entegrasyon ayarlar\u0131n\u0131n backend mimarisi, AJAX buton g\xfcvenilirli\u011fini art\u0131racak \u015fekilde g\xfcncellendi. |\\n| \u2699\ufe0f Kararl\u0131l\u0131k | Asenkron isteklerde \'-1\' hatas\u0131n\u0131 \xf6nlemek i\xe7in AJAX hook kay\u0131t sistemi iyile\u015ftirildi. |\\n| \u2699\ufe0f Kararl\u0131l\u0131k | REST ayarlar\u0131nda IP listesi sanitizasyon hatalar\u0131 giderildi. |\\n| \u26a1 \u0130yile\u015ftirme | Proje kaynak kodu dok\xfcmantasyonu WPCS uyumlulu\u011fu i\xe7in tamamen \u0130ngilizce\'ye \xe7evrildi. |\\n\\n### Detaylar\\nBu s\xfcr\xfcmle birlikte mesajla\u015fma sistemindeki arama fonksiyonlar\u0131 ve AJAX tabanl\u0131 ayar kaydediciler daha g\xfcvenli ve kararl\u0131 hale getirildi. \xd6zellikle geli\u015ftiriciler i\xe7in kod taban\u0131ndaki yorum sat\u0131rlar\u0131 d\xfcnya standartlar\u0131na (WPCS) uygun hale getirildi."},{"id":"v4.6.2-security-update","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.2-security-update","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-01-22-v4.6.2-release.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-01-22-v4.6.2-release.md","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.2: G\xfcvenlik Tahkimat\u0131 ve WPCS Uyumlulu\u011fu","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.2 yay\u0131nda! Bu s\xfcr\xfcm, eklentinin t\xfcm mod\xfcllerini kapsayan devasa bir g\xfcvenlik ve altyap\u0131 g\xfc\xe7lendirme g\xfcncellemesidir. Yeni \xf6zellik eklemekten ziyade, mevcut sistemin a\u015f\u0131lmaz bir kale haline getirilmesine odakland\u0131k.","date":"2026-01-22T06:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"},{"inline":true,"label":"wpcs","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/wpcs"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"}],"readingTime":1.21,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4.6.2-security-update","title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.2: G\xfcvenlik Tahkimat\u0131 ve WPCS Uyumlulu\u011fu","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","security","wpcs","update"],"date":"2026-01-22T06:00"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.3: SQL G\xfcvenli\u011fi ve REST API Kararl\u0131l\u0131\u011f\u0131","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.3-release-summary"},"nextItem":{"title":"v4.6.1 Yay\u0131nda! \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4-6-1-released"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.6.2** yay\u0131nda! Bu s\xfcr\xfcm, eklentinin t\xfcm mod\xfcllerini kapsayan devasa bir g\xfcvenlik ve altyap\u0131 g\xfc\xe7lendirme g\xfcncellemesidir. Yeni \xf6zellik eklemekten ziyade, mevcut sistemin **a\u015f\u0131lmaz bir kale** haline getirilmesine odakland\u0131k.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f G\xfcvenlik Denetimi \xd6zeti\\n\\nSon 24 saat i\xe7inde, MHM Rentiva\'n\u0131n 22 farkl\u0131 mod\xfcl\xfc \xfczerinde sat\u0131r sat\u0131r kod analizi ger\xe7ekle\u015ftirdik. Hedefimiz sadece \\"\xe7al\u0131\u015fan\\" bir eklenti de\u011fil, \\"en g\xfcvenli\\" kiralama eklentisi olmakt\u0131r.\\n\\n\u0130\u015fte bu g\xfcncellemenin karnesi:\\n\\n| Metrik | De\u011fer |\\n|--------|-------|\\n| **Denetlenen Mod\xfcller** | 22 (T\xfcm\xfc) |\\n| **D\xfczenlenen Dosyalar** | 59+ |\\n| **Nonce (CSRF) Yamas\u0131** | 91+ |\\n| **WPCS Uyumlulu\u011fu** | %100 |\\n\\n### Neler De\u011fi\u015fti?\\n\\n#### 1. Tam Kapsaml\u0131 Nonce Korumas\u0131\\nWordPress\'in g\xfcvenlik mekanizmas\u0131 olan `nonce` (number used once) kullan\u0131m\u0131 t\xfcm form ve AJAX i\u015flemlerinde standartla\u015ft\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131. Her bir do\u011frulama i\u015flemi art\u0131k `sanitize_text_field(wp_unslash())` sarmalay\u0131c\u0131s\u0131 ile ekstra bir temizlik katman\u0131ndan ge\xe7iriliyor.\\n\\n#### 2. REST API ve Rate Limiting\\nAPI taraf\u0131nda **H\u0131z S\u0131n\u0131rlama (Rate Limiting)** ve **IP K\u0131s\u0131tlama** mekanizmalar\u0131 \xe7ekirdek yap\u0131ya daha s\u0131k\u0131 entegre edildi. Art\u0131k `CoreSettings` yerine `RESTSettings` \xfczerinden y\xf6netilen bu yap\u0131, yetkisiz eri\u015fim denemelerini an\u0131nda engelliyor.\\n\\n> Detaylar i\xe7in yenilenen [REST API Dok\xfcmantasyonu](../docs/api/overview) sayfas\u0131n\u0131 inceleyebilirsiniz.\\n\\n#### 3. Kod Kalitesi ve PHP 8.4+ Uyumu\\nGelece\u011fe haz\u0131rl\u0131k kapsam\u0131nda, PHP 8.4 ve \xfczeri s\xfcr\xfcmlerde ortaya \xe7\u0131kabilecek \\"Implicit Nullable Parameter\\" uyar\u0131lar\u0131 giderildi. Kod taban\u0131 daha modern, temiz ve hatas\u0131z hale getirildi.\\n\\n## \ud83c\udfd7\ufe0f Yeni Teknik Dok\xfcmantasyon\\n\\nMod\xfcler yap\u0131m\u0131z\u0131 daha iyi anlatabilmek ve geli\u015ftiricilere rehberlik etmek i\xe7in dok\xfcmantasyonumuza yeni bir b\xf6l\xfcm ekledik:\\n\\n*   [**Mod\xfcl Mimarisi ve Teknik Harita:**](../docs/developer/core/technical-architecture) Eklentinin 22 mod\xfcl\xfcn\xfcn ili\u015fkilerini, dosya yap\u0131s\u0131n\u0131 ve g\xfcvenlik durumunu g\xf6steren kapsaml\u0131 bir rehber.\\n\\n---\\n\\nMHM Rentiva ile g\xfcvenli ve performansl\u0131 kiralamalar dileriz! \ud83d\ude80"},{"id":"v4-6-1-released","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4-6-1-released","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-01-21-v4-6-1-released.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-01-21-v4-6-1-released.md","title":"v4.6.1 Yay\u0131nda! \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.1 s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu s\xfcr\xfcm, veri b\xfct\xfcnl\xfc\u011f\xfc, g\xfcvenlik ve WooCommerce entegrasyonu konular\u0131nda kritik iyile\u015ftirmeler i\xe7eren bir g\xfcvenlik ve kararl\u0131l\u0131k g\xfcncellemesidir.","date":"2026-01-21T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"v4.6.1","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/v-4-6-1"},{"inline":true,"label":"security","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/security"},{"inline":true,"label":"critical","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/critical"},{"inline":true,"label":"woocommerce","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/woocommerce"}],"readingTime":1.18,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4-6-1-released","title":"v4.6.1 Yay\u0131nda! \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","v4.6.1","security","critical","woocommerce"],"date":"2026-01-21T00:00:00.000Z"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.2: G\xfcvenlik Tahkimat\u0131 ve WPCS Uyumlulu\u011fu","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4.6.2-security-update"},"nextItem":{"title":"v4.6.0 Yay\u0131nda! \ud83d\ude80","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4-6-0-released"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.6.1** s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu s\xfcr\xfcm, **veri b\xfct\xfcnl\xfc\u011f\xfc**, **g\xfcvenlik** ve **WooCommerce entegrasyonu** konular\u0131nda kritik iyile\u015ftirmeler i\xe7eren bir g\xfcvenlik ve kararl\u0131l\u0131k g\xfcncellemesidir.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Kritik G\xfcvenlik ve Veri Koruma\\n\\n### \ud83e\uddf9 DatabaseCleaner \u0130yile\u015ftirmesi\\nVeritaban\u0131 temizleme arac\u0131m\u0131z, art\u0131k \xe7ok daha ak\u0131ll\u0131 ve g\xfcvenli.\\n- **Geni\u015fletilmi\u015f Koruma:** WooCommerce sipari\u015f ID\'leri, \xf6deme detaylar\u0131 ve m\xfc\u015fteri meta verileri dahil olmak \xfczere **40\'tan fazla kritik meta anahtar** (`_mhm_` prefixli) koruma listesine eklendi.\\n- **Veri Kayb\u0131 \xd6nleme:** Bak\u0131m i\u015flemleri s\u0131ras\u0131nda yanl\u0131\u015fl\u0131kla veri silinmesinin \xf6n\xfcne ge\xe7mek i\xe7in koruma mekanizmalar\u0131 g\xfc\xe7lendirildi.\\n\\n### \ud83d\udd12 SQL G\xfcvenli\u011fi (Hardening)\\nSistem genelinde SQL sorgular\u0131 g\xf6zden ge\xe7irildi ve g\xfcvenlik seviyesi art\u0131r\u0131ld\u0131.\\n- **Prepared Statements:** `BookingColumns` ve `ExportStats` s\u0131n\u0131flar\u0131ndaki dinamik sorgular, SQL Injection risklerine kar\u015f\u0131 `wpdb->prepare()` kullan\u0131larak standardize edildi.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udecd\ufe0f WooCommerce ve \xd6deme \u0130yile\u015ftirmeleri\\n\\n### \u269b\ufe0f Atomik \xc7ak\u0131\u015fma Kilidi (Atomic Overlap Lock)\\nYo\u011fun rezervasyon trafi\u011fi olan siteler i\xe7in hayati bir \xf6zellik eklendi.\\n- **\xc7ift Rezervasyon \xd6nleme:** WooCommerce \xfczerinden ayn\u0131 saniyede gelen rezervasyon isteklerinde \xe7ak\u0131\u015fmay\u0131 \xf6nlemek i\xe7in veritaban\u0131 seviyesinde atomik kilit mekanizmas\u0131 devreye al\u0131nd\u0131.\\n\\n### \ud83d\udcb0 Vergi Hesaplama D\xfczeltmesi\\n- **Do\u011fru Vergi Matrah\u0131:** Depozito \xf6demelerinde verginin sadece \xf6denen depozito \xfczerinden de\u011fil, **toplam rezervasyon tutar\u0131** \xfczerinden hesaplanmas\u0131 sa\u011fland\u0131. Bu sayede faturaland\u0131rma ve muhasebe s\xfcre\xe7leri hatas\u0131z hale getirildi.\\n\\n### \ud83c\udfa8 Kullan\u0131c\u0131 Aray\xfcz\xfc\\n- **\xd6deme Ayarlar\u0131 Uyar\u0131s\u0131:** WooCommerce aktif oldu\u011funda, kullan\u0131c\u0131lar\u0131n yanl\u0131\u015f (lokal) \xf6deme ayarlar\u0131yla vakit kaybetmesini \xf6nlemek i\xe7in \\"\xd6deme i\u015flemleri WooCommerce taraf\u0131ndan y\xf6netilmektedir\\" \u015feklinde bilgilendirici bir uyar\u0131 eklendi.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Nas\u0131l G\xfcncellerim?**\\nWordPress y\xf6netim panelinizden **Eklentiler** sayfas\u0131n\u0131 ziyaret ederek g\xfcncellemeyi tek t\u0131kla y\xfckleyebilirsiniz. Bu s\xfcr\xfcm **Kritik** olarak i\u015faretlenmi\u015ftir, t\xfcm kullan\u0131c\u0131lar\u0131n en k\u0131sa s\xfcrede ge\xe7i\u015f yapmas\u0131 \xf6nerilir.\\n\\nG\xfcvenli ve keyifli kiralamalar! \ud83d\ude97\ud83d\udca8"},{"id":"v4-6-0-released","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4-6-0-released","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-01-16-v4-6-0-released.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-01-16-v4-6-0-released.md","title":"v4.6.0 Yay\u0131nda! \ud83d\ude80","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.6.0 s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu s\xfcr\xfcm, uzun zamand\u0131r beklenen VIP Transfer Mod\xfcl\xfc, geli\u015fmi\u015f rota y\xf6netimi ve esnek fiyatland\u0131rma motoru gibi b\xfcy\xfck \xf6zellikler i\xe7eriyor.","date":"2026-01-16T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"v4.6.0","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/v-4-6-0"},{"inline":true,"label":"vip-transfer","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/vip-transfer"}],"readingTime":1.5,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4-6-0-released","title":"v4.6.0 Yay\u0131nda! \ud83d\ude80","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","v4.6.0","vip-transfer"],"date":"2026-01-16T00:00:00.000Z"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"v4.6.1 Yay\u0131nda! \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4-6-1-released"},"nextItem":{"title":"v4.5.5 Yay\u0131nda! \ud83d\ude80","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4-5-5-released"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.6.0** s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu s\xfcr\xfcm, uzun zamand\u0131r beklenen **VIP Transfer Mod\xfcl\xfc**, geli\u015fmi\u015f rota y\xf6netimi ve esnek fiyatland\u0131rma motoru gibi b\xfcy\xfck \xf6zellikler i\xe7eriyor.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n:::info Written before 6.0.0\\nThis post is the record of a release that shipped **before 6.0.0**, which renamed the plugin\'s post types, taxonomies, options, meta keys and hooks. The identifiers below are the names those versions actually used, and they are kept that way on purpose. For the current names \u2014 and a conversion table \u2014 see [the 6.0.7 release post](./2026-08-23-rentiva-v6.0.7-release.md).\\n:::\\n\\n## \ud83c\udf1f \xd6ne \xc7\u0131kanlar\\n\\n### \ud83d\ude80 VIP Transfer Mod\xfcl\xfc (\u015eof\xf6rl\xfc Hizmet)\\nArt\u0131k sadece ara\xe7 kiralama de\u011fil, **VIP Transfer** hizmeti de verebilirsiniz!\\n- **Noktadan Noktaya Transfer:** Belirli lokasyonlar aras\u0131nda sabit veya mesafeye dayal\u0131 fiyatland\u0131rma.\\n- **\u015eof\xf6rl\xfc Ara\xe7 Kiralama:** Saatlik veya g\xfcnl\xfck \u015fof\xf6rl\xfc ara\xe7 opsiyonlar\u0131.\\n- **Ekstra Hizmetler:** Kar\u015f\u0131lama, bebek koltu\u011fu, ikramlar gibi ekstralar.\\n\\n### \ud83d\uddfa\ufe0f Rota ve Lokasyon Y\xf6netimi\\nAdmin panelinden detayl\u0131 **Rota Y\xf6netimi** yapabilirsiniz.\\n- Kalk\u0131\u015f ve Var\u0131\u015f noktalar\u0131 i\xe7in \xf6zel fiyatlar tan\u0131mlay\u0131n.\\n- \u0130ki nokta aras\u0131ndaki mesafeyi ve s\xfcreyi otomatik hesaplay\u0131n veya manuel girin.\\n\\n### \ud83d\udcb0 Esnek Fiyatland\u0131rma Motoru\\nTransferler i\xe7in geli\u015fmi\u015f fiyatland\u0131rma se\xe7enekleri:\\n- **Sabit Fiyat:** \\"Havaliman\u0131 -> \u015eehir Merkezi: 500 TL\\" gibi sabit rotalar olu\u015fturun.\\n- **Mesafe Bazl\u0131:** KM ba\u015f\u0131na \xfccretlendirme ile dinamik fiyatlar hesaplay\u0131n.\\n\\n### \ud83d\udd0d Geli\u015fmi\u015f Transfer Arama\\nYeni **`[mhm_rentiva_transfer_search]`** k\u0131sa kodu ile web sitenize profesyonel bir transfer arama motoru ekleyin.\\n- Tarih, saat, kalk\u0131\u015f ve var\u0131\u015f noktas\u0131 se\xe7imi.\\n- Yolcu say\u0131s\u0131 ve bagaj kapasitesine g\xf6re ara\xe7 filtreleme.\\n\\n### \ud83d\udee1\ufe0f Operasyonel Kontrol (Buffer Time)\\nAra\xe7lar\u0131n\u0131z\u0131n temizli\u011fi ve haz\u0131rl\u0131\u011f\u0131 i\xe7in iki rezervasyon aras\u0131na otomatik **Tampon S\xfcre (Buffer Time)** ekleyebilirsiniz. Art\u0131k ara\xe7lar\u0131n\u0131z\u0131n \\"M\xfcsait\\" durumu daha ger\xe7ek\xe7i y\xf6netiliyor.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f D\xfczeltmeler ve \u0130yile\u015ftirmeler\\n\\n- **Cart & Payment:** WooCommerce sepet entegrasyonu \\"Depozito\\" veya \\"Tam \xd6deme\\" se\xe7enekleriyle g\xfc\xe7lendirildi.\\n- **Data Integrity:** Transfer detaylar\u0131 (kalk\u0131\u015f/var\u0131\u015f, yolcu say\u0131s\u0131) art\u0131k sipari\u015f notlar\u0131na ve meta verilerine eksiksiz kaydediliyor.\\n\\n---\\n\\n**Nas\u0131l G\xfcncellerim?**\\nWordPress panelinizden otomatik g\xfcncelleme yapabilirsiniz. Herhangi bir sorun ya\u015farsan\u0131z l\xfctfen GitHub \xfczerinden veya destek sayfam\u0131zdan bize ula\u015f\u0131n.\\n\\nKeyifli s\xfcr\xfc\u015fler! \ud83c\udfce\ufe0f\ud83d\udca8"},{"id":"v4-5-5-released","metadata":{"permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4-5-5-released","editUrl":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade/mhm-rentiva-docs/tree/main/blog/2026-01-15-v4-5-5-released.md","source":"@site/i18n/de/docusaurus-plugin-content-blog/2026-01-15-v4-5-5-released.md","title":"v4.5.5 Yay\u0131nda! \ud83d\ude80","description":"MHM Rentiva v4.5.5 s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu s\xfcr\xfcm, kararl\u0131l\u0131k iyile\u015ftirmeleri, kritik performans d\xfczeltmeleri ve dok\xfcmantasyon altyap\u0131s\u0131nda b\xfcy\xfck yenilikler i\xe7eriyor.","date":"2026-01-15T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":true,"label":"release","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/release"},{"inline":true,"label":"update","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/update"},{"inline":true,"label":"v4.5.5","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/tags/v-4-5-5"}],"readingTime":0.64,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"MaxHandMade","title":"Maintainer","url":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade","imageURL":"https://github.com/MaxHandMade.png","key":"maxhandmade","page":null}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"v4-5-5-released","title":"v4.5.5 Yay\u0131nda! \ud83d\ude80","authors":["maxhandmade"],"tags":["release","update","v4.5.5"],"date":"2026-01-15T00:00:00.000Z"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"v4.6.0 Yay\u0131nda! \ud83d\ude80","permalink":"/mhm-rentiva-docs/de/blog/v4-6-0-released"}},"content":"MHM Rentiva **v4.5.5** s\xfcr\xfcm\xfc yay\u0131nland\u0131! Bu s\xfcr\xfcm, kararl\u0131l\u0131k iyile\u015ftirmeleri, kritik performans d\xfczeltmeleri ve dok\xfcmantasyon altyap\u0131s\u0131nda b\xfcy\xfck yenilikler i\xe7eriyor.\\n\\n\x3c!--truncate--\x3e\\n\\n## \ud83c\udf1f \xd6ne \xc7\u0131kanlar\\n\\n*   **G\xfcvenlik & Mimari:** Plugin kaynak kodlar\u0131 art\u0131k Private bir repoda korunurken, dok\xfcmantasyon (bu site) Public bir repoda herkesin eri\u015fimine a\xe7\u0131k hale getirildi.\\n*   **Performans:** Raporlama mod\xfcl\xfcndeki SQL sorgular\u0131, `DATE()` fonksiyonu kald\u0131r\u0131larak indeks kullan\u0131m\u0131na uygun hale getirildi. Art\u0131k \xe7ok daha h\u0131zl\u0131 \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor.\\n*   **Mobil Uyumluluk:** Ara\xe7 detay sayfalar\u0131 mobilde art\u0131k ta\u015fma yapm\u0131yor, butonlar ve g\xf6rseller tam uyumlu.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udee0\ufe0f D\xfczeltmeler\\n\\n*   **Fixed:** `Plugin.php` i\xe7indeki m\xfckerrer kodlar temizlendi.\\n*   **Fixed:** `ReportRepository` s\u0131n\u0131f\u0131ndaki yava\u015f sorgular optimize edildi.\\n*   **Fixed:** Ara\xe7 k\u0131yaslama sayfas\u0131ndaki hizalama sorunlar\u0131 giderildi.\\n*   **Fixed:** \\"Hizmete Kapal\u0131\\" (Out of Use) etiketi art\u0131k varyasyonlu \xfcr\xfcnlerde de do\u011fru \xe7al\u0131\u015f\u0131yor.\\n\\n## \ud83d\udce6 Y\xfckseltme\\n\\nWordPress panelinizden otomatik g\xfcncelleme yapabilirsiniz. Herhangi bir sorun ya\u015farsan\u0131z l\xfctfen GitHub \xfczerinden veya destek sayfam\u0131zdan bize ula\u015f\u0131n.\\n\\nKeyifli kiralamalar! \ud83d\ude97\ud83d\udca8"}]}}')}}]);